{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates","id":1437660,"title":"[5E] The Clan Updates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-02T11:18:03-08:00","id":1437660,"title":"[5E] The Clan Updates","content":"So, we now have all 13 Clans updated as well as a good chunk of bloodlines.<br /> <br /> So this is a thread where we actually GET TO CRITICIZE!<br /> <br /> (not that we don't elsewhere)<br /> <br /> But also approve.<br /> <br /> This is a thread for discussing what updates were the best and the worst of 5E. What you liked and didn't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:44:45-08:00","id":1437667,"title":"","content":"<b>The Good</b><br /> <br /> I really think the <b>Tzimisce</b> are the best update for the game and that's going to be a controversial pick at best. I think that they were always sort of hamstrung by the fact they've been tied to the <i>Necroscope</i> franchise as the utterly alien EVIL vampires that wear people's skin. I felt they were kind of a joke in the Modern Nights. I have always preferred the more dark, elegant, and sinister ones as portrayed in the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> However, I will say that the problem with them is they're a little too tied to Romanian legends and depictions that make them a bit of a cariacture. I think that the new versions being &quot;dragons in human form&quot; which are obsessed with owning things and being feudal overlords all across the globe is a more interesting take on them,<br /> <br /> <b>The Bad</b><br /> <br /> I think my biggest issue is with <b>The Thin Bloods</b>. I absolutely love that they have a bigger role in the game and am going to applaud a lot of the changes like the fact they're the only vampires who are effectively &quot;alive&quot; and only need a fraction of animal blood compared to most vampires. Plus, they can daywalk and not frenzy. It makes them useful if you want to play a Friendly Neighborhood Vampire.<br /> <br /> But I'm not feeling Thin Blooded Alchemy. I feel like they should be able to get at least one Discipline to be able to put 3 dots in or maybe learn 1 dot in any Discipline they want. Thin Blooded Alchemy as a form of Hedge Magic is fine but it seems to be something that I think most Thin Bloods wouldn't have.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mixed</b><br /> <br /> I have mixed feelings on the handling of both the <b>Lasombra</b> and <b>Tremere</b>. I think the Lasombra joining the Camarilla was a big and well-justified stunt but I feel like the portrayal would have benefited if it had come with a write up of the 50% or so who had stayed with the Sabbat. Ditto, I think the Tremere Council of Seven being destroyed was a big shake up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:01:09-08:00","id":1437669,"title":"","content":"<b>The Good</b><br /> <br /> Everything I bloody well wrote.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bad</b><br /> <br /> Whither Grumbleduke?<br /> <br /> <b>The Mixed</b><br /> <br /> Everything I didn't write, because I didn't write it, which ipso facto can't be as good as the material I did write.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:04:57-08:00","id":1437670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437669#post1437669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Good</b><br /> <br /> Everything I bloody well wrote.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bad</b><br /> <br /> Whither Grumbleduke?<br /> <br /> <b>The Mixed</b><br /> <br /> Everything I didn't write, because I didn't write it, which ipso facto can't be as good as the material I did write.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHITHER GRUMBLEDUKE IS THE BEST!<br /> <br /> You are so wrong!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:19:56-08:00","id":1437674,"title":"","content":"I like the way the Tremere, Hecata, and Lasombra received the biggest in-game changes. These makes all three clans more playable. I also like the Tzimisce changes, which are less a change in setting than redefining what the clan has always been.<br /> <br /> I am ambivalent about the changes to the other clans - because there have been few changes to the other clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T13:25:11-08:00","id":1437686,"title":"","content":"The Good<br /> It's no secret that V5 isn't my favourite edition, so if we ignore all other editions and just focus on what's good in V5, the <b>Gangrel</b> are kinda the standout winners among the clans. Animalism, Fortitude and Protean are some of the V5 winners, with plenty of possible synergistic options that enable players to really design very different powersets. I'd say the <b>Ventrue</b>, if you ignore the unfortunate 'balancing' of Dominate, also come off as quite interesting; Presence is more well rounded and has never been so powerful and somewhat makes up for the lackluster Dominate.<br /> <br /> Mixed:<br /> The <b>Hecata</b>. The schematic for the house is a sound one, but the execution, and then how they've decorated, is a no-no. The Flesh eaters shouldn't be here, for starters. There are some good ideas here, really, I just feel that the place where the Hecata is now would work best as a temporary stop; The necromancers can't stand one-another, naturally, their sect should fracture, and finally we should be able to work them into games as normalized bloodlines that we don't need to think of an excuse for every time we want to put them in the city. V5 has set up the Dominoes, we need to see them fall.<br /> <b>Ravnos</b>- This is just a different clan. They're nothing alike. It's not a bad bloodline, but I liked the Ravnos.<br /> <b>Malkavians</b>- Nothing wrong fluff wise. Weakness is fine. It's just their discipline spread got hit the hardest.<br /> <br /> Agonizing:<br /> <b>Tremere</b>.<br /> I see what they're doing, I know why they're doing it. I understand why they're doing it. I know some people like this stuff. But the Tremere... Nobody likes the Tremere, that's how they roll. You're not supposed to like them. They're not supposed to have a number of different groups and you can find one that reflects your values. The Weakness of the Tremere has always been that you're a Tremere wth a giant fucking pyramid behind you, and the strength of being a Tremere is that you've got a giant fucking pyramid behind you. This just takes all that away. I've gone to great lengths justifying the fluff; The story is salvagable. It can be made to work, but I don't like what I've seen so far.<br /> Mechanically they're an absolute disaster. Also, maybe I'm more hardcore than most, but the -we actually researched motherfucking RL wizardry and let those philosophies influence our setting- of prior editions was amazing, and it's sorely missing here.<br /> <br /> Just bad<br /> <b>Lasombra</b>- Oblivion's just bad, and the weakness is nonsense. The defection just shouldn't work.<br /> <b>Tzmisce</b>- The nuance is gone. The camp is also gone. What's there to love? (Edit: actually the bane is good, the rest is terrible tho) <br /> <br /> I Hate it<br /> <b>Thin-Bloods- </b> If they can't normally use disciplines AND don't know shit, they can't survive at all as vampires. Thin blood alchemy is metaphysically <i>wrong </i>because the vampire state itself is alchemy and they're incomplete and.... Like, they're halfway between ghouls and vampires, but instead of being mechanically halfway between ghouls and vampires, they're something entirely different? Also thin blood alchemy's just... you're mixing your blood with baking soda? Chaos magic isn't just fucking shitting in buckets and then wearing them on your head while singing your favourite <i>Queen</i> songs to work miracles.<u> If you're going to give us new magic, don't do it by showing your absolute contempt for magic</u>. And they gain a clan by eating up? The whole thinblood writeup just strikes me as so.... not World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-04-2021, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T13:25:11-08:00","id":1437687,"title":"","content":"<b>The Good:</b><br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are easily at the top of the list for me, as little as we finally got of them. Though I will say that I do have some issues with them. Mostly their new discipline spread and using Dominate+Protean for Fleshcrafting.<br /> <br /> At a close second is the Hecata. While I know plenty dislike the merging of the Bloodlines of Death into something that's one part Clan, one part Sect, one part Cult, I love them. For starters it adds some real interesting politics to one of the most organized Clans of the setting that they sorely lacking. Sure you could have local Giovanni doing their personal scheming but now we have some real factionalism within the Clan that can really play well into chronicles.<br /> <br /> Though I will concede that the inclusion of the Nagaraja (as all the other Bloodlines had ties to the original Clan of Death) is a bit of an oddity and maybe doesn't entirely work.<br /> <br /> But also one of the things nice things about their write-up that I think the Giovanni were long overdue for is them taking about how the Clan can interact with the Sects as well as how individual members can join non-Hecata coteries.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mixed:</b><br /> <br /> The Ravnos. They feel very one step forward, one step back. I supposed part of it could be blamed on how short the Companion is and that it came out long, long after other books that could have given some pages to flesh them out more. <br /> <br /> <b>The Bad:</b><br /> <br /> The Thin-bloods. Like CTPhipps, I'm not a fan of Thin-blood Alchemy. Though I'm also not a big fan of Thin-bloods period and them getting into the V5 Rulebook while six of Clans didn't and it years to get them all, has long left a bitter taste in my mouth. So I'm not exactly an unbiased person when it comes to them.<br /> <br /> The Salubri. While I was never the biggest fan of them, I did like their chapter in Lore of the Bloodlines, especially getting away from the Seven being the extent of the Healer Caste outside of certain parts of the world. So naturally when the Companion basically dialed them back to what they were in the early days of VtM, complete with omitting the other two Castes (to say nothing of the possibilities in this changing modern world to see a reunification of the Castes) was frustrating.<br /> <br /> Finally, that it too so damn long for us to get all thirteen Clans. While there has been many questionable decisions in V5, that we didn't get all 13 Clans in Rulebook or failing that, all of them by the second V5 book, was one of the worst in my eyes. It's made many of the books since the Rulebook feel incomplete, missing important important parts.<br /> <br /> I get the appeal of trying to go back to the early days of VtM, to try and capture some of that old charm but VtM has long moved beyond those nights. Cutting out half the Clans after years and years of us having access to them and have gotten used to the world with all 13 Clans around was stupid move that hindered the development of the V5 world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T15:17:20-08:00","id":1437702,"title":"","content":"<b>The Good:<br /> Brujah</b><br /> I like what's been written about their manipulative side. <i>Anarch</i> has lots of ideas about involvement with fringe political groups, which aren't all attribute to Brujah, but they fit well enough.<br /> <b>Malkavians</b><br /> The interest in blood properties, self-medication and kine with overlooked minds are fun touches. The gatekeeping prerequisites over dementation is annoying like several amalgams, although I've no complaints about the power itself. The only old dementation power that I'm sorry to see missing is passion. Without the requirement to assign a mechanically defined derangement, I find it tempting to not even bother presenting a recognisable mental illness, rather simply deciding how they act and feel when the bane kicks in.<br /> <b>Banu Haqim</b><br /> They're almost a fixture of the Camarilla now, whereas they look more like guests in previous editions. As I've suggested for several clans, they could be detailed further in a book that isn't directly about them, in their case one about Ashirra or even a specific Ashirra domain.<br /> <b>Ministry</b><br /> I suspect that I'm choosing to interprete the Ministry in my own preferred way rather than sincerely taking them as written. Sometimes it sounds like a super cult with a lot of black sheep and sometimes it sounds like any other decentralised clan. I'm glad that one their three disciplines isn't themed around snakes, corruption and Egyptian mythology any more. I kind of want to use them as a louche alternative to Toreador; maybe a missired Brujah is more appropriate. As with Banu Haqim, their inclusion into a sect simplifies their inclusion, as main characters, into games based within that sect.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mixed:</b><br /> <b>Gangrel</b><br /> I think they need more culture. A lot of it could be shared with kindred of other clans who live in their coteries/packs. I also think that Earth Meld is substantially lacking compared to its VtR counterpart. It makes internal sense that a whole body transformation is more advanced than a partial one and that doesn't extend to clothes, but if it were that much easier, the ability to survive without a haven could a bigger part of the clan's identity.<br /> <b>Lasombra</b><br /> One of the old stereotypes about them said that if everybody thinks that your a good manipulator, how good you can be? These Lasombra sound so self-serving and insincere that it's a wonder anyone tolerates them, even next to other kindred. At least Dark Ages editions had plenty of earnest Keepers.<br /> I think that their access to obtenebration as vampires should be more justified. I've recently been toying with the notion that Oblivion itself is nothing rather than the first and last realm of the cosmos, but I'm guessing that couldn't adequately explain aspects of it, like how &quot;nothing&quot; could be used to pick up objects.<br /> On bright side, I do like what <i>Shadows of New York</i> had to say about them.<br /> <b>Toreador</b><br /> That bane is brutal, but it has interesting cultural implications. Ideally, you want shape anywhere you need to use disciplines and avoid places where you can't do that, which is probably almost everywhere. That leaves them in very gilded cages, which makes their loyalty to the Camarilla understandable. I'd rather their base instincts be more base, but they've been something like this in every edition, excluding Ishtarri and Revised antitribu.<br /> <b>Tzimisce</b><br /> They exceeded my low expectations and evoked some concepts that I hadn't previously considered, but I can imagine how those of you who liked Tzimisce in the first place could feel constrained by the possessive theme.<br /> And they need the revenants back. The Sabbat book might be a good place to do that.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bad:</b><br /> <b>Ravnos</b><br /> Well they're not culturally problematic or pigeon-holed, but tricksters? Dare devils? Rogues? I don't see the point. I could say the same about chimerstry in any of its iterations. This is the one I prefer in previous editions. But I was never fussed about them anyway.<br /> <b>Compulsions</b><br /> With so many clans, some of the compulsions are bit too specific for my taste.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Rest:</b><br /> I haven't decided about these because either I haven't given them the attention that they deserve (Nosferatu, Ventrue and thin-bloods), I think I need more detail (Tremere), I'm not invested enough (Salubri) or I like the Giovanni so much that I can't criticise their clan in good faith. I'd only disapprove if the Giovanni were killed off, white-washed or if their Mafia stereotype was confirmed; bonus disapproval points if they were specifically based on Italian-American stereotypes. Damn Fianna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-02-2021, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T15:28:40-08:00","id":1437703,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm going against the grain, but I am not a fan of the Tzimisce revamp at all. I feel that swapping Auspex for Dominate removes the clan\u2019s history as erudite seers and mystics with a thirst for knowledge, while a clan-wide mastery of Dominate adds a level of redundancy in Sabbat Leadership with Lasombra (making Lasombra a redundancy in both sects now), and undermines/deletes their millenia-forged legacy of control through fear and mastery of blood bonds.<br /> <br /> The compulsion sounds like a stereotypical Ravnos vice, which I thought we were trying to get away from.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Ravnos, not a screaming fan of the their changes, either. I feel the &quot;Obfuscate &amp; Presence combo because they are sneaky, smooth talkers&quot; schtick was already repetitive with two clans.<br /> <br /> Other than those two, I have no complaints about the clans in V5. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T18:40:11-08:00","id":1437727,"title":"","content":"I admit, I have mixed feelings on the <b>Ravnos</b> update because I didn't think the clan was broken as of RAVNOS: REVISED. I felt like they were properly updated by expanding them to be a clan that incorporated the Indian Rakshasa myth. I've always disliked the European centrism of the game and incorporating another alternative to the Caine myth (the Followers of Set otherwise standing alone) felt like a good thing.<br /> <br /> However, I admit have a bigger reason to dislike the Ravnos update in the fact that I think they've royally stepped into what I loved about the Malkavians. Ever since Second Edition, I've always been a fan of the idea of them as tricksters with their &quot;pranks&quot; being designed to strike at the haughty and powerful.<br /> <br /> Now the Ravnos has seemingly taken this role and it annoys me. What do the Malkavians do then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T20:00:34-08:00","id":1437735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437727#post1437727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I have mixed feelings on the <b>Ravnos</b> update because I didn't think the clan was broken as of RAVNOS: REVISED. I felt like they were properly updated by expanding them to be a clan that incorporated the Indian Rakshasa myth. I've always disliked the European centrism of the game and incorporating another alternative to the Caine myth (the Followers of Set otherwise standing alone) felt like a good thing.<br /> <br /> However, I admit have a bigger reason to dislike the Ravnos update in the fact that I think they've royally stepped into what I loved about the Malkavians. Ever since Second Edition, I've always been a fan of the idea of them as tricksters with their &quot;pranks&quot; being designed to strike at the haughty and powerful.<br /> <br /> Now the Ravnos has seemingly taken this role and it annoys me. What do the Malkavians do then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree for the most part. Though I've had some issue with the idea of Malkavians as tricksters mostly because of the bad ideas it can give players about the Clan. But then I've long become paranoid about having player have little experience with declaring they want to play a Malk because of some early horrible Fishmalk encounters I've had.<br /> <br /> And it's another reason why I find the removal of the full 13 Clans from Rulebook to be so frustrating. The V5 Companion write-up would have been more tolerable if it had just been the Clan write-up in the Rulebook with later books adding to it. Like I recall the Camarilla book talking about their recent in-roads in India. If we had the Ravnos from the start, that would have been a perfect setup to talk about the Indian Ravnos. In fact, I would have had the Indian Ravnos join the Camarilla like the Banu Haqim did, with a more detailed write-up on that branch of the Clan present in that book. Perhaps even an alternate Clan Compulsion for them.<br /> <br /> But then I could say the same for the Lasombra, Tzimisce and Hecata as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T20:07:50-08:00","id":1437740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437727#post1437727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I admit have a bigger reason to dislike the Ravnos update in the fact that I think they've royally stepped into what I loved about the Malkavians. Ever since Second Edition, I've always been a fan of the idea of them as tricksters with their &quot;pranks&quot; being designed to strike at the haughty and powerful.<br /> <br /> Now the Ravnos has seemingly taken this role and it annoys me. What do the Malkavians do then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Malkavian tricksters are crazy and want to show people the true nature of reality through their pranks. Ravnos tricksters are vagabonds and grifters who sucker people with illusions. They want to conceal rather than reveal the truth. <br /> <br /> Both clans are tricksters, but the Ventrue, Lasombra, and Tzimisce are all aristocrats. Arguably the Giovanni too. Some degree of overlap is inevitable with 13 clans. Instead of trying to make each clan do different things, which I think is an exercise in futility, it's better to have multiple clans do similar things differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T21:36:41-08:00","id":1437748,"title":"","content":"As someone who approaches V4 mostly from the angle of &quot;what can I poach for my V20 games&quot; here's my perspective on the winners and losers of V5's clans...<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Good:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Assamite/Banu Haqim:</b> hate the name change (those in the Cam are rejecting Haqim), but appreciate that moving Quietus under the auspices of Blood Sorcery (a pretty easy change to make even in V20) eliminates the need to present the castes as separate bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador:</b> The change to their bane from &quot;get lost in a fugue state whenever beautiful things turn up to &quot;suffer penalty to discipline use if not surrounded by beauty&quot; (with the fugue state aspect being worked into the Clan Compulsion) is a big improvement whether in V5 or adapted into V20.<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce:</b> I'd personally have made Vicissitude into a path of Blood Sorcery and made the clan disciplines Animalism, Blood Sorcery and Protean so like the Assamites/Banu Haqim you eliminate the mechanical need for separate bloodlines and make the New vs. Old Clan a purely cultural element with both the body sculptors and Koldun employing Blood Sorcery in ways that are different culturally, but still connected. The main thing I love about the update is the revision to the Clan Weakness to make it both more meaningful (the charge need not be just native soil) and that instead of degrading checks, its degrading willpower which is slightly more manageable. It also makes them basically the Anti-Ravnos in that their bane requires them to maintain a stable location, while the Ravnos bane requires them to NOT establish roots.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue:</b> The main thing I like about the V5 update is again the change to the clan weakness. Changing it from &quot;gets nothing without feeding on prey type&quot; to &quot;must spend willpower to feed on a non-prey type&quot; makes them slightly less ridiculous, particularly given some past examples whose prey type amounted to a single person or otherwise very limited group that would be hard to maintain long term. It also makes it a bit easier to run a chronicle with a bit more travel where not having their chosen prey available meant that Ventrue would be utterly incapable of feeding. Now its just difficult vs. impossible.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Bad:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos:</b> Its great that their bane is all thematic and all, but at a certain point campaign playability has to enter the decision making process and being unable to set down basic roots without burning to death makes Ravnos far more difficult to integrate than most other clans. Its either going to be a major pain in the butt or not come up at all. It's also the only bane I physically changed from V5 in adapting the new ones into V20... switching from possible agg damage to willpower loss (making it the opposite of the Tzimisce) for staying in one place too long.<br /> <br /> <b>Thinbloods:</b> I don't even quite know where to begin other than &quot;WHY!?!&quot; Thinblood Alchemy is the single best argument for V5 occurring a parallel universe to the previous material as it so utterly contradicts everything we've previously been presented about the thin-blooded. Throw in &quot;gain a dot in a discipline based on what I last ate&quot; and &quot;can't actually permanently learn disciplines&quot; and they just feel like a foreign invasive species instead of a logical offshoot of previous VtM lore.<br /> <br /> <b>Hecata:</b> Not so much for the Giovanni as all the other cultures appropriated via the merger of the other bloodlines into one giant potpourri that for some reason ended up with the Giovanni clan weakness but the Cappadocian discipline spread... except Oblivion sucks. The Loresheets feel like weak consolation in V5, but this is one of the &quot;I'm just going to ignore this one in my V20 game as long as possible&quot; elements.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra:</b> I know their own flaw could be weaksauce, but increased difficulty using modern tech, plus the horrid Oblivion rework combine to make this not good. I adapted the change about looking weird both in mirrors and through cameras into my V20 adaptation, but left the tech penalties off and kept Obtenebration because it doesn't suck.<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu:</b> Not a fan of the change to the class weakness basically making it harder to use their signature Obfuscate to actually disguise their appearance.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Meh:</b></u><br /> <br /> The <b>Brujah</b>, <b>Caitiff</b>, <b>Gangrel</b> and <b>Setites/Ministry</b> didn't change appreciably so not much to say there.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavians:</b> I tend to prefer the Dominate Malks to the Dementation Malks in V20 mainly because Auspex + Dominate already give you 90% of the tools Dementation does, but with greater flexibility overall... so making the Dominate Malk discipline standard is an improvement to me. The downside is that the bane is a lot harder to apply in V20 until I figure out a way to incorporate compulsions into V20 in a reasonable way.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere:</b> Version differences on Blood Sorcery/Thaumaturgy I consider a separate issue from the Clans proper and the change to their bane from being easier to blood bond to having a harder time creating them is just very 'change for change's sake' for me... hence meh.<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri:</b> I've legitimately never seen a Salubri played or attempted to add one as an NPC to these are more just &quot;Meh&quot; by reason of don't care enough to even fully read the entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T01:06:19-08:00","id":1437770,"title":"","content":"Ah, I forgot a few factions<br /> <br /> Meh- <b>Salubri</b>- Don't care for it. Wasted a good chance to give us the warriors. Also feels like someone who only had a cursory glance at the old clan wrote this up; the Salubri are more than this. No effort involved.<br /> <br /> Agonizing- The <b>Setites</b><br /> They've adapted to the absurdities of the V5 metaplot pretty well; throwing most of the Setites behind the Anarchs is a good and interesting development. What I can't stand is this absolutely absurd two-party split, both taking up the opposite and most extreme ends of Heresy. Yeah, both sides are Heretical. Imagine 90% of political thought just decided to flock to the extremes of either destroying all computers or uploading our brains into machines, and nobody thought up a middle ground. That's this setite split. You're either against Set by willfully misinterpreting his philosophy or you're against Set by siding with a bunch of heretics who're following radically different faiths; either way you're an apostate. And thus 100% of those formerly within the Settite faith are now apostates... Whut? I feel this is more to reflect some American reality of bipartisan political lines, but it doesn't work at all for a religion. Some really bone-headed stuff.<br /> <br /> Bad- &quot;<b>Banu Haqim</b>&quot;<br /> Coming off a prior edition, this is just terrible; the caste system they've worked so hard to establish is uprooted, Quietus is magic even though they've been weird about magic and... Yeah.<br /> In V5, it's just meh. I have reservations about the use of a new Arabic name for a clan that's supposedly half-diversifying and half-hating Islam; it's just backwards, perhaps a little pretentious. I will give credit where credit's due; The new logo is an improvement; It's nice to have something I can casually draw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-03-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T01:09:34-08:00","id":1437771,"title":"","content":"I, like some others, have imported the bits I like into V20. I've scrapped the rest.<br /> <br /> I went with the Ravnos weakness reducing Willpower rather than agg damage. The latter is just too deadly. Other than that, I like their new write-up.<br /> <br /> I sort of like the new Tzimisce flaw, but I feel there's definitely a loss of a lot of good thematic stuff for the clan as a whole. As such, I use the old flaw with the V5 version being for the Old Clan. I use the Discipline spread from V20, but if I used V5 rules, I would just make it be Animalism, Auspex and Blood Sorcery (with Vicissitude as rituals, given the length of time they take anyway; this also allows Kolduns to use the same spread).<br /> <br /> The Salubri weakness seems too harsh, as well. I'd go with the V20 version for the Healers and Warriors.<br /> <br /> I'm not sold on the Hecata yet, or the Camarilla Lasombra. The Hecata thing feels too neat and the Lasombra thing feels too forced, even with the lengthy rationale for why it happened. But then again, I also think the Gehenna War thing is iffy, and sort of trivialises the conflicts in the Middle East (i.e., all the vampire religious fanatics have gone there to blow themselves up in an edition that otherwise goes to great lengths to walk back harmful stereotypes).<br /> <br /> The Ministry I'm ambivalent about. I would never make them Anarch, for instance, but I don't mind the move away from Conan-esque evil serpent worshippers. I've made the serpent faction more explicitly Biblical/Gnostic, so the main Setite faction can be affiliated with the Typhonic Beast (as in V20DA). I know that's sort of been the direction since Revised anyway, but then we still had all the evil snake powers until DA offered alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-03-2021, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T01:37:38-08:00","id":1437774,"title":"","content":"Oh, I forgot the Thin-Bloods! I have to say, I massively preferred them in V20 and Revised. Those versions of the Thin-Blooded actually made me want to play one--a combination of the Insight Background, the ability to Incept new Disciplines (or spontaneously learn old ones), and the specific balance of weaknesses and strengths.<br /> <br /> I wasn't sold on Thin-Blood Flaws offering a pick and mix approach to the highest Generations, and I just don't like Thin-Blood Alchemy or free Disciplines from drinking blood. This may be tied to how Blood Sorcery is generally not my bag in V5 anyway, however, and the way Resonance turns humans from walking vitae batteries into walking Discipline batteries instead.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's all highly subjective. Maybe my excitement for the 14th-16th Generations came from seeing them for the first time and the cool lore around them. Perhaps if V5 was my intro to the game, I'd be as excited by this new iteration. (Though, the more I think about it, the more I think it was precisely the lore that drew me in, rather than the rules. The lore is different now, and that may explain it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T02:26:45-08:00","id":1437777,"title":"","content":"i think it's a fairly mixed bag<br /> <br /> certain things like allowing the tzimisce bane to tie the tzimisce to other stuff then dirt for example i think was an excellent idea but the good is mostly refinment of already established stuff which i apresiate but isn't particularly interesting to discuss but it's worth a mention.<br /> <br /> that said there are some big problems with certain clans<br /> <br /> the lasombra changes are fine in theory but completely botched in execution: (both their integration into the camarilla and making obtenebration more necromancy-ish for oblivion.)<br /> <br /> the hecata are interesting but making loresheets the only way the different bloodlines express themselves a massively missed opportunity to create younger hecata that could have influence from different bloodlines in them. (for example make it so their bite have slightly different effects in their flavor text so the samedi bite causes necrosis or giving their oblivion powers different negative consequences for a crit rouse themed around the bloodlines)<br /> <br /> also i think the changes to the ravnos as somebody else said one step forward 2 steps back because while this is the first one that properly got rid of the whole gypsie stuff, it sorta left them with no vampiric identity. (for example the malkavians are these creatures where you never know what mad scheme they're working towards because they're both very knowledgeable but also mad as a hatter. or the gangrel being these violent predators of the wild.)<br /> also it's very obvious that the only reason they have presence is because they couldn't think of another discipline to combo with obfuscate for the chimerestry amalgam and their new bane is to harsh as it stands.<br /> <br /> i never really cared for the salubri but their bane is waaaaay to harsh. you either need a very forgiving ST or need to be bugfuck mad to want to play that<br /> <br /> other then that it's mostly smaller changes like giving the tzimisce dominate or the precise mechanics of the nos bane that i take issue with (things that need refining and are worth mentioning as wel but not so interesting to discuss).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 03-03-2021, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T03:24:34-08:00","id":1437781,"title":"","content":"Personally, I actually find the Thin Bloods to be the best addition to the game and I really like Thin Blood Alchemy as an alternative set of powers. The potential for an all-Thin Blood Chronicle is high, although they can be problematic to include in a full Vampire chronicle for various reasons.<br /> <br /> I quite like what they have done with The Ministry also, to a degree, as their inclusion mainly as Anarchs gives a new spin on that sect. The Tzmisce and Ravnos are OK, although I mainly see their uses as NPCs to be honest, along with the Salubri. I haven\u2019t seen any player clambering to play Banu Haqim either, which is another other \u2018add-on\u2019 Clan from the core, although at least one player opted for Lasombra in the Chronicle I am currently running and I personally like the Hecata Clan, if I could get to include one moving on. <br /> <br /> Of the ones I find a bit more difficult in their development, I\u2019d say it is the Tremere. Their weakness to make Blood Bonds (and susceptibility) isn\u2019t as much of a disadvantage as being already Blood Bonded to Elders in the Clan I feel and, thematically, it feels strange that they aren\u2019t ensconced in their own ultra-organized pyramid power structure anymore. I think they have become too easy to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T07:29:55-08:00","id":1437811,"title":"","content":"I would also like to state that I think the <b>Salubri</b> are the second most improved group of the Clans.<br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because I actually think it's possible now to use the Salubri in a standard V:TM horror game and not have them utterly wreck the mood. I've used the Salubri less than virtually every other Clan in the setting and part of that is they simply don't fit the Gothic Punk &quot;personal horror&quot; game of the setting. Being able to heal the injuries of the living and having a flaw of being unable to feed on the unwilling is like a Friendly Neighborhood Vampire Jackpot. You could still kill people during frenzy but they mostly seemed like a boon to those around them and that's terrible if you want to play vampires as a plague to humanity.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% behind the fact the Salubri are just magically tasty as a weakness now (albeit, what a shitty time for any Salubri who shares blood with an Assamite--NO SEX FOR THESE TWO!). However, the fact that they don't have anything that prevents them from feeding on regular people and their Third Eye bleeds during the use of their Disciplines makes it a pretty decent flaw alternative.<br /> <br /> Its been centuries since the Tremere wiped away most records of the Salubri so the majority of vampires have no idea who the hell they are or what they did. If the Salubri are among Anarch territory, they might as well be claiming they're from Clan Pokemon. That means that they're actually somewhat useful in a long term game if you're in a city that has weak Camarilla presence or is controlled by a cult too.<br /> <br /> I also am going to probably get some flack for the fact that I think that nerfing Obeah was the correct decision. Making it so that it is a power of MENTAL healing is something that is a lot less grandiose than other healing and has a severe consequence by screwing with your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T08:35:32-08:00","id":1437816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437811#post1437811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like to state that I think the <b>Salubri</b> are the second most improved group of the Clans... I've used the Salubri less than virtually every other Clan in the setting and part of that is they simply don't fit the Gothic Punk &quot;personal horror&quot; game of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put me down still under MEH. Punk and &quot;personal horror&quot; are extremely overrated. Indeed, I find the more you attempt to tie &quot;horror&quot; to mechanics the LESS horrific it becomes... most terrifying campaign I ever played was a D&amp;D with a GM who knew how to invoke mood and atmosphere through their descriptions (and insisted on playing in their basement by candlelight.<br /> <br /> The fact that the &quot;friendly neighborhood vampire&quot; can try and do all these things to help and yet still won't make a meaningful difference because of all the other vampires, things that go bump in the night, and just ordinary humans being horrible to each other is better at evoking the tragedy of their existence than just making them another garden variety monster. That you have to employ different techniques than you use for every other vampire is, to me as a GM, a plus rather than a negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T08:47:08-08:00","id":1437818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437816#post1437816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put me down still under MEH. Punk and &quot;personal horror&quot; are extremely overrated. Indeed, I find the more you attempt to tie &quot;horror&quot; to mechanics the LESS horrific it becomes... most terrifying campaign I ever played was a D&amp;D with a GM who knew how to invoke mood and atmosphere through their descriptions (and insisted on playing in their basement by candlelight.<br /> <br /> The fact that the &quot;friendly neighborhood vampire&quot; can try and do all these things to help and yet still won't make a meaningful difference because of all the other vampires, things that go bump in the night, and just ordinary humans being horrible to each other is better at evoking the tragedy of their existence than just making them another garden variety monster. That you have to employ different techniques than you use for every other vampire is, to me as a GM, a plus rather than a negative.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a vampire doesn't have to feed on people and isn't a danger to regular humans, it's not a vampire.<br /> <br /> That's the problem of the Salubri.<br /> <br /> If you don't care about the humans you feed on, you're not doing it right either...or it's a Sabbat game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T10:35:31-08:00","id":1437823,"title":"","content":"Without getting into the other clans, I like what 5e has done with thin-bloods a lot.<br /> <br /> First, streamlining what they are. In Revised, you had 14th generation vampires with or without the Thin-Blooded Flaw, who may or may not have been Caitiff, giving you four different potential &quot;types&quot; of thin-bloods. 15th-generation vampires who were all Caitiff with the Thin-Blooded Flaw, plus more severe weaknesses, brought that up to five. OPP introducing 16th-generation vampires brought that up to six. While this was interesting from a conceptual standpoint, and gave a sense of evolution (or devolution) to the youngest generations, the distinctions were only likely to be meaningful in games with lots of thin-bloods. It's better to just give each thin-blood a buffet of Merits and Flaws to pick from.<br /> <br /> The &quot;extra emphasis on Merits and Flaws&quot; approach is more streamlined and gives each thin-blood a lot of customization options. I also like the flavor that past the 13th generation, the rules go out the window, and you never know what powers and weaknesses a given thin-blood is going to manifest. I find that more interesting than each generation growing progressively more feeble in ways predictable enough to have a chart for. Thin-bloods are supposed to be big unknowns and that's harder to maintain when they've been established parts of the setting for 20+ years. (PCs in my current game have met a daywalker thin-blood and they now assume, falsely, this is something all thin-bloods can do.)<br /> <br /> Daywalker thin-bloods are cool. Revised just had 15th-generation ones take a little longer to crisp, which doesn't have nearly the same conceptual oomph. Losing access to Disciplines, Dracula-style, was a good trade-off to pair that with.<br /> <br /> Removing frenzy is cool too, and a big way to drive home that these aren't your ordinary vampires. I've seen frenzy come up vastly more often in games than I have sunlight vulnerability. I <i>might</i> have tweaked it so that thin-bloods still frenzy when they are hungry or starving, but as a whole, good direction.<br /> <br /> Being able to diablerize their way into a clan or become human again is cool. Losing thin-bloodedness via diablerie was already a thing in Revised. I don't see this kind of reward being offered to thin-bloods as often as the setting makes out, though. Maybe among the Anarchs, independents, or Sabbat, but the Camarilla has every reason to discourage diablerie.<br /> <br /> I like the new &quot;you are what you eat&quot; Discipline system for thin-bloods. Personally, I never saw them walking around with more than a handful of Disciplines; they aren't meant to be supernatural powerhouses. The way V5 does it is more interesting than simply capping how many Disciplines they can have, and also lets a clever thin-blood leverage their weakness into a strength if they know in advance there's a particular Discipline they're going to need. Swapping out Disciplines isn't something ordinary vampires get to do. If someone really wants a given thin-blood to have more Disciplines, make &quot;Permanent Discipline Dot or Two&quot; a Merit they can take.<br /> <br /> I also like how it preserves (in spirit) their previous inceptor angle. Thin-bloods inventing new Disciplines in Revised was interesting, but Revised also suffered from significant Discipline bloat. There wasn't really a place for thin-bloods to author entirely new ones under the new rules anymore. (I can understand this being a con to people who preferred the old Discipline system, but I loved V5 trimming things down to a core list and instead opening up multiple powers at each level.)<br /> <br /> I don't see most thin-bloods having Thin-Blood Alchemy, but I dig the gutter magic-slash-&quot;Walter White meth lab&quot; feel to it. We already had chaos magic vampires in the game. Gutter magic is new.<br /> <br /> What I mainly miss is Insight. That should have been a thin-blood-exclusive Discipline alongside Thin-Blood Alchemy. What happened to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T10:42:18-08:00","id":1437824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe among the Anarchs, independents, or Sabbat, but the Camarilla has every reason to discourage diablerie. </div> </div> </div>I've always viewed the Blood Hunt as a carrot and a stick in the Camarilla. The Camarilla isn't nearly as against diablerie as it seems because the threat of it is something they hang over the head of every vampire who lives in their society. The Blood Hunt means that whenever you die, if you're of a Low Enough generation then you can't trust anyone who is weaker to not turn on you. Longtime allies, friends, and lovers may all kill you because the chance to become an Elder is too strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T10:48:12-08:00","id":1437826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437818#post1437818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a vampire doesn't have to feed on people and isn't a danger to regular humans, it's not a vampire.<br /> <br /> That's the problem of the Salubri.<br /> <br /> If you don't care about the humans you feed on, you're not doing it right either...or it's a Sabbat game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your exaggeration doesn\u2019t help your argument.<br /> <br /> V20 Salubri still have to feed from people; they just lose willpower if they feed from unwilling people (and the V20 Sabbat/Warrior Salubri MUST take blood by force or they get no nourishment at all). They gain no special nourishment from animals. They also don\u2019t have special clan traits or disciplines that enable them to better resist Frenzy so a hungry Salubri is every bit as dangerous to humans as any ofher vampire (more dangerous really; a frenzying Salubri is still vulnerable to its clan weakness and so after ripping through its first victim probably has little to no willpower left to try and direct the frenzy).<br /> <br /> Similarly, plenty of vampires have herds of willing vessels, but I hear no complaints from you that those vampires aren\u2019t a danger to regular humans even though they\u2019re functionally identical to Salubri in feeding patterns and risks.<br /> <br /> Likewise, unless you\u2019re letting players run 6th Gens there\u2019s nothing a V20 Salubri can do that heals mortals any better than just giving a mortal your blood directly and letting them burn it to heal themselves (1 BP per health level because humans take Agg as Lethal damage; level 3 Obeah is only a cost savings for vampires needing aggravated wounds healed).<br /> <br /> So I\u2019m not seeing this \u201cfriendly neighborhood vampire\u201d or \u201ccan\u2019t do personal horror\u201d angles as something exclusively Salubri. It\u2019s something any high humanity vampire could choose to be.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s fine to like the V5 Salubri presentation; but mischaracterizing what the previous presentation was just comes off as if you don\u2019t believe the V5 presentation is strong enough to stand on its own against the pre-V5 version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T10:55:53-08:00","id":1437828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437826#post1437826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s fine to like the V5 Salubri presentation; but mischaracterizing what the previous presentation was just comes off as if you don\u2019t believe the V5 presentation is strong enough to stand on its own against the pre-V5 version.</div> </div> </div> </div>A weird argument when my point is I felt the Pre-V5 version sucked and the new one is much more playable.<br /> <br /> But, hey, I'm glad the old Salubri worked for you.<br /> <br /> They just weren't my bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-03-2021, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T12:19:12-08:00","id":1437846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437828#post1437828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A weird argument when my point is I felt the Pre-V5 version sucked and the new one is much more playable.<br /> <br /> But, hey, I'm glad the old Salubri worked for you.<br /> <br /> They just weren't my bag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you stated your argument poorly...<br /> <br /> \u201cIf a vampire doesn't have to feed on people and isn't a danger to regular humans, it's not a vampire.<br /> That's the problem of the Salubri.\u201d<br /> <br /> ...is not an argument of disliking the prior presentation; it\u2019s mischaracterizing the prior presentation as something it is not (i.e. it\u2019s not something capable of personal horror and is never dangerous to humans) seemingly in order to justify your preference for the V5 version.<br /> <br /> A V20 Salubri is every bit as dangerous as any other vampire. Feeding on an unwilling vessel costs it a single willpower even if it drinks them dry (and if true to its demeanor or nature during the night gets that back when they sleep). It is just as prone to frenzy as any other vampire and there is nothing in its nature that prevents a frenzied V20 Salubri from feeding on the closest available human and killing it). It\u2019s signature discipline doesn\u2019t heal humans any better than just feeding them vitae directly would unless you can somehow learn Obeah 7.<br /> <br /> Hell, there\u2019s nothing that prevents a pre-V5 Salubri from being a serial killer. A dead human whose neck you snapped isn\u2019t unwilling to be fed upon anymore and so can be drained dry without even costing the willpower point (or wounds in pre-V20 versions). I may even use that to hide the killer in a vampire murder mystery at some point (if you focus only on the obvious exsanguination you\u2019ll miss that the cause of death was the neck snap and the feeding postmortem).<br /> <br /> So, again, you liking the V5 Salubri better than previous iteration is fine (I said as much previously), but that wasn\u2019t what you said that I replied to. My reply was to correct what you actually said about the previous incarnation that was factually incorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T12:25:52-08:00","id":1437847,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Over all I like the Tzimisce changes. I always preferred the Old Clan I liked the idea of them being feudal lords whose domains were completely and totally theirs. These flavor changes are certainly in that direction. I like changing Vicissitude to Protean and I\u2019m fine with getting rid of Auspex, it never suited them well in my opinion. Animalism, Dominate, and Protean are the Dracula Disciplines so that seems appropriate. I do think that maybe some kind of Sorcery might have been better. The Tzimiscre are lords and command their subjects, this is true, but Dominate is so immediate and convenient. A Ventrue needs to fix a police report or get an advantage in a business deal, he dominates some people and it\u2019s done. I don\u2019t see the Tzimisce that way. I see their dominance as being more permanent, slower, more of an investment in ownership. The Tzimisce have ghouls, they have revenants, the have serfs who have served for generations. The instantaneousness of Dominate seems a bit less thematic too me, plus I thought that the Tzimisce were cool in that they were a ruler Clan that didn\u2019t have a social Discipline. It\u2019s not a big problem for me though, over all I like the changes. I have always wanted Camarilla Tzimisce and now it seems a bit more acceptable, if rare as the book describes.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T12:56:08-08:00","id":1437851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437846#post1437846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you stated your argument poorly...<br /> <br /> \u201cIf a vampire doesn't have to feed on people and isn't a danger to regular humans, it's not a vampire.<br /> That's the problem of the Salubri.\u201d<br /> <br /> ...is not an argument of disliking the prior presentation; it\u2019s mischaracterizing the prior presentation as something it is not (i.e. it\u2019s not something capable of personal horror and is never dangerous to humans) seemingly in order to justify your preference for the V5 version</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Salubri healing actually makes it significantly easier and encourages Salubri to seek out willing vessels as a mechanical incentive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T13:05:19-08:00","id":1437853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437824#post1437824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always viewed the Blood Hunt as a carrot and a stick in the Camarilla. The Camarilla isn't nearly as against diablerie as it seems because the threat of it is something they hang over the head of every vampire who lives in their society. The Blood Hunt means that whenever you die, if you're of a Low Enough generation then you can't trust anyone who is weaker to not turn on you. Longtime allies, friends, and lovers may all kill you because the chance to become an Elder is too strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with sanctioned diablerie during blood hunts is that it's a city-wide event where only one lick gets to claim the prize, and the losers might then get the bright idea to commit diablerie during &quot;off-season.&quot; Or the winner might develop a taste for it and decide they don't want to wait until the next blood hunt. They probably have low odds of &quot;winning&quot; again when there are so many competitors. <br /> <br /> I see some princes allowing diablerie during hunts, but I don't see that as universal. Some princes (I forget where I saw this) may follow the custom that only a sire can diablerize their childe during a blood hunt. Other princes simply don't allow diablerie at all. It's a lot easier to open that door than to shut it after it's open. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla is largely fine with past diablerie committed by elders. They're already low generation and don't have as much incentive to do it again. Even when they do (ala Tyler and Procet), they're part of the club and are likely to keep the matter quiet, lest their childer turn on them. (I doubt that any of Chicago's other primogen knew that Tyler diablerized him; they probably just thought she killed him.) <br /> <br /> Ancillae and neonates have every reason to commit diablerie, more incentive to commit multiple diableries, and they've been known to share how awesome it is with their friends. See: The original Anarch Revolt. As a result, I don't see diablerie being common knowledge in the Camarilla, and don't portray it as such in my games. It's not an especially difficult secret to discover, but most sires don't tell their childer about it as part of Vampire 101. Why would they?<br /> <br /> I don't see it being given out to thin-bloods as a standard reward for loyal service, either. They just have too much incentive to do it again, given their high generations. They have even more incentive to share its benefits with any thin-blooded pals they might have. When elders want to &quot;promote&quot; a thin-blood, I see it being common practice for them to Dominate the whelp into forgetting exactly what happened, and to then make up something about a mumbo jumbo mystic ritual. Only works to elevate thin-bloods into proper clans, can't do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T13:12:28-08:00","id":1437854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437853#post1437853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with sanctioned diablerie during blood hunts is that it's a city-wide event where only one lick gets to claim the prize, and the losers might then get the bright idea to commit diablerie during &quot;off-season.&quot; Or the winner might develop a taste for it and decide they don't want to wait until the next blood hunt. They probably have low odds of &quot;winning&quot; again when there are so many competitors.<br /> <br /> I see some princes allowing diablerie during hunts, but I don't see that as universal. Some princes (I forget where I saw this) may follow the custom that only a sire can diablerize their childe during a blood hunt. Other princes simply don't allow diablerie at all. It's a lot easier to open that door than to shut it after it's open.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is largely fine with past diablerie committed by elders. They're already low generation and don't have as much incentive to do it again. Even when they do (ala Tyler and Procet), they're part of the club and are likely to keep the matter quiet, lest their childer turn on them. (I doubt that any of Chicago's other primogen knew that Tyler diablerized him; they probably just thought she killed him.)<br /> <br /> Ancillae and neonates have every reason to commit diablerie, more incentive to commit multiple diableries, and they've been known to share how awesome it is with their friends. See: The original Anarch Revolt. As a result, I don't see diablerie being common knowledge in the Camarilla, and don't portray it as such in my games. It's not an especially difficult secret to discover, but most sires don't tell their childer about it as part of Vampire 101. Why would they?<br /> <br /> I don't see it being given out to thin-bloods as a standard reward for loyal service, either. They just have too much incentive to do it again, given their high generations. They have even more incentive to share its benefits with any thin-blooded pals they might have. When elders want to &quot;promote&quot; a thin-blood, I see it being common practice for them to Dominate the whelp into forgetting exactly what happened, and to then make up something about a mumbo jumbo mystic ritual. Only works to elevate thin-bloods into proper clans, can't do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's any situation where diablerie is off the table with a Blood Hunt canonically. It's sanctioned for all them.<br /> <br /> I think the only Camarilla offenders that you CANT diablerize are the Red List. Diablerizing one of them is punishable by death. Obviously, a Storyteller is welcome to make it different at their home games. However, I actually think diablerie should be way more common than the books tend to portray it. The constant conflict between vampires for blood and devouring of the young by the old as well as the reverse is something that I think makes the whole thing more interesting.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm assuming the chance for a Thin Blood to diablerize another vampire and be accepted as a vampire in the first place is very-very rare to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-03-2021, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T13:22:25-08:00","id":1437855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437851#post1437851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Salubri healing actually makes it significantly easier and encourages Salubri to seek out willing vessels as a mechanical incentive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I\u2019m just not seeing your argument.<br /> <br /> ANY vampire could heal a mortal just as efficiently by just feeding the mortal their blood (and if you have to heal the same mortal more than twice in year; you\u2019re probably doing something wrong).<br /> <br /> V20 Salubri healing costs 1BP per health level restored; ergo there is ZERO mechanical advantage over just feeding them blood directly (just less physically gross because you\u2019re laying hands instead of biting open your wrist so they can drink).<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can live forever as my ghoul in exchange for me getting to drink from your naturally replenishing mortal blood\u201d is EVERY bit the same level of incentive to get mortals to be willing vessels as \u201cI can spend the blood I take from you, minus what I need to live, to heal people\u201d is.<br /> <br /> And again... in V20 a Salubri can feed on anyone unwilling by either spending a single willpower point or killing the person first and drinking after. It\u2019s basically no different than the V5 Ventrue bane with a prey type of \u201cwilling mortals only.\u201d<br /> <br /> Hell, a V20 Ventrue with its designated prey type as \u201cfreely consenting mortals\u201d would be even MORE of a \u201cfriendly neighborhood vampire\u201d than any Salubri as it couldn\u2019t even spend a willpower or use its disciplines to get a meal and could heal human injuries as easily as any Salubri (and would have to be even more careful since a blood bound mortal can\u2019t be freely consenting and ergo lost as a vessel).<br /> <br /> That\u2019s ultimately why your argument falls flat; there\u2019s nothing innate to the Salubri that actually makes it a \u201cfriendly neighborhood vampire\u201d as compared to any random high humanity vampire of any other clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T15:02:42-08:00","id":1437861,"title":"","content":"Warrior Salubri's where it's at. What a great mistep to treat the healers as the primary Salubri when the Warriors outnumber them so greatly. The Healer Salubri were always a clan of -We were made to die-. <br /> (This is someone who thinks the watcher cast is a bunch of hogshit, though I don't mind the African line) <br /> <br /> The V20 weakness is fair, the V5 weakness is... Garbage. It's a miracle they lasted till the Tremere showed up; simply too dysfunctional. But they're such an inconsequentual clan in modern nights it doesn't really matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T15:12:46-08:00","id":1437864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437861#post1437861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warrior Salubri's where it's at. What a great mistep to treat the healers as the primary Salubri when the Warriors outnumber them so greatly. The Healer Salubri were always a clan of -We were made to die-.<br /> (This is someone who thinks the watcher cast is a bunch of hogshit, though I don't mind the African line)<br /> <br /> The V20 weakness is fair, the V5 weakness is... Garbage. It's a miracle they lasted till the Tremere showed up; simply too dysfunctional. But they're such an inconsequentual clan in modern nights it doesn't really matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do confess I think the Sabbat having Salubri is ridiculous. The Salubri getting dialed back to healers but mental healers (which can be associated with Soul Manipulation) works better, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Warrior Salubri would get annihilated by the Tremere first because, well, they'd fight them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T17:00:25-08:00","id":1437882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437864#post1437864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do confess I think the Sabbat having Salubri is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked them for the irony. And the mystery, as their supposed origin cannot be verified. And you are assuming warrior Salubri are the stereotypical nice Salubri, rather than hard ass paladins who want to kill and are good at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T22:43:38-08:00","id":1437919,"title":"","content":"Some people mentioned that Salubri can't heal physical injury any more, but the Fortitude 2 power, Valeren does this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T01:01:10-08:00","id":1437932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437864#post1437864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warrior Salubri would get annihilated by the Tremere first because, well, they'd fight them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could certainly see at least one or two them embracing the idea of, &quot;He who fights and runs away, (un)lives to fight another <s>day</s> night.&quot; And certainly after the Tremere joined the Camarilla and had the Camarilla's sanction to hunt down and kill the Salubri it would make sense for the few survivors to offer their abilities to the Sabbat since there's no other group who would be able to protect them, and likewise, no other group that could be used as a successful weapon against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> One thing I found interesting about them in the older editions was that the Sabbat Salburi had very little knowledge of their own origins, to the point that they were trying to make deals with the Wan Kuei in order to find out more about the history of their clan. I always figured that it was maybe 2 or 3 warrior Salubri who managed to survive and seek haven with the Sabbat, and they were probably fairly young and recently embraced, and they didn't know very much about their own clan when they joined the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T01:37:48-08:00","id":1437934,"title":"","content":"I always saw the old Salubri Healers as especially thematic, TBH. They're tragic, hunted, desperately trying to be good but maligned as soul-suckers. There's plenty of personal horror, and Gothic Punk, there if you want it.<br /> <br /> That said, the Warriors are indeed where it's at. They were always one of my favourite Sabbat bloodlines, alongside the Harbingers. I guess I have a thing for wronged former-clans who rightfully want to reclaim what's theirs by fighting The Man who stole their shit--which is very punk, BTW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T03:51:45-08:00","id":1437938,"title":"","content":"Another way of doing things <br /> <br /> -Things I'd like to Take forward<br /> <b>Assamites</b>- New clan symbol. The old one was pretty, but too complicated<br /> <b>Tzmisce</b>- The new Bane. Just much more interesting, and we can fall back to -jar of dirt- if it suits us. <br /> <br /> Things I'm nervous about, but probably would take forward<br /> The new <b>Ventrue</b> weakness. I feel they're more leniant on ventrue now for the resonance system, which I don't like, but on the otherhand, it is a more... sensible weakness. The real thing that makes me hesitant is that murdering the ventrue's precious herd to get him to starve to death now just became murdering his herd to make him a bit depressed... But it's <i>probably </i> a good thing. <br /> The new <b>Malkavian</b> weakness. Hmm. Maybe I'd do something different, but it's an improvement at least. <br /> <br /> - I can work with this for a few games, it won't be my default, but it could be an interesting story; I'll most likely do it different from intended. <br /> Splintering of the <b>Tremere</b>. <br /> A <b>Ravnos</b> bloodline with Animalism, Chimestry (not obfuscate) and Presence. They sound like they could start some fun parties. <br /> <b>Toreador</b> weakness- It's not better, it's not worse. Maybe for a bloodline? My only reason to oppose it is continuity, and that I don't think it's an upgrade otherwise. <br /> <br /> -Nice idea, terrible execution, I (anyone) can do it better. <br /> -<b>Hecata</b>. We'll run through the coup and killing Augustus, factions will be trying to bring all the necromancers under one banner, and then have it fail and have the necromancers diffuse among the mainstream kindred pop. The families will continue to be incestuous messes, but it's smaller scale and each family is more at competition with one another. <br /> -<b>Followers of Set</b> &quot;splintering&quot; with some flocking to the anarchs.<br /> -New <b>Ravnos</b> symbol. The cross sucked and needed replacing. What we've got now sucks. Maybe it'll be specific to the new bloodline I mentioned. <br /> <b>- Lasombra </b>becoming more prevalent in the cam. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No<br /> -<b>Brujah</b> leaving the Cam. Hasn't been mentioned so far, so needs mentioning. <br /> -Every change I haven't mentioned. I don't want this section to look like an essay, but there's much more wrong than right. If I've mentioned a change to a clan about a thing I liked, but didn't mention the rest of the changes, they go here. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T05:11:04-08:00","id":1437943,"title":"","content":"<b>The Good.</b><br /> <b>Thin-Bloods:</b> Well, I am actually running a campaign right now with one Thin-Blood and it's quite amazing. We don't see any issue, even though the two other PC\u05d3 are full Vamps. VTM was never a game of power levels for me, more of a personal horror story. So far it's working great for us. The alchemy is cool and progresses slowly and through story events, recipes, and knowledge, which adds more things for the player to look for in the world. And we really like the discipline versatility with resonence. <br /> In other editions, they were just nerfed vampires. Here they are something else, the PC in our campaign unlike the rest of the coterie has some hope of a &quot;normal&quot; life, and it's something they fight for. And it's cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Mixed.</b><br /> <b>Oblivion:</b> I don't know about this one. Really. The more books that come out the more it's clear that the Lasombra part doesn't really mix with the Necromancy staff. In my game, I just separated them. These powers belong to two different clans with a very different theme, and having them share this very spotlight-heavy power doesn't work for me.<br /> <b>Clan-wide changes:</b> Another thing I don't get. Something happens to a clan and suddenly their bane or their clan discipline changes all over the world for everyone. I don't buy it. One day your Giovanni woke up and Dominate and Potence just stopped being their clan disciplines. Amazing.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bad:<br /> Nosferatu:</b> I don't like it that they went easy on their bane. They are my favorite clan, and their bane was the main thing that made them appealing in my eyes. There was a lot of creativity involved in customizing your own Nosferatu deformity. And now apparently they don't break the masquerade. They are just, somewhat ugly people. <br /> <br /> It was really hard for me to find things that I really don't like. I love V5 it's amazing and works really great for my group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T06:00:12-08:00","id":1437945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437919#post1437919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people mentioned that Salubri can't heal physical injury any more, but the Fortitude 2 power, Valeren does this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, only vampires.<br /> <br /> Not humans anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T08:27:49-08:00","id":1437962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437938#post1437938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No<br /> -<b>Brujah</b> leaving the Cam. Hasn't been mentioned so far, so needs mentioning.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pigeonholing of the Clans to specific sects in general just feels so... whatever the clan equivalent of racist would be.<br /> <br /> Basically, V5 doesn\u2019t seem to view identity as something that can exist independent of clan, at least not by default. If you\u2019re a Brujah then you\u2019re an Anarch, full stop. You can\u2019t be in the Camarilla and be authentically Brujah. Your clan (which you have no more control over than the color of your skin) trumps any beliefs or experiences you have as an individual.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s before you consider that neither the Brujah nor the Gangrel are the sort of clans where \u201cWell, some guy claiming to be our leader says we\u2019re doing something so we\u2019re all going to fall into lockstep\u201d makes any sort of sense.<br /> <br /> I suspect some of this may come down to Paradox being more of a video game studio than a tabletop rpg studio and those sorts of binaries (ex. Horde vs. Alliance, Empire vs. Republic... Camarilla vs. Anarchs) with each faction having exclusive race/class options is just part of the initial perceptual blinders while the supplemental material produced outside Paradox walks some of this back or at least provides context.<br /> <br /> ex. the Camarilla supplement notes that the Brujah who remained loyal to the Cam rebranded themselves \u2018Hellenes\u2019 as part of distancing themselves from the members of the Anarch movement... thus, all the Brujah are Anarchs, but only because the ones in the Camarilla now identify as Hellenes.<br /> <br /> And THAT is something that feels both realistic and useful to add into a V20 game. The Brujah were not always called Brujah any more than any other current Clan name is the original one. Having a real time rebranding due to factionalism drives that home and plays into current events with various groups and movements rebranding due to scandals or segments of the group being disavowed.<br /> <br /> One sees it to an extent with the Banu Haqim (except that the generally playable ones are those who reject Haqim... so it\u2019s a stupid name choice; Rafidi Haqim - \u201cThose Who Reject Haqim\u201d would be a much better name for the ones in the Camarilla), Ministry (way easier to sell others on than \u201cSet Worshippers\u201d) and Hecata (political rebranding to project unity)... but the Brujah/Hellenes split is the first that\u2019s establishing that the factions of the clan wish to distinguish themselves.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d like to see that extended across the Sects; ex. the Ventue who joined the Anarchs don\u2019t think of themselves as Ventrue, but instead call themselves \u201cClan Reyes\u201d (Spanish for Kings... perhaps a name initially localized to the Anarch Free States in California, but spreading to other Anarch cities) to emphasize their political break with their brethren in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> That sort of in-universe branding would better sell the idea of the Sects as movements greater than one\u2019s political party (i.e. as presented, Anarch vs. Camarilla is more on the level of Republicans vs. Democrats instead of, say, Americans vs. the British).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T08:46:05-08:00","id":1437963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437962#post1437962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pigeonholing of the Clans to specific sects in general just feels so... whatever the clan equivalent of racist would be.<br /> <br /> Basically, V5 doesn\u2019t seem to view identity as something that can exist independent of clan, at least not by default. If you\u2019re a Brujah then you\u2019re an Anarch, full stop. You can\u2019t be in the Camarilla and be authentically Brujah. Your clan (which you have no more control over than the color of your skin) trumps any beliefs or experiences you have as an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>This confuses me because one of the things V5 has done has separate Clan from sect.<br /> <br /> So I'm like...what?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T10:57:12-08:00","id":1437981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437962#post1437962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pigeonholing of the Clans to specific sects in general just feels so... whatever the clan equivalent of racist would be.<br /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, in-universe, I think the clans are meant to be very clanist towards one another; malks are nutters, Toreador are degenerates, Nosferatu have a handfull of personalities, Brujah are idiots... That's the attitude of clans that get along in the Cam. Tzmisce have a degenerative space-alien demon-disease discipline and the Lasombra are calling upon hell.... Yet I feel that with the combining of disciplines and the break-down of sects these barriers are fading and there's less in-universe reason to be clanist, which robs the world of a lot of character and satirical value. Meanwhile the writers are doing silly shit like getting the Brujah out of the Cam and replacing them with Lasombra to conveniently fill the worldviews and biases they have and it doesn't at all make sense in-universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T10:59:25-08:00","id":1437982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1437981#post1437981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, in-universe, I think the clans are meant to be very clanist towards one another; malks are nutters, Toreador are degenerates, Nosferatu have a handfull of personalities, Brujah are idiots... That's the attitude of clans that get along in the Cam.<b> Tzmisce have a degenerative space-alien demon-disease discipline </b>and the Lasombra are calling upon hell.... Yet I feel that with the combining of disciplines and the break-down of sects these barriers are fading and there's less in-universe reason to be clanist, which robs the world of a lot of character and satirical value. Meanwhile the writers are doing silly shit like getting the Brujah out of the Cam and replacing them with Lasombra to conveniently fill the worldviews and biases they have and it doesn't at all make sense in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we all agreed that Vicissitude being a Umbral parasite was....silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T11:07:39-08:00","id":1437984,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the <b>Lasombra </b>being part of the Camarilla are &quot;It's a good idea with some caveats.&quot;<br /> <br /> The previous Editions seemed dead set on making the Lasombra violently crazy about hunting down the Antitribu of their Clan and treating the idea of Lasombra in the sect as weird. Marcus Vitel was treated as a traitor to the Camarilla when his true Clan became known even though he was one of the most powerful vampires in the New World.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I've always felt that the Camarilla is a place where the Lasombra can shine. Being a sociopathic social Darwinist is pretty much how the Camarilla runs and the fact that they are there to make trouble for the Toreador, Tremere, and Ventrue just feels like it should naturally be a part of the system. Really, the Ventrue should have someone who is there undermining them and keeping them on their toes like the Shadow Lords do the Silver Fangs. The Tremere just aren't like that since they have been established as having almost no interest in mundane politics [which is a shame because &quot;Evil Wizard&quot; seems like it would be a great thing for a Seneschal role].<br /> <br /> I also am of the mind that if you're going to make as radical a change as &quot;The Lasombra join the Camarilla&quot; that they probably did it about as best as they possibly could. I personally think that &quot;Oh, btw, our Antediluvian is ALIVE&quot; is something that should shake the Lasombra down to their foundation because all of their propaganda is based around this. It's the equivalent of Jesus arriving and whipping all of the GOP on the Senate floor before banishing them to Hell. You'll have people denying it but it's a thing that needs to be addressed.<br /> <br /> OTOH, I don't think they needed to make it so overt. WIth as many casualties as the Gehenna War and Second Inquisition have inflicted, saying, &quot;A few dozen to a couple of hundred Lasombra defected to the Camarilla, Blood Cults, or Anarchs&quot; pretty much means the exact same thing for the Clan's power halving.<br /> <br /> Plus, I really wish they'd come up with a Ritual or Maguffin to explain how the Vinculum was overcome even though I don't think it was ever as effective as some people believed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5