":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T08:12:00-08:00","id":1438313,"title":"","content":"Dominate fits the clans and bloodlines which control one another extensively: Ventrue,Tremere, Lasombra, Tzmisce, Giovanni, Malkavians (The malks don't think they do, but they do), Nagajarajarajrajra, the... actually not many bloodlines have it, I suppose it's because they're not in the possition to boss people around. <br /> <br /> The Tzmisce do not belong in that club. They're possitively <i>fuedal </i> and fuedalism was basically defined by vassals not obeying their rullers and squabling all the time. A Tzmisce has his land, and doesn't care for what's outside of it. The only thing that binds them together is manners. Dominate just doesn't suit such a clan. <br /> Also they're more Erudite Doctors than slapstick demon surgeons but... the ones that stand out tend to define. <br /> <br /> You give them Auspex because they're intelectuals, Animalism because they're rich gentlemen with private land and they like a good hunt, and Vicissitude because, well, an intellect should not be wasted. <br /> <br /> The old clan can have Dominate tho. Because they're deluding themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T08:34:37-08:00","id":1438318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438311#post1438311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. 'Post human flesh crafting mystics' isn't a national stereotype, backwards, greedy warlords and criminals is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except they can now become crazy Comic Book Hoarders. It's also again, dragons, not Eastern Europeans that they're invoking as repeated about a dozen times in the text.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438313#post1438313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate fits the clans and bloodlines which control one another extensively: Ventrue,Tremere, Lasombra, Tzmisce, Giovanni, Malkavians (The malks don't think they do, but they do), Nagajarajarajrajra, the... actually not many bloodlines have it, I suppose it's because they're not in the possition to boss people around.<br /> <br /> The Tzmisce do not belong in that club. They're possitively <i>fuedal </i> and fuedalism was basically defined by vassals not obeying their rullers and squabling all the time. A Tzmisce has his land, and doesn't care for what's outside of it. The only thing that binds them together is manners. Dominate just doesn't suit such a clan.<br /> Also they're more Erudite Doctors than slapstick demon surgeons but... the ones that stand out tend to define.<br /> <br /> You give them Auspex because they're intelectuals, Animalism because they're rich gentlemen with private land and they like a good hunt, and Vicissitude because, well, an intellect should not be wasted.<br /> <br /> The old clan can have Dominate tho. Because they're deluding themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, that Dominate is one of the classic abilities of....Dracula.<br /> <br /> ALSO the Necroscope vampires.<br /> <br /> Which makes its exclusion previously silly.<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce's powers allow it to totally command its land both animal and mankind and that's a better thing than Auspex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T08:51:40-08:00","id":1438323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438318#post1438318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1)Except they can now become crazy Comic Book Hoarders. It's also again, dragons, not Eastern Europeans that they're invoking as repeated about a dozen times in the text.<br /> <br /> <br /> Except, of course, that Dominate is one of the classic abilities of....Dracula.<br /> <br /> ALSO the Necroscope vampires.<br /> <br /> Which makes its exclusion previously silly.<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce's powers allow it to totally command its land both animal and mankind and that's a better thing than Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) They are invoking Dracula, and he is a racist stereotype made disgusting flesh, Stoker might not of meant to, but he hit it note for note. (I'll give him some credit and guess editors and fair for it's day, like Shylock from Shakespeare) The less he appears the better, let that caricature fade, renaming it Dragon doesn't change the obvious origins (which is a mistake they also made with the Ravnos, they could have gone for a broader trickster archetype, or illusionist, or bizarre paradox cultist, instead they said 'traveller' when they meant gypsy and hoped it would fly. It's strange the ideas that worked are cut out to focus down on the negative stereotypes that made up the edge case. (Like Dracula was considered a freak and a failure by mainline Tzim...now they are all suddenly supposed to be like him...huh? Plus he was only Tzim because he was Slav, and that was Tzim turf he would have been better as a Ventrue or maybe Gangrel )<br /> <br /> 2) Auspex allowed mind reading, surveillance, mysticism, the ultimate unliving Big Brother, Dominate makes the entire clan make no sense, the reliance on the blood oath, on ghouls and animals moulded into war machines makes no sense when dominate is in the tool box, it makes those ideas pointless at best and counter productive at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-06-2021, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T09:09:32-08:00","id":1438328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438323#post1438323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) They are invoking Dracula, and he is a racist stereotype made disgusting flesh, Stoker might not of meant to, but he hit it note for note. (I'll give him some credit and guess editors and fair for it's day, like Shylock from Shakespeare) The less he appears the better, let that caricature fade, renaming it Dragon doesn't change the obvious origins (which is a mistake they also made with the Ravnos, they could have gone for a broader trickster archetype, or illusionist, or bizarre paradox cultist, instead they said 'traveller' when they meant gypsy and hoped it would fly. It's strange the ideas that worked are cut out to focus down on the negative stereotypes that made up the edge case. (Like Dracula was considered a freak and a failure by mainline Tzim...now they are all suddenly supposed to be like him...huh? Plus he was only Tzim because he was Slav, and that was Tzim turf he would have been better as a Ventrue or maybe Gangrel )<br /> <br /> 2) Auspex allowed mind reading, surveillance, mysticism, the ultimate unliving Big Brother, Dominate makes the entire clan make no sense, the reliance on the blood oath, on ghouls and animals moulded into war machines makes no sense when dominate is in the tool box, it makes those ideas pointless at best and counter productive at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then flat out I just think you're wrong. Especially since I think the Tzimisce of old were a terrible clan that did have many nasty stereotypes that have since been toned down or removed.<br /> <br /> Oh well, good talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T09:41:13-08:00","id":1438330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438328#post1438328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then flat out I just think you're wrong. Especially since I think the Tzimisce of old were a terrible clan that did have many nasty stereotypes that have since been toned down or removed.<br /> <br /> Oh well, good talk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fair enough. I see the Dracula/Dragon stuff as the problem (and anecdotally it was what the few Ukrainians I know who play the game are bothered by, but it could just be them, and I don't know them via WoD stuff anyway), with the Necroscope stuff (tho I prefered it when it went to The Strain/The Thing ends) being fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T10:15:41-08:00","id":1438335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438318#post1438318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, of course, that Dominate is one of the classic abilities of....Dracula.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Dracula's a Tzmisce, the Tzmisce aren't Dracula. Dracula's supposedly a revenant bloodline to boot, and it's not like Tzmisce can't get a few levels of Out-of-Clan disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T21:32:36-08:00","id":1438524,"title":"","content":"So, as I mentioned before, I like the Tzimisce changes, though I think I might have gone with Blood Sorcery instead of Dominate. Not a big deal for me though. Its hard to do Tzimisce when there is no Sabbat, so the Tzimisce as they are seem a bit homeless. I do like the idea of Camarilla Tzimisce though, so I feel like this version of them are a little less heretical in a Camarilla game.<br /> <br /> I like the Lasombra in the Camarilla, though I\u2019m so sure about how they were put in their. Mass exoduses always seem a bit far fetched to me. I think that if I were going to do it, I would have it so that the Camarilla Lasombra had been gaining in power and numbers gradually over time and that when the Brujah left the Camarilla, essentially starting their own Anarch Revolt, the Camarilla Lasombra said that they were tired of not having full Clan status and said that they would go to the Anarchs if they didn\u2019t receive full recognition as a Camarilla Clan and all rights and privileges included, so the Inner Circle decided it was worth it and so recognized the Lasombra as a full Camarilla Clan and then a bunch of Lasombra across Camarilla territory can come out of the closet and it turns out that there were lots of them. It could be from this position of power that other Lasombra could join the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> On the topic of the Lasombra, I\u2019m not sure I like Oblivion and all of the implications of combining Obtenebration with Necromancy. It seems to change the character of both the Lasombra and the Necromancy Bloodlines (Hecata)<br /> <br /> I like the changes with the Ravnos. I long thought that they were hopeless and kind of wrote them off or heavily altered them. This, I suppose, counts as a heavy alteration because they aren\u2019t ethnic at all anymore, which is what the Clan needed for rehabilitation. A long time ago I said I would give them Celerity, Obfuscate, and Presence and this edition almost brought them in line with that. I think that they are better in this edition than in any previous canon edition. I\u2019m not sure how much it matters as they are still small.<br /> <br /> I mentioned earlier that I didn\u2019t like the Assamites/Banu Haquim in the Camarilla and I still feel that way. I\u2019d have them in the Anarchs if anything, with the Ministry in the Camarilla. Someone wanted me to go into more detail about why and I will in a future post.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like what happened with the Tremere. I feel like the change is too drastic and undermines a lot of what made the Tremere so flavorful. They are supposed to be a unified extremely hierarchical Clan, removing that makes them less interesting to me. Also, their Vienna Chantry getting blown up seems too gonzo to me as well.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I see the Gangrel as Anarchs either. They seem more appropriate as an independent Clan, the Anarchs are too political and organized. Really, I\u2019m not sure if they should have made the Anarchs into a Sect like the Sabbat. I have often wanted VtM to be more about Elders vs Anarchs, but by having Camarilla Clans and Anarch Clans, it seems to become the same sort of conflict as existed with the Camarilla and the Sabbat. Open warfare with individual cities held by one faction or another, each Sect having its elders and neonates, rather than the elders vs the youth.<br /> <br /> The Hecata seem like they shouldn\u2019t be a unified group, as has been said before. I think it might be interesting to have certain of these bloodlines side with the Camarilla, certain side with the Anarchs, certain with the Sabbat. Then you can have a Necromancer regardless of the Sect your Chronicle focuses on. <br /> <br /> Actually, I could see a similar approach with a number of Clans: detach Clan from Sect by focusing one Bloodlines/castes of each Clan joining different Sects. They did do this with the Tremere, kind of, with the difference Houses, strangely one of the Clans I think such factions are inappropriate for.<br /> <br /> I guess over all, my response is mixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T23:30:16-08:00","id":1438530,"title":"","content":"It strikes me that Dominate is a bit of an awkward fit for the Tzimisci. The history of the Clan involves them having created the Vinculumn specifically because the Elders were Blood Bonding new vampires and sending them off to die in war against the Tremere. The Blood Bond was their primary tool, because in older editions the clan didn't have enough Elders specializing in Dominate for that to have been the explanation. <br /> <br /> It's also why the Sabbat Tzimisci all favored Visscisitude (besides spoopy alien infection) because the Sabbat Tzim were nearly all descendedfrom the Elders who relied on the Blood Bond to keep them in line. The Old Clan, who favored Dominate, never had their childer rise up en masse to slaughter them, at least not to the same degree because they relied less on the Blood Bond and the Vinculumn does nothing against Dominate. So the fact that a significant proportion of Tzimisci were forced to rely on the Blood Bond rather than Dominate to control others was a pretty central point to the Clan history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-08-2021, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T00:06:41-08:00","id":1438532,"title":"","content":"Dominate is a very silly discipline for Tzmisce because they're disorganized fuedal lords who keep to their own places. Also they had Vicissitude and animalism so it's redundant.<br /> <b>But the loss of Auspex is sad</b>.<br /> It pairs well with Vicissitude; A surgeon, especially one literally working with their hands, needs as much attention to detail as possible. Detailed tactile information, and the ability to details without magnification tools, are huge benefits.<br /> They need something to monitor their demenses. From a flavour standpoint, the thing I love about the Tzmisce is their hospitality and their -if you break a rule I will turn you into furniture- shtick. Being able to casually monitor a guest with all the powers of both forensics and observer teams is great.<br /> <br /> <i>I gave you everything; my best room, my best food, my most expensive wine, and you hath tumbled my maids, and I asked for one thing; not to touch this door, and yet the handle has been turned by none other than your hand; how could you do this to me, who has cared for you so well these nights? Well sir my hospitality has ran out; You wanted to see what was behind the door, and I shall take you there.</i><br /> <br /> You can't really do that without auspex.<br /> Also Dominate just doesn't cut it like Auspex when it comes to metamorphosists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T04:37:33-08:00","id":1438548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438532#post1438532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate is a very silly discipline for Tzmisce because they're disorganized fuedal lords who keep to their own places. Also they had Vicissitude and animalism so it's redundant.<br /> <b>But the loss of Auspex is sad</b>.<br /> It pairs well with Vicissitude; A surgeon, especially one literally working with their hands, needs as much attention to detail as possible. Detailed tactile information, and the ability to details without magnification tools, are huge benefits.<br /> They need something to monitor their demenses. From a flavour standpoint, the thing I love about the Tzmisce is their hospitality and their -if you break a rule I will turn you into furniture- shtick. Being able to casually monitor a guest with all the powers of both forensics and observer teams is great.<br /> <br /> <i>I gave you everything; my best room, my best food, my most expensive wine, and you hath tumbled my maids, and I asked for one thing; not to touch this door, and yet the handle has been turned by none other than your hand; how could you do this to me, who has cared for you so well these nights? Well sir my hospitality has ran out; You wanted to see what was behind the door, and I shall take you there.</i><br /> <br /> You can't really do that without auspex.<br /> Also Dominate just doesn't cut it like Auspex when it comes to metamorphosists.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feelings are mostly the same. Dominate works for the small Old Clan faction, and should have been a Lore Sheet for them, if anything, where Dominate replaces Vicissitude/Protean. Tying Vicissitude to Dominate for use feels ham-fisted and makes zero sense. The rationale is absurd: &quot;you command your own flesh to obey.&quot; If you have any artistic, crafting or medical experience under your belt (former EMT here), you would link Vicissitude's molding, tucking, sculpting, invasive surgeries, et al., to Auspex (heightened senses, mental acuity, insight, awareness) before <i>literally any other Discipline</i>...and that's if it needed an amalgam at all, which it really doesn't. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not even as much against them having Dominate as I\u2019m angry they\u2019ve lost their otherworldy senses, telepathy, far sight, prognostication, oracular abilities, psychic/spirit vision, etc. And yes, that fits well with the Dracula clan, as pointed out by the anti-Tzimisce/Pro-Dracula crowd above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dracula (using his ability to see vast distances) </div> </div> </div>One of the writers said &quot;in V5, you can still play a Tzimisce with Auspex&quot; like we're stupid and didn't realize that. You can also play a Gangrel with Oblivion, too, but it doesn't color their lore or flavor their history. (And that's aside from the nearly-prohibitive-unless-House-Ruled out-of-clan cost expenditure discussion.) <br /> <br /> #AnimalismAuspexVicissitude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","user":"Garygeneric","date":". 03-08-2021, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:14:10-08:00","id":1438554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438279#post1438279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Flesh eaters I always forget the spelling of (not the dunsirn, the Nagajara, or Najagara, or naragaragaja; Do I pronounces the J like a Y like most languages do or should I stick with an english J or maybe go spanish with a h...) They're pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an easy way to remember the pronunciation:<br /> <br /> Naga (snake) + Raja (king)<br /> <br /> Naga is like Nagini in Harry Potter. (Nagini is the feminine version of naga. These are serpents who appear in Hindu and Buddhist mythology.) <br /> <br /> Raja is like the Indian Raja, or the British Raj.<br /> <br /> They are literally the Snake Kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:23:15-08:00","id":1438557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438554#post1438554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They are literally the Snake Kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there I was thinking they were being quiet about their settite blood. <br /> I don't think I can play them straight anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:30:43-08:00","id":1438558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438557#post1438557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there I was thinking they were being quiet about their settite blood.<br /> I don't think I can play them straight anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nagaraja being Euthanatos always struck me as a much bigger deal. They be like, &quot;We had snakes WAY before the Setites ever did.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, the books are iffy if the Setites are snake-like because they're cribbing Judeo-Christianity or because they're talking about Apophis the actual Egyptian God of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:49:51-08:00","id":1438560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438554#post1438554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an easy way to remember the pronunciation:<br /> <br /> Naga (snake) + Raja (king)<br /> <br /> Naga is like Nagini in Harry Potter. (Nagini is the feminine version of naga. These are serpents who appear in Hindu and Buddhist mythology.)<br /> <br /> Raja is like the Indian Raja, or the British Raj.<br /> <br /> They are literally the Snake Kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always offended my sensibilities that the &quot;Snake Kings&quot; were necromancers in a setting where the Serpentis Discipline exists. Nagaraja should have been a name for an Indian branch of the Setites. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438558#post1438558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Nagaraja being Euthanatos always struck me as a much bigger deal. They be like, &quot;We had snakes WAY before the Setites ever did.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, the books are iffy if the Setites are snake-like because they're cribbing Judeo-Christianity or because they're talking about Apophis the actual Egyptian God of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably from Conan. I get the sense that the original creators of V:tM didn't give a lot of thought to the Independent Clans when they first created them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:53:21-08:00","id":1438561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438560#post1438560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's always offended my sensibilities that the &quot;Snake Kings&quot; were necromancers in a setting where the Serpentis Discipline exists. Nagaraja should have been a name for an Indian branch of the Setites.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the name fits for snake-themed Setites, it'd be a weird fit given they have nothing else in common with them other than the motif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:56:58-08:00","id":1438563,"title":"","content":"Intention may have changed from author to author. My view, having the benefit of coming into WoD late and having the priveledge to look back on all the editions impartially and blend them together, is that the snakes of apep/apophis are one and the same with the Wyrm of Wt:A fame, or perhaps just an aspect of it, and Set basically took power from the Wyrm. (Alternate theory: Apep's a vampire and this tale is about how he got embraced) . Similarly, perhaps the serpent in the garden is part of the Wyrm (cursed be snakes). or perhaps people just like putting snakes into their myths because snakes are weird things. Tales, especially ones with metaphores, get skewed over time in any case. I do think they're genuinely getting into apep/apophis with their snake stuff.<br /> <br /> But I also hold that Settites are world class bullshiters who're lying about the lies their lied-to sire told them. Set himself probably doesn't have a clue. <br /> <br /> If germanic paganism took over abrahamic faiths, the Settites would be into Jorgunmundr and/or nidhogg, and if the Vedics were the big religion they'd be into Vritra or the snake next to shiva, and if the americans somehow held onto the Americaas the Settites would be delving into the horned serpent or the many south american serpent-dragons. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T07:00:19-08:00","id":1438565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438561#post1438561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the name fits for snake-themed Setites, it'd be a weird fit given they have nothing else in common with them other than the motif.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brujah: &quot;Well, you could work a little snake into your powers somewhere. I mean you've got Necromancy, you've got this Dominate and Auspex thing going on, but it's like everything BUT Serpentis. <br /> Nagaraja&quot; &quot;Well, if we could just step out of our literal minds, just for a moment...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T07:42:49-08:00","id":1438571,"title":"","content":"<b>My thoughts on the Hecata</b><br /> <br /> I have one issue with the Hecata and that I don't think they needed the Reunion at all. There was no need to magically bind all of the Hecate together and make it so they all shared the same Clan Flaw and were siring people without the deformities or Flaws of all. For me, the Hecate would have been better not as a Clan but as a Blood Cult or more precisely, &quot;Mini Sect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the Sabbat is essentially one enormous Cult of Caine, so should the Hecata have been a Necromancy Cult that had two Clans (Cappadocians and Giovanni) with a bunch of Bloodlines added onto it too. I don't see why this wouldn't be perfectly useful for a campaign and require a lot fewer steps to pull off. There's also no reason why the Nagaraja just can't join this group even if I think the Cappadocians could be &quot;revealed&quot; to be their ancestors instead of the Setites.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T07:52:02-08:00","id":1438574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438571#post1438571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My thoughts on the Hecata</b><br /> <br /> I have one issue with the Hecata and that I don't think they needed the Reunion at all. There was no need to magically bind all of the Hecate together and make it so they all shared the same Clan Flaw and were siring people without the deformities or Flaws of all. For me, the Hecate would have been better not as a Clan but as a Blood Cult or more precisely, &quot;Mini Sect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the Sabbat is essentially one enormous Cult of Caine, so should the Hecata have been a Necromancy Cult that had two Clans (Cappadocians and Giovanni) with a bunch of Bloodlines added onto it too. I don't see why this wouldn't be perfectly useful for a campaign and require a lot fewer steps to pull off. There's also no reason why the Nagaraja just can't join this group even if I think the Cappadocians could be &quot;revealed&quot; to be their ancestors instead of the Setites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> simple answer: they reduced bloodlines to loresheets instead of being a mini-clan and decided that rather then give several clans a necromancy bloodline loresheet they decided to make a necromancy clan with several bloodlines loresheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T08:03:54-08:00","id":1438575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438557#post1438557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there I was thinking they were being quiet about their settite blood. <br /> I don't think I can play them straight anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right? I still love them, though. And it's at least less on-the-nose than Clan Wanderer (Gangrel), Clan Pot-Belly (Ventrue) or Clan 'The Shadow' (Lasombra).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438571#post1438571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My thoughts on the Hecata</b><br /> <br /> I have one issue with the Hecata and that I don't think they needed the Reunion at all. There was no need to magically bind all of the Hecate together and make it so they all shared the same Clan Flaw and were siring people without the deformities or Flaws of all. For me, the Hecate would have been better not as a Clan but as a Blood Cult or more precisely, &amp;quot;Mini Sect.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the Sabbat is essentially one enormous Cult of Caine, so should the Hecata have been a Necromancy Cult that had two Clans (Cappadocians and Giovanni) with a bunch of Bloodlines added onto it too. I don't see why this wouldn't be perfectly useful for a campaign and require a lot fewer steps to pull off. There's also no reason why the Nagaraja just can't join this group even if I think the Cappadocians could be &amp;quot;revealed&amp;quot; to be their ancestors instead of the Setites.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'd have done it. Make them like the Bahari rather than a megaclan, and give them separate Clans and Bloodlines with shares Loresheets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T08:19:06-08:00","id":1438576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438575#post1438575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right? I still love them, though. And it's at least less on-the-nose than Clan Wanderer (Gangrel), Clan Pot-Belly (Ventrue) or Clan 'The Shadow' (Lasombra).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're a musician, there's no harm in calling yourself a musician. Calling yourself a 'snake-king' when you're not a king or a snake... Just sounds like a shitty gang/band name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T08:33:33-08:00","id":1438579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438532#post1438532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>But the loss of Auspex is sad</b>.<br /> ...<br /> You can't really do that without auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree Dominate doesn\u2019t work, I think your \u201ccross clan disciplines exist\u201d argument as you applied it to Dracula works just as well for Auspex as it does for Dominate.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is me speaking from a more V20 perspective (I don\u2019t have discipline powers for V5 memorized like I do the common V20 disciplines), but other than the general heightened senses you get with the first dot, there\u2019s not much that really helps an aspiring feudal lord suss out the sort of things you\u2019re looking for.<br /> <br /> Aura reading doesn\u2019t detect lies. Object reading requires the person you\u2019re trying to get information about to have significant contact with it (the subject needs to be the primary user of said door to know when he last touched it, because long-time users drown out one-time touchers). Telepathy is difficult to use against fellow undead and the strongwilled. Psychic projection still requires you to be around in astral form to witness things.<br /> <br /> It can be useful, but I think animal spies and blood bound servants are probably just as, if not more, useful for general observation and information gathering.<br /> <br /> Personally, my V20 rebuild to be a bit more V5-ish (with a specific goal of not needing mechanically separate bloodlines just to cover all a clan\u2019s concepts) makes Vicissitude a path of Blood Sorcery and gives the Tzmisce the clan disciplines of Animalism, Blood Sorcery and Protean. Animalism lets them command animal spies and quell the beast to make subjects more passive. Blood Sorcery not only includes Vicissitude in this rebuild, but also weather control, telekinesis, conjuring fire and rituals that include scrying. Protean allows sight in darkness, melding with the earth, turning into wild beasts or mist (which is nearly as good as astral projection for spying). Throw in blood bonds and ghouls and you have basically all your classic Eastern European vampire abilities covered and the Necroscope variety are still easily doable with Vicissitude as their primary Blood Sorcery path.<br /> <br /> Admittedly though, the main reason I dropped Auspex is that, after the merging of Vicissitude into Blood Sorcery, the Tzmisce would have shared two of three disciplines with the Tremere (Auspex, Blood Sorcery, Dominate) if I\u2019d gone Animalism, Auspex, Blood Sorcery. Overall the spread I chose just felt like a better fit in terms of applying to all the Tzmisce, whether they be the vicissitude-using followers of the Path of Metamorphosis, the Koldunic Sorcerers and the reclusive Eastern European warlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T08:43:59-08:00","id":1438580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438571#post1438571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My thoughts on the Hecata</b><br /> <br /> I have one issue with the Hecata and that I don't think they needed the Reunion at all. There was no need to magically bind all of the Hecate together and make it so they all shared the same Clan Flaw and were siring people without the deformities or Flaws of all. For me, the Hecate would have been better not as a Clan but as a Blood Cult or more precisely, &quot;Mini Sect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the Sabbat is essentially one enormous Cult of Caine, so should the Hecata have been a Necromancy Cult that had two Clans (Cappadocians and Giovanni) with a bunch of Bloodlines added onto it too. I don't see why this wouldn't be perfectly useful for a campaign and require a lot fewer steps to pull off. There's also no reason why the Nagaraja just can't join this group even if I think the Cappadocians could be &quot;revealed&quot; to be their ancestors instead of the Setites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is my issue with the Hecata as well. I guess you could say that my issue with the Hecata is that they exist, that is a pretty big issue. <br /> <br /> A direction that V5 goes in occasionally that I approve of is separating Clan from Sect. They do it in some ways but not others. I would like to see a more thorough across the board effort to put the different Clans in the different Sects with an explanation for their presence there and a description of how they fit in. This could have been done pretty simply with those Bloodlines that got grouped into the Hecata, as mentioned earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438286#post1438286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather see, hmmm...<br /> I know the names of some prominent Giovanni families, but I don't know which way they'd swing, so I'll make a few up.<br /> <br /> The Smith family serve the Camarilla<br /> The Williams family serve the Sabbat<br /> The White Family serve the Camarilla<br /> The Yang family serve both<br /> The Collins family are nominally a part of the Anarchs.<br /> The Achebe family serve the cam.<br /> The Green family serve themselves<br /> The Orange family serve whoever's dominant in Texas.<br /> The Black Family are sponsored by the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> ...and so on and so forth. The same may be true for different lineages of Harbringers of skulls.<br /> The Samedi work through the Nosferatu.<br /> The flesh eaters work through whatever works for them, many of them probably also work through the nosferatu</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not exactly sure which families/bloodlines/factions go where. Though I think it's an interesting question. Any ideas on that, MWIS?<br /> <br /> I think in 2028 we should have the Giovanni Clan/Family/Bloodline do something interesting. Until then, I suppose they remain independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T08:50:21-08:00","id":1438581,"title":"","content":"Most 'intelectual' clans have Auspex. (Clans that are 'intelectual' that don't have Auspex generally have obfuscate) <br /> and again, Dracula is a Tzmisce (Formerly a Basarab revenant; they have Dominate, Protean and Vicissitude), but Tzmisce aren't Dracula. <br /> <br /> Dominate is just redundant when you have Animalism and Vicissitude. Protean is redundant when you have Vicissitude and Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T09:08:35-08:00","id":1438582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438580#post1438580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not exactly sure which families/bloodlines/factions go where. Though I think it's an interesting question. Any ideas on that, MWIS?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with the families is that they're big and they've intermaried and such and there's -main families- and -branch families- and stuff like that. A lot of dramas are big on dynastic conflicts, and it's likely one branch of the family will go one way an off-shoot cousin will go another way just to escape the control; Your uncle becomes your worst enemy and your cousin wants to kill you. Thus we're likely to have people surnamed Giovanni in all sects. We're also likely to have people declare new families once the Giovanni overlords are beheaded. It'll all be very game-of-thrones in terms of -my little brother wants to kill me, my sister is married to my enemy and I've married his cousin, we both have sisters married into family X and we both want to forge ties with family Y and... The messier, the better. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Ventrue will certainly pull one (I think they already have in v20). The Nosferatu are likely to pull another. The Tremere will try. I think it's likely that very powerful elders and a few princes will sponsor families. I feel the Nosferatu would be the biggest beneficiaries to the whole thing; only thing more distasteful than a bloated corpse is a man who enjoys fucking bloated corpses; they're just distasteful. The Toreador will hate them. Necromancers and Nosferatu make natural allies, especially with all the incestual family shenanigans they got going on allowing for good business (and the Samedi also being cursed like the Nos)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:05:51-08:00","id":1438586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438580#post1438580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is my issue with the Hecata as well. I guess you could say that my issue with the Hecata is that they exist, that is a pretty big issue</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to say something like that, please say why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438581#post1438581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most 'intelectual' clans have Auspex. (Clans that are 'intelectual' that don't have Auspex generally have obfuscate)<br /> and again, Dracula is a Tzmisce (Formerly a Basarab revenant; they have Dominate, Protean and Vicissitude), but Tzmisce aren't Dracula.<br /> <br /> Dominate is just redundant when you have Animalism and Vicissitude. Protean is redundant when you have Vicissitude and Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably why they ended up combining so many Disciplines. Vicissitude, Serpentis, and Protean are all variants of the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:26:41-08:00","id":1438587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438586#post1438586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably why they ended up combining so many Disciplines. Vicissitude, Serpentis, and Protean are all variants of the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat of a side tangent, I admit, but I\u2019m not sure combining those Disciplines was the best idea. By their logic, they could combine Animalism, Dominate and Obfuscate into a \u201cmental trickery\u201d Discipline. Fortitude and Potence into a \u201cbody power\u201d Discipline. Etc.<br /> <br /> I feel that Vicissitude and Protean are unique and interesting enough individually without forcing an \u201ceither/or\u201d decision on players.<br /> <br /> Sometimes less is more, but sometimes more is more, too. <br /> <br /> But anyways...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:37:01-08:00","id":1438591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438587#post1438587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somewhat of a side tangent, I admit, but I\u2019m not sure combining those Disciplines was the best idea. By their logic, they could combine Animalism, Dominate and Obfuscate into a \u201cmental trickery\u201d Discipline. Fortitude and Potence into a \u201cbody power\u201d Discipline. Etc.<br /> <br /> I feel that Vicissitude and Protean are unique and interesting enough individually without forcing an \u201ceither/or\u201d decision on players.<br /> <br /> Sometimes less is more, but sometimes more is more, too.<br /> <br /> But anyways...</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, the thing about Vicissitude is that it always felt like two powers. You have &quot;Change Yourself&quot; and you have &quot;Change Others&quot; which I feel like should have been a much higher level or a separate discipline or Path of Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> But I do think the biggest problem is that V5 rules nerf the benefits of this.<br /> <br /> If I could change any rule in V5, it would be limiting the number of Discipline levels you can buy at any given level. A guy with Protean 3 should be able to buy as many Protean 3/Vicissitude/Serpebntis powers as he wants.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:49:42-08:00","id":1438592,"title":"","content":"Serpentis was always low-key Protean. As is Thanatosis and Visceraticka and probably most inceptor disciplines; Protean's whole deal was how.... protean it is; it changes fast and frequently. Even if you were a gangrel, you could get different powers of the same level, for example they've always had plenty of options for level 2 power: Claws, fins, tusks. Protean has always been described as something very personal, you're basically asking the beast to manifest physical changes, like a short term formor.<br /> Viscissitude was never Protean. It has some superficial similarities with the 4th and 5th power, but fundamentally, it's a different kettle of fish. You're scultping, and the changes you make are permanent changes to the physical form.<br /> <br /> 30 clear and concise disciplines are just better than 10 messy disciplines that have as many powers as 30 disciplines for hundreds of potential combinations. Mergers for the sake of mergers are stupid.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, it's really helpful to compartmentalize things. I can remember most of the v20 mechanics of the common disciplines without looking at the book, plus a few rare ones; I know what I need to know and what I don't need to know. With V5, that's hopeless, maybe I can try to remember what my coterie has, but no more than that, and I'll have to string it out of them which powers they selected...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-08-2021, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T11:08:12-08:00","id":1438596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438592#post1438592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Viscissitude was never Protean. It has some superficial similarities with the 4th and 5th power, but fundamentally, it's a different kettle of fish. You're scultping, and the changes you make are permanent changes to the physical form.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I see it. As diverse as Protean changes are, they are still usually static. Barring rare merits, your eyes glow the same red, your wolf form is the same every time you shift, and you eventually have to power off and revert to your \u201cnatural\u201d undead form.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is a different ball of soft, melted pink wax. The changes permanently alter one\u2019s Pattern unless the strength of more powerful blood can \u201cheal\u201d it. If it absolutely needed to be rewritten, it makes much more sense as Blood Sorcery. This not only keeps the Protean waters clear but keeps Tzimisce as a \u201clearned clan.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T12:26:55-08:00","id":1438598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438582#post1438582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the families is that they're big and they've intermaried and such and there's -main families- and -branch families- and stuff like that. A lot of dramas are big on dynastic conflicts, and it's likely one branch of the family will go one way an off-shoot cousin will go another way just to escape the control; Your uncle becomes your worst enemy and your cousin wants to kill you. Thus we're likely to have people surnamed Giovanni in all sects. We're also likely to have people declare new families once the Giovanni overlords are beheaded. It'll all be very game-of-thrones in terms of -my little brother wants to kill me, my sister is married to my enemy and I've married his cousin, we both have sisters married into family X and we both want to forge ties with family Y and... The messier, the better.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ventrue will certainly pull one (I think they already have in v20). The Nosferatu are likely to pull another. The Tremere will try. I think it's likely that very powerful elders and a few princes will sponsor families. I feel the Nosferatu would be the biggest beneficiaries to the whole thing; only thing more distasteful than a bloated corpse is a man who enjoys fucking bloated corpses; they're just distasteful. The Toreador will hate them. Necromancers and Nosferatu make natural allies, especially with all the incestual family shenanigans they got going on allowing for good business (and the Samedi also being cursed like the Nos)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that if another family breaks off and becomes enemies with the official Giovanni family, that a lot of people with the last name of Giovanni would change it. Kind of like how the royal family of Great Britain changed from the House of Saxe-Coberg and Gotha to the House of Windsor during World War One. <br /> <br /> If the high ups in among the Giovanni are killed, I have trouble imaging the survivors bending the knee to the people who killed them. It seems like that would become an irreconcilable rift within what would become the Hecata. <br /> <br /> It's also a bit challenging to say who joins the Sabbat when we don't know much about the Sabbat. Would the Harbringers stay in the Sabbat? It doesn't seem like they would be that invested in the Sabbat or their war at this point, not that they were necessarily that invested to start with. I seem to recall reading somewhere that the Harbringers might go Camarilla. As per V20 Ghouls book, the Rosselini are a Revenant family in addition to a Giovanni sub-family. It might be interesting to see them do something. It seems like maybe the Gorgons/Lamia might go Sabbat, they are a Lilith cult I recall and that kind of thing always tends towards Sabbat. <br /> <br /> Weird idea: What if Cappadocius wanted the Harbringers to be the ones who survived, it was the other Cappadocians who were unfit who would die at the hands of the Giovanni? Which could be why the Harbringers are now called the Harbringers of Ashur. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438586#post1438586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to say something like that, please say why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, saying that they shouldn't exist sounds harsh. But the Hecata are a collection of bloodlines in a single organization. To say that this organization shouldn't exist and that the bloodlines should be in different organizations is the same as saying that the Hecata shouldn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T12:57:57-08:00","id":1438604,"title":"","content":"Splitting up the corpse-fuckers also does a great job in legitimizing a -your guys here- kinda thing; When you get your former-giovanni to the table, you can create a household behind them with a history, a speciality or philosophy, a business interest, how they approached the coup, how they got into the city they're in now... a player can do creative things with background points, merits and flaws.. and a storyteller can ensure it's very interesting. It's so much easier getting into the character of a -family man- when you've got a good amount of say in how that family is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T13:26:47-08:00","id":1438610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438604#post1438604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splitting up the corpse-fuckers also does a great job in legitimizing a -your guys here- kinda thing; When you get your former-giovanni to the table, you can create a household behind them with a history, a speciality or philosophy, a business interest, how they approached the coup, how they got into the city they're in now... a player can do creative things with background points, merits and flaws.. and a storyteller can ensure it's very interesting. It's so much easier getting into the character of a -family man- when you've got a good amount of say in how that family is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. The Hecata as a single independent organization might make for an interesting Necromancer game: one person is a Samedi, another is a Giovanni, one is a Cappadocians, etc. But for most chronicles, the other characters will be form other Clans in one of the major sects. The Hecata sort of makes any Necromancer an odd man out in a game focused on characters from one of the major Sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T13:28:18-08:00","id":1438611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438610#post1438610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree. The Hecata as a single independent organization might make for an interesting Necromancer game: one person is a Samedi, another is a Giovanni, one is a Cappadocians, etc. But for most chronicles, the other characters will be form other Clans in one of the major sects. The Hecata sort of makes any Necromancer an odd man out in a game focused on characters from one of the major Sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Blood Cults show dual citizenship is very popular. Plenty of Church of Caine and Mithras Camarilla or Anarch members.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T14:18:51-08:00","id":1438622,"title":"","content":"If you can pull yourself past the hopelessly edgy intro, I'm sure it does, but players storytellers generally prefer -naturally belongs, no justification needed- to -weird outsider, justification to be here isn't difficult but it is absolutely necessary to go through the trouble-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T14:21:03-08:00","id":1438623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438591#post1438591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could change any rule in V5, it would be limiting the number of Discipline levels you can buy at any given level. A guy with Protean 3 should be able to buy as many Protean 3/Vicissitude/Serpebntis powers as he wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are hints that such may be possible. In addition to language such as &quot;Vampire characters <i>normally</i> have an equal number of dots and powers in a Discipline...&quot;, there's that Descendant of Montano loresheet that lets Lasombra temporarily use an Oblivion power they don't know at or below their rating in the discipline. The text implies that Montano himself likely knows how to use <b>ALL</b> Oblivion powers at will. It might be tied to Blood Potency rather than just being open season on all the powers you want, but that actually works to make the elders comparatively more impressive, a complaint many people have had about the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T14:58:11-08:00","id":1438631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438610#post1438610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree. The Hecata as a single independent organization might make for an interesting Necromancer game: one person is a Samedi, another is a Giovanni, one is a Cappadocians, etc. But for most chronicles, the other characters will be form other Clans in one of the major sects. The Hecata sort of makes any Necromancer an odd man out in a game focused on characters from one of the major Sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't that different from previous editions, Dark Ages aside. Giovanni have always been their own sect and tighter than the Tremere. The Harbingers joined the Sabbat first, which isn't supported yet anyway. Some Samedi explicitly stayed out of the Hecata sect and associate with the Ministry, so they're pretty much Anarchs. The rest are so uncommon that they're unusual anywhere. Although there are those characters like Dr. Banerjee in <i>Fall of London</i>, who are Hecata, without any clear ties to a bloodline or explanation for existing in spite of the Giovanni.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T15:16:23-08:00","id":1438635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438598#post1438598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird idea: What if Cappadocius wanted the Harbringers to be the ones who survived, it was the other Cappadocians who were unfit who would die at the hands of the Giovanni? Which could be why the Harbringers are now called the Harbringers of Ashur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same thought too so I don't think it's weird! Furthermore, it isn't even necessary for all those entombed during the Feast of Folly to be the grouped that is saved. Cappadocious asked a lot of questions. So he might have determined that so many were going to be destroyed, and a certain group that fit a profile to be lead into a secret cavern that was going to protect them while all the others frenzied from their Hunger. I don't believe people can predict the future with clarity, but it's possible Cappadocious knew something was going to happen by that time and wanted a select group kept safe. But he hid his intent by masking a series of questions that hid his attempt to do so.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> <br /> As for Giovanni who join certain sects, I think it is definitely possible. In the old setting it was simply a matter of whether the new sect was willing to protect their new members from the inevitable retaliation. I think the Milliners would be the most likely to defect from the Camarilla. They were embraced quite late and have only tangential reasons to support Augustus's plan; have their own goals, and they are chafing from Giovanni control over them. If they felt that a sufficiently powerful Justicar could protect them combined with their own knowledge, I think they could defect in the hope they would prosper more. I think any of the other minor families embraced quite late (and almost all non-Italian) -and thus have weak ties to the Giovanni family - could join them if they saw the benefit in doing so.<br /> <br /> The Pisanob are probably the ones most likely to defect to the Sabbat. They already exist in a Sabbat stronghold and likely have dealings with them. Furthermore, the Sabbat have already demonstrated the ability to protect the Serpents of the Light from the Setities. So I think if they wanted to, they could. But for now they likely don't see a reason unless the Giovanni tried to impose greater control over them. Another possible candidate might be the Dunsirn who seem to be long lost kinfolk to the White Howlers, and thus have distant relations to the Black Spiral Dancers, and the Dancers have ties to the Sabbat. If the Dancers reestablished contact, the Dunsirn might see advantages working with them instead. However, they are in an exposed geographic location - close to the Giovanni center of power, and surrounded by the Camarilla. They would risk losing a lot by an open defection. But it is possible for them to deal extensively with the Sabbat and BSDs on the down low while keeping a public image of loyalty to the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> I would consider most of the Italian/Mediterranean families of the Giovanni to be so closely connected to them, that they are essentially part of the same faction and would remain loyal.<br /> <br /> I always thought the Independent Clans were supposed to be few in number - nowhere near like the Camarilla clans or the Sabbat. And the Giovanni in particular were very small. I know many people did not hold the same opinion and had a very large clan that equivalent or near equivalent to the Camarilla clans (or at least their small members like Malkavian or Tremere). But for my own chronicles I came up with a list of maybe a dozen cities where the Giovanni were prominent enough that they had equal proportions in the domain as any other clan, and another dozen cities where they had a few members. So their worldwide population in my chronicles were between 100-200. So while such defectors might impact a significant proportion of the clan, each sect would only grow by only a few dozen members at best (your chronicles might be different). So it might not be worth it to them to alienate the Giovanni (the Serpents of Light are also few in number, but they cemented Sabbat power in Haiti and more importantly the Sabbat had likely already designated the Antedeluvian loving Setites as a future enemy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T15:41:31-08:00","id":1438642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438610#post1438610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree. The Hecata as a single independent organization might make for an interesting Necromancer game: one person is a Samedi, another is a Giovanni, one is a Cappadocians, etc. But for most chronicles, the other characters will be form other Clans in one of the major sects. The Hecata sort of makes any Necromancer an odd man out in a game focused on characters from one of the major Sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think there is something good to say about recognizing all the Cappadocian bloodlines as a single clan again. I liked that in the original game, it was a mystery to be worked out as Gehenna approached. But at this point, we can all admit that Giovanni, Samedi, Harbingers, and a few more are all Cappadocians (or whatever new name you want to give them). But there was no reason for the Nagaraja to be part of that group.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, simply recognizing these groups as part of the same clan does not mean all members of the clan are politically together. What makes sense would be 1) the core Giovanni to remain independent, 2) the more humane Cappadocian survivors to join the Camarilla, and 3) the more monstrous or inhuman Path Cappadocian survivors that couldn't fit in with Humanity-Masquerade loving Camarilla would go to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I was never a big fan of the Harbingers being members of the Sabbat. They suddenly appeared - along with others - as Sabbat simply to give that sect a big boost to make them even more of a threat in a scenario where Gehenna has started. As such, they had weak IC motivations. It was all OOC scripting reasons. (Same thing with the Salubri anti-tribu's membership. - &quot;I thirst for unholy vengeance against those who persecuted me for centuries!&quot; &quot;Dude, weren't you just embraced like 3 days ago? And the Sabbat has Tremere too and all the Sabbat clans likewise left you to die.&quot;) The Cappadocians were known for their alliance with the Ventrue, and weren't particularly inhumane. And there was a decent chance that some of the Harbingers could still claim some sort of friendship, perhaps even boons, among very old Camarilla elders from the time before they disappeared. That doesn't mean there is not an argument for the Sabbat. But clearly there should have been division among them. Splitting up the Harbingers makes better sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T15:46:30-08:00","id":1438644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438642#post1438642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think there is something good to say about recognizing all the Cappadocian bloodlines as a single clan again. I liked that in the original game, it was a mystery to be worked out as Gehenna approached. But at this point, we can all admit that Giovanni, Samedi, Harbingers, and a few more are all Cappadocians (or whatever new name you want to give them). But there was no reason for the Nagaraja to be part of that group.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, simply recognizing these groups as part of the same clan does not mean all members of the clan are politically together. What makes sense would be 1) the core Giovanni to remain independent, 2) the more humane Cappadocian survivors to join the Camarilla, and 3) the more monstrous or inhuman Path Cappadocian survivors that couldn't fit in with Humanity-Masquerade loving Camarilla would go to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I was never a big fan of the Harbingers being members of the Sabbat. They suddenly appeared - along with others - as Sabbat simply to give that sect a big boost to make them even more of a threat in a scenario where Gehenna has started. As such, they had weak IC motivations. It was all OOC scripting reasons. (Same thing with the Salubri anti-tribu's membership. - &quot;I thirst for unholy vengeance against those who persecuted me for centuries!&quot; &quot;Dude, weren't you just embraced like 3 days ago? And the Sabbat has Tremere too and all the Sabbat clans likewise left you to die.&quot;) The Cappadocians were known for their alliance with the Ventrue, and weren't particularly inhumane. And there was a decent chance that some of the Harbingers could still claim some sort of friendship, perhaps even boons, among very old Camarilla elders from the time before they disappeared. That doesn't mean there is not an argument for the Sabbat. But clearly there should have been division among them. Splitting up the Harbingers makes better sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, the Sabbat didn't have Tremere at that time. Honestly, I think they killed all of the Tremere Antitribu solely so they could introduce the Salubri Antitribu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T15:52:35-08:00","id":1438646,"title":"","content":"I misremembered the timing then on what happened when.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T16:02:48-08:00","id":1438647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438646#post1438646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I misremembered the timing then on what happened when.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never much cared for the mass murder of the Tremere Antis....and not just because I played a Tremere antitribu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T20:28:05-08:00","id":1438672,"title":"","content":"The Harbringers in general always felt pretty awkward to me. Their main beef was with the Giovanni. But the Sabbat and Giovanni never really had any deep grudges with one another. The Giovanni weren't part of the Camarilla. They didn't support the Antediluvians. In fact their leader had killed one of the Antediluvians and wiped out his clan of loyal followers. If anything there was probably a certain amount of grudging respect for the Giovanni because what he pulled off is exactly what many of the Antitribu clans in the Sabbat want to do someday. Certainly there might have been certain areas (political, economic, etc) in which the Giovanni and the Sabbat were rivals, but for the most part I have to imagine the Giovanni would have been at or very near the bottom of the Sabbat's hit list.<br /> <br /> But even even their beef with the Giovanni was awkward. The Harbingers were survivors of the Feast of Folly and had been entombed and trapped by Cappadocius and the extent of their problem with the Giovanni seemed to be, &quot;We wanted to kill Cappadocius but by the time we escaped you guys had already killed him and we're really, really pissed off about it.&quot; The whole thing was just badly written. The Harbringers should have been a sect of Cappadocians who had been banished to the Shadow Realm by Augustus, at least then their grudge would have been a bit more sensible.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Harbringers wanted to use the Sabbat against the Giovanni, but the Sabbat didn't care much about the Giovanni. And the Sabbat wanted to used the Harbringers against the Camarilla, but the Harbringers didn't care much about the Camarilla. It was a temporary alliance of convenience at best and it wouldn't be a surprise that it didn't end up working out in the long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-08-2021, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T21:02:28-08:00","id":1438678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438647#post1438647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never much cared for the mass murder of the Tremere Antis....and not just because I played a Tremere antitribu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was a very cool and interesting chronicle event. However, it works best as something an individual ST does in a home chronicle, not as a permanent change to the setting that takes away the toy for someone else to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T21:02:29-08:00","id":1438679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438672#post1438672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Harbringers in general always felt pretty awkward to me. Their main beef was with the Giovanni. But the Sabbat and Giovanni never really had any deep grudges with one another. The Giovanni weren't part of the Camarilla. They didn't support the Antediluvians. In fact their leader had killed one of the Antediluvians and wiped out his clan of loyal followers. If anything there was probably a certain amount of grudging respect for the Giovanni because what he pulled off is exactly what many of the Antitribu clans in the Sabbat want to do someday. Certainly there might have been certain areas (political, economic, etc) in which the Giovanni and the Sabbat were rivals, but for the most part I have to imagine the Giovanni would have been at or very near the bottom of the Sabbat's hit list.<br /> <br /> But even even their beef with the Giovanni was awkward. The Harbingers were survivors of the Feast of Folly and had been entombed and trapped by Cappadocius and the extent of their problem with the Giovanni seemed to be, &quot;We wanted to kill Cappadocius but by the time we escaped you guys had already killed him and we're really, really pissed off about it.&quot; The whole thing was just badly written. The Harbringers should have been a sect of Cappadocians who had been banished to the Shadow Realm by Augustus, at least then their grudge would have been a bit more sensible.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Harbringers wanted to use the Sabbat against the Giovanni, but the Sabbat didn't care much about the Giovanni. And the Sabbat wanted to used the Harbringers against the Camarilla, but the Harbringers didn't care much about the Camarilla. It was a temporary alliance of convenience at best and it wouldn't be a surprise that it didn't end up working out in the long term.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, you can literally not underestimate how much of a petty bunch of assholes that any group of vampires might be. Mind you, the Harbingers feel like they are constantly moving from one band of crazy to another.<br /> <br /> Harbingers: After a 1000 years, I'm free, TIME TO CONQUER EARTH!<br /> <br /> True Hand: Hey, we helped free you.<br /> <br /> Harbingers: Oh, sweet, awesome.<br /> <br /> True Hand: We worship the Antediluvians and are trying to bring about Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Harbingers: What the absolute fuck. *slowly steps back*<br /> <br /> True Hand: No, no, we'll survive! Honest! Oh and these are our new friends: the Baali!<br /> <br /> Harbingers: Uh huh.<br /> <br /> True Hand: But the good Baali who want to keep Cthulhu asleep by the screams of dead infants we sacrifice!<br /> <br /> Harbingers: Right, let's go join the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Hey, we're all going to Syria where all the Elders have been Beckoned! TO FIGHT THE ANTEDILUVIANS! In hand to hand combat!<br /> <br /> Ravnos: They're probably unlike the one who required three nukes and a satellite weapon! Oh and who killed 90% of his clan with his dying breath!<br /> <br /> Harbingers: You know, maybe we should think about making peace with the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Isabel: NEVER! You are the Old Clan and our Loyalty is to our master!<br /> <br /> Augustus: Oh shit, lost control of those 10,000,000 souls who all want to kill us.<br /> <br /> Isabel: Okay, what's your plan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-09-2021, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T21:18:01-08:00","id":1438681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438672#post1438672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Harbringers in general always felt pretty awkward to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I honestly don\u2019t feel like the revenge motive makes sense directed at the Giovanni. Sure, they might be irritated that the Giovanni killed Cappadocius instead, but it shouldn\u2019t be this all consuming thirst for revenge. It would make a lot more sense for loyalist Cappadocians to awaken and want revenge because they were loyal to Cappadocius. That is one reason I like the theory that the Harbringers were the chosen of Cappadocius and over time they changed in some way that Cappadocius wanted and they came to realize this. They want revenge because they know their master was protecting and improving them. <br /> <br /> Also, as you say, the Sabbat isn\u2019t really the place to go for revenge against Giovanni. They would be better off staying neutral and just going after the Giovanni by themselves.<br /> <br /> If we go with the theory that Cappadocius saw what was coming, then the Harbringers of Ashur (why name yourself after the one who locked you away to die?) could still be carrying out his plans or even orders that go beyond simple revenge. It could be that the creation of the Hecata is part of that plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T23:43:45-08:00","id":1438689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438679#post1438679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, you can literally not underestimate how much of a petty bunch of assholes that any group of vampires might be. Mind you, the Harbingers feel like they are constantly moving from one band of crazy to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean yeah, that's was my issue. The extent of the reasoning for the Harbringers to join the Sabbat was that they're petty and spiteful. Which isn't implausible or anything (people do all kinds of shit purely out of pettiness or spite), but petty spitefulness hardly makes a solid basis for an alliance, or at least not a long lasting one.<br /> <br /> eally, the Harbringers were always going to be part of the Sabbat only for as long as it took them to realize that the Sabbat would not be a useful tool in their quest for vengeance. So having them out of the Sabbat is great because it was rather silly for them to be in the Sabbat to begin with. It always felt like the writers had a cool idea but never really finished thinking it through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438679#post1438679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Hand: We worship the Antediluvians and are trying to bring about Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Harbingers: What the absolute fuck. *slowly steps back*<br /> <br /> True Hand: No, no, we'll survive! Honest! Oh and these are our new friends: the Baali!</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, the True Hand are just so adorable. I want to pinch all of their cheeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T00:06:47-08:00","id":1438691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438681#post1438681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make a lot more sense for loyalist Cappadocians to awaken and want revenge because they were loyal to Cappadocius.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would have made more sense to learn that the Giovanni claim to have hunted down and destroyed all the Cappadocians was just flat out wrong, and that tons of Cappadocians had simply melded into the earth or otherwise hid until there was a better time to fight back when the Giovanni had become complacent and vampire politics was very different. <br /> <br /> At least when the Tremere ostensibly hunted the Salubri, they had several more centuries to do so, convinced all other vampires that the Salubri were a menace (so they didn't have to kill them by themselves), and already had an extensive system of chantries and new recruits they could use to do so. The Giovanni just had... their own family in one city. One of the other Cappadocian elders could have easily arranged things to save whatever Cappadocians he wanted, perhaps at the antedeluvian's behest or their own initiative.<br /> <br /> However, the Feast of Folly is evocative and was obviously the Chekhov's Gun of the Dark Ages clanbook, so it had to be fired at some point. What might have been a better twist is for the loyal Cappadocians to awake first to go after the Giovanni, and then later some of the survivors for the Feast to finally escape and get revenge of every other clan member that escaped being consigned to the Feast (both the loyalists and the Giovanni since they were the childer of someone Cappadocious embraced afterwards).<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> <br /> I also think that the reason Cappadocious embraced Augustus Giovanni should have been better. Like a lot of supposed master plots in VtM, it doesn't really come together. The Underpants Gnomes strike again. If Cappadocious just wanted to die in order for his plot to succeed, he could have achieved it by much easier means. Why did he need to be diablerized? What was the point of the Giovanni developing Necromancy (or just new Paths of it now that Necromancy has many paths independent of the Giovanni)? Does it make sense that this small family of Venetian necromancers developed the Discipline as opposed to having thousands of years of other vampires to do the same, plus an entire civilization obsessed with death like Egypt? And why did &quot;all&quot; the Cappadocians need to die? Why shouldn't the surviving Cappadocians have defeated the Giovanni? These points really don't connect with one another. (At least the various theories about Saulot and the Tremere make some sort of theoretical sense.)<br /> <br /> Well the reason is that people were making things up as they went along and did the best they could while trying to stick to established continuity. I don't want to be too harsh on the writers - they created a lot of cool stuff under deadline pressure.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind doing a retcon, you would want something that ties everything together. Cappadocious embraces Augustus because he knows he'll develop some unique Necromancy magic. Your manipulate him so he becomes aware of some strange necromantic ritual that he'll want to use, but which will actually help Cappadocious instead. The ritual involves killing off all other members of Cappadocious's bloodline for some reason. If Cappadocious is sacrificed as part of this ritual, then Cappadocius would benefit by this self-sacrifice in the same away other mythic figures sacrificed themselves. Augustus does this thinking he'll benefit from it when it will actually benefit Cappadocious. But for some reason Cappadocious can't be the one who performs the ritual, so he cons Augustus into doing it for him. Perhaps the intention was for the plan to succeed only when the entirety of Cappadocius's vitae is destroyed in the sense of him and all of his childer are gone, so not only does it require all Cappadocians to be destroyed, but for the Giovanni themselves to inadvertently destroy themselves (perhaps through Augustus's own crazy plans inspired by Cappadocious's earlier manipulations). Only then would Cappadocious &quot;move&quot; to the final stage. (It's entirely likely that Cappadocious intended a magical reenactment of the death of Jesus with Augustus acting as Judas, thinking that he'll somehow be Resurrected and attain godhood. But if so we should see something blasphemous like a series of events where Cappadocious undergoes a magical allegory of the Stations of the Cross.) There's a lot that would still need to be figured out, but in theory this would help explain why things happened as they did. It's OK for the plot to have somehow failed - either because something went wrong or most likely because it was insane and would never work. But at least it would explain things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T01:26:12-08:00","id":1438697,"title":"","content":"The Capadocians are by far the most uninteresting of necromancers, perhaps vampires in general. <br /> <br /> Fortitude and Auspex are great disciplines*, but disciplines tell a story of how vampires hunt and thus who they are (fuck resonances), and Fortitude and Auspex are by far the least useful in hunting. The Caps have three supporting disciplines, but no breadwinner. They'll have stronger elders, but their neonates will struggle more as a result. They're poor, lonely scholars. <br /> Also corporeal death magic (corpse in the monster, bones, humour) is just flat inferior to incomporeal necromancy (Sephulcre, ash, virteous, ceno) <br /> <br /> Frankly, they deserved to get ashed by the Giovanni. Potence and dominate is a combo for assertive, agressive, dominant, overbearing vampires who want to get shit done. It fits the Giovanni (and the Lasombra) perfectly. The Giovanni just aren't an Auspex-Fortitude people. <br /> <br /> *Auspex is a must have. Fortitude is laughably weak in revised and v20, but pretty good in v1/v2/v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T02:38:55-08:00","id":1438703,"title":"","content":"Someone mentioned the Tremere and Tzimisce having almost identical Discipline spreads, but I can't find the post to quote it now. Anyway, I think that makes sense, since the Tremere used Tzimisce blood in their own creation.<br /> <br /> Re: Harbingers, I always assumed a) they were insane after centuries of imprisonment, b) they were conflicted in their vengeance (they want vengeance on the Giovanni for killing Cappadocius, but also for usurping them as a clan and having what should be theirs, by right), c) most of them are old enough to remember and hold these grudges, and d) their Sabbat membership could be tied to the Tal'mahe'Ra's habit of infiltrating the other two sects for various reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438576#post1438576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a musician, there's no harm in calling yourself a musician. Calling yourself a 'snake-king' when you're not a king or a snake... Just sounds like a shitty gang/band name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed it was a clue to their ancestry (descent from the Setites). But yeah, I can totally see that now. I also thought it could be a generally 'exotic Eastern' name like the Sanskrit version of Evil McEvilFace or something.<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining them as the Serpents from Riverside, though, complete with matching jackets and 30-year old teenagers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T03:20:20-08:00","id":1438705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438691#post1438691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the Feast of Folly is evocative and was obviously the Chekhov's Gun of the Dark Ages clanbook, so it had to be fired at some point. What might have been a better twist is for the loyal Cappadocians to awake first to go after the Giovanni, and then later some of the survivors for the Feast to finally escape and get revenge of every other clan member that escaped being consigned to the Feast (both the loyalists and the Giovanni since they were the childer of someone Cappadocious embraced afterwards).</div> </div> </div> </div>Always thought it would have made more sense for the Harbringers to have a grudge against Lazarus and his brood, as well as the Setites rather than the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Lazarus skipped out on the Feast of Folly because he knew Cappadocius was planning something and felt he'd end up being a victim. He allied with the Followers of Set in order to get protection, and later when Caias (the first childer of Cappadocius) showed up, Lazarus murdered him and then stayed in Egypt under the protection of the Setites. Lazarus knew all about the Feast of Folly, he knew what happened, he knew there were lots of other Cappadocians entombed there, and after the Giovanni killed Cappadocius nothing was really stopping Lazarus from going to Kaymalki and freeing his brothers who were trapped there. But he didn't and just stayed in Egypt with the Setites and left them to rot for a thousand years.<br /> <br /> Of course things were a bit more complicated than that, Lazarus ended up going into Topor after his fight and even if he'd been awake would have had to be careful of the Giovani, but for angry Harbringers those would have been minor issues.<br /> <br /> So I always felt that the Harbringers, on getting free, would have been rather more upset at Lazarus, and by extension the Followers of Set who had protected him, than at the Giovanni who weren't even created until well after they'd all been locked away. And, of course, (beyond the simple fact that the Followers are everything the Sabbat hates) since the Sabbat had given its protection to the Serpents of Light, the sect was functionally at war with the Followers of Set, so the Harbringers joining the Sabbat to get revenge against the Setites would have been eminently practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-09-2021, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T15:48:02-08:00","id":1438832,"title":"","content":"It made more sense to me that the Harbingers, having been on the other side of the Shroud until recently, would have run afoul of all sorts of ghostly Giovanni shenanigans over the last 5 centuries and developed antipathy based on being nibbled to death by ducks rather than revenge for a single great betrayal (and of someone who betrayed them!). Not so much &quot;you must all die for your patriarch's crime of diablerizing our beloved clan founder!&quot; as &quot;these are the meddling kids that have been snatching the ghosts crucial to our plans to return or turning them into spectres and cost us a half millennium in the netherworld\u2014step on the fuckers like roaches!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T19:51:01-08:00","id":1438872,"title":"","content":"As long time Giovanni fan and someone that generally likes the Hecata and what has been done to them, I thought I'd share some of my own thoughts on stuff that's being talked about.<br /> <br /> With regards to the Giovanni and the Harbingers, their whole thing has always been off. The earliest write-ups of them have always been vague on why exactly they hated the Giovanni. But it has also been noted that the Pisanob bloodline in particular had been receiving a lot of their attention. Now the first thing that comes to mind in that is that Pisanob are the Giovanni based in South and Central America, where the Sabbat are strong. Obviously many Harbingers would target them first due to their proximity to Sabbat strongholds but there are two things that put an interesting spin on that. First in V5 it's noted that the Harbingers had brought the Bloodline to near destruction until their founder and leader offered his life up in exchange for the survival of the rest of the Pisanob. An odd thing for a Giovanni Bloodline to get more attention than the main family. Until we factor in the second thing, the Pisanobs were vampires before the Giovanni found them. Their founder and leader, Pochtli was long suspected to be a Cappadocian.<br /> <br /> And that piece might just be the thing to explain it all.<br /> <br /> Now this is pure speculation on my part but I think there are two things that drove their aggression against the Giovanni (well aside from the fact that as rival Necromancers they are a threat to them), the first being vengeance by proxy. They can't get revenge against Cappadocious anymore but they can go after the ones that still carry his Blood, Augustus and those Giovanni embraced before Cappa's death. The second reason is to go after those Cappadocians that defected to the Giovanni to save their own hides. Like I said, Pochtli was almost certainly a Cappadocian but there's also been vague talk over the years that some of the Premascine within the Giovanni were of Cappadocian Blood but not Giovanni stock. To a Harbinger, they would be worse than the Giovanni. They abandoned their Clan mates to their fate to save themselves just as so many Cappadocians abandoned them during the Feast of Folly.<br /> <br /> It would help explain why they were so against the Giovanni yet also willing to take part in the Family Reunion and join the Hecata. Those that were focus of their ire were by that point dead or subdued while they are now a leading voice in the Clan of Death (something they likely never had with the Cappadocians) as well as regaining their ability to Embrace. In fact of all the Bloodlines, the Harbingers have gained the most from the Family Reunion. They've even eclipsed their Cappadocian kin in terms of power and prominence.<br /> <br /> Finally, Lazarus and the Harbingers. On the surface of things, I could see why some would think that the Harbingers should hate him but if the material from V20 on the matter holds true in V5 (which in this case I don't see why it wouldn't) then the generally it would be reverse. In the V20 Black Hand book it was revealed that the Capuchin is a trio of Cappadocians (rather two Cappa and the wraith of one), Japheth, Byzar and Lazarus. And the Capuchin has long been a shadow player in the Giovanni as well as potentially one that freed at least some of the Harbingers. In fact one in Lore of the Bloodlines claims that the Capuchin unmasked himself to them, revealing himself to be Lazarus and that he gave them their name, the Harbingers of Skulls. Of course another Harbinger claims otherwise, muddying the situation. But generally their chapter presents Lazarus as a respected figure among the Harbingers, even those that dispute him saving them acknowledge him as someone to respect.<br /> <br /> And given the Capuchin was involved in the Family Reunion, with it being suggested that he gave them their new name, it wouldn't surprise me if the Capuchin was the driving force behind the Reunion and that to do he unmasks himself as Lazarus to get the Harbingers and Cappadocians to general play ball. Or even the aforementioned trio to reveal themselves as the Capuchin. Which actually now that I say that out loud I realize that the reveal of the Capuchin being three people would play into the trinity motif that is present in the Hecata.<br /> <br /> As for the Hecata and the other Sects, there are some points in V5 Cults that I wish to bring up. First is that the book notes that not all Cappadocians rescued from Torpor aren't okay with joining up with the Giovanni and that they are looking to join the Camarilla. The other being that most outside the Hecata don't know that the Hecata are what they are and are using that to their ends. At the moment, the Cam and Anarchs think that the Giovanni has just reorganized and rebranded themselves. And with the Giovanni continuing to be the face of the Clan, others are offering their services as alternatives to the Giovanni when in reality they're buying the services of the same group.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the book very much takes a stance that I've long held with the Giovanni in my games, that neutrality does not equal inactivity. In my games, I've long had the Giovanni be a fixture of local politics, regardless of whether the city's Cam or Anarch. Giovanni reps frequently appear at Elysium and other major events because the Princes and Barons don't trust them but also can't afford to alienate them lest they decide to quietly send aid to their rivals and foes or worse.<br /> <br /> And with the uneasy new politics of the Hecata, there's plenty of room to get non-Hecata dragged into their schemes and games. Hell, that the Hecata chronicle within the book includes a sample coterie with non-Hecata in it is proof of that alone.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T23:36:55-08:00","id":1438900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438697#post1438697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Capadocians are by far the most uninteresting of necromancers, perhaps vampires in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some of this is due to them being the most undeveloped of the clans. They've only been treated as a real clan once in the Dark Ages game, and any other time it's only been as a metaplot element. So they're detailed in one clanbook set in the Dark Ages. In contrast, all the other clans have had two clanbooks, a Dark Ages supplement, and much greater use as NPCs and addressed in sect sourcebooks. If the Cappadocians had gotten the same treatment, they'd likely seem much more interesting.<br /> <br /> A big part of vampire lore is showing vampires laying in crypts, dead relatives coming back to your home, and deathly pale pallor. That is somewhat neglected in VtM, and the Cappadocians are a natural fit there. I think they have a lot of potential even in a modern setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438697#post1438697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortitude and Auspex are great disciplines*, but disciplines tell a story of how vampires hunt and thus who they are (fuck resonances), and Fortitude and Auspex are by far the least useful in hunting. The Caps have three supporting disciplines, but no breadwinner. They'll have stronger elders, but their neonates will struggle more as a result. They're poor, lonely scholars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that it seems to be one of the poorer in-clan sets. The in-clan discipline sets really do help determine the <i>feel</i> of the clan, and these are all so passive. It'd help if one of them was a more active use Discipline - something they do to someone else.<br /> <br /> I have never been a fan of the idea of Disciplines changing or sub-clans having different in-clans. I think that's a sign of poor design. In an ideal reboot, I'd prefer for all the sub-clans of the Cappadocians to have the same Discipline set, including the Giovanni. So it'd have to be something that fits both within the theme of the original Cappadocians (scholars of death) and the Giovanni (modern decadent Borgias). We need to keep Necromancy or whatever V5 call its. I also think Auspex works for both. Scholars and degenerates could make use of it. So that leaves swapping Fortitude for something else. Does Potence make sense (it could be a rigor mortis theme)? Dominate to represent their willpower as they explore the mysteries? It's not a natural fit, but it'd help them feed. Or is something else better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T00:20:32-08:00","id":1438902,"title":"","content":"I feel capadocians have passive/defensive disciplines does well to give them low numbers and makes them a perfect metaphor for how old-fashioned, scholarly loners will get wrecked by agressive big-business (The Giovanni come into power during the late medieval/early renaissance, where banks and merchants are getting their big break; it's not a coincidence)<br /> Also, I imagine virtually all capadocians as very penitent monks, i'm sure some weren't, but it's the archtype that comes to mind most. Auspex, Fortitude and Necromancy just become the most -this fits the character- disciplines we have. Auspex and necromancy for -scholarly monk- and Fortitude and Necromancy for -I must suffer- monk living.<br /> <br /> Making necromancy an out-of-clan might work, but some people are very attached to -clan of death- idea and wouldn't ever want that.<br /> Giving up fortitude? No, we must applaud their masochism.<br /> Giving up Auspex... well, they are rather delusional... it's the lesser crime I think. You don't need auspex to find ghosts if you have necromancy, but the other issue is that the cappadocians are idiots and put zombies above ghosts so they often didn't have sephulcre; that could do with a retcon.<br /> <br /> But what to replace it with?<br /> <br /> Animalism- The guy plays with bodies all day. Probably reeks of embalming fluid. No.<br /> Celerity- There's the quick and the dead. A guy who hangs around with corpses all day shouldn't be embracing the quick.<br /> Dominate- Gives the impression they're well oranized, and they aren't, the giovanni are. Conflict is more interesting narratively when two sides hold directly opposing views.<br /> Obfuscate, by far the most beneficial for what I think a capadocian playstyle should be, but their corpse-palor would need to become Samedi-ugly or else they'd be cheating.<br /> Potence- It could work well, Interesting juxtoposition to the 'defensive' stereotype of capadocians. Maybe a little redundant with fortitude (Where you'll still win fights against mortals for feeding, they'll just take longer and maybe involve more noise... hmm...)<br /> Presence- Hahahaha no.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say best options would be Necromancy, Fortitude, Obfuscate, (Samedi called) or Auspex, Obfuscate, fortitude (Like the toughest malkavian you'd ever seen, you'd never kill them all) or you tread on the Lamia's toes with a potence replacement. If you gave them obfuscate, a weakness fix (that isn't appearance 0) would be to have the -looks deathly, can't blush of life- show effects no matter how they use mask of a thousand faces. Necromancy as an -out-of-clan- discipline in general isn't a terrible idea (The Samedi and Kiasyd do it so) because it's reallly no good at getting you food...<br /> <br /> After all that brainstorming, I still think I'd stick to Auspex,Fortitude, Necromancy and the same clan weakness. Having a poorer spread is a feature, not a bug, when you're doomed to fail anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T04:22:25-08:00","id":1438922,"title":"","content":"I would be okay with Potence for Cappadocians. Fortitude works pretty well to prevent death, which fits the Clan of Death both ironically and unironically, but the idea of deathly ill, corpse-like figures actually having the strength of ten men is actually pretty scary when encountered. If you've worked in healthcare, you have probably encountered &quot;old man strength;&quot; sometimes the frailest-looking people get a hand on you and for a moment, you wonder how the rest of your life will turn out after they've torn your arm off. Gives their <i>Grip Of Death</i> phrase another facet.<br /> <br /> Also, not to put too fine a point on it, but moving a body is actually pretty hard, and one does not usually set up one's lab right where one's subject keeled over. Not to mention mausoleum doors, sarcophagus lids, etc.<br /> <br /> Plus, OOC, no other Clan has the Auspex &amp; Potence line up, even though heightened senses and super strength are pretty much the standard tropes in 99% of all vampire depictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","user":"Garygeneric","date":". 03-10-2021, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T05:45:31-08:00","id":1438929,"title":"","content":"The issue with potence+auspex (and the dead weight of necromancy) is that it leaves potence alone as the feeding strat. I might houserule that Potence greatly allows for safe knockouts but the default doesn't. The clans with potence all have a compliment to potence that lets them get away with it: they can talk, sneak or speed their way out of the potential consequences of assault-for-food (if for whatever reason that was their first choice, as it rarely is). Potence+ Auspex just gives us a violent thug who knows to attack when others arent around. Fortitude at least brings the implication that someones willing to suffer for a meal and play things safe. <br /> <br /> as for lifting bodies: yes, but i also feel vampires, not needing to breath while being supernaturally tough, dont have a problem with exherting themselves more than humans would normally commit to: a vamp doesnt need to worry about saving energy, and can sprint marathons without supporting disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T06:42:25-08:00","id":1438930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438872#post1438872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long time Giovanni fan and someone that generally likes the Hecata and what has been done to them, I thought I'd share some of my own thoughts on stuff that's being talked about.<br /> <br /> With regards to the Giovanni and the Harbingers, their whole thing has always been off. The earliest write-ups of them have always been vague on why exactly they hated the Giovanni. But it has also been noted that the Pisanob bloodline in particular had been receiving a lot of their attention. Now the first thing that comes to mind in that is that Pisanob are the Giovanni based in South and Central America, where the Sabbat are strong. Obviously many Harbingers would target them first due to their proximity to Sabbat strongholds but there are two things that put an interesting spin on that. First in V5 it's noted that the Harbingers had brought the Bloodline to near destruction until their founder and leader offered his life up in exchange for the survival of the rest of the Pisanob. An odd thing for a Giovanni Bloodline to get more attention than the main family. Until we factor in the second thing, the Pisanobs were vampires before the Giovanni found them. Their founder and leader, Pochtli was long suspected to be a Cappadocian.<br /> <br /> And that piece might just be the thing to explain it all.<br /> <br /> Now this is pure speculation on my part but I think there are two things that drove their aggression against the Giovanni (well aside from the fact that as rival Necromancers they are a threat to them), the first being vengeance by proxy. They can't get revenge against Cappadocious anymore but they can go after the ones that still carry his Blood, Augustus and those Giovanni embraced before Cappa's death. The second reason is to go after those Cappadocians that defected to the Giovanni to save their own hides. Like I said, Pochtli was almost certainly a Cappadocian but there's also been vague talk over the years that some of the Premascine within the Giovanni were of Cappadocian Blood but not Giovanni stock. To a Harbinger, they would be worse than the Giovanni. They abandoned their Clan mates to their fate to save themselves just as so many Cappadocians abandoned them during the Feast of Folly.<br /> <br /> It would help explain why they were so against the Giovanni yet also willing to take part in the Family Reunion and join the Hecata. Those that were focus of their ire were by that point dead or subdued while they are now a leading voice in the Clan of Death (something they likely never had with the Cappadocians) as well as regaining their ability to Embrace. In fact of all the Bloodlines, the Harbingers have gained the most from the Family Reunion. They've even eclipsed their Cappadocian kin in terms of power and prominence.<br /> <br /> Finally, Lazarus and the Harbingers. On the surface of things, I could see why some would think that the Harbingers should hate him but if the material from V20 on the matter holds true in V5 (which in this case I don't see why it wouldn't) then the generally it would be reverse. In the V20 Black Hand book it was revealed that the Capuchin is a trio of Cappadocians (rather two Cappa and the wraith of one), Japheth, Byzar and Lazarus. And the Capuchin has long been a shadow player in the Giovanni as well as potentially one that freed at least some of the Harbingers. In fact one in Lore of the Bloodlines claims that the Capuchin unmasked himself to them, revealing himself to be Lazarus and that he gave them their name, the Harbingers of Skulls. Of course another Harbinger claims otherwise, muddying the situation. But generally their chapter presents Lazarus as a respected figure among the Harbingers, even those that dispute him saving them acknowledge him as someone to respect.<br /> <br /> And given the Capuchin was involved in the Family Reunion, with it being suggested that he gave them their new name, it wouldn't surprise me if the Capuchin was the driving force behind the Reunion and that to do he unmasks himself as Lazarus to get the Harbingers and Cappadocians to general play ball. Or even the aforementioned trio to reveal themselves as the Capuchin. Which actually now that I say that out loud I realize that the reveal of the Capuchin being three people would play into the trinity motif that is present in the Hecata.<br /> <br /> As for the Hecata and the other Sects, there are some points in V5 Cults that I wish to bring up. First is that the book notes that not all Cappadocians rescued from Torpor aren't okay with joining up with the Giovanni and that they are looking to join the Camarilla. The other being that most outside the Hecata don't know that the Hecata are what they are and are using that to their ends. At the moment, the Cam and Anarchs think that the Giovanni has just reorganized and rebranded themselves. And with the Giovanni continuing to be the face of the Clan, others are offering their services as alternatives to the Giovanni when in reality they're buying the services of the same group.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the book very much takes a stance that I've long held with the Giovanni in my games, that neutrality does not equal inactivity. In my games, I've long had the Giovanni be a fixture of local politics, regardless of whether the city's Cam or Anarch. Giovanni reps frequently appear at Elysium and other major events because the Princes and Barons don't trust them but also can't afford to alienate them lest they decide to quietly send aid to their rivals and foes or worse.<br /> <br /> And with the uneasy new politics of the Hecata, there's plenty of room to get non-Hecata dragged into their schemes and games. Hell, that the Hecata chronicle within the book includes a sample coterie with non-Hecata in it is proof of that alone.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like your theory here about the HoS. It makes sense, though I think there are some other things potentially going on.<br /> <br /> I was also going to point out the same thing with Lazarus--he's been connected to the Harbingers since they appeared. They're nicknamed the Lazarenes, Unre/Constancia attributes the return of the HoS to the Capuchin, and the description of the Capuchin in CB:GioRev implies it's Laz (the first letter of each line spells out his name).<br /> <br /> Interestingly, older descriptions of Unre say she and her sire worked on different sides of the Shroud to return the Harbingers to the world. Now that we know Japheth is a wraith, however, it seems they were on opposite sides to the sides we previously assumed (Unre, as a Risen, would have been in the Skinlands, with her sire in the Shadowlands). Previously we assumed that Japheth was still undead and Unre was trapped in the Underworld. This way around makes more sense of their given histories, though.<br /> <br /> There was one more reason for Unre's hatred of the Giovanni, which might also apply to the Harbingers, and that was that they had taken the Sargon Fragment and the Anexhexeton (which she herself sought). I think competing for limited resources is a valid source of conflict, and would certainly aggravate (or be aggravated by) all the nasty business of usurpation.<br /> <br /> If we consider the V20 lore, the Cult of the Capuchin was also looking to bring about Gehenna. So it's entirely possible Laz and co were playing everyone off each other to this end--it doesn't really matter if the rivalry made sense, but he was in the perfect place to stoke it (on both sides).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T07:10:07-08:00","id":1438933,"title":"","content":"Idea that came to me<br /> The Brujah didn't leave.<br /> The Camarilla kicked them out. <br /> They are the clan that most needs culling. too much of a masquerade risk with their Beasts so difficult to control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T07:22:53-08:00","id":1438935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438933#post1438933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea that came to me<br /> The Brujah didn't leave.<br /> The Camarilla kicked them out.<br /> They are the clan that most needs culling. too much of a masquerade risk with their Beasts so difficult to control.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were kicked out in canon.<br /> <br /> You know, Theo Bell and Hardelstadt.<br /> <br /> Even then it was more just removing their Inner Council member (who was already assassinated according to THE CAMARILLA) and Justicar and not replacing them.<br /> <br /> It's just making this kind of blanket pronunciation pissed off so many (Brujah, really?) caused the majority to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T08:24:09-08:00","id":1438941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438929#post1438929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with potence+auspex (and the dead weight of necromancy) is that it leaves potence alone as the feeding strat. I might houserule that Potence greatly allows for safe knockouts but the default doesn't. The clans with potence all have a compliment to potence that lets them get away with it: they can talk, sneak or speed their way out of the potential consequences of assault-for-food (if for whatever reason that was their first choice, as it rarely is). Potence+ Auspex just gives us a violent thug who knows to attack when others arent around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think predation via \u201calpha strike\u201d is a valid feeding strategy. They\u2019re the vampire that hits the lone person taking that shortcut through a dark alley with a chokehold that, if left alive, gets chalked up to a mugger... and can always drag off the corpse for study and it\u2019s another missing person last seen walking home alone after work through the bad part of town.<br /> <br /> That said, for a merger of Cappadocians and Giovanni, I\u2019d say a hybrid spread of Dominate (Giovanni), Fortitude (Cappadocian) and Necromancy (shared) would better capture both sides (in V20 a high natural strength/blood pumping can get most of Potence\u2019s effects and Necromancy includes ways to see ghosts). Feeding is commanding the souls of the living (and the high end includes possession of those bodies you\u2019ve ripped the souls out of) and the resilience to take a hit when it goes wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T09:25:14-08:00","id":1438954,"title":"","content":"In an emergency? Yeah. But on the regular? No. If you're going to feed and research do it sustainably. Murdering for food is not only humanity taxing, likely to attract hunters, and likely to set you against the kindred community, but it's also either really wasteful or dangerous; Your average human has how many points of blood? Ten? Either you're killing, topping yourself up, and letting the blood degrade to disgusting and worthless or you're letting yourself get empty enough to consume a whole human which, unless you're 7th gen or lower, is extremely dangerous in it's own right. In modern times the murder/missing rate is too low to disguise a vampire doing that, and historically settlement sizes have been considerably smaller. <br /> <br /> <br /> Quite simply I think these bloodlines shouldn't be merged because that's needless and stupid and why the fuck would you want to? <br /> <br /> Capadocians, I think, survived by hanging around the dying; the sick and the injured and the old.The Auspex is to find them and the Fortitude is to tank whatever sickness or poison they're suffering from (or perhaps resist the final struggles of dying people). Because there's only so many spots where people are dying, the Capadocians must be limited in number.<br /> Modern places where people are dying tend to be too few and far between, too secure and too bureaucratic.. the Capas deserved to die off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T10:10:52-08:00","id":1438961,"title":"","content":"To feed, vampires need some kind of an angle, I\u2019ve always thought that. They can\u2019t go out and kill humans regularly, in fact even \u201chunting\u201d is extremely dangerous and foolish unless there is dire need. You wouldn\u2019t want to do it as standard operating procedure. <br /> <br /> Vampires need a herd, ghouls, plentiful access to animals, blood banks, or something else along those lines. Hecata would have a hard time not only in that they have no feeding related Disciplines but because their bites are horribly painful. Nobody is going to want to feel a Hecata sinking it\u2019s fangs in, they are unlikely to submit to it or forget it barring magic.<br /> <br /> What is a Hecata to do? Ghouls maybe? If a Hecata had a bunch of human ghouls, those ghouls could either allow their blood to be drawn (phlebotomy style most likely, no bite) or to procure blood for their masters some other way: such as owning a blood bank or slaughterhouse. <br /> <br /> The Hecata/Cappadocians would be the ghoul Clan, they don\u2019t have as many other methods of winning friends or influencing people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T11:04:27-08:00","id":1438975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438922#post1438922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, OOC, no other Clan has the Auspex &amp; Potence line up, even though heightened senses and super strength are pretty much the standard tropes in 99% of all vampire depictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gave a lot of reasons why Potence would be thematically appropriate. Lifting that heavy crypt lid and mausoleum door certainly requires it! And having a unique set in Auspex &amp; Potence (I had not noticed that before) is another sign in its favor. (I always heavily disliked the Giovanni set because Dominate + Potence + Unique Discipline was already taken by the Lasombra, and I thought this was just lazy to reuse it again for the Giovanni.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438941#post1438941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, for a merger of Cappadocians and Giovanni, I\u2019d say a hybrid spread of Dominate (Giovanni), Fortitude (Cappadocian) and Necromancy (shared) would better capture both sides (in V20 a high natural strength/blood pumping can get most of Potence\u2019s effects and Necromancy includes ways to see ghosts). Feeding is commanding the souls of the living (and the high end includes possession of those bodies you\u2019ve ripped the souls out of) and the resilience to take a hit when it goes wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, this is a a compelling argument as well. It would certainly cement the clan's reputation around the idea of &quot;souls&quot;, but less about the dead body per se. <br /> <br /> I think either could work, but it would lead to slightly different feel for the clan. I'm leading to the Potence option right now, but this is a strong argument for people who want to go the other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438954#post1438954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an emergency? Yeah. But on the regular? No. If you're going to feed and research do it sustainably. Murdering for food is not only humanity taxing, likely to attract hunters, and likely to set you against the kindred community, but it's also either really wasteful or dangerous;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an important consideration, but I think you're underestimating what is possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438954#post1438954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite simply I think these bloodlines shouldn't be merged because that's needless and stupid and why the fuck would you want to?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a fine opinion, and obviously the game defaults to that. And given your tastes, I know you won't be converted. But I don't think it is either needless or stupid. To me, it does not make sense why the Giovanni would have a different Weakness or set of In-Clan Disciplines. They are Cappadocians. Even in the Dark Ages setting, they are Cappadocians. It doesn't make sense to me why the Curse would change or have in-clans changed. It's a needless complication. It likely only exists because nobody originally thought this through. The Giovanni were their own thing so who cares what their original clan was like. But after the Cappadocians were created for the Dark Ages setting, they were stuck with having two different versions because the original Giovanni discipline set simply seemed inappropriate for who the Cappadocians should be back in the Middle Ages. <br /> <br /> This kind of thing is common in creative situations like this. I understand that for published settings, you simply go with contradictions that result from not thinking things through originally. It's hard to retcon if you are trying to keep to continuity. But for home chronicles, there is no reason to go with it unless you happen to like it. I don't. I'd rather have something that is more coherent. Others might as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438954#post1438954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern places where people are dying tend to be too few and far between, too secure and too bureaucratic.. the Capas deserved to die off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think you are right that a major way Cappadocians historically hunted was to go after the sick and dying. But I don't think that is no longer an option. After all, people die everywhere and all the time for the simple fact that everyone eventually dies. And there are places where a lot of people die relatively close by. And I don't think they are necessarily in places too secure or too bureaucratic.<br /> <br /> You can control a medical practice that specializes in geriatrics, and have a list of lots of old people and where they live. You can control a hospice service and have the same. You can prowl retirement communities using any number of disguises. But let's say you want to feed on more than just old people. You have lots of other options too.<br /> <br /> There's still lots of homeless people because they're drug addicts or mentally ill. They tend to congregate in many of the same spaces. They're open and exposed. They're deaths really won't be investigated heavily. You could pose as one of them, or as a charity worker running any number of things. Simply running a clean needle exchange will likely give you a large list of targets.<br /> <br /> Or you can go into grief counselling or support groups, and find lots of potential victims that way. Befriend them, and then feed on them or even kill them later in a way that won't draw suspicion. It could simply be to do it when they are sleeping, incapacitated, or not paying attention because you're someone they trust.<br /> <br /> This kind of thing would take lots of planning and work, but in terms of mechanics, it just means having a large amount of Herd, knowing where they leave, and feeding on them while they sleep. It's neither hard nor impossible with the genre conventions. It's no more unbelievable than any of the other ways Kindred are supposed to feed.<br /> <br /> So I think Cappadocians in a modern setting are perfectly viable. And that's just tactics being kept &quot;in character.&quot; There are other options available. And of course, once a character learns some out of clans, more things open up. Now a lot of Players may not like to play this route. They want something more active. That's fine. They either generate their own concept, or choose a different clan. It's fine for not all clans to be equally popular - I'm sure a small number of clans dominate the number of PCs played.<br /> <br /> This strategy is also viable for Giovanni concepts. They are a corrupt, decadent family with deep familial loyalties as a result of malign vampire influence. They partially feed on their family which constitutes part of their Herd. Their wealth attracts people to them. Their various business enterprises gives them lots of cover stories. Concepts can run medical practices, funeral homes, etc. All standard Giovanni stuff as well as Cappadocian stuff. The gangsters of their family can feed on rivals they kill, or people who won't attract attention if they go missing. Legitimate business men can run casino resorts which can attract lots of people who also won't draw attention, and whose rooms you can monitor at night. Rich bankers can host fancy social events for their family, and identify which people are the ones who are so attracted to the Giovanni wealth that they willingly ignore any danger signs and put themselves into a position where they can be fed upon. Whether they have Dominate or Potence or perhaps something else, can adjust their tactics accordingly. It'll still work for them even if they only have one of those Disciplines and not both.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly fine if none of this is to your taste. But I think it's too dismissive to say the clan couldn't be made to work simply because they are not your cup of tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T11:47:13-08:00","id":1438983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438975#post1438975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, this is a a compelling argument as well. It would certainly cement the clan's reputation around the idea of &quot;souls&quot;, but less about the dead body per se.<br /> <br /> I think either could work, but it would lead to slightly different feel for the clan. I'm leading to the Potence option right now, but this is a strong argument for people who want to go the other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main reason I leaned Presence over Potence from the Giovanni side is because, given their clan weakness the ability to use Command (&quot;Silence!&quot;) and Forgetful Mind are a HUGE boon to successful feeding. Potence lets you overpower people to feed, but doesn't negate them screaming bloody murder in the process. Commanding victims to suffer in silence is something right out of a horror film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T11:53:37-08:00","id":1438986,"title":"","content":"If you're not afraid of losing Humanity, I don't see any problem with feeding in a hospice. They're everywhere and no one will question people dying in them. Your biggest issue will probably be that you will be high off your gourd all the time unless you're denying them pain medication. Indeed, I'm sure that hospices are places that vampires absolutely love to get control over as territories.<br /> <br /> However, I've always felt the Giovanni have been inclined to be baggers and bankers more than most Kindred. It's homebrew but in my games, I always give Giovanni NECROMANTIC RITUALS around feeding to make their lives easier.<br /> <br /> A couple of the ones I created are:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Feast of the Dead (Oblivion 1)</b>: The Hecata who uses this causes blood of someone who has died within 2-3 days to have their blood rendered appetizing and fresh enough to be stored. It lacks the hot rush and heroin-like feeling of fresh blood but it is bland and satisfying to remove Hunger Dice until 1. It is a very common use of the ability and a ritual that makes it easier for Hecata to feed.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Cleansing the Corpse (Oblivion 1)</b>: This ritual cleanses a corpse's blood of all medications and leaves it perfectly valid for feeding upon as long as it is fresh. It does not make it any easier to remove the blood from the body but it can be used on blood that is already extracted as long as the subject is dead. Why this distinction matters is a subject of some debate.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Drain a corpse (Oblivion 2)</b>: The Hecata can remove all the blood within a body without extensive efforts, causing the heart to pump post mortem and push all of the blood outside of it through a wound the vampire has opened. It cannot remove the final Hunger Dice but allows the Hecata to have access to blood that would otherwise go to waste or be difficult to remove.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Ecotoplasm (Oblivion 3)</b>: This allows a Hecata to feed on a ghost that has been summoned around them and drain a bit of their Corpus away to feed upon the life force within. It does 2 points of Corpus damage for every point of Hunger it reduces. It cannot be used in combat but must actually be used upon a ghost that has been summoned. It can be used to remove the final dice of hunger but it will require discorporating the Wraith for a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2021, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:18:32-08:00","id":1438991,"title":"","content":"Not all hospice care is done in hospices with centralized patient care in one place. In some hospice care services, the caregivers drive out to the homes and take care of their clients there. And not all people receiving hospice care are in pain. They have other medical and care needs. Nor do all patients receiving pain medication get them all the time, or are allowed the option to self-administer. So there can be a period of time when a vampire could feed yet not suffer the effects of drugs in the bloodstream.<br /> <br /> I can definitely see certain vampires feeding on hospice care patients and losing Humanity. They see it as something to exploit. Most vampires would be there. But I also see certain vampires feeding on them and not losing Humanity at all. A very humane vampire who actually cares about the patients might even raise their humanity in certain situations. It all depends on the context of how the vampire treats them and his motivation for doing so. Now I think in practice, vampires won't be raising their Humanity at all, and the Beast could easily take over in that situation. Even reasons that were originally altruistic can easily become self-serving. But for those PCs who want to retain high Humanity, it should still be an option in this scenario.<br /> <br /> So your scenario is plausible, but not the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:42:03-08:00","id":1438998,"title":"","content":"I think your Feast of the Dead is too strong (making a lot of resources where there are none) Perhaps you should change it so that it preserves a fresh corpse, and maybe make it a higher level so it's not something any serial killer can pick up. I believe there's a nagaraja/TMR ritual that preserves corpses for their eating. I like Drain a corpse, but you can probably add some fun and flavourful things like needing to hang the body or something perversely giovanni. As for feeding from ghosts, that's always been the abilitity I've envied the Nagajara for, and it'd be weird to just give that to everybody.<br /> <br /> Re-Feeding from hospice folk<br /> If they're dying, it might be relief to send them off. It's hard to see people cling to life, even as their existence has been reduced to only suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-10-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:44:18-08:00","id":1439000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438983#post1438983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason I leaned Presence over Potence from the Giovanni side is because, given their clan weakness the ability to use Command (&quot;Silence!&quot;) and Forgetful Mind are a HUGE boon to successful feeding. Potence lets you overpower people to feed, but doesn't negate them screaming bloody murder in the process. Commanding victims to suffer in silence is something right out of a horror film.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first and second edition, the Giovanni weakness &quot;merely&quot; caused extra Health Damage for each blood point consumed. There was no mention that it caused excruciating pain. That was added in Revised. That made sense, but might not have been the intent originally. Revised made a lot of changes simply to make the setting a much darker place, sometimes needlessly so. <br /> <br /> But if an ST simply reverted to the old rules, then the &quot;pain&quot; does not become an issue - there's nothing more than any other vampire. But they still risk killing those they feed upon more easily.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, while the Flaw Grip of the Damned explicitly says the victim gains no ecstasy from feeding, the Giovanni weakness doesn't mention that. It might be implied, but one could make the argument that the victim experiences both pain and pleasure at the same time - something noticeable, but perhaps still experiencing some of the benefits of the standard Kiss.<br /> <br /> That's not an argument against your statement. It's still valid. But there could be other ways possible to feed depending on the ST's interpretations and preferences on the Giovanni curse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T13:10:25-08:00","id":1439009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438998#post1438998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-Feeding from hospice folk<br /> If they're dying, it might be relief to send them off. It's hard to see people cling to life, even as their existence has been reduced to only suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I've always liked Roads but not Paths.<br /> <br /> With Roads, you basically are supposed to have a consistent moral system that is DIFFERENT from Judeo-Christianity but not something that is so alien that you can't see their point. Mage's Euthanatos would never be on the Path of Humanity but I don't think of them as EVIL either. I think the same of the Cappadocians or at least they should be.<br /> <br /> They aren't people who view death the same way as your average person but I wouldn't put them in the same category as the Sabbat either.<br /> <br /> I admit the fact I was a fan of Planescape's Dustmen kind of makes me automatically like the Cappys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-10-2021, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T13:53:31-08:00","id":1439022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439009#post1439009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage's Euthanatos would never be on the Path of Humanity but I don't think of them as EVIL either. I think the same of the Cappadocians or at least they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutist statements like this are where a lot of your arguments run aground.<br /> <br /> I've run Mage almost constantly for nearly a quarter century now and have seen DOZENS of Euthanatos played that would easily fall onto the Path of Humanity and I've found from personal experience that its actually easier to run a proper Roman Catholic mystic under their paradigm than it is to run one under the Celestial Chorus which is a bit too unitarian every faith is equally valid to be anything other than heresy under Roman Catholic canon law.<br /> <br /> By contrast, guarding the cycle of life from conception to natural death and miracle-working through spiritual union with the divine (that little tidbit buried away in the Revised Tradition Book was my key to finally grokking the whole tradition's magic) are both elements of the Roman Catholic faith. They wouldn't be a &quot;main line&quot; Euthanatos, but they fit better there than any other mystic tradition (they also function okay in the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts who view magick entirely outside a mystic paradigm) because guarding the natural cycle doesn't require condoning euthanasia (one could just as easily argue its a disruption of the natural cycle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:14:23-08:00","id":1439030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439022#post1439022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutist statements like this are where a lot of your arguments run aground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your problem is you're taking it as an absolutist statement versus a generality. The Euthanatos being not on the Path of Humanity is the fact that they consider death to be merciful and better for people than life in many cases with an entire life philosophy around that.<br /> <br /> Many don't but this is a generality.<br /> <br /> And it is a good example of how that isn't remotely &quot;Path of Humanity&quot; but it's not BAD necessarily.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T18:49:14-08:00","id":1439083,"title":"","content":"I think the FEAST OF FOLLY has kind of become way more important than it ever should have been. The Harbingers and every other surviving Cappadocian has been tied to it and I feel that undermines them rather than the reverse. Bluntly, the Feast of Folly was a disposal of all the lame, illiterate, and poorly chosen Cappadocians that had become a pestilance on the Earth. Making the Harbingers into the descendants of that event means that they're the lame Cappadocians that couldn't make the grade.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the gameline has made the Antediluvian doing a massacre of inferior vampires into a bigger event than it should be. While Antediluvians are awake, I would assume that cleaning house and devouring the unworthy is pretty much what they <i>do</i>.<br /> <br /> The way CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS treats it, it was like their own version of Gehenna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T20:44:13-08:00","id":1439091,"title":"","content":"It wasn't only the lame, illiterate ones. Also the ones who hadn't built a church or temple, and those who didn't follow the Road of Heaven and others besides. No doubt there were some great and learned vampires who nevertheless didn't happen to adhere to every single article on the laundry list of traits Cappadocius was specifically looking for and ended up being locked away. I imagine the Harbringers are generally the cream of that crop.<br /> <br /> Now, it ended up being kind of a big thing because it's the only real defining event that the Cappadocians ever had (other than being hunted to near extinction by the Giovanni) since they only ever got explored in a single book. Though, to be fair, I believe it's also a fairly unique event in the annals of the Vampire clans as I can't think of any other event where the clan founder culled the clan members in quite the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T21:01:56-08:00","id":1439093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439091#post1439091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't only the lame, illiterate ones. Also the ones who hadn't built a church or temple, and those who didn't follow the Road of Heaven and others besides. No doubt there were some great and learned vampires who nevertheless didn't happen to adhere to every single article on the laundry list of traits Cappadocius was specifically looking for and ended up being locked away. I imagine the Harbringers are generally the cream of that crop.<br /> <br /> Now, it ended up being kind of a big thing because it's the only real defining event that the Cappadocians ever had (other than being hunted to near extinction by the Giovanni) since they only ever got explored in a single book. Though, to be fair, I believe it's also a fairly unique event in the annals of the Vampire clans as I can't think of any other event where the clan founder culled the clan members in quite the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how they explore the Cyclical Gehenna thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T21:12:22-08:00","id":1439094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439030#post1439030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your problem is you're taking it as an absolutist statement versus a generality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not a psychic, so I can only take statements as they\u2019re written. As an author, you know words mean things and that written text requires more care than the spoken because there is no inflection or emotion behind it to provide context.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMage's Euthanatos would <b>never</b> be on the Path of Humanity\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Never means \u201cnever.\u201d It does not mean \u201crarely.\u201d You do this quite a bit with your statements; use absolutist terms that apparently you don\u2019t mean. I suspect you\u2019d get far less pushback on the boards if you\u2019d just clarify a bit. For example...<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMany of Mage\u2019s Euthanatos would not be on the Path of Humanity.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> ...is apparently both closer to what you intended to say and also something I wouldn\u2019t even disagree with.<br /> <br /> * * * *<br /> <br /> To the topic at hand though; I\u2019m going to disagree on Paths being superior to Humanity. I think only using humanity is something V5 probably got right because, ultimately, the Paths are constructs created by humans (the writers of the game and, in universe, humans cursed with vampirism) that basically amount to \u201csubset of human motivation we want to justify as playable\u201d in the same way fantasy races generally are just representations of a subset of broader human nature.<br /> <br /> Also I\u2019ve seen damnably few players actually be able to divorce themselves enough from humanity to be able to play one as anything other than varying levels Humanity with an excuse for why a particular sin is actually justified.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can feed on the dying and not be a monster because I\u2019m ending their pain\u201d doesn\u2019t feel like a path of enlightenment to me... it feels like a high conscience rating justifying why harming others isn\u2019t \u2018really\u2019 harming others. \u201cNo,\u201d you tell yourself, \u201cits actually a good thing and you aren\u2019t getting any closer to the Beast for doing it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Paths feel like a cheat on the personal horror elements to me by giving you a choose your own morality system where whatever sins you want to commit are justified so you can keep playing the PC instead of losing them the same way you would in any other game with a PC morality clause (ex. WEG Star Wars and Dark Side Point accumulation eventually turning you into an NPC).<br /> <br /> They feel like a workaround that was added to the game because the mechanics for the Humanity 1-4 range that most Sabbat would otherwise have were given far too severe hindrances to allow them to be playable (emergency daylight action and torpor length particularly) without some alternative morality systems that let them have better daylight dice pools and torpor lengths short enough to not make a torpored PC effectively \u201cdead\u201d as far as the chronicle is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T00:32:22-08:00","id":1439109,"title":"","content":"I think you are being unfair to the capadocians and theur lack of materials. The capadocians werent an independent sect like the assamites , settites or later Giovanni, they were just another one of the many ordinary clans, like the Toreador or Nosferatu or Malkavians. Only they got devoured. You shouldnt expect some kind of grand cultural narrative for every clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T01:17:27-08:00","id":1439116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439083#post1439083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the FEAST OF FOLLY has kind of become way more important than it ever should have been. The Harbingers and every other surviving Cappadocian has been tied to it and I feel that undermines them rather than the reverse. Bluntly, the Feast of Folly was a disposal of all the lame, illiterate, and poorly chosen Cappadocians that had become a pestilance on the Earth. Making the Harbingers into the descendants of that event means that they're the lame Cappadocians that couldn't make the grade.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the gameline has made the Antediluvian doing a massacre of inferior vampires into a bigger event than it should be. While Antediluvians are awake, I would assume that cleaning house and devouring the unworthy is pretty much what they <i>do</i>.<br /> <br /> The way CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS treats it, it was like their own version of Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> An Aside: Given how pathetic the so called Blood Gods are this edition, how long do you think it will be until neonate coeteries are offing them like raid bosses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T01:20:26-08:00","id":1439117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439094#post1439094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not a psychic, so I can only take statements as they\u2019re written. As an author, you know words mean things and that written text requires more care than the spoken because there is no inflection or emotion behind it to provide context.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMage's Euthanatos would <b>never</b> be on the Path of Humanity\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Never means \u201cnever.\u201d It does not mean \u201crarely.\u201d You do this quite a bit with your statements; use absolutist terms that apparently you don\u2019t mean. I suspect you\u2019d get far less pushback on the boards if you\u2019d just clarify a bit. For example...<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMany of Mage\u2019s Euthanatos would not be on the Path of Humanity.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> ...is apparently both closer to what you intended to say and also something I wouldn\u2019t even disagree with.<br /> <br /> * * * *<br /> <br /> To the topic at hand though; I\u2019m going to disagree on Paths being superior to Humanity. I think only using humanity is something V5 probably got right because, ultimately, the Paths are constructs created by humans (the writers of the game and, in universe, humans cursed with vampirism) that basically amount to \u201csubset of human motivation we want to justify as playable\u201d in the same way fantasy races generally are just representations of a subset of broader human nature.<br /> <br /> Also I\u2019ve seen damnably few players actually be able to divorce themselves enough from humanity to be able to play one as anything other than varying levels Humanity with an excuse for why a particular sin is actually justified.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can feed on the dying and not be a monster because I\u2019m ending their pain\u201d doesn\u2019t feel like a path of enlightenment to me... it feels like a high conscience rating justifying why harming others isn\u2019t \u2018really\u2019 harming others. \u201cNo,\u201d you tell yourself, \u201cits actually a good thing and you aren\u2019t getting any closer to the Beast for doing it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Paths feel like a cheat on the personal horror elements to me by giving you a choose your own morality system where whatever sins you want to commit are justified so you can keep playing the PC instead of losing them the same way you would in any other game with a PC morality clause (ex. WEG Star Wars and Dark Side Point accumulation eventually turning you into an NPC).<br /> <br /> They feel like a workaround that was added to the game because the mechanics for the Humanity 1-4 range that most Sabbat would otherwise have were given far too severe hindrances to allow them to be playable (emergency daylight action and torpor length particularly) without some alternative morality systems that let them have better daylight dice pools and torpor lengths short enough to not make a torpored PC effectively \u201cdead\u201d as far as the chronicle is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Paths are the main part of the system that interests me. So much so that I have not, and will never, play a character on humanity again, it's just not interesting or fun. But then I preferred 1e Humanity when killing for what ever reason, even in frenzy or under domination, was a rating 2 sin (either it actually was, or that is how the ST at the time interpreted it), So on that front: Either have Humanity be as hard to hold as paths, or don't do it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-11-2021, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T06:50:13-08:00","id":1439156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439117#post1439117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Paths are the main part of the system that interests me. So much so that I have not, and will never, play a character on humanity again, it's just not interesting or fun. But then I preferred 1e Humanity when killing for what ever reason, even in frenzy or under domination, was a rating 2 sin (either it actually was, or that is how the ST at the time interpreted it), So on that front: Either have Humanity be as hard to hold as paths, or don't do it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been reading V1 again, and unintentional killing was a Humanity 6 sin. Outright murder was Humanity 2. But the Hierarchy of Sins was more a suggestion back then, rather than a hard code. Those were given as examples and the ST was supposed to invent their own.<br /> <br /> You may be happy with the Sabbat book, however, as my reading of this latest V5 development blog suggests the Paths will be introduced as alternate splats in that book: <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/development-blog-defining-clans\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news...defining-clans</a> (where Paths are compared to Clans and Tribes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-11-2021, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:10:10-08:00","id":1439159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439117#post1439117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Paths are the main part of the system that interests me. So much so that I have not, and will never, play a character on humanity again, it's just not interesting or fun. But then I preferred 1e Humanity when killing for what ever reason, even in frenzy or under domination, was a rating 2 sin (either it actually was, or that is how the ST at the time interpreted it), So on that front: Either have Humanity be as hard to hold as paths, or don't do it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the inflexibility about killing was something I always considered silly and inconsistent about the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm glad V20 fixed it so that killing was a much less big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:12:54-08:00","id":1439195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439159#post1439159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the inflexibility about killing was something I always considered silly and inconsistent about the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm glad V20 fixed it so that killing was a much less big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains your stance on &quot;killing Princes&quot; being right and just and using the Camarilla as little more than preening antagonists. I remember thinking what a strange take on <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> that was, because my experiences with the game have always been very different. From its release, <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> set itself apart as the more dangerous and violent world, but the Modern Nights setting always had a strong stance against violence as your primary means of conflict resolution. Mark Rein-Hagen talked in an interview about how that was entirely deliberate: the game was supposed to be about trying to work together, not grinding your opposition into the dust.<br /> <br /> The anti-violence stance set <i>Vampire</i> apart from other roleplaying games of the time. What seems &quot;fixed&quot; to you in the more recent iterations of the game, I can't help but see as going against the original intent. To this day, I think killing another vampire should be a momentous occasion in a chronicle, with grave psychological and sociopolitical repercussions -- not something you flippantly do every other session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:18:39-08:00","id":1439196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439195#post1439195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That explains your stance on &quot;killing Princes&quot; being right and just and using the Camarilla as little more than preening antagonists. I remember thinking what a strange take on <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> that was, because my experiences with the game have always been very different. From its release, <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> set itself apart as the more dangerous and violent world, but the Modern Nights setting always had a strong stance against violence as your primary means of conflict resolution. Mark Rein-Hagen talked in an interview about how that was entirely deliberate: the game was supposed to be about trying to work together, not grinding your opposition into the dust.<br /> <br /> The anti-violence stance set <i>Vampire</i> apart from other roleplaying games of the time. What seems &quot;fixed&quot; to you in the more recent iterations of the game, I can't help but see as going against the original intent. To this day, I think killing another vampire should be a momentous occasion in a chronicle, with grave psychological and sociopolitical repercussions -- not something you flippantly do every other session.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that the above has ever been supported by anything other than 1st Edition (ironically) given that 2nd Edition was full of massive amounts of conflict between the Sabbat vs. The Camarilla/Anarchs with Revised being equally so. <i>Under a Blood Red Moon</i> was one of the first major supplements for the game and the high point of the entire line was the adaptation to the video games of <i>Redemption</i> as well as <i>Bloodlines</i>. Vampire &quot;action&quot; is certainly something that has always been part of the setting, hence why Celerity was so popular.<br /> <br /> Even in the 90s, it was very clear that &quot;trenchcoat, katana, dragonsbreath shotgun&quot; were the defacto equipment of player characters. But yes, it's not that PLAYERS should be violent. It's the fact that the Humanity system DOES NOT WORK for Elders. Elder vampires and the Prince are people who should be murdering people left and right because they're the bad guys. However, the Prince and people like, say, Lucita are going to be habitual killers.<br /> <br /> They also shouldn't be close to wassail or on Paths because people on Paths are well, COMPLETELY INSANE, and utterly removed from the way that even someone like Dracula would think. Lodin is an ASSHOLE but he's not inhuman. He kills people for sex, money, or just because he's irritated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:43:00-08:00","id":1439203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439196#post1439196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that the above has ever been supported by anything other than 1st Edition (ironically) given that 2nd Edition was full of massive amounts of conflict between the Sabbat vs. The Camarilla/Anarchs with Revised being equally so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see anything ironic about that. To me, the 1st Edition core remains the beating undead heart of the game. I'm not going to tell anyone else how to run their games, but from my point of view, the seven original clans of the Camarilla trying to work together is what the game is all about. Even in 2nd Edition, the Sabbat and Independents are entirely supplemental material, meant for the occasional dip into ultraviolence before getting back to your typical chronicle.<br /> <br /> Characterizing a crossover splat like <i>Under a Blood Red Moon,</i> as much a <i>Werewolf</i> supplement as a <i>Vampire</i> one, as &quot;one of the first major supplements&quot; for <i>Vampire</i> seems disingenuous to me. <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> for example, was released a full year before it, and is much more relevant to the discussion, even if I ultimately think it doesn't affect my point. Video game adaptations are even less interesting to me -- video games have always been casual with violence, regardless of the source material.<br /> <br /> Using Elders and Princes as purely bad guys with zero nuance has no interest to me, so I can't really comment on that. But even if I agreed that Elders were all inhuman monsters, I would point out that a Humanity 0 vampire used to be a perfectly functional character -- as an NPC. The Humanity tracker was meaningful for player characters only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:58:46-08:00","id":1439206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439196#post1439196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also shouldn't be close to wassail or on Paths because people on Paths are well, COMPLETELY INSANE, and utterly removed from the way that even someone like Dracula would think.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I also think you're being a little hyperbolic in how you represent the Paths of Enlightenment. What is completely insane and utterly removed about the Path of Harmony or the Path of Honorable Accord, just to pick two of the more &quot;humane&quot; Paths from the original <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat?</i> I re-read <i>Dracula</i> just a few months ago, so the novel is pretty fresh in my mind, and the title character certainly behaves more abominably there than I would expect a typical follower of either Path to behave, as a general thing.<br /> <br /> This &quot;Paths are <i>completely insane&quot;</i> line of thinking seems more like the way the Revised era writers wanted to represent the Paths of Enlightenment, rather than what was actually written in the original books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:01:57-08:00","id":1439207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439196#post1439196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the fact that the Humanity system DOES NOT WORK for Elders. Elder vampires and the Prince are people who should be murdering people left and right because they're the bad guys. However, the Prince and people like, say, Lucita are going to be habitual killers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again with the absolutist stances. Not &quot;humanity doesn't work for some elders.&quot; Not &quot;most elders and princes function as antagonists for the PCs.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is why so many find many of your statements to be unsupportable; because you refuse to use even an iota of nuance when presenting them. As written you're saying all elders and princes must always be portrayed as bad guys without exception. Again, I'm not psychic and you're supposed to be someone who works with words for a living, so taking you at your written word, I find your position to be ridiculous and about as complex as the morality in a Captain Planet cartoon.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if all elders are universally evil all the time, then this is the stalest freaking roleplaying game around with every campaign just being a repeat of &quot;try to survive the evil elders until we gain enough power to overthrow them. Lather, rinse, repeat.&quot; Its banal, flat and utterly uninteresting after the first go around. It makes D&amp;D look morally deep and complex since at least there can be good and evil kings and wizards in the setting.<br /> <br /> Variety is the spice of life and varying the plot is essential to keeping people engaged. If every novel you wrote had the protagonists love interest killed off as the inciting incident, then you'd have a hard time getting anyone to invest in the love interest character... why bother? They're always dead by the end of act one. The same with &quot;the elders are always asshole villains and casual killers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the hierarchy of sins is identical in V20 as in the previous ones... injury is 8, accidental killing is 6, impassioned killing is 4, planned killing is 3, casual killing is 2... so I don't see what is actually fixed about it. Your elders and ancients floating around humanity 3-4 is just fine if you want them to be villainous; no Paths other than humanity needed. In fact, I believe the game has always stated that most elders float in the 3-5 humanity range (and note that use of the word &quot;most&quot;... not &quot;all&quot; or similar absolutist remarks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:12:11-08:00","id":1439212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439207#post1439207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, if all elders are universally evil all the time, then this is the stalest freaking roleplaying game around with every campaign just being a repeat of &quot;try to survive the evil elders until we gain enough power to overthrow them. Lather, rinse, repeat.&quot; Its banal, flat and utterly uninteresting after the first go around. It makes D&amp;D look morally deep and complex since at least there can be good and evil kings and wizards in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. Again, if this is not what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> wants to say, then that's all well and good, but going simply by what is written, that's how these supposedly kill-happy <i>Vampire</i> chronicles come across to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:33:13-08:00","id":1439220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439196#post1439196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .<br /> <br /> They also shouldn't be close to wassail or on Paths because people on Paths are well, COMPLETELY INSANE, and utterly removed from the way that even someone like Dracula would think. Lodin is an ASSHOLE but he's not inhuman. He kills people for sex, money, or just because he's irritated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dracula is not a valid argument, for anything. People on Paths aren't crazy, that is an insult both to them, and to people with genuine mental illnesses. They are applying ethics and morality to build a frame work for a state that is fundamentally inhuman, intellect vs instinct, that core conflict, and a different answer to beast I be lest beast I become. Yes some paths ended up being badly handled, or to focused, but the concept is the most interesting part about VtM for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:34:06-08:00","id":1439222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439206#post1439206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I also think you're being a little hyperbolic in how you represent the Paths of Enlightenment. What is completely insane and utterly removed about the Path of Harmony or the Path of Honorable Accord, just to pick two of the more &quot;humane&quot; Paths from the original <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat?</i> I re-read <i>Dracula</i> just a few months ago, so the novel is pretty fresh in my mind, and the title character certainly behaves more abominably there than I would expect a typical follower of either Path to behave, as a general thing.<br /> <br /> This &quot;Paths are <i>completely insane&quot;</i> line of thinking seems more like the way the Revised era writers wanted to represent the Paths of Enlightenment, rather than what was actually written in the original books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remind you that canonically the Path of Harmony was exterminated because it wasn't evil enough to work in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> My opinion on that, playing Path of Harmony characters, was....not good.<br /> <br /> I have since come around to the Revised position that Paths are utterly evil and if you want to follow a non-Humanity view that isn't evil, you'd need to follow a Road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:36:33-08:00","id":1439226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439206#post1439206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I also think you're being a little hyperbolic in how you represent the Paths of Enlightenment. What is completely insane and utterly removed about the Path of Harmony or the Path of Honorable Accord, just to pick two of the more &quot;humane&quot; Paths from the original <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat?</i> I re-read <i>Dracula</i> just a few months ago, so the novel is pretty fresh in my mind, and the title character certainly behaves more abominably there than I would expect a typical follower of either Path to behave, as a general thing.<br /> <br /> This &quot;Paths are <i>completely insane&quot;</i> line of thinking seems more like the way the Revised era writers wanted to represent the Paths of Enlightenment, rather than what was actually written in the original books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd put Dracula (If I have to) On Road of Kings, or maybe Chivalry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:37:22-08:00","id":1439227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439222#post1439222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remind you that canonically the Path of Harmony was exterminated because it wasn't evil enough to work in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> My opinion on that, playing Path of Harmony characters, was....not good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> welcome to Revised ruining the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:40:47-08:00","id":1439229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439227#post1439227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome to Revised ruining the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Sabbat fan, I came around to the view that Revised wasn't dancing around the fact of what the Sabbat were meant to be. Which was people who rejected human morality and exalted in the murder of the innocent as well as defiling of traditional morality.<br /> <br /> It's a different take but one that I don't think is wrong.<br /> <br /> YMMV obviously. Also, there's no wrong answer because it's what's true at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:44:38-08:00","id":1439230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439229#post1439229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Sabbat fan, I came around to the view that Revised wasn't dancing around the fact of what the Sabbat were meant to be. Which was people who rejected human morality and exalted in the murder of the innocent as well as defiling of traditional morality.<br /> <br /> It's a different take but one that I don't think is wrong.<br /> <br /> YMMV obviously. Also, there's no wrong answer because it's what's true at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more the influx of true sabbat on humanity, and paths being relegated to this weird thing in the background that was openly called by the devs degenerate and the verbal and written attacks on the people who liked them that got me. I get it, the Revised devs hated the sabbat, and some of them are writing the sabbat again, which is why I have zero trust in their good faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:47:44-08:00","id":1439232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439203#post1439203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see anything ironic about that. To me, the 1st Edition core remains the beating undead heart of the game. I'm not going to tell anyone else how to run their games, but from my point of view, the seven original clans of the Camarilla trying to work together is what the game is all about. Even in 2nd Edition, the Sabbat and Independents are entirely supplemental material, meant for the occasional dip into ultraviolence before getting back to your typical chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a first Edition fan, the Seven clans are BITTER enemies that are fighting between the Anarchs and the Camarilla. They just have to work together when the Sabbat RARELY shows up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Characterizing a crossover splat like <i>Under a Blood Red Moon,</i> as much a <i>Werewolf</i> supplement as a <i>Vampire</i> one, as &quot;one of the first major supplements&quot; for <i>Vampire</i> seems disingenuous to me. <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> for example, was released a full year before it, and is much more relevant to the discussion, even if I ultimately think it doesn't affect my point. Video game adaptations are even less interesting to me -- video games have always been casual with violence, regardless of the source material. </div> </div> </div>Being a vampire is fundamentally about being a creature that is required to do violence as part of their existence. Even if they are the nicest vampire in the world, they must feed on the blood of the innocent (or not so innocent) and are one frenzy away from killing people. Their powers are also a constant temptation to do evil because they can warp minds and souls or physically hurt individuals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using Elders and Princes as purely bad guys with zero nuance has no interest to me, so I can't really comment on that. But even if I agreed that Elders were all inhuman monsters, I would point out that a Humanity 0 vampire used to be a perfectly functional character -- as an NPC. The Humanity tracker was meaningful for player characters only. </div> </div> </div>If you think evil means no nuance then I strongly disagree. Bluntly, I think the point of the game is to explore the concept of evil and damnation. Frankly, I think it's bad storytelling that darkness and corruption are something that you can't engage with as a player. Bluntly, I don't believe that player characters should ever be the GOOD guys in Vampire games. They can certainly TRY but a large part of what makes the game good is they're usually the lesser evil and possessed of their own terrible violent flaws.<br /> <br /> One of the things I encourage my players at my table to do is engage with this.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who has your character killed that is an innocent person? Because at some point, unless you are REALLY wanting to play it otherwise, they have.&quot;<br /> <br /> * A bad feeding<br /> * A frenzy<br /> * Someone your sire gave you to feed on and drain dry<br /> * A case of mistaken identity<br /> <br /> <u>All your characters are murderers.</u> How you deal with that is part of the roleplaying exercise.<br /> <br /> Generally, I encourage my player characters to be 5-6 Humanity. They're the good vampires, actively fighting against evil. They're contrasted against the 2-4 Humanity vampires who are further down the slide to pure evil.<br /> <br /> If you want to play Humanity 8-10 then you should play a Thin Blood or high generation with deep self-loathing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:53:30-08:00","id":1439233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439230#post1439230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was more the influx of true sabbat on humanity, and paths being relegated to this weird thing in the background that was openly called by the devs degenerate and the verbal and written attacks on the people who liked them that got me. I get it, the Revised devs hated the sabbat, and some of them are writing the sabbat again, which is why I have zero trust in their good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Sabbat on Paths were made by people who hated them. I think putting most Sabbat on Humanity showed that Sabbat on Paths were an Elite.<br /> <br /> They're the people who have made a conscious choice to Embrace (pun intended) with Sabbat ideology.<br /> <br /> Sabbat on Humanity are just the surface-level followers or weekend warrior types. They don't get Sabbat ideology is more than, &quot;Do whatever the fuck I want.&quot; The Paths become something for intellectual, spiritual, and superior beings.<br /> <br /> I mean if all it took for a Path was to be, &quot;I believe that humans are cattle and that as a superior being I can feed on them&quot; then no one would have Low Humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:59:28-08:00","id":1439237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439233#post1439233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the Sabbat on Paths were made by people who hated them. I think putting most Sabbat on Humanity showed that Sabbat on Paths were an Elite.<br /> <br /> They're the people who have made a conscious choice to Embrace (pun intended) with Sabbat ideology.<br /> <br /> Sabbat on Humanity are just the surface-level followers or weekend warrior types. They don't get Sabbat ideology is more than, &quot;Do whatever the fuck I want.&quot; The Paths become something for intellectual, spiritual, and superior beings.<br /> <br /> I mean if all it took for a Path was to be, &quot;I believe that humans are cattle and that as a superior being I can feed on them&quot; then no one would have Low Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> notice the qualifier 'true sabbat' meaning sure, shovel heads and war fodder on humanity, ok. But if you want progress get on a Path, show that strength and conviction. Also don't have devs insulting sabbat fans, but hey, also can't find what he said, so I may be miss remembering how bad it was (and no, I am not going to name said person)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-11-2021, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:00:20-08:00","id":1439238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439207#post1439207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why so many find many of your statements to be unsupportable; because you refuse to use even an iota of nuance when presenting them. As written you're saying all elders and princes must always be portrayed as bad guys without exception. Again, I'm not psychic and you're supposed to be someone who works with words for a living, so taking you at your written word, I find your position to be ridiculous and about as complex as the morality in a Captain Planet cartoon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple of points here:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes, all Elders and Princes are bad guys without exception because they're vampires. You're assuming the player characters can or should be good guys. The Camarilla is something I turn to mafia movies like THE GODFATHER and GOODFELLAS as an example of how to run. To me, it is an organized criminal syndicate and the player characters are part of it. They are not the cops, they are other gangsters.<br /> 2. Being a gangster in a game and rising to the top of the Camarilla is a good game to play. SCARFACE is an excellent Vampire: The Masquerade game. Tony Montana starts off as a Neonate in Florida and gradually rises to become the Sheriff of Miami before he is betrayed by his Prince then proceeds to kill him. He then becomes Prince of Miami himself but soon finds himself forced to work for a Justicar that turns on him when he won't do something evil (murder children). Tony then has Archons sent after him and dies after he has alienated his progeny as well as few remaining allies.<br /> 3. Vampire, to me, is very much about being antiheroes and dark players who likely have a lot of storytelling. This isn't to say you can't have sympathetic or moral(ish) Elders but all of them have blood on their hands<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frankly, if all elders are universally evil all the time, then this is the stalest freaking roleplaying game around with every campaign just being a repeat of &quot;try to survive the evil elders until we gain enough power to overthrow them. Lather, rinse, repeat.&quot; Its banal, flat and utterly uninteresting after the first go around. It makes D&amp;D look morally deep and complex since at least there can be good and evil kings and wizards in the setting. </div> </div> </div>Why is evil uninteresting?<br /> <br /> One of my favorite characters, okay my favorite, from the aborted KINDRED THE EMBRACED was Lily Langtree the Toreador. Lily is evil but she is a complex 3-dimensional character that is motivated by extremely understandable feelings of love, jealousy, and passion. Julian is our ostensible hero and is trying to regain his humanity by being a fair and noble prince. However, being a high humanity Prince (high-ish) is actually SELFISH because it undermines his rule and puts his friends in danger. He takes up with a mortal to feel alive and moral but humiliates his long-time lover in the process.<br /> <br /> I like those kinds of questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the hierarchy of sins is identical in V20 as in the previous ones... injury is 8, accidental killing is 6, impassioned killing is 4, planned killing is 3, casual killing is 2... so I don't see what is actually fixed about it. Your elders and ancients floating around humanity 3-4 is just fine if you want them to be villainous; no Paths other than humanity needed. In fact, I believe the game has always stated that most elders float in the 3-5 humanity range (and note that use of the word &quot;most&quot;... not &quot;all&quot; or similar absolutist remarks). </div> </div> </div>Read the description for Humanity:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity 4<br /> <br /> The vampire begins an inevitable slide into urge<br /> indulgence. A Humanity of 4 indicates that killing is<br /> acceptable to this Kindred, so long as his victim is \u201cdeserving.\u201d<br /> Many vampire elders hover around this level<br /> of Humanity, if they haven\u2019t adopted some other moral<br /> code. Destruction, theft, injury \u2014 these are all tools,<br /> rather than taboos, for a vampire with Humanity 4.<br /> The vampire\u2019s own agenda becomes paramount at this<br /> point, and screw whoever gets in the way.<br /> <br /> Humanity 3-2<br /> <br /> The lives and property of others are irrelevant to<br /> a Kindred this far gone. The vampire likely indulges<br /> twisted pleasures and aberrant whims, which may in-<br /> clude any manner of atrocity. Perversion, callous murder,<br /> mutilation of victims, and wickedness for its own<br /> sake are the hallmarks of a Kindred with very low Humanity.<br /> Few vampires maintain ratings this low and<br /> lower for very long \u2014 their damnation is all but certain<br /> at this point. Physical changes show up at this stage;<br /> while not hideous in the sense of the Nosferatu or certain<br /> Gangrel, the vampire acquires a pallid, corpselike,<br /> and noticeably unwholesome aspect. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:00:28-08:00","id":1439239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439212#post1439212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts exactly. Again, if this is not what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> wants to say, then that's all well and good, but going simply by what is written, that's how these supposedly kill-happy <i>Vampire</i> chronicles come across to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an example of nuance... in my campaign the Prince and most of the elders hover around a Humanity 5; they don't try to kill mortals, but accidents happen and the Prince spends considerable capitol on cleaning those up in as least disruptive a way as possible. A few of the old guard (including the previous Prince who &quot;retired&quot; to focus on his own pursuits) and the Scourge are humanity 4 and no one likes dealing with them. By contrast the Sheriff is up at Humanity 6; he doesn't like accidents, largely because he and his people deal with cleaning them up first hand. There's also a couple of other elders in the 6-7 range and one who's even an 8 (a bagger who protects thinbloods and mentors talented mortal artists as a way of using his immortality to improve the world).<br /> <br /> So, in other words; there's a variety and range and each has different assets and desires and its up to the PCs to figure them out and which they make allies of and which become enemies.<br /> <br /> ETA: So apparently CTPhipps really is a one-note &quot;everyone's a bad guy&quot; sort of GM. Good for him, but something many find abhorrent and have no interest in playing (there's a reason I only play if I'm allowed to run a Dhampir or mortal). Great news though... I can run/play the way my players enjoy and Phipps can play his and life is grand.<br /> <br /> ETA2: Yes, evil is banal and boring and two-dimensional and amounts to &quot;I'm going to hurt X to get what I want.&quot; Far more interesting is to set up the antagonist (note, not the same as a villain) with understandable goals that conflict with those of the protagonist (not the same as a hero) and then set the lines each is willing to cross to get their goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 03-11-2021, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:08:50-08:00","id":1439241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439239#post1439239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an example of nuance... in my campaign the Prince and most of the elders hover around a Humanity 5; they don't try to kill mortals, but accidents happen and the Prince spends considerable capitol on cleaning those up in as least disruptive a way as possible. A few of the old guard (including the previous Prince who &quot;retired&quot; to focus on his own pursuits) and the Scourge are humanity 4 and no one likes dealing with them. By contrast the Sheriff is up at Humanity 6; he doesn't like accidents, largely because he and his people deal with cleaning them up first hand. There's also a couple of other elders in the 6-7 range and one who's even an 8 (a bagger who protects thinbloods and mentors talented mortal artists as a way of using his immortality to improve the world).<br /> <br /> So, in other words; there's a variety and range and each has different assets and desires and its up to the PCs to figure them out and which they make allies of and which become enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems about what I'd do with them as Humanity 4 is where I say someone is &quot;evil.&quot; I would also add that my Princes also kill the following people are part of those victims:<br /> <br /> * Witnesses to the Masquerade being violated that are not easily brainwashed<br /> * People who stand in the way of the Elders getting wealth or power<br /> * People they view as pawns of their rivals or enemies in the Jyhad<br /> * People who infuriate them into losing control<br /> * Loved ones of Neonates who need to put in their place about obeying the Rules.<br /> <br /> Yours is how a &quot;soft&quot; or &quot;good&quot; Prince would work but there's some others are mean about it. About the best you can expect from the system. Not unbelievable but there's a lot of &quot;bad&quot; princes too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:10:27-08:00","id":1439242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439222#post1439222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remind you that canonically the Path of Harmony was exterminated because it wasn't evil enough to work in the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I need no reminder -- this is precisely why I wrote that the above line of thinking seems more like the way the Revised era writers wanted to represent the Paths of Enlightenment, rather than what was actually written in the original books. As with so many other Revised era &quot;course corrections,&quot; I find the in-game &quot;extermination&quot; of a Path and its followers an incredibly clumsy and crude way of handling the matter.<br /> <br /> The idea of &quot;following a Road&quot; in the modern setting is essentially a non-starter for me, because I do not like mixing the Dark Medieval and Modern Nights settings with each other. The entire point of releasing <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> was to provide a <i>different</i> setting for vampires to play in! I genuinely don't understand why people want to take two highly developed settings with strong and unique themes and... mash them together into one indistinguishable goop. Every time someone has the bright idea of bringing <i>Dark Ages</i> elements into the modern setting, I mentally sigh and roll my eyes. Cappadocians, Lamia, Salubri warriors, the Baali as a major force, Roads... All of these elements belong in the Dark Medieval, and the continual mixing only diminishes both <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> and <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i> In my opinion, of course.<br /> <br /> Case in point: Retconning the Paths of Enlightenment into what essentially amounts to dumbass frat boy versions of Roads. The Paths were written first, and in the setting lore, they were supposed to have been a recent development, a product of the last 500 years as a result of the Sabbat's spiritual development. Demoting that achievement into the Sabbat having merely debased the work of their elder superiors is one of the many indignities heaped upon the Sabbat in Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:19:42-08:00","id":1439244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439242#post1439242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point: Retconning the Paths of Enlightenment into what essentially amounts to dumbass frat boy versions of Roads. The Paths were written first, and in the setting lore, they were supposed to have been a recent development, a product of the last 500 years as a result of the Sabbat's spiritual development. Demoting that achievement into the Sabbat having merely debased the work of their elder superiors is one of the many indignities heaped upon the Sabbat in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting thought I had is the problem of the Sabbat and the Technocracy is the fact that both of them run into the fact that if you make them too nuanced, they essentially are no longer the group they are meant to be. It also brings the question as to why they're doing what they're doing in the game.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat was created, essentially, to fill the vacancy of the vampires who are complete pieces of shit. A vampire historically is a monster that does that scene in NEAR DARK where the family goes into a bar, terrorises everyone, kills them, and gorges themselves. You can't do that under the rules of Humanity so an entire system was created just so they can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mKacEeyjhiA\" data-code=\"mKacEeyjhiA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mKacEeyjhiA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The more you focus on giving the Sabbat nuance, depth, and reasons for their evil -- all good things in storytelling, you run the risk of forgetting one thing, &quot;These are still the people that will go into a bar and murder everyone just for shits and giggles.&quot; You can't lose sight of that element even if you <i><b>kind of want to.</b></i><br /> <br /> Part of the issue the Technocracy ran into is the Revised Convention books showed them as heroes and just a different philosophical perspective. Except the past 20 years have been filled with ample evidence that the REAL Masters of the world are a bunch of power-hungry assholes who want to kill the poor and brown people. So either the Technocracy wants to kill the poor or they don't control the world.<br /> <br /> It's not that banal scummy evil is unrealistic, it's just that it's very rare that it's INTERESTING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:21:48-08:00","id":1439245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439239#post1439239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an example of nuance... in my campaign the Prince and most of the elders hover around a Humanity 5; they don't try to kill mortals, but accidents happen and the Prince spends considerable capitol on cleaning those up in as least disruptive a way as possible. A few of the old guard (including the previous Prince who &quot;retired&quot; to focus on his own pursuits) and the Scourge are humanity 4 and no one likes dealing with them. By contrast the Sheriff is up at Humanity 6; he doesn't like accidents, largely because he and his people deal with cleaning them up first hand. There's also a couple of other elders in the 6-7 range and one who's even an 8 (a bagger who protects thinbloods and mentors talented mortal artists as a way of using his immortality to improve the world).<br /> <br /> So, in other words; there's a variety and range and each has different assets and desires and its up to the PCs to figure them out and which they make allies of and which become enemies.<br /> <br /> ETA: So apparently CTPhipps really is a one-note &quot;everyone's a bad guy&quot; sort of GM. Good for him, but something many find abhorrent and have no interest in playing. Great news though... I can run/play the way my players enjoy and Phipps can play his and life is grand.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's what you've got from it then I'm sorry. I don't think you'd have fun at my 20 year long gaming group. I feel like we've done some fantastic deep and epic storytelling you don't seem like you'd appreciate.<br /> <br /> But you do you. I'm sure you have a game you enjoy and that's all that matters.<br /> <br /> Having fun.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I am curious, though, what sort of &quot;Good Guy&quot; vampires exist in your game and what kind of dealing with the Beast/Frenzy/Hunger they have. How often are they tempted to do evil with their powers and the Blood Bond?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:24:08-08:00","id":1439246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439232#post1439232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluntly, I don't believe that player characters should ever be the GOOD guys in Vampire games. They can certainly TRY but a large part of what makes the game good is they're usually the lesser evil and possessed of their own terrible violent flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>That helps to put your views about the game in context. I agree with you, to an extent -- every <i>Vampire</i> character should be morally compromised in some manner, simply because that's a great way to generate conflict. When you keep stressing how Always Chaotic Evil the Elders are, it's easy to get the impression that they're only there as foils for the good guy player characters, but since that's not what you are saying, we're much more in agreement about the basics than it would seem at first blush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:27:10-08:00","id":1439247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439246#post1439246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That helps to put your views about the game in context. I agree with you, to an extent -- every <i>Vampire</i> character should be morally compromised in some manner, simply because that's a great way to generate conflict. When you keep stressing how Always Chaotic Evil the Elders are, it's easy to get the impression that they're only there as foils for the good guy player characters, but since that's not what you are saying, we're much more in agreement about the basics than it would seem at first blush.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I meant.<br /> <br /> I love the Anarchs but Mark Rein Hagen made it clear in the literal first group of NPCs that they're just as much a bunch of assholes as the Camarilla too.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean, JUGGLER is the first Anarch we ever meet. Fledglings are mostly decent because they haven't had centuries to grind down their idealism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:47:44-08:00","id":1439253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439244#post1439244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An interesting thought I had is the problem of the Sabbat and the Technocracy is the fact that both of them run into the fact that if you make them too nuanced, they essentially are no longer the group they are meant to be. It also brings the question as to why they're doing what they're doing in the game.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat was created, essentially, to fill the vacancy of the vampires who are complete pieces of shit. A vampire historically is a monster that does that scene in NEAR DARK where the family goes into a bar, terrorises everyone, kills them, and gorges themselves. You can't do that under the rules of Humanity so an entire system was created just so they can.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The more you focus on giving the Sabbat nuance, depth, and reasons for their evil -- all good things in storytelling, you run the risk of forgetting one thing, &quot;These are still the people that will go into a bar and murder everyone just for shits and giggles.&quot; You can't lose sight of that element even if you <i><b>kind of want to.</b></i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thing is 'being a complete pos' and 'having interesting and complex motives, that can ask interesting questions' aren't mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:48:36-08:00","id":1439254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439244#post1439244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat was created, essentially, to fill the vacancy of the vampires who are complete pieces of shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was certainly their function in 1st Edition, when they essentially had no writeup of their own, only a couple of paragraphs that amounted to Here There Be Assholes. But even in the 1st Edition core, the text said that most Camarilla vampires simply don't know much about the Sabbat, and could just as well be wrong about everything. And they <i>were</i> wrong, to an extent, as <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat</i> showed a year later.<br /> <br /> Was that a retcon of the Sabbat's function? Or simply an expansion of the setting? Does the game absolutely <i>need</i> an entire sect of vampires who are complete pieces of shit? These are not facetious questions -- the answers are genuinely for each Storyteller to decide for themselves. I absolutely do not mind a nuanced, playable Sabbat or Technocracy, myself. The Sabbat presented in <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat</i> can still have the exact same function in a Camarilla game they had from the start.<br /> <br /> I would only challenge your suggestion that the Paths of Enlightenment were created solely as a hack for inflexible Humanity rules. The game originally had perfectly functional, suave, well-dressed zero Humanity vampires, as you well know if you're a fan of the original <i>Chicago by Night.</i> As a Storyteller, you can always just say that your NPC has Humanity 0 but isn't a ravening monster, because the needs of an NPC are completely different from those of a player character. A zero Humanity character was not originally unsuited for players because they had become a <i>28 Days Later</i> zombie, but because <i>they no longer had any inner conflict</i> about who they were. The Paths of Enlightenment were a way to restore inner conflict to Sabbat characters, who were originally envisioned as all having zero Humanity. That's an elegant expansion of the game's concepts, not a crude hack for Humanity rules that should, in my opinion, only apply to PCs anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:26:02-08:00","id":1439364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439156#post1439156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been reading V1 again, and unintentional killing was a Humanity 6 sin. Outright murder was Humanity 2. But the Hierarchy of Sins was more a suggestion back then, rather than a hard code. Those were given as examples and the ST was supposed to invent their own.<br /> <br /> You may be happy with the Sabbat book, however, as my reading of this latest V5 development blog suggests the Paths will be introduced as alternate splats in that book: <a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/development-blog-defining-clans&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news...defining-clans</a> (where Paths are compared to Clans and Tribes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's just say I hate that blog post with every fiber of my being and leave it at that. TOS being what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:40:21-08:00","id":1439366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439364#post1439364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's just say I hate that blog post with every fiber of my being and leave it at that. TOS being what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full respect, Taggie.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Sabbat book will be great for you because while we both love the Sabbat, Justin Achilli the mind behind Revised is the new Prince in town.<br /> <br /> He is TOTES going to make the Revised Sabbat for V5.<br /> <br /> I'm calling it now.<br /> <br /> I do think Paths will be returning, though, which is necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:42:51-08:00","id":1439367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439366#post1439366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Full respect, Taggie.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Sabbat book will be great for you because while we both love the Sabbat, Justin Achilli the mind behind Revised is the new Prince in town.<br /> <br /> He is TOTES going to make the Revised Sabbat for V5.<br /> <br /> I'm calling it now.<br /> <br /> I do think Paths will be returning, though, which is necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you knowI think Dracula has as much place in defining the Tzimisce as the gollywog do in defining gangrel, for.tne same reason ! I didn't used to realize how hugely racist and offensive he was until some slav friends explained it, so anecdotal but I will take their word for it. And in universe he was regarded as a.joke, a failure and a.freak, not core clan identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:46:08-08:00","id":1439368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439367#post1439367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you knowI think Dracula has as much place in defining the Tzimisce as the gollywog do in defining gangrel, for.tne same reason</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you do think that an anti-fascist horror monster is a racist caricature versus a deliberate anachronism.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I am suspicious of any attempts to lionize nationalist ethnostate dictators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:50:38-08:00","id":1439369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439368#post1439368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you do think that an anti-fascist horror monster is a racist caricature versus a deliberate anachronism.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I am suspicious of any attempts to lionize nationalist ethnostate dictators.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll grant that maybe additional works and context change the narrative of the original novel, but they almost don't matter, because they are not what the majority of people think of when they hear the name, the core novel and (more likely) the movies are and in most of them we have Victorian racist stereotypes writ large (some times with added red scare)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:59:22-08:00","id":1439373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439369#post1439369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll grant that maybe additional works and context change the narrative of the original novel, but they almost don't matter, because they are not what the majority of people think of when they hear the name, the core novel and (more likely) the movies are and in most of them we have Victorian racist stereotypes writ large (some times with added red scare)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware of what people made of it.<br /> <br /> However, the fact is that the novel itself takes numerous pot shots and insults at British society as well as forwards a anti-Imperial narrative.<br /> <br /> Because the British people are helpless and its a &quot;New Woman&quot; working class woman and an American Cowboy with a Dutch scientist versus the Anti-Christ.<br /> <br /> Notably, the novel also makes it clear that Dracula is from a dead lineage. This is a mistake on Stoker's part because Dracula has a shit ton of descendants [matrineal lines only now] but the point was that he was a guy from a long fallen nobility that had no relationship to existing bloodlines because he was meant to be a cartoon villain, not a commentary on existing royal houses.<br /> <br /> He's not a representative of a living lineage, he's meant to be a guy who lives in a literal abandoned castle.<br /> <br /> The interpretation of it being British white imperialism vs. ancient Eastern superstition is a product of the movies given that, again, the book takes constant pot shots at the British. Probably because Stoker was Irish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:05:46-08:00","id":1439376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439373#post1439373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I'm aware of what people made of it.<br /> <br /> However, the fact is that the novel itself takes numerous pot shots and insults at British society as well as forwards a anti-Imperial narrative.<br /> <br /> Because the British people are helpless and its a &quot;New Woman&quot; working class woman and an American Cowboy with a Dutch scientist versus the Anti-Christ.<br /> <br /> Notably, the novel also makes it clear that Dracula is from a dead lineage. This is a mistake on Stoker's part because Dracula has a shit ton of descendants [matrineal lines only now] but the point was that he was a guy from a long fallen nobility that had no relationship to existing bloodlines because he was meant to be a cartoon villain, not a commentary on existing royal houses.<br /> <br /> He's not a representative of a living lineage, he's meant to be a guy who lives in a literal abandoned castle.<br /> <br /> The interpretation of it being British white imperialism vs. ancient Eastern superstition is a product of the movies given that, again, the book takes constant pot shots at the British. Probably because Stoker was Irish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death of the Author. What he meant to achieve is difficult from what his character represents (Shakespeare with Shylock is the quickest comparison, he meant the 'Do I not bleed' speech, and the characters love of family, to be humanising and relatable, that isn't what happened)<br /> <br /> Yet WW decided to turn what had been a weird sideline regarded as a failure by his clanmates and basically living in exile, to the core identity of the clan l, throwing out all the Mysticism and transhumanism, whilr changing the discipline spread to make most of that either impossible or pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:10:12-08:00","id":1439378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439376#post1439376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death of the Author. What he meant to achieve is difficult from what his character represents (Shakespeare with Shylock is the quickest comparison, he meant the 'Do I not bleed' speech, and the characters love of family, to be humanising and relatable, that isn't what happened)</div> </div> </div> </div>True but I also don't blame Nietszche for what others made of his works.<br /> <br /> Either way, what I like about the Tzimisce isn't that they're european. It's that they're FEUDAL and I think that makes them interesting whether they're Hungarian, Spanish, Japanese [we have confirmed Tzimsice in Tokyo], or the American guy who runs an apartment building.<br /> <br /> I am VERY biased because one of my first Sabbat characters was a Tzimisce who owned an apartment building where every single person was his slave and he used surveillance cameras to keep them under watch at all times. Oddly enough inspired by the music video for &quot;Hungry Eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-rati