humbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2ssCL292DQA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And yes, I admit, my opinion in the Modern Day is &quot;Fuck Feudalism!&quot; But autocratic all controlling vampires obsessed with their slaves is a good archetype for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Tzim have either been post humanist thinkers, mystics of flesh and bone or body horror mad scientists. None of those themes work any more, and none of them are welcome. Vykos, the poster childe of the Clan, doesn't function at all with the new Tzim setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:53:56-08:00","id":1439387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439385#post1439385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Tzim have either been post humanist thinkers, mystics of flesh and bone or body horror mad scientists. None of those themes work any more, and none of them are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?<br /> <br /> Serious question.<br /> <br /> or it just the Humanity thing and not the Tzimisce write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-12-2021, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T23:06:42-08:00","id":1439388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439226#post1439226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'd put Dracula (If I have to) On Road of Kings, or maybe Chivalry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Renfield (his Blood Bound Thrall or Ghoul, of course) referred to Enoch (saying that he feels like Enoch before he ascended to Heaven), he seems more like a possible Noddist to me. This also explains his callousness and tormenting of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-12-2021, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T23:10:59-08:00","id":1439389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439388#post1439388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Renfield (his Blood Bound Thrall or Ghoul, of course) referred to Enoch (saying he feels like Enoch before he ascended to Heaven), he seems more like a possible Noddist to me. This also explains his callousness and tormenting of mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Book Dracula?<br /> <br /> I'd go full, &quot;Path of Evil Revelations&quot; since he studied at the Scholomance.<br /> <br /> V:TM Dracula seems a much nicer guy and I'd put him on the Road of Chivalry having had a REALLY bad time of it in Stoker's book and possibly Mina relating it to them with considerable bias.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T23:15:10-08:00","id":1439390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439387#post1439387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you figure?<br /> <br /> Serious question.<br /> <br /> or it just the Humanity thing and not the Tzimisce write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Tzimisce write up and new discipline spread (Paths in some form being either a given, or just ignoring the morality system). Disciplines and weaknesses explain vampire stereotypes: Why do Ventrue create herds? Because prey limitations, and easy mind control make that the best option for them. Why do Toreador love art? Because Auspex and Fascination make it their crack, Why do Nosferatu spy? Because they cannot blend normally due to the curse, but Animalism and Obfuscate make finding information easy, and that role is always needed etc etc.<br /> <br /> Sure you can play against those stereotypes, but the Weakness and Disciplines act to 'force' you back onto type.<br /> <br /> That brings us to the Tzimisce: Why do Tzimisce make war ghouls and revnant families? Because they don't have mind control any other way so use this inefficient and weak method. Why are Tzimisce so bonded to a haven? Weakness, Animalism and Auspex synergise into a mystic link with home, by object read, by spirit sight, by the very soil and bricks talking to them, and the beasts paying them homage. Now that is gone. Replaced by the same old same old High Clan mind control. Only a complete idiot would make war ghouls now, or waste the time on revenant families, only the deranged talk to the spirits now. All that is gone.<br /> <br /> All that is left is the wannabe ventrue Dracula imitator. The weaknesses and write up are laser focused on that, any other idea is badwrongfun. (Seriously read the related twitter thread, they practically issue bad fake accents)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T01:42:00-08:00","id":1439402,"title":"","content":"I'm sympathetic to the overall point that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> is making, and I agree that the original Tzimisce clan disciplines better represented what the Fiends as written <i>were</i> (the Wamphyri clan) rather than what a subset of players seems to have <i>wanted</i> them to be (the Dracula clan).<br /> <br /> But at the same time, I cannot help but feel like maybe the decision to bump up the costs of purchasing and raising disciplines across the board made out-of-clan disciplines too onerous for most players to consider. In 1st Edition, discipline costs used to be current level \u00d73 for clan disciplines and \u00d75 for other disciplines, rather than the \u00d75 and \u00d77 that most players are used to.<br /> <br /> I feel like even with the original clan discipline spread, it should be relatively easy for Tzimisce characters to pick up a few levels of Dominate if they so choose. Certainly the Tzimisce who are powerful enough to make war ghouls and cultivate revenant families would have enough experience to buy basic Dominate dots many times over? The reasoning that the clan must make do with &quot;inefficient&quot; methods of control because they don't &quot;have&quot; Dominate doesn't quite ring true to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T01:46:31-08:00","id":1439403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439402#post1439402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sympathetic to the overall point that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> is making, and I agree that the original Tzimisce clan disciplines better represented what the Fiends as written <i>were</i> (the Wamphyri clan) rather than what a subset of players seems to have <i>wanted</i> them to be (the Dracula clan).<br /> <br /> But at the same time, I cannot help but feel like maybe the decision to bump up the costs of purchasing and raising disciplines across the board made out-of-clan disciplines too onerous for most players to consider. In 1st Edition, discipline costs used to be current level \u00d73 for clan disciplines and \u00d75 for other disciplines, rather than the \u00d75 and \u00d77 that most players are used to.<br /> <br /> I feel like even with the original clan discipline spread, it should be relatively easy for Tzimisce characters to pick up a few levels of Dominate if they so choose. Certainly the Tzimisce who are powerful enough to make war ghouls and cultivate revenant families would have enough experience to buy basic Dominate dots many times over? The reasoning that the clan must make do with &quot;inefficient&quot; methods of control because they don't &quot;have&quot; Dominate doesn't quite ring true to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who would they have learned Dominate from? They were at war with the Tremere, and rivals of the Ventrue and Lasombra, and Malkavians,,well if you DID have Dominate, why would you teach other Tzimisce? Learning out of clan used to be a huge deal. Except for the physical ones (At least in games I played)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T02:04:29-08:00","id":1439404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439403#post1439403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would they have learned Dominate from? They were at war with the Tremere, and rivals of the Ventrue and Lasombra, and Malkavians,,well if you DID have Dominate, why would you teach other Tzimisce? Learning out of clan used to be a huge deal. Except for the physical ones (At least in games I played)</div> </div> </div> </div>Different expectations at different tables, I suppose. I've never been a fan of the idea that any of the original 10 disciplines, with the possible exception of Thaumaturgy, are particularly hard to get a hold of. There are a ton of Tzimisce characters in the books with Dominate -- basically all of the infamous Tzimisce NPCs in the game have at least a couple of dots in the discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T02:19:07-08:00","id":1439405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439404#post1439404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different expectations at different tables, I suppose. I've never been a fan of the idea that any of the original 10 disciplines, with the possible exception of Thaumaturgy, are particularly hard to get a hold of. There are a ton of Tzimisce characters in the books with Dominate -- basically all of the infamous Tzimisce NPCs in the game have at least a couple of dots in the discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True the Voivodes do, but those are the Voivodes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, or they are Sabbat Bishops, the Sabbat is slightly better about instruction in out of clan than the Cam were, and the Anarchs are freer than both but the basic assumption I usually see is out of clan will cost you favors, concessions etc to get, and you have to really be concerned about the price. But ymmv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T03:09:58-08:00","id":1439410,"title":"","content":"It's easy enough to let a subset of Tzimisce learn Auspex in place of Dominate. The only issue then is Vicissitude, as it's been forced into a Dominate/Protean amalgam. <br /> <br /> I'd fix that by making it an Animalism/Protean amalgam. Animalism is the Discipline for controlling the Beast anyway, so that seems more appropriate, as the exterior body is shaped in a way that better reflects the Beast within.<br /> <br /> There's something appropriate about the inner self and outer body both becoming more monstrous and/or alien, as the Tzimisce manipulates your flesh and base urges to transform you into something horrific. Because Vicissitude tortures your mind and soul as much as your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T03:18:52-08:00","id":1439415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439410#post1439410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy enough to let a subset of Tzimisce learn Auspex in place of Dominate. The only issue then is Vicissitude, as it's been forced into a Dominate/Protean amalgam.</div> </div> </div> </div>if you're going to give tzimisce auspex instead of dominate you might as well make vis an auspex/protean amalgam (or just throw out the amalgam system as a replacement for clan abilities entirely since they fucked it up with both the ravnos and salubri anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T05:58:21-08:00","id":1439430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439385#post1439385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My Tzim have either been post humanist thinkers, mystics of flesh and bone or body horror mad scientists. None of those themes work any more, and none of them are welcome. Vykos, the poster childe of the Clan, doesn't function at all with the new Tzim setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree that preternatural awareness and knowledge fit the clan lore and history better than simple, straight-up mind control, but for me, what un-Tzimisces the Nu-Tzimisce more than anything else is the Compulsion. It reads like a 2nd Ed Ravnos vice. Far too rude and crass for Tzimisce, and it feels counter to their Merit of Membership: Old World Hospitality...until I get a wild hair across it and decide to steal your shit.<br /> <br /> Side-note concerning Amalgams: I get that they were trying to flavor certain Discipline levels per Clan, but I feel that if you want to do away with clan-specific Disciplines for streamlining purposes, maybe don\u2019t try to shoe-horn clan-specific powers back in via extraneous gamey mechanics. Doesn\u2019t feel like a happy medium and I think they can be comfortably ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:15:23-08:00","id":1439437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439415#post1439415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> if you're going to give tzimisce auspex instead of dominate you might as well make vis an auspex/protean amalgam (or just throw out the amalgam system as a replacement for clan abilities entirely since they fucked it up with both the ravnos and salubri anyway)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you give all Tzimisce Auspex, that's the way to do it. If it's just an alternate Clan Discipline (like Dominate Malkavians), then it would need to be an amalgam all Tzimisce could access, and Animalism would then be the shared Discipline besides Protean. <br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't have given them Protean at all. I would have kept Vicissitude or made it a collection of Blood Sorcery Rituals. I agree with others that it becomes tortuous when you try to squeeze everything back into a select few Disciplines, which negates the whole point of getting rid of the rarer Disciplines in the first place. But my suggestion was specifically for what to do within a V5 ruleset, even if it's not a ruleset I use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T12:46:15-08:00","id":1439498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439404#post1439404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different expectations at different tables, I suppose. I've never been a fan of the idea that any of the original 10 disciplines, with the possible exception of Thaumaturgy, are particularly hard to get a hold of. There are a ton of Tzimisce characters in the books with Dominate -- basically all of the infamous Tzimisce NPCs in the game have at least a couple of dots in the discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. In my first tabletop games, the standard Disciplines were assumed to be learned by anyone except special things like Thaumaturgy. We even treated Protean the same way.<br /> <br /> However, once the non-Camarilla clans and bloodlines were introduced with their own specialty Discipline, it suddenly became an issue of who could learn them. Then people started saying Disciplines could not be learn without a teacher except the in-clans that were &quot;inherent.&quot; That was doubled downed in LARP games where certain Disciplines were much more valuable in that context than other Disciplines. Soon everyone had those Disciplines which really negated the feel of each clan being different. So barriers were put in place (which were quickly overcome because LARP involves putting 12-30 people into a confined space together, so you quickly find people who swap Disciplines.)<br /> <br /> Unique Disciplines created an issue that didn't exist before because those Disciplines were presented as unique to those clans and unknown outside them, or at least outside the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T13:05:01-08:00","id":1439501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439402#post1439402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sympathetic to the overall point that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> is making, and I agree that the original Tzimisce clan disciplines better represented what the Fiends as written <i>were</i> (the Wamphyri clan) rather than what a subset of players seems to have <i>wanted</i> them to be (the Dracula clan).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this encapsulates the entire issue. You either want Wamphyri style vampires in your game, or you don't. Unfortunately, the depiction of Wamphyri in Necroscope is really alien to the legendry of Vampire as originally written. I am all about toolbox approaches, and the original Discipline and Umbral Disease angle is a good way to shoehorn that into the game, but it creates problems if you just don't want to have Wamphyri in your game either because you don't like them or think this shoehorning creates its own problems. (And I think many people don't as we've seen various attempts by the game to slowly remove those influences from the game, beginning with Revised eliminating the umbral disease angle.)<br /> <br /> If you want Wamphyri, then the original Tzimisce are great. I totally understand that.<br /> <br /> I don't so I eliminated all the Necroscope style stuff from my chronicles a LONG time ago. No Vicissitude. I gave the Tzimisce Protean and moved on. All my players liked that because none of us liked Wamphyri style vampires. As ST, I can make any adjustments to history or characters or with Merits/Flaws as needed to accommodate that.<br /> <br /> But that is harder in the published setting because canon is out there, and the Tzimisce and Vicissitude are an old part of the game and a very recognizable part of it. You have to deal with continuity in that case. You just can't say that is Earth-1 where Vicissitude exists, but our game now takes place on Earth-2 where it doesn't. Fans get upset as we clearly see.<br /> <br /> Instead what we have is a strange hybrid, where Vicissitude has to exist because its canon, but is treated like a red headed step child that the setting wants to ignore.<br /> <br /> At least, that is my impression because I only have these forums to go by - I don't buy V5 products.<br /> <br /> I think what would be best is to keep the lore as is, but in some sourcebook as an optional rule/variant setting, give rules for non-Vicissitude Tzimisce more like Dracula and provide a revised history that takes it into account. That way both groups are satisfied, but you acknowledge it's a different setting if you get rid of Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T13:13:15-08:00","id":1439502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439501#post1439501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what would be best is to keep the lore as is, but in some sourcebook as an optional rule/variant setting, give rules for non-Vicissitude Tzimisce more like Dracula and provide a revised history that takes it into account. That way both groups are satisfied, but you acknowledge it's a different setting if you get rid of Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's kinda what V5 did by making vis an amalgam of dominate/protean (not the alternate lore)<br /> <br /> and if i recall correctly old clan tzimisce rejected vis so there already are tzimisce without vis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T13:31:55-08:00","id":1439503,"title":"","content":"only at a cursory glance do 'unique disciplines' pose a problem. <br /> .<br /> First off, while powerful, unique disciplines are very much specialist powers that you are going to use less than more general, commonly available powers. Obtenebration and Chimestry for example are expensive to use and come with considerable drawbacks like how obviously supernatural Obten is and how Chimestry becomes a lot less effective when they know you have it. Meanwhile, most of the common disciplines are cheap in blood and willpower (ignoring v5) mostly dont fuck the masquerade (not including protean). The common disciplines are just broadly applicable and are going to be used all the time. The rare disciplines just shouldn't , and investing in rare disciplines takes your xp away from the generalist powers. Remember, In nature, generalists trump specialists. <br /> <br /> Secondly, you should consider how disciplines are cultivated. Ignoring V5 and out-of touch ideas about resonnances, we only have the basis that out of clan disciplines need a tutor for the first dot (sorcery excluded) and that discipines, like all other abilities, improve as you use them. But what does that actually mean for rare disciplines? for chimestry, you're burning through your own will and trying to believe your own lies. For Viscissitude and Quietus, you're getting quite a body count. For Obtenebration, you're sitting in a dark corner, sacrificing vast amounts of blood and making contact with a malevolent alien dimension. These are not the actions of a mentally or socially healthy person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T13:41:41-08:00","id":1439504,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think that no vampire should just have Clan Disciplines as their only Disciplines by the time they hit Ancilla. The idea of Revenant families as substitutes for Dominate is a weird post-factor justification when I think the reason they had Revenant families was BECAUSE they had Vicissitude and Thaumaturgy. They were already interested in the ability to warp the flesh and use weird magical energies to enhance people so of course they'd create a better class of servant.<br /> <br /> Auspex doesn't help that.<br /> <br /> DOMINATE does help in controlling your newly enhanced super-soldiers.<br /> <br /> Honestly, on my end I would have made Tzimisce have Protean [change self] and Vicisstiude be a Blood Sorcery/Protean combo to change OTHERS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:04:22-08:00","id":1439566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439504#post1439504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think that no vampire should just have Clan Disciplines as their only Disciplines by the time they hit Ancilla. The idea of Revenant families as substitutes for Dominate is a weird post-factor justification when I think the reason they had Revenant families was BECAUSE they had Vicissitude and Thaumaturgy. They were already interested in the ability to warp the flesh and use weird magical energies to enhance people so of course they'd create a better class of servant.<br /> <br /> Auspex doesn't help that.<br /> <br /> DOMINATE does help in controlling your newly enhanced super-soldiers.<br /> <br /> Honestly, on my end I would have made Tzimisce have Protean [change self] and Vicisstiude be a Blood Sorcery/Protean combo to change OTHERS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flat disagree. You control your pathetic revenants and war ghouls (and they are terrible, we have their stats) with fear and blood oath, because you don't have anything better, they aren't a tool anyone with a choice would use. Which is why no one with Dominate would.ever make any, they do have better options. Given how truly bad Viscittitude is now, and that you can't actually have all of the powers, even if you wanted to, why they had to add insult to injury by turning the entire clan into two dimensional caricatures as well.. I simply don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-12-2021, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:07:17-08:00","id":1439568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439566#post1439566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flat disagree. You control your pathetic revenants and war ghouls (and they are terrible, we have their stats) with fear and blood oath, because you don't have anything better, they aren't a tool anyone with a choice would use. Which is why no one with Dominate would.ever make any, they do have better options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfft.<br /> <br /> Who WOULDN'T want an army of monsters?<br /> <br /> The Silence of Blood is for weaklings!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:23:26-08:00","id":1439571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439568#post1439568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pfft.<br /> <br /> Who WOULDN'T want an army of monsters?<br /> <br /> The Silence of Blood is for weaklings!</div> </div> </div> </div>Rule of cool is not a survival trait","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:33:36-08:00","id":1439574,"title":"","content":"Sometimes what is the most powerful or most useful isn\u2019t the coolest. The Tzimisce having to use ghouls, including revenant families, rather than use Dominate isn\u2019t optimal but it\u2019s cool because it fits in with their theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:51:01-08:00","id":1439576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439574#post1439574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes what is the most powerful or most useful isn\u2019t the coolest. The Tzimisce having to use ghouls, including revenant families, rather than use Dominate isn\u2019t optimal but it\u2019s cool because it fits in with their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, to go a bit further, too powerful is definitely not cool. With the ability to control armies of beasts (and Beasts) as well as Nosferatu and Gangrel, control mortals and their institutions as well as any Lasombra and Ventrue, and wield the fearsome natural weaponry of Protean and Vicissitude both as in-clan cost (while nerfed in V5, Feral Weapons and Horrid Form are still fairly formidable), I have to wonder why Tzimisce ever needed Lasombra in the Sabbat...or why they aren't the ultimate clan in modern nights, for that matter.<br /> <br /> I know we're not supposed to worry about clan lore any more, but for me, reading the lore is one of the more interested facets to choosing a clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","user":"Garygeneric","date":". 03-12-2021, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T19:16:38-08:00","id":1439581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439574#post1439574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes what is the most powerful or most useful isn\u2019t the coolest. The Tzimisce having to use ghouls, including revenant families, rather than use Dominate isn\u2019t optimal but it\u2019s cool because it fits in with their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I point out they can do both.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Tremere have a Revenant Family after all. Also, THE OLD CLAN TZIMISCE already had Revenants AND Dominate. Remember, the Tzimisce who made the Revenant Families weren't the dirty-dirty Vicisstude Infectees.<br /> <br /> The idea of the Vicissitude Tzimisce being the original Tzimisce is an idea from Revised.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan (With Dominate) originally created the Revenants.<br /> <br /> Also, in addition to the Tremere, the Old Clan brought their ghoul families to the True Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T20:08:52-08:00","id":1439584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439576#post1439576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, to go a bit further, too powerful is definitely not cool. With the ability to control armies of beasts (and Beasts) as well as Nosferatu and Gangrel, control mortals and their institutions as well as any Lasombra and Ventrue, and wield the fearsome natural weaponry of Protean and Vicissitude both as in-clan cost (while nerfed in V5, Feral Weapons and Horrid Form are still fairly formidable), I have to wonder why Tzimisce ever needed Lasombra in the Sabbat...or why they aren't the ultimate clan in modern nights, for that matter.<br /> <br /> I know we're not supposed to worry about clan lore any more, but for me, reading the lore is one of the more interested facets to choosing a clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think that this new combination is really that overpowered. I mean sure, it\u2019s useful but lots of combinations of Disciplines can be. With Dominate, they do step on the Lasombra\u2019s toes a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439581#post1439581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I point out they can do both.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Tremere have a Revenant Family after all. Also, THE OLD CLAN TZIMISCE already had Revenants AND Dominate. Remember, the Tzimisce who made the Revenant Families weren't the dirty-dirty Vicisstude Infectees.<br /> <br /> The idea of the Vicissitude Tzimisce being the original Tzimisce is an idea from Revised.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan (With Dominate) originally created the Revenants.<br /> <br /> Also, in addition to the Tremere, the Old Clan brought their ghoul families to the True Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that is possible. I recall somebody on this forum recently suggested giving players the option of either Auspex, Dominate, or Sorcery as a Discipline to go with Animalism and Protean. I wouldn\u2019t object to that idea. Then again, you could just about do that same thing with any Clan. <br /> <br /> I think that my own preference might be Animalism, Sorcery, and Protean with some Vicissitude powers resulting from Sorcery + Protean. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve actually always been a big revenant fan, I think it might be neat to have revenant based factions within the Clan who have their family Discipline set instead of the standard Tzimisce one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T01:54:53-08:00","id":1439617,"title":"","content":"The Tzmisce were based on the nobility of eastern europe. Most of their Terminology comes from Polish (Note, Dracula fanboys, none of it comes from Romanian). One of the defining things of eastern nobility (specifically, the Poland-Lithuania commonwealth) was that they were relatively rich, while their serfs were relatively poor compared to the west. As the financial cost of warfare rose, Western Europe adapted by taking emphasis away from expensive knights and strengthening their non-noble infantry from levies to mostly-professional soldiers, which was cost effective, while poland could still afford ludicrusly expensive cavalry (the famed Winged Hussars) and didn't bother to improve their common soldiers. later, when east was fighting west, the westerners (particularly the swedes) could learn from the way poland used it's terrifying cavalry, but although the Polish admired and envied the better infantry of the west, they would not make reforms, because professional soldiers among their peasantry could become an uncontrollable threat to the rule of nobles. An increasingly obsolescent army with too much emphasis on very expensive and hard to replace units, and Poland's very decentralized nature as a commonwealth lead to it's downfall...<br /> <br /> Now, Poland here is the perfect metaphor for Tzmisce, and their immediate neighbours in the west' is, in vampire, literally dominated by Hardestardt the Ventrue and the Tremere. The Tmisce, like Poland and unlike the ventrue, never had a good grasp over it's commoners. and really hated centralized power. And The Tzmisce, again like historical poland, put a lot of emphasis on animals and a few very expensive creations (Fleshcrafted super-ghouls) and would never risk mass control (Dominate/Presence)<br /> <br /> <br /> RE- Ravnos<br /> Nobody fucking likes the Ravnos. That's half their deal. Giving them Presence implies they're likeable. They aren't, they're a public menace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T07:59:04-08:00","id":1439655,"title":"","content":"Martyn a.k.a Outstar offers a LOT of fascinating Polish insights onto the Tzimisce and their terminology during her Redemption playthrough.<br /> <br /> And she insists <b><i>she's</i></b> Toreador.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T09:06:03-08:00","id":1439674,"title":"","content":"The original concept of the Ravnos is such a mess, anything would be an improvement, and I think that V5 is for them. Also, nobody likes politicians yet they tend to be charismatic. A group can be known for being charismatic and yet disliked for what they do with that charisma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:39:35-08:00","id":1439693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439674#post1439674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original concept of the Ravnos is such a mess, anything would be an improvement, and I think that V5 is for them. Also, nobody likes politicians yet they tend to be charismatic. A group can be known for being charismatic and yet disliked for what they do with that charisma.</div> </div> </div> </div>i already explained that to you in another thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.