ing=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T15:24:35-08:00","id":1439728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439695#post1439695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, all the Ravnos I know are either Gambit or a bellydancer.<br /> <br /> My players are not imaginative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the few I see are now Loki or Coyote.... I kinda wanted them to lean into that Trickster asshole vibe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-13-2021, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T16:25:50-08:00","id":1439736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439728#post1439728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The few I see are now Loki or Coyote.... I kinda wanted them to lean into that Trickster asshole vibe...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of awkward because my Anarch Trickster illusionist was a Malkavian.<br /> <br /> He just had Dementation instead of Chimestry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:16:40-07:00","id":1439891,"title":"","content":"I've never seen the Ravnos archetype as likeable. They're generally <b>charming</b>, which is not the same thing, though it can have superficially similar effects on the people the charm is being used on. Onlookers who aren't the Ravnos' marks can definitely see the difference, though, and think less of both parties because of it.<br /> <br /> Should I get involved in a V5 ancillae-level game, the default character I'm bringing to the table is a Ravnos <i>antitribu</i> lupine hunter who makes the new clan weakness work with her vocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:19:57-07:00","id":1439892,"title":"","content":"I think v5 ravnos are a functional bloodline. But they arent the Ravnos, and I like the Ravnos. <br /> <br /> Obfuscate/Presence is seemingly the go to for the corruptors: setited, baali,a certain african lasombra bloodline. The Ravnos aren't them. The Ravnos arent 'corruptors' who cater to others: their whole shtick was having thick skin and a very self driven, defiant ethos. <br /> <br /> Presence is a discipline for the supremely likeable. Sure, we may resent the idea of the pompous Ventrue, the bitchy Toreador, The crude Brujah, or the... Settite oil sailsman, but when you actually meet these vampires, they're almost always immensely likeable or otherwise impressively magnetic. <br /> Just decieving people is not providence for in-clan Presence. You need special power, and the Ravnos have always been adverse to tying themselves to so many mortals for reasons of their curse and for their &quot;religion&quot; (path of Paradox says dont try Humanity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T03:01:11-07:00","id":1439994,"title":"","content":"Chimestry has always been about 'physical' illususions (made from an illusory substance) whilst obfuscate has been about mental tricks. This had a profound impact on their worldview and their perception of reality. <br /> <br /> The ravnos have always had this amazing spiral of - Compelled to do something bad &gt; self loathing and jealousy&gt; develop an ideology about how you're really fulfilling your unlife's purpose and how really humane vampires are just pieces of shit denying the reality they should be finding themselves in &gt; Do bad things on your own accord. <br /> <br /> But they also had this idea that, outside of fulfilling their own &quot;purpose&quot; they shouldnt be fucking with the destiny of mortals all that much. So Presence isn't really appropriate for them. Thus Animalism and Fortitude were really perfect for them; Animals not really having significant destinies makes them ok to manipulate on the regular and providing the lonely Ravnos comfort is very much beneficial, whilst Fortitude is... just the most obvious choice for someone who's living a hard life and constantly threatened with retribution. <br /> <br /> They're just far more interesting and well developed pre-v5 than post. Were it not for the unfortunate elephant-flaw of the gypsie baggage, there would be considerable outrage concerning the clan's replacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T05:54:07-07:00","id":1440015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1439994#post1439994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chimestry has always been about 'physical' illususions (made from an illusory substance) whilst obfuscate has been about mental tricks. This had a profound impact on their worldview and their perception of reality.<br /> <br /> The ravnos have always had this amazing spiral of - Compelled to do something bad &gt; self loathing and jealousy&gt; develop an ideology about how you're really fulfilling your unlife's purpose and how really humane vampires are just pieces of shit denying the reality they should be finding themselves in &gt; Do bad things on your own accord.<br /> <br /> But they also had this idea that, outside of fulfilling their own &quot;purpose&quot; they shouldnt be fucking with the destiny of mortals all that much. So Presence isn't really appropriate for them. Thus Animalism and Fortitude were really perfect for them; Animals not really having significant destinies makes them ok to manipulate on the regular and providing the lonely Ravnos comfort is very much beneficial, whilst Fortitude is... just the most obvious choice for someone who's living a hard life and constantly threatened with retribution.<br /> <br /> They're just far more interesting and well developed pre-v5 than post. Were it not for the unfortunate elephant-flaw of the gypsie baggage, there would be considerable outrage concerning the clan's replacement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. It is very clear that the only reason we see Presence here is because of the amalgam rules, and the fact that they couldn't find a way to combine their old disciplines to create the effects of Chimerstry. I think that in my games I will replace the requirement for Presence with Fortitude. In V5 Fortitude also makes the mind stronger and thus you know how to exploit the weakness in others, as you combine it with Obfuscate. Strong unnatural will and the ability to hide reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T06:08:32-07:00","id":1440017,"title":"","content":"There is also the game design perspective to consider. I think it's pretty obvious that the original 13 clans were assigned clan disciplines with maximum variety in mind, in addition to the usual considerations for what best supported the clan concepts. When you look at the disciplines shared between clans in 1st and 2nd Edition (ignoring proprietary disciplines), the following pattern emerges:<br /> <br /> 4 clans share Animalism<br /> 4 clans share Auspex<br /> 3 clans share Celerity<br /> 5 clans share Dominate<br /> 3 clans share Fortitude<br /> 4 clans share Obfuscate<br /> 4 clans share Potence<br /> 4 clans share Presence<br /> <br /> You can immediately see why Revised Edition chose to replace Dominate with Dementation for Malkavians, &quot;fixing&quot; the spreads so that only 4 clans share Dominate between them. When 4 is the maximum number of times a discipline is allowed to be shared between the clans, the result is a pretty even spread of disciplines among the various character options.<br /> <br /> I don't think the current crop of designers care as much about this kind of parity between the disciplines, which is why the V5 discipline spreads look a little more lopsided -- five clans share Dominate, Obfuscate, and Presence now. On the plus side, the drastically reduced number of proprietary disciplines means that Protean, for example, is shared by 3 clans, making it on par with Celerity and Potence in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T06:22:28-07:00","id":1440019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440017#post1440017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the game design perspective to consider. I think it's pretty obvious that the original 13 clans were assigned clan disciplines with maximum variety in mind, in addition to the usual considerations for what best supported the clan concepts. When you look at the disciplines shared between clans in 1st and 2nd Edition (ignoring proprietary disciplines), the following pattern emerges:<br /> <br /> 4 clans share Animalism<br /> 4 clans share Auspex<br /> 3 clans share Celerity<br /> 5 clans share Dominate<br /> 3 clans share Fortitude<br /> 4 clans share Obfuscate<br /> 4 clans share Potence<br /> 4 clans share Presence<br /> <br /> You can immediately see why Revised Edition chose to replace Dominate with Dementation for Malkavians, &quot;fixing&quot; the spreads so that only 4 clans share Dominate between them. When 4 is the maximum number of times a discipline is allowed to be shared between the clans, the result is a pretty even spread of disciplines among the various character options.<br /> <br /> I don't think the current crop of designers care as much about this kind of parity between the disciplines, which is why the V5 discipline spreads look a little more lopsided -- five clans share Dominate, Obfuscate, and Presence now. On the plus side, the drastically reduced number of proprietary disciplines means that Protean, for example, is shared by 3 clans, making it on par with Celerity and Potence in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>while that might be the case it doesn't really excuse things as they are in V5 because you can still do all that without amalgams. and even with amalgams some decisions still don't really work (like dominate on tzimisce or presence on ravnos)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 03-15-2021, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T06:30:11-07:00","id":1440020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440019#post1440019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> while that might be the case it doesn't really excuse things as they are in V5 because you can still do all that without amalgams. and even with amalgams some decisions still don't really work (like dominate on tzimisce or presence on ravnos)</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think that back in the day we had this bloodline Old Clan Tzimisce that had Auspex, Animalism, Dominate. No? they were like against the cult of Metamorphosis or something like that.<br /> It feels like they tried to combine the two aspects of the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T06:46:11-07:00","id":1440023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440020#post1440020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I think that back in the day we had this bloodline Old Clan Tzimisce that had Auspex, Animalism, Dominate. No? they were like against the cult of Metamorphosis or something like that.<br /> It feels like they tried to combine the two aspects of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's absolutely right but there was alot of flavor in the tzimisce that was lost by giving dominate to the base clan and even then dominate always felt like a filler discipline for the old clan who themselves were a bloodline that existed purely because they wanted tzimisce to be playable for ppl that didn't want to use visisitude (which isn't an issue in V5).<br /> <br /> i get what they were trying to do, i'm not claiming there was no thought put behind the decision, i'm saying they could've done alot better then what they choose to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T07:01:22-07:00","id":1440026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440020#post1440020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I think that back in the day we had this bloodline Old Clan Tzimisce that had Auspex, Animalism, Dominate. No? they were like against the cult of Metamorphosis or something like that.<br /> It feels like they tried to combine the two aspects of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Replacing Auspex with Dominate because a small faction had Dominate instead of Vicissitude isn\u2019t a great argument. It\u2019s like if they had the entire Ministry replacing Presence with Potence because Warrior Setites had Potence instead of Obfuscate. <br /> <br /> The whole Alamgam thing stems from wanting to homogenize Discipline content while trying to retain \u201cclan flavor.\u201d But it feels forced, like lore is being replaced by extraneous rules. Makes V:tM feel more theme park video game, less sandbox RPG.<br /> <br /> Imagine being forced to learn Dominate 2 (or literally any other Discipline for that matter) before you can get started on your Vicissitude career. That would be silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","user":"Garygeneric","date":". 03-15-2021, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T08:08:32-07:00","id":1440031,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with amalgams is that some Disciplines are round pegs being forced into two completely separate square holes. And in the end, because you can't purchase multiple powers of the same level, they end up being truncated versions of the old Disciplines anyway... So why not just have the old Disciplines to keep it simple?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T08:51:45-07:00","id":1440038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440031#post1440031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the end, because you can't purchase multiple powers of the same level, they end up being truncated versions of the old Disciplines anyway... So why not just have the old Disciplines to keep it simple?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really the crux of the issue. I never found the additional disciplines in the various supplements to be a problem, but there is an argument to be made for maintaining a small and coherent set of vampiric powers in a new edition of the game. Pick one approach or the other, though -- the current amalgam approach wants to have it both ways without really satisfying anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T08:55:41-07:00","id":1440041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440017#post1440017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the game design perspective to consider. I think it's pretty obvious that the original 13 clans were assigned clan disciplines with maximum variety in mind, in addition to the usual considerations for what best supported the clan concepts. When you look at the disciplines shared between clans in 1st and 2nd Edition (ignoring proprietary disciplines), the following pattern emerges:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is? I thought they were just going for archtypes; Liberal elite, Big-business elite, Country guy, Rabble rouser, Fixer, new-money professionals, and the Malkavians who belong as part of this but I can't quite articulate how. The Lasombra came in as psycho professionals, the Tzmisce as an archaic gentry/nobility, the Setites for cults, the assamites as assassins, and the giovanni came in to play happy family. The first seven clans were, quite smartly, very much -universal-, whilst the latter clans have a bit too much cultural baggage. Still, the clans felt like they were trying to encapsulate -types of people- and clan-as-archtype seems more prominent than -clans as character classes... maybe they just did well, but I never came to the thought that they were actively trying to balance how many clans had what discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T08:58:37-07:00","id":1440042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440038#post1440038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really the crux of the issue. I never found the additional disciplines in the various supplements to be a problem, but there is an argument to be made for maintaining a small and coherent set of vampiric powers in a new edition of the game. Pick one approach or the other, though -- the current amalgam approach wants to have it both ways without really satisfying anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think it could've worked to have a smaller discipline set and still have clan specific abilities, it's just amalgams are a terrible system for clan abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:08:17-07:00","id":1440045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440042#post1440042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i think it could've worked to have a smaller discipline set and still have clan specific abilities, it's just amalgams are a terrible system for clan abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would simply put in the description \u201cthis power is common to Clan X. Others may learn it from a Clan X tutor\u201d so that in-character roleplaying might be encouraged and rewarded, rather than \u201cin order to learn that, you first have to spend X number of month\u2019s worth of XP on a completely separate Discipline while you hold off learning any levels is that other Discipline.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:16:13-07:00","id":1440046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440041#post1440041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is? I thought they were just going for archtypes; Liberal elite, Big-business elite, Country guy, Rabble rouser, Fixer, new-money professionals, and the Malkavians who belong as part of this but I can't quite articulate how. The Lasombra came in as psycho professionals, the Tzmisce as an archaic gentry/nobility, the Setites for cults, the assamites as assassins, and the giovanni came in to play happy family. The first seven clans were, quite smartly, very much -universal-, whilst the latter clans have a bit too much cultural baggage. Still, the clans felt like they were trying to encapsulate -types of people- and clan-as-archtype seems more prominent than -clans as character classes... maybe they just did well, but I never came to the thought that they were actively trying to balance how many clans had what discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Gangrel. Who were weirdly associated with Travellers in 1e and 2e, while no other core clan had such ethnic connections until the other clans were published as Sabbat and Independents.<br /> <br /> Though even 1e said there were 13 Clans, so I think they must have planned some or all of the additional splats in advance. Perhaps their thinking was that the other six would be less numerous precisely because they were more parochial? I can see why that logic might have crept in, even if I don't agree with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:16:30-07:00","id":1440047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440045#post1440045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would simply put in the description \u201cthis power is common to Clan X. Others may learn it from a Clan X tutor\u201d so that in-character roleplaying might be encouraged and rewarded, rather than \u201cin order to learn that, you first have to spend X number of month\u2019s worth of XP on a completely separate Discipline while you hold off learning any levels is that other Discipline.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>it's also a much simpler system. the only issue then is that if you've already maxed out a discipline you cant learn it later but even then that could be solved by letting players learn multiple abilities per discipline dot or even just letting them switch out powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:16:41-07:00","id":1440048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440026#post1440026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole Alamgam thing stems from wanting to homogenize Discipline content while trying to retain \u201cclan flavor.\u201d But it feels forced, like lore is being replaced by extraneous rules. Makes V:tM feel more theme park video game, less sandbox RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think they\u2019d have been better served going the opposite direction and developed a unique discipline for each clan akin to how Dementation is a rather specific expression of Dominate with a bit of Auspex thrown in.<br /> <br /> Two-thirds of the work was already done; Assamite (Quietus), Setite (Serpentis), Ravnos (Chimerstry), Lasombra (Obtenebration), Giovanni/Hecata (Necromancy), Tzmisce (Vicissitude), Tremere (Thaumaturgy), Gangrel (Protean), Malkavian (Dementation)... leaving just Brujah, Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue.<br /> <br /> So develop, say, a clan-specific Brujah discipline that, say, replaces Potence with something that has more specialized applications of supernatural strength that perhaps overlap slightly with supernatural speed and presence... or a Ventrue discipline that is a Presence more focused on invoking obedience/loyalty reflecting Dominate and Fortitude (the influence is more resilient) leaking into it... or a Nosferatu discipline that\u2019s basically Animalism+ focusing on empowering animal servants through the use of vitae.<br /> <br /> This would be even easier in V5 given its focus on specific powers over a more holistic discipline approach (ex. how Chimerstry starts with static images and higher tiers add additional senses, motion and permanence).<br /> <br /> If the devs had gone that approach they probably could have skipped amalgam powers entirely and made the identity of each clan stronger via the unique discipline each possesed in addition to the other general disciplines, banes and compulsions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:22:28-07:00","id":1440051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440048#post1440048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I think they\u2019d have been better served going the opposite direction and developed a unique discipline for each clan akin to how Dementation is a rather specific expression of Dominate with a bit of Auspex thrown in.<br /> <br /> Two-thirds of the work was already done; Assamite (Quietus), Setite (Serpentis), Ravnos (Chimerstry), Lasombra (Obtenebration), Giovanni/Hecata (Necromancy), Tzmisce (Vicissitude), Tremere (Thaumaturgy), Gangrel (Protean), Malkavian (Dementation)... leaving just Brujah, Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue.<br /> <br /> So develop, say, a clan-specific Brujah discipline that, say, replaces Potence with something that has more specialized applications of supernatural strength that perhaps overlap slightly with supernatural speed and presence... or a Ventrue discipline that is a Presence more focused on invoking obedience/loyalty reflecting Dominate and Fortitude (the influence is more resilient) leaking into it... or a Nosferatu discipline that\u2019s basically Animalism+ focusing on empowering animal servants through the use of vitae.<br /> <br /> This would be even easier in V5 given its focus on specific powers over a more holistic discipline approach (ex. how Chimerstry starts with static images and higher tiers add additional senses, motion and permanence).<br /> <br /> If the devs had gone that approach they probably could have skipped amalgam powers entirely and made the identity of each clan stronger via the unique discipline each possesed in addition to the other general disciplines, banes and compulsions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the main reason they didn't was presumably because the system was getting to bloated with unique disciplines, especially when you throw in all the bloodline specific disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:25:48-07:00","id":1440053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440051#post1440051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> the main reason they didn't was presumably because the system was getting to bloated with unique disciplines, especially when you throw in all the bloodline specific disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, unique disciplines undermine the ability for players to do the character power spread they want to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:48:44-07:00","id":1440056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440053#post1440053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, unique disciplines undermine the ability for players to do the character power spread they want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does whatever v5 thinks it's doing. So many possibilities are crushed via -one power per turn- , amalgams, and in general V5 powers being unreasonably specific or otherwise less powerful. <br /> <br /> Personally, I just have a system of free synergistic powers to differentiate clans using their disciplines-. Essentially, free combination disciplines, but less specific. For instance, Brujah are absurdly mobile thanks to Celerity and Potence, and both have some strange combinations with presence. anyone can get these combinations, they're just less likely to have high levels of them . Someday I'll get out of the slump and muster the effort to make it all look nice and then release it to the public, but not today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:05:28-07:00","id":1440059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440053#post1440053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, unique disciplines undermine the ability for players to do the character power spread they want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reverse argument also holds true: my Animalism/Auspex/Vicissitude Tzimisce feel pretty undermined right now. <br /> <br /> Not to mention their own published NPCs. Erzulie, for example. Not only are her stats wrong now, but now that I think of it, the fact that it\u2019s considerably easier and cheaper for a Ventrue to learn Vicissitude than a Toreador feels completely wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:21:18-07:00","id":1440061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440059#post1440059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reverse argument also holds true: my Animalism/Auspex/Vicissitude Tzimisce feel pretty undermined right now.<br /> <br /> Not to mention their own published NPCs. Erzulie, for example. Not only are her stats wrong now, but now that I think of it, the fact that it\u2019s considerably easier and cheaper for a Ventrue to learn Vicissitude than a Toreador feels completely wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? I was surprised at how non-nerfed Vicissitude was. It seems like all their old powers are the same, just as Alternate Powers.<br /> <br /> As for Ventrue and Toreador: Previously you'd have to find a Sabbat to do it for you.<br /> <br /> Its now a much more common discipline I'd presume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:26:19-07:00","id":1440063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440061#post1440061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are they? I was surprised at how non-nerfed Vicissitude was. It seems like all their old powers are the same, just as Alternate Powers.<br /> <br /> As for Ventrue and Toreador: Previously you'd have to find a Sabbat to do it for you.<br /> <br /> Its now a much more common discipline I'd presume.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> he meant that toreador of the sabbath would learn vis because sculpting, however it's easier for a ventrue to learn vis it because it's dominate/protean instead of say auspex/protean which would be easier to learn by toreador.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:32:58-07:00","id":1440064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440063#post1440063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> he meant that toreador of the sabbath would learn vis because sculpting, however it's easier for a ventrue to learn vis it because it's dominate/protean instead of say auspex/protean which would be easier to learn by toreador.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah.<br /> <br /> Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:37:54-07:00","id":1440065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440061#post1440061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are they? I was surprised at how non-nerfed Vicissitude was. It seems like all their old powers are the same, just as Alternate Powers.<br /> <br /> As for Ventrue and Toreador: Previously you'd have to find a Sabbat to do it for you.<br /> <br /> Its now a much more common discipline I'd presume.</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally can\u2019t have the traditional Animalism, Auspex, Vicissitude line-up now. You not only need Dominate 2, but you need it first.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude being sect-locked made a lot more sense than being \u201cmore common, but cheaper for X Clan than Y Clan because of X Clan\u2019s other, completely separate Discipline that isn\u2019t Protean.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:48:54-07:00","id":1440067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440041#post1440041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, the clans felt like they were trying to encapsulate -types of people- and clan-as-archtype seems more prominent than -clans as character classes... maybe they just did well, but I never came to the thought that they were actively trying to balance how many clans had what discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting clan design from archetypes and keeping discipline parity in mind are not mutually exclusive design principles, like I suggested above. I think the common disciplines are simply too evenly spread out among the 13 clans in the original gameline for it to be a mere coincidence. It's very easy to end up with different results -- even some of the later official products that rejuggle the clan disciplines end up wildly imbalanced. For example, in the 20th Anniversary Edition of <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages,</i> six clans have Auspex in common, while only two clans share Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:53:56-07:00","id":1440069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440065#post1440065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You literally can\u2019t have the traditional Animalism, Auspex, Vicissitude line-up now. You not only need Dominate 2, but you need it first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advanced Vicissitude powers requiring more than a Neonates initial powers seems fair given how powerful the Discipline is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T11:02:25-07:00","id":1440072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440069#post1440069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Advanced Vicissitude powers requiring more than a Neonates initial powers seems fair given how powerful the Discipline is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is not 'advanced powers' Dominate is the requirement for having any powers at all. You have to destroy part of what made Tzim society make sense, to have their signature power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T11:10:13-07:00","id":1440074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440069#post1440069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Advanced Vicissitude powers requiring more than a Neonates initial powers seems fair given how powerful the Discipline is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vicissitude isn't anymore powerful than any common discipline like Animalism or Potence, and requires a lot of investment in skills you wouldn't normally use. <br /> Sure, you can mess someoneup real good with it, but you can mess someone's up with a lot of things. You don't need to spend XP (or blood) on most other methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T11:13:32-07:00","id":1440076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440069#post1440069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Advanced Vicissitude powers requiring more than a Neonates initial powers seems fair given how powerful the Discipline is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can roll up a fresh character with Protean 2 and Dominate 2 and start gameplay with Vicissitude. But you won\u2019t have Animalism and/or Auspex. Hell, if your ST allows neonate exp option at chargen, you can roll out with Protean 3, Dominate 2 and be a fleshcrafting maniac right out of the gate, so it\u2019s not a question of advanced powerz. It\u2019s that the traditional Tzimisce archetype feels almost prohibited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T00:16:35-07:00","id":1440155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440042#post1440042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i think it could've worked to have a smaller discipline set and still have clan specific abilities, it's just amalgams are a terrible system for clan abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just house rule that only the specific clan can take these powers without the amalgam requirement, and if someone out of the clan wishes to learn it make him just jump the usual hoops for learning out of clan power including the XP penalty. Nothing bad with homebrewing if something just doesn't add up. I did it with Desire and Ambition, it didn't work for us for 3 campaigns in a raw so I just took the Mask and Dirge from V:tR and it's great now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T01:27:57-07:00","id":1440164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440051#post1440051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the main reason they didn't was presumably because the system was getting to bloated with unique disciplines, especially when you throw in all the bloodline specific disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. But instead of a bloated number of overall Disciplines, organised in a straight line to make them easy to use (one dot to nine dots), now they have a bloated number of Discipline powers and amalgams that are organised as a web (sort of like Charm trees, which are a nightmare to navigate in Exalted, but here with more restrictions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440053#post1440053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, unique disciplines undermine the ability for players to do the character power spread they want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the exact opposite is true. By gating most unique powers behind amalgams and limiting PCs to one power per level, this is actually a way more restrictive system that presents the illusion of freedom. As others have said, it's now impossible to have some combinations of powers, because to take one means forgoing another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T04:23:35-07:00","id":1440179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440155#post1440155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just house rule that only the specific clan can take these powers without the amalgam requirement, and if someone out of the clan wishes to learn it make him just jump the usual hoops for learning out of clan power including the XP penalty. Nothing bad with homebrewing if something just doesn't add up.</div> </div> </div> </div>kinda what i was already planning but it'd be nice if we just had a good system instead of needing to homebrew one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T04:53:41-07:00","id":1440181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440179#post1440179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kinda what i was already planning but it'd be nice if we just had a good system instead of needing to homebrew one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for me and my group V5 works really nice. We love the hunger system, and the touchstones, the humanity, all the other rules, we play it very rules light. We don't even use initiative in combat. But I am playing this game for like 25 years. And the World of Darkness that was created from so many years of play can't just change because the devs decided that some clans work differently. Sorry, the moment you play in this world you create your own &quot;alternate timeline&quot;. So, to my point, I don't think that switching dominate with auspex is homebrewing a system, it's a tiny tweak. <br /> <br /> I have players that play characters from the 20th anniversary. I am not just going to tell them, &quot;um, Steve, Ravnos don't have fortitude anymore, please switch your 3 dots to presence, thank you!&quot; lol <br /> <br /> I agree though that there was no need to make things so different. Change for the sake of change has no value IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T04:58:48-07:00","id":1440182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440181#post1440181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for me and my group V5 works really nice. We love the hunger system, and the touchstones, the humanity, all the other rules, we play it very rules light. We don't even use initiative in combat. But I am playing this game for like 25 years. And the World of Darkness that was created from so many years of play can't just change because the devs decided that some clans work differently. Sorry, the moment you play in this world you create your own &quot;alternate timeline&quot;. So, to my point, I don't think that switching dominate with auspex is homebrewing a system, it's a tiny tweak.<br /> <br /> I have players that play characters from the 20th anniversary. I am not just going to tell them, &quot;um, Steve, Ravnos don't have fortitude anymore, please switch your 3 dots to presence, thank you!&quot; lol<br /> <br /> I agree though that there was no need to make things so different. Change for the sake of change has no value IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>i was only really talking about amalgams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T14:25:14-07:00","id":1440751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440181#post1440181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for me and my group V5 works really nice. We love the hunger system, and the touchstones, the humanity, all the other rules, we play it very rules light. We don't even use initiative in combat. But I am playing this game for like 25 years. And the World of Darkness that was created from so many years of play can't just change because the devs decided that some clans work differently. Sorry, the moment you play in this world you create your own &quot;alternate timeline&quot;. So, to my point, I don't think that switching dominate with auspex is homebrewing a system, it's a tiny tweak.<br /> <br /> I have players that play characters from the 20th anniversary. I am not just going to tell them, &quot;um, Steve, Ravnos don't have fortitude anymore, please switch your 3 dots to presence, thank you!&quot; lol<br /> <br /> I agree though that there was no need to make things so different. Change for the sake of change has no value IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will never be any reason why you can\u2019t interpret or house rule any of these games in your own preferred way. In fact, there are times when I feel this is becoming a lost art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:24:59-07:00","id":1440770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440751#post1440751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There will never be any reason why you can\u2019t interpret or house rule any of these games in your own preferred way. In fact, there are times when I feel this is becoming a lost art.</div> </div> </div> </div>not really, basically everybody i know homebrews all the time, not just V5 but any system we try. it's just &quot;don't like it, just homebrew it&quot; is not an excuse or even a decent defense of some of the baffeling decisions in V5 or the poor execution of many of it's ideas. V5 has a shit ton of issues, the ability to homebrew said issues doesn't change that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T16:56:48-07:00","id":1440777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440770#post1440770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not really, basically everybody i know homebrews all the time, not just V5 but any system we try. it's just &quot;don't like it, just homebrew it&quot; is not an excuse or even a decent defense of some of the baffeling decisions in V5 or the poor execution of many of it's ideas. V5 has a shit ton of issues, the ability to homebrew said issues doesn't change that fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is a brilliant game with brilliant ideas. Unfortunately, you cannot account for all tastes or general comprehension. Except, of course, by saying you can do whatever you want with it around your own game table. So yes, it is a good defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T17:16:28-07:00","id":1440782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440777#post1440777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 is a brilliant game with brilliant ideas. Unfortunately, you cannot account for all tastes or general comprehension. Except, of course, by saying you can do whatever you want with it around your own game table. So yes, it is a good defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>calm down there buckaroo, V5 ain't gonna cancel your wedding for being called imperfect. and no, not all criticism is a matter of taste, that's completely asinine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T17:33:39-07:00","id":1440784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440782#post1440782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">calm down there buckaroo, V5 ain't gonna cancel your wedding for being called imperfect. and no, not all criticism is a matter of taste, that's completely asinine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Calm yourself down, buckeroo. When you start making actual criticisms of the game that don\u2019t amount to 'this game isn\u2019t the same as the game in my head\u2019 feel free to discuss them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 03-20-2021, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T17:54:23-07:00","id":1440787,"title":"","content":"Its fine guys, criticism is fine as long as its justified and not hatedom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T21:31:57-07:00","id":1440805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440770#post1440770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not really, basically everybody i know homebrews all the time, not just V5 but any system we try. it's just &quot;don't like it, just homebrew it&quot; is not an excuse or even a decent defense of some of the baffeling decisions in V5 or the poor execution of many of it's ideas. V5 has a shit ton of issues, the ability to homebrew said issues doesn't change that fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are some really good ideas in the fluff and some of the mechanics. For an example of a mechanic I like; I generally prefer the combo of Banes and Clan Compulsions to a lot of the older weaknesses; many of which could be either crippling or ignored entirely depending on the campaign. I like that moving Quietus into Blood Sorcery means that you can give every caste of the Assamite/Banu Haqim clan the same disciplines rather than having them be separate bloodlines. I think the opening Presence power (+1 to social rolls per rank) is way more useful for social vampires than the V20 rank 1 power where its unclear if its all that much better than just having the attribute+ability at 5 dots each without the discipline.<br /> <br /> That said, ALL of those ideas were easier for me to import into V20 than try and make V5 work for my players because there were so many other things that just didn't work for us. Like turning Potence from something extremely flexible even at low ranks (strength has a lot of applications) into specific powers where converting a ghoul with Potence means they either jump (and not all that much better than a skilled athlete would be expected to be able) or deal extra damage to mortals... no breaking a steal door of its hinges or throwing a loaded trash bin through the air with enough force to bowl guys over; just video game power one (Force Jump) or video game power two (semi-Damage Boost vs. Mooks; how often does it matter if you kill vs. just knock out human opponents?).<br /> <br /> Our games have always been a bit more combat detail focused so the amount of abstraction in using Pool vs. Pool tests w. margin damage to the loser and a strongly suggested limit of three tests to keep the story going just isn't appealing with that mindset and a single opposing Firearms vs. Firearms test instead of two sets of Firearms vs. Dodge tests just doesn't remotely capture the level of detail we prefer.<br /> <br /> So there's a few gems of ideas there; I just really wish they hadn't gone the WotC route of completely rewriting the system with a new edition instead of continuing the polish the previous engine... ex. V20 moving Dodge into Athletics made a HUGE difference in terms of expressing concepts than having it as a separate &quot;feat tax.&quot;<br /> <br /> V5 cleaning up the abilities into Physical, Mental and Social to match the attribute groups instead of as the rather more arbitrary Talents, Skills and Knowledges and having most Discipline tests be Attribute + Discipline Ranks instead of Attribute + Ability opened up more flexibility in picking Abilities for concept reasons instead of just to max out the Discipline tests were both good ideas; Hunger dice instead of Blood Pool and Stains and Touchstones instead of Virtues were ideas that really only work in a few types of game styles vs. the broader number of styles the older editions could support.<br /> <br /> I like a lot of the metaplot elements too; though I think they play a LOT better by introducing them one at a time every few sessions into an existing campaign instead of &quot;oh, and all this stuff happened 5-10 years ago between editions.&quot; For example, right now there's quite a bit of buzz with the news that the Tremere Prime Chantry got blown up. Rumors in the local Elysium are flying about who may have survived, who may have died, which vampire group was behind it (no one expects The Second Inquisition) and where the local Tremere Primogen has disappeared to are stirring up all sorts of conflict, particularly since the Tremere Whip and the next in line for Regen of the city's Chantry are two different Tremere and while the Tremere PC is keeping it dead secret right now (along with all the other Tremere), the change to the Clan Curse with all the Blood Bonds breaking is absolutely something that's happening too and why, even if they don't have all the details yet, the Tremere PC knows whatever went down is BAD.<br /> <br /> Having it happen in the Now makes it far better story material than how it was presented in V5 as an event that occurred a decade and a half ago with all the fallout already sorted. Right now its shaking up everyone's plans... particularly given the missing Tremere primogen's stranglehold on the city's charity blood drives making him THE source you had to buy from if you wanted to be a Bagger in the city. There's now a bunch of vampires including the PCs ready to go to war over that resource.<br /> <br /> And again, there's nothing about the fluff that is particularly hard to just bring into V20... the biggest mechanical-based fluff change is Thinblood Alchemy which I HATE anyway so that's a development I'll just ignore as I write the other elements into the campaign one at at time.<br /> <br /> Next on the agenda will be as soon as the Tremere strife is nearly settled, the 8th Gen Giovanni who's been an &quot;ally&quot; (more mutual business partners) of the PCs is going to have a problem because apparently he was deemed problematic and in need of removal from the mortal coil as part of the Family Reunion... so some Harbingers will be coming to town to remove him before the actual rituals are to be enacted to bind the clan/bloodlines into the Hecata. So he's going to start calling in all the markers of all the Kindred in the city who owe him for his century and a half of smuggling in whatever they happened to need (at cost for those he felt favors owed would be more useful than more money in the bank).<br /> <br /> So, again... great story potential in making it personal and in the Now instead of a settled past event.<br /> <br /> Because of this... if I had to pick one edition where I could only play it Rules as Written, I'd stick with V20 in a heartbeat. If I can homebrew to my heart's content I'd still take V20, but I'd happily add the ideas from V5 I did like into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T23:58:50-07:00","id":1440812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440777#post1440777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 is a brilliant game with brilliant ideas. Unfortunately, you cannot account for all tastes or general comprehension. Except, of course, by saying you can do whatever you want with it around your own game table. So yes, it is a good defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't agree more. I and my friends are having a blast with this system. And as I said before, the moment you create characters and start playing, it becomes your World of Darkness. And I and my gang played it so much that many NPCs are former PCs or NPCs from different campaigns, and it feels like a lived-in world. Our world.<br /> The Moment the game becomes yours, the best way to play it is your way, maybe even the only way. There is no way around it. Because, after you play it long enough it takes a life of its own, and you have to account for it with lore, and house rules. And it is an amazing thing that the system gives you the tools to be creative, and is flexible enough for you to tell your own stories. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T01:41:14-07:00","id":1440813,"title":"","content":"Another thing that really doesn't work with me, that I erase from memory because how bombastically stupid it is, is clan compulsions. That's just putting the cart before the horse. A clan embraces people that make good fits for them (most of the time, and when it doesn't, they often become caitiff). They don't embrace people just anyone and expect, under the influence of the blood, they become little petty clones of the antideluvian. A ventrue acts like a ventrue because the Ventrue saw a person who embodied the qualities of a good ventrue. Not because the blood has this magical power to transform any tom,dick or harry into a refined gentleman who likes to control people (Favoured disciplines and a weakness may encourage certain behaviours, but they don't make a compulsion out of it, unless you're an unfortunate malkavian) <br /> <br /> There's a wider argument about how influentual the Beast should be. Personally I loath V5's unpredictable and unplacatable Beast in comparison to the earlier -A beast I am, lest a Beast I become- approach where there's clear divisions between the Beast having control and you having control (IE -the Beast made me do it- doesn't fly in prior editions, but is an absolutely essential excuse in V5) But, to add on to that; should the Beast be influenced by the Ego of clan founders? Especially since the Beast is, y'know, an animal, and doesn't really have any good survival reason to cause you to go through with a clan compulsion. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T01:54:49-07:00","id":1440814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440813#post1440813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A clan embraces people that make good fits for them (most of the time, and when it doesn't, they often become caitiff).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't embrace people just anyone and expect, under the influence of the blood, they become little petty clones of the antideluvian. A ventrue acts like a ventrue because the Ventrue saw a person who embodied the qualities of a good ventrue. Not because the blood has this magical power to transform any tom,dick or harry into a refined gentleman who likes to control people (Favoured disciplines and a weakness may encourage certain behaviours, but they don't make a compulsion out of it, unless you're an unfortunate malkavian) </div> </div> </div>Who said they do?<br /> <br /> From my perspective the Disciplines aren\u2019t just \u2018powers\u2019, as much as they are refined skills - disciplines - that a vampire develops to aid with their hunting instincts for obtaining blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a wider argument about how influentual the Beast should be. Personally I loath V5's unpredictable and unplacatable Beast in comparison to the earlier -A beast I am, lest a Beast I become- approach where there's clear divisions between the Beast having control and you having control (IE -the Beast made me do it- doesn't fly in prior editions, but is an absolutely essential excuse in V5) But, to add on to that; should the Beast be influenced by the Ego of clan founders? Especially since the Beast is, y'know, an animal, and doesn't really have any good survival reason to cause you to go through with a clan compulsion. </div> </div> </div>The Beast has always been written in the game, along with the theme of \u2018A Beast I am lest a Beast I become\u2019 - notwithstanding the efficacy of the system to capture this theme in a mechanical sense. The Beast is influenced by the respective instincts of the Clan rather than the Ego of the Clan founders - it is just the Clan members are inherently related to the Clan founders\u2019 instincts too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T02:14:30-07:00","id":1440815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440814#post1440814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah.The Beast has always been written in the game, along with the theme of \u2018A Beast I am lest a Beast I become\u2019 - notwithstanding the efficacy of the system to capture this theme in a mechanical sense. The Beast is influenced by the respective instincts of the Clan rather than the Ego of the Clan founders - it is just the Clan members are inherently related to the Clan founders\u2019 instincts too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret that as vampires have to be somewhat monstrous to avoid becoming ALL monstrous.<br /> <br /> The only other option is Final Death or Golconda (if it exists).<br /> <br /> And yes, like a few other things in V5, I think Clan Compulsions are... silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T04:32:54-07:00","id":1440825,"title":"","content":"I love compulsions so much. It works amazingly at our table, makes everyone a little bit more on edge, you don't know when the Beast will drive you to do something. Makes the PCs be a little bit afraid of themselves, makes them know that they are monsters even if they try hard to hide it. It's really cool, and we had amazing scenes with this system.<br /> <br /> I understand that maybe people that like more control and less randomness imposed on their characters won't like it as much as I do. But for us it's a very nice improv tool, that put us on the spot. I guess it's a playstyle thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T09:09:50-07:00","id":1440833,"title":"","content":"Once you remember that a good chunk of the older clan weaknesses were psychological; Brujah tempers, Malkavian madness, Ravnos vices, Toreador art fugue or Assamite blood thirst (or the Vizier\u2019s obsessive-compulsive disorder); the concept behind the V5 clan compulsions starts to make more sense. Heck, the Malk Bane in V5 is that the suffer extra penalities when subject to a compulsion.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is that the Clan Compulsion is just one possible compulsion they could suffer from the Beast; the Random compulsion roll is 1-3 Hunger, 4-5 Dominance, 6-7 Harm, 8-9 Paranoia, 0 Clan.<br /> <br /> So just 10% of the Beast\u2019s compulsions will be Clan related. The other 90% are the need to feed, revel in one\u2019s strength, inflict pain and hypersensitivity to potential threats; i.e. basic predatory urges that distract you for a scene if you do not indulge them.<br /> <br /> Because that\u2019s the other half of the compulsion rules. When they strike they do not force the action; they inflict a 2 dice penalty for the rest of the scene until you act on it. The Beast is beckoning, but you don\u2019t have to answer it... just take the penalty.<br /> <br /> In working them into V20, I tied their onset to failed Virtue tests... when virtue slips, the Beast\u2019s pull becomes stronger. The other thing I changed was that instead of it being a random compulsion like above; it\u2019s a general one to all of the above. The Beast beckons with a +2 difficulty penalty to tests until you indulge it with feeding, violence, domination, withdrawing from those nearby or whatever drive is unique to your Clan.<br /> <br /> Within that greater space the Brujah\u2019s Rebellion (domination or violence), the Gangrel\u2019s Feral Impulses (hunger, paranoia), Tremere\u2019s Perfectionism (domination), Ventrue\u2019s Arrogance (domination), etc. are just slight variations on the basic compulsions of the Beast, essentially throwing the odds an extra 10% in favor of the Clan\u2019s predelictions (which is why I just made it general indulgence rather than picking one each time for my V20 tweak).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T09:58:19-07:00","id":1440834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440833#post1440833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you remember that a good chunk of the older clan weaknesses were psychological; Brujah tempers, Malkavian madness, Ravnos vices, Toreador art fugue or Assamite blood thirst (or the Vizier\u2019s obsessive-compulsive disorder); the concept behind the V5 clan compulsions starts to make more sense. Heck, the Malk Bane in V5 is that the suffer extra penalities when subject to a compulsion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that some of the old weaknesses were essentially clan compulsions, but now every clan has to have one. It's not easy to think of 15 different compulsions that make the clan more interesting and fun to play without pidgeon-holing them or attaching a concept that doesn't otherwise fit their concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T10:04:55-07:00","id":1440835,"title":"","content":"I quite like Clan Compulsions. As others have said, they're relatively rare anyway, but they add lots of flavour to the clans. I've imported them for V20, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T12:22:43-07:00","id":1440845,"title":"","content":"I like the bigger focus on the Banes and Compulsions, it's one of my favourite things of the V5.<br /> <br /> Probably my favourite change is the new Toreader Bane. It works great at some many levels and in subtle ways.<br /> I think maybe game-wise it's too unforgiving, but I still have to see how it works in actual play.<br /> <br /> I like the nomad Bane of the Ravnos, I will miss the personalization opportunities that the old bane gave but I can forgive it.<br /> I'd just have retconned that it was always their bane, just like with the Toreador and others, it would have made things easier for different historical times.<br /> <br /> I have mixed feelings on the blowing up of Vienna and the Seven, but I like the Tremere splitting in sub-factions.<br /> I think the new Bane is a missed opportunity to give them a meaningful Bane. They went from the old bane (who often never came into play if the ST didn't work actively on it), from another that depending on the player's style it can be ignored... As I said missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> Instead of going &quot;clan x goes with the camarilla, clan y goes with the anarchs&quot;, since there was a shake-up I would just said that all clans were splitted in the various sect by different numbers but no more &quot;official memembership&quot; due to clan. It was something I would have avoided<br /> <br /> I'm unable to appreciate the Family Reunion thing. It obliterates some beloved bloodlines with also the purpose of transforming the Giovanni in... Still the Giovanni but with a different name?<br /> Why exactly? It's a shake-up that isn't really a shake-up at certain levels, but with also the fault of eliminating said bloodlines<br /> <br /> What I'm really not able to like are the renaming of Clans.<br /> &quot;the Ministry&quot; must be the dullest name for a vampire clan ever. I get some writers want names that &quot;make sense&quot;, but I more the type that leans on the rule of cool. &quot;Brujah&quot; is a cool name. Is like witch but in spanish plus an h. Does it make much sense? No, but I don't care.<br /> Couldn't they just be called Setites?<br /> Similarly &quot;Giovanni&quot; was much odder and cooler and made little sense (I'll point out I'm italian before someone points me out the more obvious stuff), but it's still better than another thing named after a greek deity (they're really overused).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T13:18:46-07:00","id":1440850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm really not able to like are the renaming of Clans.<br /> &quot;the Ministry&quot; must be the dullest name for a vampire clan ever. I get some writers want names that &quot;make sense&quot;, but I more the type that leans on the rule of cool. &quot;Brujah&quot; is a cool name. Is like witch but in spanish plus an h. Does it make much sense? No, but I don't care.<br /> Couldn't they just be called Setites? </div> </div> </div>Like the Serpents of Light, the Ministry includes a lot of non-Set worshipers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T13:31:52-07:00","id":1440852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440850#post1440850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like the Serpents of Light, the Ministry includes a lot of non-Set worshipers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're trying to make sense out of it. My humble opinion is that is not necessary. My personal opinion is a clan name should sound cooler or at least more intriguing than a common everyday word.<br /> Also Tremere are still called Tremere because supposedly descending from Tremere, so the argument that Setites can't be called Setites because not everyone believes or wants to be descended by Set is not that great an argument.<br /> The Ministry is like if Tremere being renamed The Coven, Brujah become The Rebellion, Ventrue become The Directorate, and Ravnos become The Carnival.<br /> It doesn't sound good to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T13:37:54-07:00","id":1440854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440852#post1440852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're trying to make sense out of it. My humble opinion is that is not necessary. My personal opinion is a clan name should sound cooler or at least more intriguing than a common everyday word.<br /> Also Tremere are still called Tremere because supposedly descending from Tremere, so the argument that Setites can't be called Setites because not everyone believes or wants to be descended by Set is not that great an argument.<br /> The Ministry is like if Tremere being renamed The Coven, Brujah become The Rebellion, Ventrue become The Directorate, and Ravnos become The Carnival.<br /> It doesn't sound good to me</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, if they're actually supposed to convert people, maybe something less overtly EVIL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T13:50:18-07:00","id":1440856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440854#post1440854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, if they're actually supposed to convert people, maybe something less overtly EVIL.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still trying to make sense and it's not my point. My point is that &quot;the clan name is a common usage word that indicates what we do&quot; is just dull.<br /> But I admit I've bited earlier, so I'll answer.<br /> <br /> It's the clan name, I didn't thought it was possible to &quot;ok let's change our name from now one we'll call ourselves differently&quot;. Mostly because elders don't want, vampires are a static society, etcetera. (Oh right they handwaved away the elders, which is I personally think was a bad move but I might go out of topic. I'll open a thread). But ok, the not-Giovanni did that too, so I suppose now it's a thing.<br /> <br /> Also Set wasn't always evil in real-world mythology. So in the V5 WOD the Setites could have just used that and say that Set being evil is all fake news, misinformation, conspiracy theory. If I remember correctly the revised clanbook played that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T14:09:34-07:00","id":1440857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440856#post1440856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Set wasn't always evil in real-world mythology. So in the V5 WOD the Setites could have just used that and say that Set being evil is all fake news, misinformation, conspiracy theory. If I remember correctly the revised clanbook played that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embracing Set as the misunderstood warrior who guarded Ra from the embodiment of darkness also plays into their clan compulsion towards transgression.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, Set was the HERO of the story until the rival kingdom that worshipped Osiris and Horus conquered everyone and rewrote him as the villain. Don\u2019t you want to know the REAL truth instead the easy lies you\u2019ve been sold?\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the line I see a Setite selling; the hidden truth can be yours if you just follow me. Set can also easily be cast as stand-in for oppressed minorities and outcasts to appeal to them.<br /> <br /> Hell, vampires are supposed to be monsters from the bowels of Hell and yet how much of modern media portrays them as sympathetic? The Followers of Set are practically meta-commentary on the fact that people want to roleplay vampires as protagonists.<br /> <br /> So yeah, in my games they\u2019re called Setites or Clan Set in the same way that a Carna neonate is still called a Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T14:18:49-07:00","id":1440858,"title":"","content":"If I were to keep them Classic Setites, I'd have made them THE CHILDREN OF APOPHIS.<br /> <br /> Darkness<br /> Snakes<br /> Black Magic<br /> <br /> The works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T15:29:47-07:00","id":1440865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440852#post1440852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're trying to make sense out of it. My humble opinion is that is not necessary. My personal opinion is a clan name should sound cooler or at least more intriguing than a common everyday word.<br /> Also Tremere are still called Tremere because supposedly descending from Tremere, so the argument that Setites can't be called Setites because not everyone believes or wants to be descended by Set is not that great an argument.<br /> The Ministry is like if Tremere being renamed The Coven, Brujah become The Rebellion, Ventrue become The Directorate, and Ravnos become The Carnival.<br /> It doesn't sound good to me</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are not called Tremere because they are descended from Tremere. They are named after the medieval House of wizards that were founded by Tremere, and diablerised the Salubri to become a vampire clan. In V5, Tremere are also called: Usurpers, Warlocks, Hemetics, Thaumaturges, Transgressors, The Broken Clan and Blood Witches. They have multiple names given as do all the Clans. The Ministry are still called Followers of Set or Setites in the Anarch book too. Curiously, the Brujah Clan are named after a word that means \u2018witch\u2019 in Spanish, but whatever...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T16:19:49-07:00","id":1440869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440865#post1440865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tremere are not called Tremere because they are descended from Tremere. They are named after the medieval House of wizards that were founded by Tremere, and diablerised the Salubri to become a vampire clan. In V5, Tremere are also called: Usurpers, Warlocks, Hemetics, Thaumaturges, Transgressors, The Broken Clan and Blood Witches. They have multiple names given as do all the Clans. The Ministry are still called Followers of Set or Setites in the Anarch book too. Curiously, the Brujah Clan are named after a word that means \u2018witch\u2019 in Spanish, but whatever...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I wrote &quot;supposedly descending from Tremere&quot; because in mind I was thinking about nenonates that heard this story about this Tremere founder dude, which might or might not be true because neonates don't know stuff (even less in V5 if I got things right). So I applied such logic in the fact the clan name stayed the same. But I admit I didn't explain such internal logic I was going thorough, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Ok we know that clan Tremere is named after House Tremere (which was one of the houses of the Order of Hermes from the game Ars Magica, later incorporated in MtA) who was named after its founder Tremere.<br /> But I don't see that all clans have multiple names. Feels like those are supposed to be nicknames. The &quot;official&quot; name is one.<br /> <br /> I don't see anything much &quot;curiously&quot; about the Brujah clan name, the game is from 1991 and the author thought up names that sounded cool after things he knew or words he heard (like Gangrel*), or names he heard like Giovanni (who in italian is not a family name but a first name**)<br /> If you want to find a possible reason in-universe, in real world history Carthage domain extended over the southern coast of spain. Given Rein-Hagen was a quite knowlageable person (or at least that's the impression I had), it's possible he considerated this but there is no mention of it anywhere<br /> <br /> *from what I gather &quot;gangrel&quot; is an old english word that means &quot;wandering beggars&quot;, but if we apply in-universe logic why would a clan &quot;name themselves&quot; (since apparently it can be done) the wandering beggars? Especially given the Gangrels surely don't see themselves as such. I could buy that it's the Ventrue calling them that, but then it becomes a Banu Haqim-like thing and a name used among themselves is needed. I think I'll stick to out-universe logic<br /> <br /> **but some italian names can sometimes be found as family names too (which sounds kinda weird to italians too), something that was more common in centuries past actually (so the Giovanni would be weird but still not-too-impossible)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T16:44:06-07:00","id":1440873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440869#post1440869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't see that all clans have multiple names. Feels like those are supposed to be nicknames. The &quot;official&quot; name is one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication I got from reading the list of titles for each Clan in V5 is that there isn\u2019t an \u2018official\u2019 name for each Clan as much as there are a bunch of names given in different circumstances/contexts. So when you say that the Followers of Set or Setites are now called The Ministry, the point is they are still called the other titles too, in particular circumstances, and there is nothing that prevents anybody in or to of game from calling them that still. There may be an element of personal taste in this too - personally, I think \u2019The Ministry\u2019 sounds a lot cooler than \u2019Setites\u2019 but whatever butters your muffin, I guess. <br /> <br /> Regarding the original naming of the Clans, I\u2019m not in a position to second guess the process, but I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if the it simply amounted to the names sounding cool, without much analysis on the meanings of each. As resultant editions and game development accrued, maybe some more thought was given on the matter - leading to alternative names. I do know this was the case in Mage at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 03-21-2021, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T17:56:15-07:00","id":1440876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440869#post1440869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *from what I gather &quot;gangrel&quot; is an old english word that means &quot;wandering beggars&quot;, but if we apply in-universe logic why would a clan &quot;name themselves&quot; (since apparently it can be done) the wandering beggars? Especially given the Gangrels surely don't see themselves as such. I could buy that it's the Ventrue calling them that, but then it becomes a Banu Haqim-like thing and a name used among themselves is needed. I think I'll stick to out-universe logic<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They probably named called themselves the children of Ennoia or whatever the Gangrel Ante was being called when they were embraced.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T18:11:31-07:00","id":1440879,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with the Followers of Set renaming themselves The Ministry since it's really just a PR move. &quot;Oh we're all about FREEDOM, and that Set guy? He's just a symbol of freedom but we don't <i>really</i> worship him and the clan name has caused no end of misunderstandings...&quot; but it's just a way to get people on board with worshipping Set as a symbol and then slowly convince them to worship him for real. <br /> <br /> Setites have a long history of creating cults among mortals to some deity or concept or another and slowly getting people to worship Set as they unveil more and more religious truths. You might have a few hardcore fundamentalists who are upset about the name change, but I imagine many true believer Setites would be okay with it since it can be argued it's basically just an elaborate cult to Set among vampires - get people on board with The Ministry, get them to start having religious beliefs involving freedom and then those vampires will eventually start worshipping Set and join the Followers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T18:43:29-07:00","id":1440887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440879#post1440879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm okay with the Followers of Set renaming themselves The Ministry since it's really just a PR move. &quot;Oh we're all about FREEDOM, and that Set guy? He's just a symbol of freedom but we don't <i>really</i> worship him and the clan name has caused no end of misunderstandings...&quot; but it's just a way to get people on board with worshipping Set as a symbol and then slowly convince them to worship him for real.<br /> <br /> Setites have a long history of creating cults among mortals to some deity or concept or another and slowly getting people to worship Set as they unveil more and more religious truths. You might have a few hardcore fundamentalists who are upset about the name change, but I imagine many true believer Setites would be okay with it since it can be argued it's basically just an elaborate cult to Set among vampires - get people on board with The Ministry, get them to start having religious beliefs involving freedom and then those vampires will eventually start worshipping Set and join the Followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, the story they settled on seems to be, &quot;The Ministry is all the Setites who were made as local cults that decided Set was just one god worth worshiping&quot; while the Church of Set was like, &quot;THOSE WORDS ARE BLASPHEMY!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/6ThpkjDgdvY/hqdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T21:17:44-07:00","id":1440904,"title":"","content":"So they're basically just the Serpents of Light? Except I guess they give no special consideration to antediluvians or clan founders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T21:28:36-07:00","id":1440905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440904#post1440904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they're basically just the Serpents of Light? Except I guess they give no special consideration to antediluvians or clan founders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Serpents are probably a good precursor to them.<br /> <br /> It also shows the Setites learned nothing from the Serpents. But yes, if you worship Loki and Eris or Damballa (who isn't evil) then don't be surprised if a bunch of people telling you they don't exist but are faces of another God entiretely aren't persuasive.<br /> <br /> It's not even that most Ministry members don't believe in Set. They just believe in other gods too. This is a problem because of the Church of Set (i.e. orthodox Setites) believing all other gods are aeons and enemies of Set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T00:35:44-07:00","id":1440910,"title":"","content":"How many Setite neonates actually believe the Clan dogma, anyway? How many just pay lip-service?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T08:36:45-07:00","id":1440947,"title":"","content":"I've always imagined that a large majority of them probably do. Setites often tend to recruit new vampires from their cults, and these cults frequently involve worshipping Set to one degree or another. Even if a cult ostensibly worships some other figure, as cultists get to higher levels it's revealed that Set was the true face of the cult all along. So many Setites (though by no means all) were already believers to one degree or another in Set. And then they get gifted with magical powers and turned into supernatural monsters which is just going to reconfirm those beliefs (it's hard to say Set is just a bunch of hokum when you've just been turned into a vampire as a demonstration). The Followers also aren't part of the Camarilla so neonates are more likely to get a fairly one-sided education where they're not taught much besides the clan's views on Set and vampirism.<br /> <br /> I tend to believe that it's actually moderately older Followers who have more extensive dealings with the Camarilla and therefore a much broader view of the vampiric condition who going to end up faltering in their beliefs whereas younger vampires (barring player characters, of course) probably don't interact with non-Follower of Set vampires on a regular basis so they don't necessarily have the knowledge of other beliefs which contradict the ones that they're taught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-22-2021, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T12:49:06-07:00","id":1440964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440947#post1440947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setites often tend to recruit new vampires from their cults, and these cults frequently involve worshipping Set to one degree or another. Even if a cult ostensibly worships some other figure, as cultists get to higher levels it's revealed that Set was the true face of the cult all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I run the clan when I ST chronicles. The clan only recruits from mortals already in their cult. When recruiting mortals into their cult, they use a variety of front organizations (including new religious groups that most people would also call cults), and mortals &quot;progress&quot; through a series of new groups and initiations where more of the truth is revealed so they can evaluate each cult member's response, until they reach a final group where all is revealed, and they only select the best candidates from that group for the embrace. It's multiple vetting for the correct criteria, weeding out people for one reason or another before the embrace is offered. Because that is how cults actually operate.<br /> <br /> Of course, that is not how things are presented in the books. There it is the typical &quot;I like this mortal for whatever reason and embrace her&quot; and then hope you can indoctrinate that person afterwards. Which is way, way too risky. Too many things can go wrong. But I think that's how most players/STs handle it, so I know I am in the minority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440947#post1440947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to believe that it's actually moderately older Followers who have more extensive dealings with the Camarilla and therefore a much broader view of the vampiric condition who going to end up faltering in their beliefs whereas younger vampires (barring player characters, of course) probably don't interact with non-Follower of Set vampires on a regular basis so they don't necessarily have the knowledge of other beliefs which contradict the ones that they're taught.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the danger point - contact with people outside the cult. Contact with other people means exposure to different ways of thinking - which is always dangerous to a cult. But at some point that needs to be done in order to achieve Set's grand plan or whatever. So you have the Setite temple lead by a trusted person, and that &quot;priest&quot; supervises the new Setite's first exposure to other vampires. They report back everything once a week, month, or whatever, so the trusted leader can evaluate if the programming is still working or if they see danger signs of independent thought. If so, they yank the person out and send them back to someone for &quot;more training&quot; before they are allowed back in contact with outsiders. There's probably some euphemism involved so that vampire thinks its a wonderful things as opposed to punishment. <br /> <br /> This may happen a few more times, but if it happens too much, the Setites realize this won't work out and they destroy the potential troublemaker in secret so as to not freak everyone else out, and they tell a cover story in case any associates or friends ask about her.<br /> <br /> The Setites have had around 3000 years to perfect their technique so it mostly works out for them. They want to prevent any situation like the Serpents of the Light, which is a case of something clearly going drastically wrong. Eventually something like that will happen, and probably has happened many times over the last 3000 years. But what usually happens is the rest of the Followers of Set successfully wipe out the local cult gone wrong. But the Serpents of the Light succeeded by a combination of good planning, luck, and the protection of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Only after that post-embrace vetting verifies that the programming holds and the person is not in danger of becoming a rebel, heretic or apostate, does the person become trusted enough to have more independence and eventual responsibility. Even then, there is likely frequent moving of individuals around so that they do not forge close association with other vampires. They only want a Setite to form close associations with other Setites. So operatives likley transfer around a lot and adopt new cover identities.<br /> <br /> Those Setites actually &quot;in&quot; the Camarilla are probably really trusted operatives whose main purpose is to act as PR and therefore undermine anti-Setite propaganda. And only in rare circumstances betray the Camarilla because that would defeat the purpose of them being there. Occasionally you may need to burn an agent, but that should be kept to a minimum.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to me, the V5 Ministry only makes sense if it is some concerted PR move to expand Setite operations. I don't think that actually makes sense because it exposes the clan too much. When the Ministry &quot;front&quot; cover has to be blown (and it will even if the plan is to take decades), it'll result in too severe an impact to the clan. Its reputation will be entirely destroyed. That can only be justified if the rewards are worth that cost, and I can't think of anything that would justify it outside resurrecting Set/Typhon himself.<br /> <br /> If it is an actual case of the cult breaking down, then this is he equivalent of an Anarch Revolt for the clan, and the Ministry become Setite anti-tribu at war with its clan.<br /> <br /> So I don't like the V5 depiction of the Ministry (No surprise there for anyone who's read my other thoughts on V5). However, that is based on my conception of the clan, and freely admit my idea is probably not most players'. So they may be fine with the new version which would fit the &quot;I hope the random schmoe I embraced ends up being indoctrinated correctly&quot; version of the clanbooks. That version of the clan can work too, it's just a very different version than what I think the clan was originally supposed to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T13:01:33-07:00","id":1440966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440964#post1440964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how I run the clan when I ST chronicles. The clan only recruits from mortals already in their cult. When recruiting mortals into their cult, they use a variety of front organizations (including new religious groups that most people would also call cults), and mortals &quot;progress&quot; through a series of new groups and initiations where more of the truth is revealed so they can evaluate each cult member's response, until they reach a final group where all is revealed, and they only select the best candidates from that group for the embrace. It's multiple vetting for the correct criteria, weeding out people for one reason or another before the embrace is offered. Because that is how cults actually operate.<br /> <br /> Of course, that is not how things are presented in the books. There it is the typical &quot;I like this mortal for whatever reason and embrace her&quot; and then hope you can indoctrinate that person afterwards. Which is way, way too risky. Too many things can go wrong. But I think that's how most players/STs handle it, so I know I am in the minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually argue that you're presenting it how the books present it but seeing the &quot;human factor&quot; as an abberation versus an inevitability.<br /> <br /> The Ministry strikes me as an inevitability too because religions are constantly undergoing revisions, schisms, doctrinal differences, debates, and conflicts over what might be otherwise small points of divergence that are SERIOUS BUSINESS. The Followers of Set in Egypt alone are going to have people who interpret Set as a Protector of Ra's Barge, those who believe he's allied with Apophis, monotheists that believe Set to be the only God worth worshiping, Coptic Christianized Gnostics who associate him with Satan, Islamic Setites who view him as Iblis, Hellenized Setites who associate him with Gaia as well as the Greek God Typhon, and Roman ones that believe he's Ares. Now imagine that plenty of these don't much care for the idea that their version is inferior to one of the others.<br /> <br /> As for the human factor, Followers of Set are subject to the exact same sort of longings that other vampires are and are going to be inclined to Embrace who they want when they want. Set embraced Kemintiri and that was a disaster but you can't really criticize your god. Hesha embraced Elizabeth because he was certain she was in love with him and events spiraled out of control. Maybe you're only getting permission to make a progeny NOW or they're terminally ill or you want them to be your inside vamp in another group. The Church encourages you to embrace only your hardened cultists for years as a reward but there's no rule to say you HAVE to and maybe you hold your followers in contempt (as most cult leaders do).<br /> <br /> I'd argue most of THESE Embraces are probably fine even if they're not as doctrinally consistent, most of them would be happy to give lip service to the cult of Set. Among the Setites there are bound to be at least a decent chunk of vampires who find the idea of Antediluvian worship to be stupid. Either because they notice that Set doesn't appear any different than the other 12 or the fact that the Setites acknowledge he's dead (probably at the hands of the Silent Striders) and it's about resurrecting him.<br /> <br /> For me the Ministry is basically just what happened when you kicked the ball down the road a long time and doctrinal drift happened. The cults of Loki, Eris, Satan, and so on became more focused on their local variants than Set themselves. The lip service element is still there or was but the Church of Set decided to eliminate some &quot;heretics&quot; and, well, they realized that was a LOT more than they expected.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-22-2021, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T13:03:47-07:00","id":1440967,"title":"","content":"One wonders what the writers think the Settite &quot;verb&quot; is supposed to be? Vampires as corrupters I would think. Which means they just need an excuse, any excuse, to corrupt people and vampires. That's much more flexible than making them a Set cult, to be sure, but robs the clan of much of its Conan era pulp flavor. I think that's why they put them in the Anarchs. Putting them in the Anarchs fits for a broad clan dedicated to general corruption, but not as a clan of Set cultists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 03-22-2021, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T13:35:43-07:00","id":1440970,"title":"","content":"The overwhelming majority of the Followers of Set are True Believers. They join a cult, they go through several trials during their time in the cult , and some who has drank enough kool-aid and successfuly gone through these ordeals may be selected for the embrace. Perhaps some Settites are embraced outside of the cult, and perhaps some settites fall out of the faith over their long, long unlives, but they're a clan of True believers. What constitutes as a &quot;True believer&quot; may actually vary though; You may have some who are all in on Set, Some who are just in on Set's message and who care a less about the guy, some who think set's alive, some who think Set a dead martyr that can't come back, some who believe Set must be resurrected, and some who believe Set has already been resurected. You have many different interpretations on who Set was and what Set did and...<br /> <br /> Even the rare fellows who slip through who don't believe in Set and don't believe in gnosticism or corruption, it's unlikely that they, as vampires, are really going to stick out. Most of the settite Modus Operandi is actually just exaggerated vampire behaviour, and most of it falls under good practice. It's only if you really fall far off the tree that you're going to cause problems. It's most likely that going with the flow, which is how you got this far, is how you'll continue. <br /> <br /> RE: African snake god/benevolent snake god/Monty Python ain't evil, so how can these people appreciate Settite Orthodoxy?<br /> Yeah, at face value that makes sense, but A setite cult could definetly make them evil. Think of all the crazy-malicious faiths that have used the banner of Jesus or Buddha .<br /> <br /> A big thing with Settite sorcery is that you actually need to genuinely believe in what's discussed to work it's magic, and you need this magic to advance among the followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-22-2021, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T13:57:50-07:00","id":1440971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440970#post1440970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big thing with Settite sorcery is that you actually need to genuinely believe in what's discussed to work it's magic, and you need this magic to advance among the followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advancing among the Followers? Perhaps. But advancing among regular Kindred? Not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T15:06:25-07:00","id":1440979,"title":"","content":"Setites are rather laisse-faire in this edition. The Anarch sourcebook says:<br /> &quot;Many Embraced into the clan abandon its ways, or are never taught them. These vampires are rarely sought for re-recruitment by their peers, and are in most cases allowed to do as they please. Unless caught revealing revealing Ministry secrets, for the punishment is usually merciless, long, and creative, the clan does not force its creed on its children.&quot;<br /> <br /> This policy makes sense to me. Wayward Ministers aren't taking away something from the orthodoxy and on whole, they're not going to make the clan's reputation worse than its core do. On the contrary, it allows a genuine #notallsetites phenomenon, which means that an individual of the clan could be:<ul><li>an orthodox follower of Set</li> <li>a basically orthodox follower of Set with a slightly different doctrine that they care about, but you don't, because they're not explicitly telling you about it</li> <li>part of front for either of the above</li> <li>part of genuinely independent cult</li> <li>someone who thinks that they're an apostate but in fact belong to a front for the orthodoxy</li> <li>someone who thinks they're orthodox but is in fact by being led by an apostatic cult</li> <li>a follower of a non-Ministry cult</li> <li>not connected to any cults at all</li> </ul><br /> So a Minister gets chummy with you, you can't be sure if their angle, if they have one, is the same as that of another Minister. Ideally for the Church of Set, assuming that every Minister is one of them would be like assuming that every Ventrue has a role in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440967#post1440967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One wonders what the writers think the Settite &quot;verb&quot; is supposed to be? Vampires as corrupters I would think. Which means they just need an excuse, any excuse, to corrupt people and vampires. That's much more flexible than making them a Set cult, to be sure, but robs the clan of much of its Conan era pulp flavor. I think that's why they put them in the Anarchs. Putting them in the Anarchs fits for a broad clan dedicated to general corruption, but not as a clan of Set cultists.</div> </div> </div> </div>A recent <a href=\"https://s3-eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/pdx-campaign-wp-data/uploads/sites/10/2021/03/11170313/clanverbs_big.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">infographic</a> made by the brand community manager lists &quot;influence, entrap, sway, deal, cultivate&quot;. &quot;Influence&quot; is shared with Ventrue and Toreador have some less business-like synonyms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T16:25:42-07:00","id":1440984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440966#post1440966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Followers of Set in Egypt alone are going to have people who interpret Set as a Protector of Ra's Barge, those who believe he's allied with Apophis, monotheists that believe Set to be the only God worth worshiping, Coptic Christianized Gnostics who associate him with Satan, Islamic Setites who view him as Iblis, Hellenized Setites who associate him with Gaia as well as the Greek God Typhon, and Roman ones that believe he's Ares. Now imagine that plenty of these don't much care for the idea that their version is inferior to one of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt there are internal disputes within the Setites. However, I don't think those debates are anything like you are presenting.<br /> <br /> First, Set himself would have clarified any official story when he reestablished the clan in the 10th century BC after being driven out of Egypt, and since he seems to have been fairly active for the next thousand years, had plenty of opportunities to set the story straight. So most of the things theologians like to debate aren't the things the Setites might debate. You won't have esoteric debates about the importance of protecting Ra's Barge, or whether the Wyrm should really be worshipped, or the thoughts of Gnostic Christians or Hellenestic philosophers about the figure of Set. Most of that will be completed eliminated because they had Set himself explain things to his clan for a long time in the historical era. The fledgling who brings up Romans identifying Set with Mars will be quickly reminded that the Romans arrived nearly a thousand years after Set left Egypt, and their opinions are irrelevant because they are obviously wrong. (One of the neat things to do as an ST of the WoD is to determine the real, secret history of these things). Instead of sounding like an erudite theologian who's very knowledgeable, he'll be seen as an ignorant clown who needs to shut up and listen. A Setite who questions the story Set himself laid down won't survive long. (We're not told those stories since they're not things most gamers actually care about.)<br /> <br /> Second, there's not necessarily a problem with contradictory myths for a pagan style religion. Religious practice in the Classical World and earlier wasn't about arguing doctrine, eliminating contradictions in myths, or creating a coherent theology. It was about performing the correct rituals and rites of the religion. How do you perform correct sacrifices to the gods? How do you avoid religious miasma or pollution? What are the mysteries we don't reveal to outsiders? What things do you to avoid offending the divine? A lot of religion is still like that today especially in the non-monotheistic parts of the world. As long as the Setite religion follows those things that Set told his followers to do, things that may seem important to you from your religious background may be totally unimportant to Setite religion, and their cult adherents would be told that. And those that kept trying to force the religion to deal with issues that Set and the elders who followed him did not think important won't last long. People from a Western style religion that prizes things like theology will just have to unlearn those things in order to understand how the Setites follow their religion. That's why it is important to indoctrinate people into the cult before you embrace them. A mortal who doesn't &quot;get&quot; it, just gets passed over when time comes to hand out the goodies. You have a lot more trouble when your newly embraced vampire doesn't &quot;get&quot; it.<br /> <br /> Third, the longevity of the vampires and the clan structure would prevent most situations where the new guy taking over the religion hijacks things. In Scientology, once L. Ron Hubbard died, David Miscavige essentially performed a palace coup, eliminated his rivals, and later began re-editing Hubbard's texts or found new clarifications. Even he didn't make major changes, just enough to force people to buy all the books they already had again. That should be much harder to do in a vampire clan. There might still be elders around who remember Set before he disappeared in AD 33. If someone starts claiming things about Set that doesn't have overwhelming consensus, he'll be shut down quickly. Also, Miscavige could get away with a lot of shenanigans because there was relatively little other Scientology members could do. Most members had no say, and the relatively few who disagreed with Miscavige could be quietly and legally removed from power. That isn't possible when your other rivals for power can respond with unbelievable violence. You either have to risk civil war, or rule by some means of consensus. That consensus probably includes &quot;don't make up shit.&quot; With Blood Sorcery and Auspex and all sort of other powers that the elders have, they can stay in direct communication with each other even in a pre-technological era. So some level of supervision should happen.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that the issues you talked about won't come up at all. But as a whole, I think the Setites would prevent or eliminate the vast majority of such cases. When needed, they would do so ruthlessly. That's why we don't have many canonical instances of heresies or apostates. They've been successfully suppressed. Sure, maybe this group or that group managed to survive for a while, but eventually the clan wipes them out. Who's to say after 200 years time even the Serpents of Light won't be extinguished?<br /> <br /> I think the things that will be disputed the most will be issues of enforcement and discipline (this person acted in a wrong way, how badly do we admonish or punish him; or she did a very good thing, how should she be rewarded?), and matters of politics (who gets to be in charge of this temple; the leader of the temple in this city wants to do this thing should the rest of us support him with resources, do nothing, or support this rival plan by this other temple leader there?). &quot;How can we best serve Set now&quot; is a valid question that can lead to disputes. As can &quot;Which one of us will wield this newly discovered powerful artifact of Set, as only one can wear the Serpent Crown.&quot; Things like &quot;what is the nature of Set&quot; likely isn't because it is either a settled point, or considered irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440966#post1440966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the human factor, Followers of Set are subject to the exact same sort of longings that other vampires are and are going to be inclined to Embrace who they want when they want. Set embraced Kemintiri and that was a disaster but you can't really criticize your god. Hesha embraced Elizabeth because he was certain she was in love with him and events spiraled out of control. Maybe you're only getting permission to make a progeny NOW or they're terminally ill or you want them to be your inside vamp in another group. The Church encourages you to embrace only your hardened cultists for years as a reward but there's no rule to say you HAVE to and maybe you hold your followers in contempt (as most cult leaders do).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where we disagree on the nature of the cult, or what the cult should be. I'm sure Setites embrace without permission just like any other vampire can. I'm also sure that the Setite elders ruthlessly punish those who do far worse than any Prince in the Camarilla because they don't have to worry about Justicars, Conclaves, Anarchs and what not. And furthermore, where does that illegally embraced Setite supposed to go? You can't exactly hide them from other Setites or claim it was some other Setite who embraced them when you meet up at the temple. Nor can you send them to safety to some random city far away from the rest of your clan, unless you don't mind them being Caitiff in some domain where Setites don't rule and who knows what will happen to them. That's essentially abandoning them. So I think this happens a lot less than you might think. It doesn't mean they can't happen, but I don't think it is any kind of routine problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440966#post1440966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the Ministry is basically just what happened when you kicked the ball down the road a long time and doctrinal drift happened. The cults of Loki, Eris, Satan, and so on became more focused on their local variants than Set themselves. The lip service element is still there or was but the Church of Set decided to eliminate some &quot;heretics&quot; and, well, they realized that was a LOT more than they expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I disagree with. There should not be cults of Loki, Eris, Satan, and so on among the Followers. Those cults are for the <i>mortals</i> as a front to introduce real Set worship. If you run a proper cult, none of those people get embraced until farther down the line after they have been taught the &quot;authentic&quot; Set religion. That final group, carefully vetted and culled, is who you select for the embrace. And they know perfectly well it isn't some Loki or Eris or Damballah or whatever figure they originally believed in by that time, but the &quot;real&quot; Set they are now worshipping. There should be a lot less drift than you think. That's to prevent the entire scenario you are talking about. We can assume Set learned some things when he lost Egypt, and this is why he reorganized the clan.<br /> <br /> I am not saying such things are impossible and don't happen. I'm sure they do every now and again. But that is not the default of the clan. At least, I don't think it should. <br /> <br /> You and the developers of V5 are making certain assumptions, and I am making other assumptions. That's fine. We're all allowed to. I know you and many others see V5 as canon and therefore the truth from All High. But I see V5 as essentially a form of fan fiction. There may be good forms of fan fiction or pastiche, and bad forms. But no matter how one may like the Conan stories of L. Sprague De Camp and Lin Carter, they're not REH's Conan. Same thing for all the many stories about Sherlock Holmes written by someone who is not Doyle. Even if in some cases they were approved by the literary estate and therefore &quot;official&quot;. I put V5 in the same category. Revised probably needs to be put there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T16:37:27-07:00","id":1440986,"title":"","content":"Actually, my idea is Set doesn't give a shit about doctrine. He's a God of Chaos and all of our surprisingly in-depth character descriptions about Set:<br /> <br /> * Kemintiri<br /> * The Osiris and Set encounters<br /> * Horus' backstory<br /> <br /> And so on indicate that Set was a loud, brash, and warlike deity who found issues of doctrine silly.<br /> <br /> He also murders every single Follower of Set in Gehenna because their religiosity offended him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KHbzSif78qQ\" data-code=\"KHbzSif78qQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/KHbzSif78qQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> My view of vampires in Blood Cults are to remember:<br /> <br /> * Vampires are liars<br /> * Vampires who are true believers will still lie for power<br /> * Vampires don't remember things nearly as well as they think they do<br /> * Vampires rewrite stories all the time ala Viktor in Underworld<br /> * Even if they know the truth, there's no benefit to promoting it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, Set himself would have clarified any official story when he reestablished the clan in the 10th century BC after being driven out of Egypt, and since he seems to have been fairly active for the next thousand years, had plenty of opportunities to set the story straight. So most of the things theologians like to debate aren't the things the Setites might debate. You won't have esoteric debates about the importance of protecting Ra's Barge, or whether the Wyrm should really be worshipped, or the thoughts of Gnostic Christians or Hellenestic philosophers about the figure of Set. Most of that will be completed eliminated because they had Set himself explain things to his clan for a long time in the historical era. <b>The fledgling who brings up Romans identifying Set with Mars will be quickly reminded that the Romans arrived nearly a thousand years after Set left Egypt, and their opinions are irrelevant because they are obviously wrong. (One of the neat things to do as an ST of the WoD is to determine the real, secret history of these things). I</b>nstead of sounding like an erudite theologian who's very knowledgeable, he'll be seen as an ignorant clown who needs to shut up and listen. A Setite who questions the story Set himself laid down won't survive long. (We're not told those stories since they're not things most gamers actually care about.) </div> </div> </div>Definitely a good reason to exterminate the filthy heretics. If they blasphem Mars then they deserve to die like the animals they are. Set will bless the Romans for diablerizing the inferior Egyptians.<br /> <br /> If that sounds insane, it is fairly accurate to large scales of human history.<br /> <br /> And Set's reaction?<br /> <br /> &quot;Where's Khonshu?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Khonshu is dead. I'm Pilate.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay. You get me my meal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or maybe Set kills Pilate and embraces someone else. It'll be a 1000 years before anyone notices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-22-2021, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T20:30:36-07:00","id":1441016,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I feel discussing things with you is like playing a game of Calvinball. And I'm Hobbes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T21:28:30-07:00","id":1441022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Vampires don't remember things nearly as well as they think they do </div> </div> </div>So, even more VtR injected in VtM? Grrr.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T21:42:28-07:00","id":1441026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441022#post1441022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, even more VtR injected in VtM? Grrr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have never been depicted as having perfect memories. They talked about the Fog of Ages as far back as Mummy in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441016#post1441016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I feel discussing things with you is like playing a game of Calvinball. And I'm Hobbes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try and do a direct response to your posts specific points tomorrow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T10:01:51-07:00","id":1441088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Setites are rather laisse-faire in this edition. The Anarch sourcebook says:<br /> &quot;Many Embraced into the clan abandon its ways, or are never taught them. These vampires are rarely sought for re-recruitment by their peers, and are in most cases allowed to do as they please. Unless caught revealing revealing Ministry secrets, for the punishment is usually merciless, long, and creative, the clan does not force its creed on its children.&quot; </div> </div> </div> what, they actually wrote this? This is garbage<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1440979#post1440979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This policy makes sense to me. Wayward Ministers aren't taking away something from the orthodoxy and on whole, they're not going to make the clan's reputation worse than its core do. On the contrary, it allows a genuine #notallsetites phenomenon, which means that an individual of the clan could be:</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense to you because you're, i assume, not a religious person and can't understand the mindset of someone who's not only deeply religious but also a member of the mother-fucking-clergy. Nevermind that they're vampires in a cult.<br /> I'm sure I read somewhere that, quite suprisingly, the <i>more </i>restrictive a religion was, the longer it'll last. you can't build a cult out of a pick-and-choose postmodern, easy going attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-23-2021, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T10:08:09-07:00","id":1441089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441088#post1441088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I read somewhere that, quite suprisingly, the <i>more </i>restrictive a religion was, the longer it'll last. you can't build a cult out of a pick-and-choose postmodern, easy going attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, the idea the Setites were able to keep themselves orthodox and pure for 2000 years is silly. History shows the evolution of Egyptian religion and subsequent ones with the civilization that supports it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T11:13:00-07:00","id":1441095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441088#post1441088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes sense to you because you're, i assume, not a religious person and can't understand the mindset of someone who's not only deeply religious but also a member of the mother-fucking-clergy. Nevermind that they're vampires in a cult.<br /> I'm sure I read somewhere that, quite suprisingly, the <i>more </i>restrictive a religion was, the longer it'll last. you can't build a cult out of a pick-and-choose postmodern, easy going attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to be, as laymen go, but different standards apply to different types of religion. I believed that all of humanity should do what God says, which meant that anyone who resolutely chose otherwise was a regrettable failure of everybody who <i>did</i> follow His teachings. The Church of Set is more exclusive than that. It destroys people before building them back. Sometimes it just destroys them. The latter cases are blamed on the initiate, not the teacher, and that's not to mention third party casualties of a prospective initiate's corruption. So it's no tragedy if an individual fails to develop, because the path isn't meant for them. They don't have the right to be liberated, they have the right to <i>pursue</i> liberation and not every Setite is needed or qualified to provide the opportunity..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T11:27:06-07:00","id":1441096,"title":"","content":"I'm sort of amused that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> thinks that a religion can remain utterly restrictive and stagnant without the oppressive measures that the Church of Set imposed in Beckett's jyhad Diary. And that he's surprised that these resulted in a breakaway sect. Even then, we already know that there were plenty of Followers of Set who weren't fanatics in the service of the cause because the books list several.<br /> <br /> Not the least being Kemintiri and any of her line, the entirety of Serpents of Light (who were Haitian Setites who violently rejected Set), and ones who never worshiped Set in the first place like the South American branches.<br /> <br /> But I don't think most Setites would tolerate followers who &quot;walked away&quot; without some attempt to win them back or destroy them. It's just the difference between a follower who gives lip service and a follower who utterly rejects Set is often just a matter of how willing they are to lie for their own survival.<br /> <br /> I like CHICAGO BY NIGHT 5th Edition's take on the Ministry as with the exception of Marcel, all of them couldn't care less about Set. I think its also very true to life that the Church of Set wants to kill Marcel for &quot;doing it wrong&quot; more than the ones who are apathetic too.<br /> <br /> <i>----<br /> <br /> Once I saw this guy on a bridge about to jump. I said, &quot;Don't do it!&quot; He said, &quot;Nobody loves me.&quot; I said, &quot;God loves you. Do you believe in God?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>He said, &quot;Yes.&quot; I said, &quot;Are you a Christian or a Jew?&quot; He said, &quot;A Christian.&quot; I said, &quot;Me, too! Protestant or Catholic?&quot; He said, &quot;Protestant.&quot; I said, &quot;Me, too! What franchise?&quot; He said, &quot;Baptist.&quot; I said, &quot;Me, too! Northern Baptist or Southern Baptist?&quot; He said, &quot;Northern Baptist.&quot; I said, &quot;Me, too! Northern Conservative Baptist or Northern Liberal Baptist?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>He said, &quot;Northern Conservative Baptist.&quot; I said, &quot;Me, too! Northern Conservative Baptist Great Lakes Region, or Northern Conservative Baptist Eastern Region?&quot; He said, &quot;Northern Conservative Baptist Great Lakes Region.&quot; I said, &quot;Me, too!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>Northern Conservative\u2020Baptist Great Lakes Region Council of 1879, or Northern Conservative Baptist Great Lakes Region Council of 1912?&quot; He said, &quot;Northern<br /> Conservative Baptist Great Lakes Region Council of 1912.&quot; I said, &quot;Die, heretic!&quot; And I pushed him over.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-23-2021, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T11:48:00-07:00","id":1441098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441026#post1441026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll try and do a direct response to your posts specific points tomorrow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessary. Just joshing. You do seem to change stances from one post to the next sometimes, but I think that's mainly an artifact of each post only being a snippet about one aspect rather than an essay of everything you think about the clan. We're all in the same boat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T11:56:28-07:00","id":1441100,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying they're utterly restrictive damnit. I'm just saying that &quot;<u>Many</u> Embraced into the clan abandon its ways, or are never taught them. These vampires are rarely sought for re-recruitment by their peers, and are in most cases allowed to do as they please....the clan does not force its creed on its children&quot; is absolutely fucking rediculous bonkers.<br /> <br /> These people are fucking <i>Vampires</i>. You don't live and let live as a God-Damned vampire. The Undead are not in the habbit of raising folks like a liberal arts college. You're better off having no-teammates than bad ones, and a childer who's no good is a child who'll do you wrong.<br /> <br /> Look, if you want, a break-away faction of Settites that don't care for the ideology of the Followers of Set is fine, It's a fun bloodline that doesn't necessarily need the full baggage of Set, but don't give us a cult who gives it's members total and unrepentant freedom, that's not how cults work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T11:56:43-07:00","id":1441101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441098#post1441098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessary. Just joshing. You do seem to change stances from one post to the next sometimes, but I think that's mainly an artifact of each post only being a snippet about one aspect rather than an essay of everything you think about the clan. We're all in the same boat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah!<br /> <br /> I have deep thoughts about clans due to 25 years of gaming (since I was 16) and they're generally divided into three categories:<br /> <br /> * How the books present Clans<br /> * How I view the Clans<br /> * How I think the Clans SHOULD be presented<br /> <br /> Which can be confusing, I know.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also acknowledge everyone is free to use them however they want in their games and have their own preferences and biases that are subject to ST Interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T12:17:30-07:00","id":1441103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441100#post1441100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying they're utterly restrictive damnit. I'm just saying that &quot;<u>Many</u> Embraced into the clan abandon its ways, or are never taught them. These vampires are rarely sought for re-recruitment by their peers, and are in most cases allowed to do as they please....the clan does not force its creed on its children&quot; is absolutely fucking rediculous bonkers.<br /> <br /> These people are fucking <i>Vampires</i>. You don't live and let live as a God-Damned vampire. The Undead are not in the habbit of raising folks like a liberal arts college. You're better off having no-teammates than bad ones, and a childer who's no good is a child who'll do you wrong.<br /> <br /> Look, if you want, a break-away faction of Settites that don't care for the ideology of the Followers of Set is fine, It's a fun bloodline that doesn't necessarily need the full baggage of Set, but don't give us a cult who gives it's members total and unrepentant freedom, that's not how cults work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a live or let live thing so much as some vampires not being worth the effort. If some Settite is created and it's sire dies before fully indoctrinating it into the Cult of Set, the rest of the clan aren't going to devote resources to destroying it. As far as they are concerned, it's just some caitiff that happens to share their powers and weaknesses. At worst, it's irrelevant, and at best it distracts the real enemies of Set because they spy on it or hunt it without actually effecting REAL Settites at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T12:31:23-07:00","id":1441104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441100#post1441100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, if you want, a break-away faction of Settites that don't care for the ideology of the Followers of Set is fine, It's a fun bloodline that doesn't necessarily need the full baggage of Set, but don't give us a cult who gives it's members total and unrepentant freedom, that's not how cults work.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Anarch sourcebook, I'd argue that it isn't a cult, but a clan that created a cult to which its plurality belongs and by which its majority is conditioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T14:17:09-07:00","id":1441130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441103#post1441103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a live or let live thing so much as some vampires not being worth the effort. If some Settite is created and it's sire dies before fully indoctrinating it into the Cult of Set, the rest of the clan aren't going to devote resources to destroying it. As far as they are concerned, it's just some caitiff that happens to share their powers and weaknesses. At worst, it's irrelevant, and at best it distracts the real enemies of Set because they spy on it or hunt it without actually effecting REAL Settites at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually see this in the Clan Novels as Elizabeth is Hesha's childe. Hesha Embraces her and she is freaked the hell out by what he shows her and runs away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T14:45:58-07:00","id":1441132,"title":"","content":"But Setites embraced from within their cults so... <br /> <br /> Look, the bloodline is fine; Weakness to light Obfuscate, Presence and... I'd say Protean for anyone who wants to play someone not initiated in a cult (Serpentis, is in my view, Protean filtered through a lense of faith, and you just wouldn't learn it without having that faith) It's a great deal for any vampire, cult or not. The issue is when you don't call these folks social-caitiff or sectless setites and start calling them the Ministry. You just don't have a thousand different religions spring up after millenia of a relatively mainstream orthadoxy and it's parrallel relatives; Indian and Egyptian Setites gave us different ensembles but ultimately they gave us the same play; that simply isn't true for the Ministry, who believe in anything, You can have Fred the Settite start his own cult, with blackjack and hookers, but half the clan isn't going to decide to also make their own cults with a variety of alternatives and also band together to fight off some ultra-orthadox (hetradox, really) radical (reactionaries but first?) tea-party/black hand/puritan/SS setites. <br /> <br /> The ministry are so loose an organization that they shouldn't be an organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T14:55:30-07:00","id":1441133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1441132#post1441132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Setites embraced from within their cults so...<br /> <br /> Look, the bloodline is fine; Weakness to light Obfuscate, Presence and... I'd say Protean for anyone who wants to play someone not initiated in a cult (Serpentis, is in my view, Protean filtered through a lense of faith, and you just wouldn't learn it without having that faith) It's a great deal for any vampire, cult or not. The issue is when you don't call these folks social-caitiff or sectless setites and start calling them the Ministry. You just don't have a thousand different religions spring up after millenia of a relatively mainstream orthadoxy and it's parrallel relatives; Indian and Egyptian Setites gave us different ensembles but ultimately they gave us the same play; that simply isn't true for the Ministry, who believe in anything, You can have Fred the Settite start his own cult, with blackjack and hookers, but half the clan isn't going to decide to also make their own cults with a variety of alternatives and also band together to fight off some ultra-orthadox (hetradox, really) radical (reactionaries but first?) tea-party/black hand/puritan/SS setites.<br /> <br /> The ministry are so loose an organization that they shouldn't be an organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony is that I would actually feel this would be the case except for the fact that the Followers of Set were conceived with the exact scenario of the Ministry from 2nd Edition. Your argument depends on the idea that the Followers of Set have an orthodox interpretation of their religion that they have control over and never drifts. Also, that the locals would be fully indoctrinated to the religion of Set and never choose local traditions over the worship of Set. It's a fine position except that it's never been the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> THE PLAYERS GUIDE introduced the Followers of Set in 1991 and THE PLAYERS GUIDE TO THE SABBAT was done in 1992. The Players Guide to the Sabbat establishes that the Serpents of Light as a bunch of Followers of Set Blood Cultists Embraced from local Haitian branches of Voodoo corrupted by the Followers. The Serpents of Light rebelled due to their refusal to worship Set and give up their traditional religion. They then switched their allegiance to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So what happened there in your opinion and why couldn't it happen again if the Followers of Set decide to crack down and offend the other local cults?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T10:27:30-07:00","id":1457278,"title":"","content":"Maybe this thread's a bit old, but I've seen older restarted so it seems like it should be OK?<br /> <br /> <u>The Good</u><br /> <b>Hecata:</b> It\u2019s the fucked up insular family-centric dynastic politicking of the Giovanni (now with <i>more </i>fucked up dynastic politicking!) without sacrificing the forbidden scholar vibe of the Cappadocians or badass aesthetic of the Harbringers and Samedi. For that, I will forgive this clan anything. (The Nagaraja shouldn't be here though.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The So=So:</u><br /> <b>Tremere:</b> I love the new weakness, I like schisms and squabbling over how to rebuild, I don\u2019t like the new houses existing instead of building on the Anarch sorcerers. Put the Hermetic paradigm back on those vampires. <i>Put it back.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce: </b>Clan flaw is an improvement. Vicissitude is not and I feel it should\u2019ve been a ritual discipline building off protean. Again. Auspex. Put it back.<br /> Failing that, do a Hecata and make the choice to swap either Auspex or Protean out for Dominate, if you must play Old Clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador: </b>I guess? I prefered the old weakness perhaps, seeing as I despise Toreadors being the &quot;arts and social clubs&quot; clan. It's limiting when there are many other aspects of culture and society to get dangerously fixated over. Military, Politics, Religion, Science, History... Where are my mad scientist Toreadors whose concept of art is the Mass Spectrometer and they keep zoning out to gve lectures about molecular chemistry and what that means for our deepening understanding of the universe?? (OK, done being daft now)<br /> <br /> <b>Thin-bloods:</b> Their unique flaws and merits are good, but that alchemy stuff should be exceedingly rare. If not nonexistent.<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu:</b> The mental image of SchreckNET now being a mass of ancient languages and a new cipher every week is amusing to me. They're basically the same, as far as I remember.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Bad</u><br /> <b>Ravnos: </b><i>Put that DAV20 weakness back or so help me.</i><br /> (And while we're at it, put fortitude back.)<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra: </b>Obtenebration. Is. Not. Necromancy. Furthermore what are the antitrubu, chopped liver? Go join the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri:</b> Why are you still alive and annoying and why are your disciplines Like That. What happened to the other two guys?<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue: </b>Prefered the Ventrue weakness to be debilitating.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel: </b>What do you <i>mean</i> the traits are even less permanent than before??<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah:</b> Being a wide spectrum of idealogies and individuals, the idea that the Brujah quit enmasse is not appealing to me. They can't <i>all</i> be anti-establishment rebels, you'd just end up with the loss of the troublemakers and the Camarilla full of reformists and fiercely pro-Tradition guys who aren't strapped to the teeth in leather (plus the ones whose rage isn't focused on Anarch vs Cam, so had no need to leave).<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Ignored</u><br /> <b>Banu Haqim/Assamites:</b> I\u2019ve never cared about this clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian: </b>Malkavian weakness never reflects their insight as I imagine it anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Setites/Ministry</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-20-2021, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T23:15:48-07:00","id":1457368,"title":"","content":"The Good<br /> <b>Tzimisce</b>. What a mess but in a good way. Is this evolution or devolution. Both? best reimaging of a Clan other than the Hecata while still being faithful ever. <br /> <b>Tremere:</b> Cool story. I really like the idea of three main houses and the possibility of so many more. I like that there are more options than just hermetic.<br /> <b>Brujah: </b>Never understood why they were in the Camarilla. Glad to see a bigger presence in the Anarchs. Hoping they will play a bigger part in Sabbat leadership now that a large contingent of Lasombra have left. <br /> <b>Hecate: </b>Best ever!!!!!! The page count and the development of bloodlines for the Family really helps flesh out the Clan/Cult/Sect. More clans need this as V5 resets much of our expectations.<br /> <br /> Mixed:<br /> <b>Ravnos:</b> This is more Good than Bad. In fact over all I like the new Ravnos. I dislike, however how their Bane and torpor interact. Seems almost like certain death. Not cool. Kind of goes against the spirit of three turns and out as stated on page 130 of the core rulebook. Easy to house rule though. <br /> <br /> The Bad<br /> <b>Salubrie:</b> This is both my most loved and hated Clan throughout all editions and permutations. It has been a rollercoaster of love and hate. I recognize V5's attempt to return the Salubrie to their earliest incarnation where they were rare and unloved by all except a few. They have had so much more growth (and set backs) since those early days though. I feel like there was so much missed story opportunity. This is a clan that was destroyed through diablerie. They are ripe for a grand return as they eat their hosts from the inside out. (Maybe they are all in the Middle East and Baltic states) This is one of the times where I felt the descriptor they used for the clan when creating them really cut off concepts rather than opening them up. Hunted is more something that is done to someone than an adjective describing what a group are. Lastly, I feel the Salubrie Bane and its mandatory hunger frenzy test in all Cainites nearby diminishes player agency. I know Hunger frenzy is a thing in all kindred but this seems extreme. <br /> <br /> <b>No Gargoyles.</b> Gargoyles from Dark Ages: Vampire are my favorite. Head Canon: First Dusk-Born. This is a bloodline on the verge of being a full blooded clan. The first Gargoyle was created in the 12 or 1300's. Their eldest are pushing near to Methuselah age. Who says the Omen war didn't bump one or two Gargoyles into a low generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T00:34:32-07:00","id":1457370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457278#post1457278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Toreador: </b>I guess? I prefered the old weakness perhaps, seeing as I despise Toreadors being the &quot;arts and social clubs&quot; clan. It's limiting when there are many other aspects of culture and society to get dangerously fixated over. Military, Politics, Religion, Science, History... Where are my mad scientist Toreadors whose concept of art is the Mass Spectrometer and they keep zoning out to gve lectures about molecular chemistry and what that means for our deepening understanding of the universe?? (OK, done being daft now)</div> </div> </div> </div>Already baked into the concept, just...woefully underexplored. I can only speak for myself, but I've always adored toying with and stretching the clan's &quot;hat&quot; and flaw when playing one. The only thing that really precludes what you're suggesting, is the memetic, self-reinforcing, association of Toreador with the visual and performing arts.<br /> <br /> You can certainly also say that applies in-universe, because...well, Toreador tend to not be &quot;deep&quot; vampires, if you catch my meaning. To be blunt about it, a two-hundred-year-old, impulse embrace, himbo whose full extent of unlife is Elysium smack-talk <i>probably </i>doesn't have a bright enough bulb to think of say, stellar spectroscopy, in terms more complex than &quot;ooh pretty rainbow&quot;. You'll get rhetoricians, writers, and the occasional philosopher in the fold because they use their word-hole real pretty, but the full utility of that to the clan is going to be...well, Elysium smack-talk. Vampires just tend to not look beyond their own, largely socially constructed and socially reinforced, frames of reference for value in the embrace -- and when the odd embrace occurs outside that frame of reference, they either adapt through conformity or get outcast (something for which Toreador are notorious).<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to throw shade anywhere, I'm just pointing out the clan doesn't <i>really</i> have a predilection for intellectual pursuit...and where they <i>do</i>, it's generally instrumentalized to far more topical affairs. It's one thing I plan to play to the hilt in my Transylvania Chronicles game come the Renaissance, when the clan takes a good, hard look at the genius it embraces during it, and says to itself, &quot;nah, fuck these nerds&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457368#post1457368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Brujah: </b>Never understood why they were in the Camarilla. Glad to see a bigger presence in the Anarchs. Hoping they will play a bigger part in Sabbat leadership now that a large contingent of Lasombra have left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes perfect sense to me. You gotta remember the whole &quot;rebel without a cause&quot; shtick is just the facade they present and the lie they tell themselves. They're violent, power-hungry, reprobates who simply cloak themselves in whatever contemporary politics best justifies it. When they do luck into power, they invariably end up every bit the tyrants they claim the Ventrue to be and then some, ripe on the vine for the next generation of violent, power-hungry reprobates to overthrow. The only difference between a Sabbat, Camarilla, and Anarch Brujah, is their level of self-awareness and self-honesty...which to be frank, Anarch Brujah represent the <i>least</i> self-awareness and self-honesty among them all.<br /> <br /> And it's totally in-character for the clan. Brujah neither can nor should ever ask themselves, &quot;...are we the baddies?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T09:24:07-07:00","id":1457400,"title":"","content":"I feel the crux of the Brujah is they're angry about something that is worth getting angry over. Injustice, poverty, crime, environmentalism, or racism or whatever.<br /> <br /> It's just that they are cursed to react horribly badly with that anger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T09:41:18-07:00","id":1457402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457400#post1457400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the crux of the Brujah is they're angry about something that is worth getting angry over. Injustice, poverty, crime, environmentalism, or racism or whatever.<br /> <br /> It's just that they are cursed to react horribly badly with that anger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...No. <br /> <br /> The Brujah are angry and frequently embrace from the passionate: The discipline spread really suggests someone who likes to advance and take action into their own hands. There's nothing about the Brujah that suggests they're more inclined towards noble goals, at least compared to other clans. Selfishness is common, and nasty viewpoints are just as likely, if not more likely than whatever you deem noble. It's a dumb fucking idea to embrace someone who's pro-racial equality if you and all the local vampires enjoy taking advantage of ethnic disparity to make feeding easier and safer. There's simply less incentive to embrace &quot;noble&quot; brujah when you're a mother-fucking vampire who takes advantage of how bent the systems are. Even if you're against the prince and you're embracing these types to screw with him, you're alienating yourself from everyone in the city by doing so, and nobody's going to take kindly to your adoption of revolutionary types in someone's orderly government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T09:44:22-07:00","id":1457403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457400#post1457400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the crux of the Brujah is they're angry about something that is worth getting angry over. Injustice, poverty, crime, environmentalism, or racism or whatever.<br /> <br /> It's just that they are cursed to react horribly badly with that anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes.<br /> The way I see it, the beast is pure fight-or-flight instinct, and that instinct is <i>exhausting as fuck</i>. Especially when it lingers for months and won't switch off. Whatever particular pet peeve(s) the vampire has are unignorable and are guaranteed to drive them up the goddamn wall.<br /> <br /> You're stressed, you're tired, you can't do things because the beast keeps taking your control away ruining any chance of a &quot;life&quot;, you struggle not to fuck up your long term plans with frenzies, you can't trust yourself around the things and people that you care about because you'll lash out at them sooner or later... The Brujah don't have to recruit from mortal activists, you can embrace the most apathetic person on the planet and within a few weeks they'll either walk into the sun or be ready to make it their life's mission to crusade against whatever stimulus sets them off, just for some peace of mind (which they'll never get). Or at least to get whatever it is somewhere it won't annoy them<br /> <br /> But<i> w</i>hat sets them off won't necessarily be what<i> others </i>see as an injustice. A Brujah's idea of injustice could be totally narcissistic and have nothing whatsoever to do with social issues of any kind, only their own ego.<br /> <br /> It won't necessarily be about the cause, but the cause is useful for attaining that end goal of making the thing pissing you off go the fuck away. Plus, even if they truly support their cause, their definition of bigotry may be<i> very</i> different... The Brujah are going to be full of assholes in positions of control/enforcement (officially or self-appointed) punching down to keep the lessers in their place and proper society clean and orderly. Those in favour of the undesirables usually don't live as long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-22-2021, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T09:55:35-07:00","id":1457406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457400#post1457400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the crux of the Brujah is they're angry about something that is worth getting angry over. Injustice, poverty, crime, environmentalism, or racism or whatever.<br /> <br /> It's just that they are cursed to react horribly badly with that anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>no the crux of the brujah is that they're angry and looking for something to direct that anger at or an excuse to lash out, if it's really worth getting angry over doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T13:37:13-07:00","id":1457421,"title":"","content":"Iconoclast, Idealist, Individualist...the Brujah are known as the most varied clan for a reason. After revised they seem to have been increasingly flanderized into &quot;<i>vampires with causes&quot;</i> A Brujah with a cause is like a Lasombra in the church. It is a stereotype, but it is a stereotype for a reason. Often based on clan subculture and embrace practices, many Brujah have causes. But most do not.<br /> <br /> They just try to live their unlife to the best of their ability. They're not, or were not, supernaturally compelled towards having a curse. Many even deny that they frenzy easier than other clans, and can be set off by the suggestion that they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T16:16:41-07:00","id":1457431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457406#post1457406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no the crux of the brujah is that they're angry and looking for something to direct that anger at or an excuse to lash out, if it's really worth getting angry over doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quoting the Clan Books but the thing is, &quot;Ripping the head off whoever pisses you off&quot; isn't usually the best solution.<br /> <br /> The Brujah have the same problem as the Garou.<br /> <br /> Systemic racism and poverty aren't solved by mass murder. Usually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457402#post1457402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...No.<br /> <br /> The Brujah are angry and frequently embrace from the passionate: The discipline spread really suggests someone who likes to advance and take action into their own hands. There's nothing about the Brujah that suggests they're more inclined towards noble goals, at least compared to other clans. Selfishness is common, and nasty viewpoints are just as likely, if not more likely than whatever you deem noble. It's a dumb fucking idea to embrace someone who's pro-racial equality if you and all the local vampires enjoy taking advantage of ethnic disparity to make feeding easier and safer. There's simply less incentive to embrace &quot;noble&quot; brujah when you're a mother-fucking vampire who takes advantage of how bent the systems are. Even if you're against the prince and you're embracing these types to screw with him, you're alienating yourself from everyone in the city by doing so, and nobody's going to take kindly to your adoption of revolutionary types in someone's orderly government.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, that seems to be a flanderized &quot;Brujah don't have any motive beyond being pissed off&quot; version of them. While the &quot;Brujah are idealists that cannot do anything but react with fury to their problems&quot; is a more interesting take.<br /> <br /> Remember each of these curses is more than a surface detail to them.<br /> <br /> Brujah can never make positive change but that doesn't mean they don't WANT to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-22-2021, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T17:44:24-07:00","id":1457443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457400#post1457400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the crux of the Brujah is they're angry about something that is worth getting angry over. Injustice, poverty, crime, environmentalism, or racism or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...precisely how many Brujah strike out to embrace civil rights attorneys, environmental lobbyists, ED's of non-profs who run houseless or DV shelters, or whatever?<br /> <br /> Not bloody many, that's how many. People like that -- and those who follow Entelechy -- are the woeful exception, not the rule. Even though they're <i>supposedly</i> those whose high-minded ideals the Brujah claim to love <i>so much</i> would otherwise be #1 on the list. Nah, instead it's the black bloc protestors, hooligans, and all-talk firebrand professors who get the chomp-n-slurp. Cause you know, bringing people onboard with a sense of organizational competence, who might have the scantest capacity to effect real, long-term progress in these <i>so incredibly important</i> causes, is the &quot;Ventrue&quot; thing to do.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, there aren't many flower children in the ranks. Compared to the horde of beret-wearing, AK-toting, dynamite-slinging howlers who smash shit up, go home singing songs about how they stuck it to the man, and sit around doing fuck-all watching the shit they just smash get rebuilt, better and stronger next time, while the people they rage against just keep piling up the cash, favors, and power on the back of the broken window fallacy.<br /> <br /> Because it ain't about &quot;the cause, man&quot;. It's about finding a cause to infest like ideological tapeworms, that lets the Brujah say &quot;the end justifies the means&quot; and unleash their libidinous rage, completely self-assured they're not <i>really</i> bloodthirsty, parasitic, monsters. Just like every other damn vampire. And that's where the useful idiots come in, those poor deluded fucks who are either too young or plainly too damn stupid to do anything but be &quot;true believers&quot; in &quot;the cause&quot;...at the end of the night, useful idiocy is still idiocy.<br /> <br /> The absolute worst thing newer editions have done is to flanderize the Brujah, implicitly vindicating them on some myopic and shallow notion that because <i>some</i> of them <i>might </i>infest <i>commendable</i> causes (while conveniently ignoring or denying the mere existence of those who infest <i>reprehensible</i> causes), there must be <i>something</i> redeeming about them. And, that conversation about what they <i>really</i> do in &quot;pursuit&quot; of those causes -- or what happens when the worst-case scenario comes to pass, they succeed and find themselves in power -- just so happens to stay neatly overstepped. The clan of &quot;the revolution&quot; is <i>also</i> the clan of the &quot;reign of terror&quot;, &quot;purge&quot;, &quot;cultural revolution&quot;, end of story.<br /> <br /> They can call themselves &quot;iconoclasts&quot; all night long, but that doesn't erase the etymology of the word...and that word is ultimately a pejorative for a <i>very</i> good reason, regardless what historical revisionists with a tale to tell and a book to sell would have one believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-22-2021, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T19:23:31-07:00","id":1457445,"title":"","content":"The Brujah are parasites who latch onto causes and might talk a big game, but in the end they're monsters who make everything worse through their sheer existence. But that's true for any vampire from any clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T23:07:52-07:00","id":1457454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457431#post1457431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm quoting the Clan Books but the thing is, &quot;Ripping the head off whoever pisses you off&quot; isn't usually the best solution.<br /> <br /> The Brujah have the same problem as the Garou.<br /> <br /> Systemic racism and poverty aren't solved by mass murder. Usually.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't know what you're responding to but it sure isn't what you're quoted there. i can genuinely not figure out what this is supposed to prove in relation to what i said.<br /> <br /> i said that the brujah aren't tragic heroes forever cursed with self sabotage because of their anger because they're not heroes tragic or otherwise they're just angry assholes latching onto movements that gives them something to direct that anger at regardless if it's a good thing or an excusable thing to which you reply with &quot;their reactions of violent anger aren't good solutions to just causes&quot;. that doesn't even remotely disproves anything i said because that's perfectly in line with what i said. why are you so bad at arguing ma dude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T23:30:01-07:00","id":1457455,"title":"","content":"I.. guess it's a good thing that he's so optimistic about the True Nature of the Brujah? I can see where he's coming from. I mean, clearly the writers fall for their own propaganda sometimes. This &quot;optimistic&quot; imagining of the Brujah no doubt fits into the idea that the Brujah should leave the Cam, which is of course utter nonsense. <br /> Trully, the Brujah are thugs, but they've got Presence so you think they're good guys. It's not an accident that some of the clan want to distance themselves from the rest of the clan. The Brujah are violent, they're 100% geared towards violence, they only have Presence instead of Fortitude or Auspex because they want to drag as many comrades into the violence as they can. The clan weakness, to a small extent, cripples their ability to build themselves up, since they may just frenzy and kill their subordinates and blow their cover. They <i>need </i>the Camarilla to give them an ample framework of organized Violence and peace; the safety net is good for them. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, A Radical, progressive Brujah is going to... die. They're going to die miserably, and they're not going to be given the chance to embrace. The sire is using them, the prince wants them dead, the primogen want them dead, the people who they're at ideological odds with will want them dead, Vampire bystanders aren't exactly keen on them, and their allies are fleeting. Furthermore, a genuine true-believer activist likely doesn't have the will to survive as a blood sucking parasite that needs to lie and cheat all the time. The &quot;alleycat&quot; feeding style is very difficult to sustain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T01:09:41-07:00","id":1457458,"title":"","content":"People tend to moralise their anger and likes, so it makes sense to me that many Brujah consider their rage part of a cause. Even if the cause is oneself, because one is simply just special and <i>better</i> than everyone else<br /> <br /> Unless it's, say, the Anarch Free States, I find it off that the majority of Brujah aren't of a pro-authoritarian or pro-status quo bent. Brujah who see their sect as a beneficial thing to be exemplified and/or supported (or at least a step in the right direction, in need of reform... ), whose rage is directed at their enemies are at least useful. Those Brujah then go on to sire like-minded people. The disidents get culled<br /> <br /> That's not to say I'm against the rebels existing, but I think they're less common than many people I know seem to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-23-2021, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T02:30:41-07:00","id":1457461,"title":"","content":"Rather than Go Blow by blow through clans and their merits I'm going to go through the roughh design intent on V5 and comment on that bearing in mind I consider V5 is a soft reboot rather than a direct continuation I'm going to approach the clans with that in mind. I'm also going to try and ignore mechanical descisions where possible as well as sect issues.<br /> <br /> The good: Their's a clear shift towards away from defining clan culture by a single unique discipline. This is overall particulary present within Tzmisce. gangrel and Ravnos. I feel this does all clans a huge service since it provides groundwork for further writting. Clan Tzmisce especially benifit from this as the emphasis on classic vampire in modern setting allowing them to branch out from Necroscope body horror.<br /> <br /> The Meh: their's a tendancy to try and generalize the clans away from their cultural and historical backgrounds in game and to create more generic vampiric clans in the style of archeotypes-EG the Hecata as the spoopy skeliton clan as opposed to the complex culturally diverse bloodlines/clans which came before or downplaying Setite egyptian cultural heritidge. while this has a certain appeal since it brings the 7 supplementry clans into allignment with the origional 7 from 1st ed. While this does synergise the 13 clans a little better and allows for a more open style of play it ignores the developement all 13 clans have had over the last 20ish years and drains a lot of flavour from the setting.<br /> <br /> The Bad. The culling of unique disciplines doesnt really enhance or benifit the game in any sense, if anything it just creates supplementry complications in lore and mechanics as you're forced to react to the cultural and mechanical obligations of each individual clan and how they function in game. clan Lasombra and death clans have been particulary harmed by this as the idea they've been using the same discipline all along is absurd.<br /> <br /> The petty stuff which upsets me personally but isnt really an larger issue.<br /> -The Harbingers of Ashur, I waited 20 years to play a modern Cappadocian and V5 craps it's pants on the finish line by fusing them with the Harbingers and incorperating them into a less interesting clan... the puttanesca Get a unique mechanics up but the origional clan of death doesnt? thanks guys<br /> -Messing up the clan disciplines has made me transferring older characters into v5 an excersise in frustration<br /> -The Broken clan Tremere isnt a very interesting concept.<br /> -I prefered the nossies as so nightmarish looking they're a masquarade breach.<br /> -the ministry just sounds a like the prelude to a &quot;the ministry off....&quot; which make it sound like the 90's wrestling stable ministry of darkness or the ministry of sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-23-2021, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T04:42:05-07:00","id":1457468,"title":"","content":"I actually really like the idea of trying to globalize the clans to a greater degree. Eastern european-caricature Tzmisce, <s>Gypsy</s> <i>Indian</i> Ravnos, These are dumb ideas. However the culture-heavy Giovanni largely made sense and the Setites are an exquisite and fascinating group, The the Assamites had a really good political reason to stay put (everyone's scared shitless of these zealous murderers, and the black/grey skin that they believe marks them as judge, jury and executioner). The Bloodlines bound to a culture, like the Samedi, made sense because they're small and young and haven't had the chance to spread out so much. <br /> <br /> Did V5 do this well? <br /> Ha<br /> No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T05:18:43-07:00","id":1457471,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, how would everybody who prefers them so globalise the clans, going forward? I don't know how I'd do it, other than tweaking the lore to ignore the culture lock. Like everybody has always been everywhere (except the Giovanni, who are one specific family that spread and aquired extra ones, because otherwise they make zero sense)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-23-2021, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T06:15:34-07:00","id":1457472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457471#post1457471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, how would everybody who prefers them so globalise the clans? I don't know how I'd do it, other than tweaking the lore to ignore the culture lock.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the broadest-possible sense, the clans aren't really &quot;globalized&quot; in newer editions. They just have (often clumsily, admitted) cultural bases edited out, and cut-and-pasted into other cultures as befits <i>western</i> sensibilities and cultural archetypes. Ventrue are <i>always</i> the politicos (and in modern nights setting that means neoliberals), Lasombra are <i>always</i> the &quot;churchies&quot; (as befits predominantly western ideas of the relation between church and state), Toreador are <i>always</i> the artsy-fartsies (regardless of individual cultures' ideals about art), and the like. That, in itself, still represents a sticky wicket as it's merely interpreting cultures around the globe through the lens of eurocentrism, albeit benevolent eurocentrism.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see a more holistic and culturally-<i>aware</i> (as opposed to culturally &quot;sensitive&quot;) approach of how each clan's internal culture would fit within the scope of each national or regional culture. It makes, for example, exactly fuck-all sense for Ventrue to be obligatory political leaders, or Lasombra tied to ecclesiarchy, in cultures with strong histories of ancestor worship, astrology, or animism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T07:06:59-07:00","id":1457476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457472#post1457472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd rather see a more holistic and culturally-<i>aware</i> (as opposed to culturally &quot;sensitive&quot;) approach of how each clan's internal culture would fit within the scope of each national or regional culture. It makes, for example, exactly fuck-all sense for Ventrue to be obligatory political leaders, or Lasombra tied to ecclesiarchy, in cultures with strong histories of ancestor worship, astrology, or animism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see ventrue being the leaders in China (ancestor veneration, Astrology) and Japan (Animism) so I don't know what the f... Oh, you mean like... non urbanized people? Then yeah you don't really have a population to support more than Gangrel, Nosferatu or Ravnos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T09:42:12-07:00","id":1457484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457471#post1457471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, how would everybody who prefers them so globalise the clans, going forward? I don't know how I'd do it, other than tweaking the lore to ignore the culture lock. Like everybody has always been everywhere (except the Giovanni, who are one specific family that spread and aquired extra ones, because otherwise they make zero sense)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd actually do the opposite with regional bloodlines for example the Mla watu or the al-amin. Effectively the same clan but filtered through local culture","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T10:02:46-07:00","id":1457487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457484#post1457484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd actually do the opposite with regional bloodlines for example the Mla watu or the al-amin. Effectively the same clan but filtered through local culture</div> </div> </div> </div>That was near enough what I meant by &quot;everyone existed everywhere.&quot; Maybe I worded it badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T11:00:51-07:00","id":1457493,"title":"","content":"Of the 13 clans <br /> Five work absolutely anywhere there's a city. You need a minimum amount of creative energy to adjust them to wherever you are: Toreador, Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavian, Nosferatu. They're as culture-nuetral as can be, and you don't need to do anything to have them work in Berlin, Bagdhad or Beijing. <br /> <br /> Though they've very much fallen for modern, soulless, corperate culture, Ventrue are very much Rome fanboys. Thus, to match them to culture, all you need to do is switch out Rome for your -Favourite Empire/Dynasty here-. <br /> <br /> You can work any culture into having a Giovanni family. <br /> <br /> Short of shitty, contrived writing, or the Ventrue turning on them, the Tremere will rule the world. Yes, the Hermetic Paradigm is a western one, but it really encompasses all, and the Tremere will have no trouble adopting anyone of moderate faith. Different houses may have their little idiosyncresies <br /> <br /> The Lasombra love the sea because it's dark and cold, and often flock to religion with duality because Obtenebration's evil as fuck and puts the fear of God in them. Also they're control freaks because of the mirror weakness. Insert your best local Darkness/Light faith and they work anywhere. <br /> <br /> If Tzmisce are super polite because that's a trap, and they're just looking for an excuse to turn you into research materials. They like their own space because they do weird things. That can work... anywhere. It's quite easy to scrap the questionable eastern european naming scheme and stereotyping. I want to retcon the dependence on carpathia out of existence, best for everyone really. <br /> <br /> The Ravnos and their Dharma shtick is SuperFuckingInteresting and I'd be upset if it was ever removed from them. Their clan culture basically stems from their vice. Vices give them a difficult relationship with humanity, which makes them jealous of people who can much more easily pull of humanity, which in turn gave them the idea that you should find your fate and stop pretending to be something you're not, and that Humane vampires are failed abominations that reject their alloted path. This is the most genius fucking spiral of self hate and I love it. That said you don't need the hindu terminology for it to function, and they could work anywhere, really. <br /> <br /> The Followers of Set were perfect the way they are. (as Followers of Set. Church/Ministry? Less so) <br /> <br /> The issue with the Assamites is that half of them think they're Judge, Jury and executioner. That's their deal, and it ruins it for the rest of the Assamites, but it also makes the Assamites super interesting. So, most vampires are going to want them the fuck out of their territory/dead. Thus they work best living in fortresses or... like vampire hunters, perhaps intimidating the prince who knows that if the local cell is killed, the Assamites will ravage the city in retribution. Assamites should embrace localy, they should probably have more big fortresses than just Amalut (and perhaps more schisms; methuselah rivalries?) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T14:36:06-07:00","id":1457514,"title":"","content":"So how I usually handle the clans is that I start from the mysterious time after the Second City and work my way out from there.<br /> <br /> Every clan gets its fangs wet in Mesopotamia. They all have some presence there although many flow outward. Clans like the Gangrel and the Nosferatu particularly spread out but every clan does. Where the founder goes effects the pyramid shape of a clan\u2019s distribution. West Asia continues to host many of the clans and their founders; particularly the Brujah, Malkavians, Toreador, &amp; Ventrue. You have the Assamites concentrate around the Iranian Plateau, the Cappadocians in Anatolia, the Lasombra in the Mediterranean, the Ravnos in South Asia, the Salubri eastward, the Tzimisce in Eastern Europe, etc.<br /> <br /> So from the early days you have clans going everywhere and so they acclimate themselves to the culture of their host region and perpetuate that through embracing out of their home region.<br /> <br /> While the territories around the Silk Road would be the artery of vampiric civilization for most of history, every clan would manifest in its own way in different places, although always with a through line derived from their Founder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T05:28:41-07:00","id":1457568,"title":"","content":"I very much <b>appreciate </b>the rework of the <b>Hecata</b>. I thought it was a terrible Idea. I bought the book. Turned out great. <br /> <br /> I strongly <b>dislike </b>almost everything done to the <b>Tremere</b>. I can understand some of the ideas, but to me nothing turned out appealing or usable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T08:22:41-07:00","id":1457577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457476#post1457476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see ventrue being the leaders in China (ancestor veneration, Astrology) and Japan (Animism) so I don't know what the f... Oh, you mean like... non urbanized people? Then yeah you don't really have a population to support more than Gangrel, Nosferatu or Ravnos.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do I elucidate this...<br /> <br /> No individual culture sprang into existence, fully-formed, in an industrialized or urbanized context. All cultures were preindustrial at some point, and industrial/postindustrial societies are built upon historico-cultural contexts that inform them. In WoD, the current &quot;niches&quot; vampire clans nominally occupy are informed by those contexts, and how each individual clan has adapted to the ages over time.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, Ventrue aren't &quot;rulers&quot; just because they one night collectively decided writ nothing they were going to be &quot;rulers&quot;; the clan leveraged its military might through mortal pawns in the Dark Ages into feudal wealth, leveraged that feudal wealth and influence through the Renaissance to reform as an aristocratic, mercantile, clan, then leveraged its mercantile influence to rebuild itself into the political class of the Modern era through the rise of western liberal democracy.<br /> <br /> The stark reality is, the Ventrue are a relic. Their flaw and discipline spread are representative of the era of hard power, empire, and serfdom. They've only been able to navigate the transition from Dark Ages to post-industrialism, by leveraging institutional momentum to preserve their grasp on power. All things being equal, they're neither positioned or endowed to negotiate the postmodern climate of soft power, negotiation and dealmaking, and fluidity in alliance particularly well, least of all in comparison to <i>other</i> clans that could readily supplant them if so-inclined.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean when I say the clans' &quot;hats&quot; are necessarily eurocentric. Clans' archetypes can only be fully understood in that specific European historico-cultural context. So what of other continents, regions, and cultures in which that specific causal chain from the fall of Rome to the invention of the steam engine didn't happen, or didn't happen in that precise order? Where <i>would</i> the clans, for their flaws and discipline spreads, <i>really</i> fall in those historico-cultural contexts, thereby granting the institutional momentum they would carry from prehistoric or preindustrial times into modern nights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-24-2021, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T08:58:28-07:00","id":1457578,"title":"","content":"Thats a lot of fallacies right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T09:01:46-07:00","id":1457579,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019re gonna throw that out there MWIS than can you at least grant us the benefit of hearing your case for why Theodrim\u2019s claims are fallacies instead of what amounts to basically thread crudding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T09:20:24-07:00","id":1457581,"title":"","content":"if it isn't obvious then sure. <br /> <br /> The Ventrue are just built to be really good with people. no other clan has two hard-social disciplines, and they have Fortitude just so they can stand out and lead while not worrying about being sniped or blown up or sneak attacked or what have you. They're the perfect officer, the perfect merchant, the perfect leader. Doesn't matter where they are, if there are people, they are going to excell. The Clan weakness encourages them to go all in on those people skills. Building up friends, resources and reputation to protect the herd. Is there a culture that does not care for friends, resources, reputation? There is not, so why would the Ventrue only work in Europe? Why would it need a drastic change to work in, say, the Golden Horde, the Tang Dynasty, or the Mali empire? How the fuck can you possibly conclude that the Ventrue are a relic when their abilities so perfectly compliment the modern oligarchy? The dude just wants to project his opinions on a class he doesnt like and ascribe these faults to the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T12:16:37-07:00","id":1457586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457577#post1457577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stark reality is, the Ventrue are a relic. Their flaw and discipline spread are representative of the era of hard power, empire, and serfdom. They've only been able to navigate the transition from Dark Ages to post-industrialism, by leveraging institutional momentum to preserve their grasp on power. All things being equal, they're neither positioned or endowed to negotiate the postmodern climate of soft power, negotiation and dealmaking, and fluidity in alliance particularly well, least of all in comparison to <i>other</i> clans that could readily supplant them if so-inclined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with MWIS - this paragraph is bollocks. Ventrue are vampires in absolute EZ Mode. Their one-two Dom-Pres Discipline set allows them to infiltrate, assimilate, assuage, inspire and/or rule anyone, anywhere, in any time period. That alone makes them wholly formidable individually, but when you toss in the survivability of a Gangrel plus their clan's solid history of Ivy League West Point Bro Code...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T13:12:00-07:00","id":1457590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457581#post1457581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it isn't obvious then sure.<br /> <br /> ...no other clan has two hard-social disciplines, and they have Fortitude just so they can stand out and lead while not worrying about being sniped or blown up or sneak attacked or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where your misunderstanding shines. Half the clans in the game have &quot;two hard-social&quot; disciplines, and almost all of them lack monstrous Achilles' heels on the scale of the Ventrue as a clan flaw.<br /> <br /> You're discounting the role Auspex plays as a social discipline. Because it allows a vampire to more easily discern social cues and non-verbal communication -- giving the vampire a leg-up figuring out their &quot;tells&quot; in gambling parlance -- at level one, detect emotions at level two, and at level four it provides means to literally read another's thoughts. And of course at level five it's the most powerful espionage and information-asymmetry power in the game, bar none.<br /> <br /> And its danger sense allows a vampire to detect and avoid &quot;being sniped or blown up or sneak attacked or what have you&quot; in the first place. Don't have to soak from an attack you weren't around to take.<br /> <br /> The critical thing you're missing, is that increasingly since the Enlightenment era but especially since the dawn of the Cold War, is that <i>soft</i> power rules the world. Nuclear weapons didn't &quot;win&quot; the Cold War, Coca-Cola and McDonald's did. And accordingly, <i>information</i> and <i>psychological </i>warfare wins conflicts, not <i>military</i> warfare. That's not merely in the realm of international relations and conflict resolution, it manifests itself in practically every aspect of contemporary culture and <i>especially</i> the corporate cultures where true power in western society lies.<br /> <br /> Dominate and Presence are a powerful combination, don't get me wrong. But it's a combination that represents the exercise of <i>hard</i> power in a world defined and ruled by <i>soft</i> power. And it's a <i>redundant</i> combination, as typified no better by the very Ventrue who seek to exercise power and resolve conflicts through one or the other, but <i>rarely</i> both in tandem.<br /> <br /> That's taking entirely out of consideration three full levels of Presence -- Dread Gaze, Summon, and Majesty -- are manifestations of <i>hard</i> power.<br /> <br /> Auspex and one of the two is a more powerful combination by orders of magnitude in contemporary society. You'll find no better diplomat, negotiator, or arbitrator than one literally capable of figuring out opposing parties' initial positions, available leverage, final negotiation positions they'd be willing to accept, BATNA, how they perceive ongoing negotiations and their perceived strength relative to the other party, and any trump cards they have remaining up their sleeve, at a literal glance.<br /> <br /> And you'll have opposition parties walking away from the table feeling considerably better about the deal made, than had you played hardball the entire time or screwed them in a way they'll figure out later. Which means they won't be looking for payback later down the line.<br /> <br /> <i>Toreador</i>, were they so-inclined, would make for better &quot;Ventrue&quot; than the damn Ventrue in a late-20th Century or early-21st Century setting. For all intents and purposes, they already are -- they command the Camarilla's internal power structure simply by being the determiners of status and prestation. <i>Nobody</i> plays &quot;let's make a deal&quot; better than the Toreador (again, when they're so inclined). Hell, Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> would make for better &quot;Ventrue&quot; than the damn Ventrue because they give up one redundant discipline for <i>Auspex</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is not, so why would the Ventrue only work in Europe? Why would it need a drastic change to work in, say, the Golden Horde, the Tang Dynasty, or the Mali empire? </div> </div> </div>Well, when your entire framework of how one secures and preserves political influence is entirely upended by a couple dots in common blood sorcery paths...Dominate and Presence would only go so far in, say, animist or ancestor-worship cultures, compared to vampires who can <i>literally summon and control what the mortals worship</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look Sir Fucksalot, you can drop Majesty all you like. I have True Faith, don't have to sleep during the day and don't explode in sunlight, and that vampire over there literally just summoned my god. If they say you gotta go, you gotta go.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is exactly why and how we ended up with goofball shit like the Danava. &quot;Ventrue, just Ventrue whose power can be justifiably explained in a culture in which the traditional origins of their power mean precisely fuck-all&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How the fuck can you possibly conclude that the Ventrue are a relic when their abilities so perfectly compliment the modern oligarchy? </div> </div> </div>Literally just said why. They <i>already had</i> the power, prestige, money, and influence, and leveraged that institutional momentum to successfully transition as culture and society shifted. We already know what would have happened to the Ventrue were it not for the rise and prosperity of the Holy Roman Empire: they're called the Tzimisce. This isn't about who had the power, prestige, money and influence today, it's about who had the power, prestige, money and influence a thousand years ago, and carried it to today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The dude just wants to project his opinions on a class he doesnt like and ascribe these faults to the Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>Hardly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-24-2021, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T01:08:29-07:00","id":1457629,"title":"","content":"Auspex is not a <i>hard</i> social discipline, it's a discipline with some social features. <i>All </i>disciplines have some social features. Celerity? Watch me dance. Potence? Worship my strength. Protean? Aren't I scary. Obviously I'm saying it's a <i>hard </i>social discipline because every fuckin' power is geared towards the direct manipulation of others.<br /> <br /> Auspex 1, at least by V20, <i>does absolutely nothing concerning social cues</i>. You've misunderstood it. Auspex 2 isn't dynamic enough to be used regularly within the same conversation; Difficulty 8 is hard, and the difficulty increases more with each use on the same person. Auspex 4 is neat, but having to go in for a 4th dot for your first carry-worthy social skill is not. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Obfuscate 3 is really nice, but that's the only social skill Obfuscate has, and it's the third level. However, A single strong persona is better for the Ventrue than multiple weak ones. </span><br /> <br /> Fortitude is better than Auspex or Obfuscate for people skills! Why? Well someone with Auspex avoids the threat, and in doing so hides from his own people. Someone with Fortitude? You can show absolute contempt for the threat. In 1912 Someone shot Teddy Rosevelt Just before his speech. He went through with his speech: Absolute legend. If he hid instead knowing there's a gunman after him, or otherwise had the event disrupted, he'd instead lose reputation. Fortitude lets you put yourself out there. It lets you be a hero.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue Clan flaw isn't anywhere near as big a deal as you think it is, unless you've got a taste for something rare and difficult to control. Really, the flaw drives Ventrue to work together and excel. What does a Ventrue need most to alleviate his curse? Backgrounds. What do Ventrue and their amazing people skills excel at most? Acquiring backgrounds. Ethnic group? Foster a community for them, encourage them to have more kids. Amputees? Reintroduce corporal punishment, or set yourself up at a hostpital/Veteran gathering site. Virgins? Encourage and fund those weird &quot;Christian&quot; abstinence groups, or anime. A vampire should always be trying to rig the game in their favour, and the Ventrue are the extreme of that.<br /> <br /> I don't understand your soft power/Hard power fallacy. The Ventrue make friends, therefore they have soft power. They have friends, therefore they have access to information networks. I feel like you're trying to convince me the moon landings were faked, when even the soviets congratulated NASA. You don't look as clever as you think you do, suggesting Ventrue ineptitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, when your entire framework of how one secures and preserves political influence is entirely upended by a couple dots in common blood sorcery paths...Dominate and Presence would only go so far in, say, animist or ancestor-worship cultures, compared to vampires who can <i>literally summon and control what the mortals worship</i>. </div> </div> </div>It took me a while to realize you're serious and don't know what a bad fucking idea this is. It's a good thing I noticed or I woulda said some horrible things.<br /> <br /> 1-Thaumaturgy either requires you to study really fucking hard, be a true believer, or some combination of both. The former means you've got to spend a lot of time as a shut-in, the later means you're unlikely to call upon a mainstream deity for personal gain.<br /> 2-You aren't summoning &quot;gods&quot; till at minimum the third dot of thaumaturgy, while Dominate and Presence are strong from the first level. Ventrue are a lot easier to raise than thaumaturges.<br /> 3- Dominate and presence directly control the crowd, Thaumaturgy is just wowing the crowd. The Ventrue's subjects are loyal to the Ventrue, The theurge's subjects are loyal to the deity. People will rapidly turn on the Theurge if someone exposes them as a cheat/usurper/heretic/demon. As for Dominate and Presence? Well, loyal is loyal, almost doesn't matter what the Ventrue did.<br /> 4-The Ventrue can directly control the thaumaturge. The Thaumaturge can't directly control the Ventrue (blood bond excluded) The Ventrue can also command the Theurge's followers to betray their priest.<br /> <br /> Necromancy is nine ways worse and one way better- you can talk to ancestor ghosts early on, so it's less an investment. But, in case you missed it, it's otherwise ... worse in every aspect. If you've paid attention to TV you should know that you can probably just bullshit that you can talk to ghosts and get similar results.<br /> <br /> Do you play with some heavy houserules for Dominate/Presence? You really seem to be underselling these extremely powerful disciplines.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Look Sir Fucksalot, you can drop Majesty all you like. I have True Faith, don't have to sleep during the day and don't explode in sunlight, and that vampire over there literally just summoned my god. If they say you gotta go, you gotta go.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Well, if True faith was good against the legion of Ventrue-adoring henchmen, which it isn't, then the Ventrue might have a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-25-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T02:19:59-07:00","id":1457631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457590#post1457590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where your misunderstanding shines. Half the clans in the game have &quot;two hard-social&quot; disciplines, and almost all of them lack monstrous Achilles' heels on the scale of the Ventrue as a clan flaw.<br /> <br /> You're discounting the role Auspex plays as a social discipline. Because it allows a vampire to more easily discern social cues and non-verbal communication -- giving the vampire a leg-up figuring out their &quot;tells&quot; in gambling parlance -- at level one, detect emotions at level two, and at level four it provides means to literally read another's thoughts. And of course at level five it's the most powerful espionage and information-asymmetry power in the game, bar none.<br /> <br /> And its danger sense allows a vampire to detect and avoid &quot;being sniped or blown up or sneak attacked or what have you&quot; in the first place. Don't have to soak from an attack you weren't around to take.<br /> <br /> The critical thing you're missing, is that increasingly since the Enlightenment era but especially since the dawn of the Cold War, is that <i>soft</i> power rules the world. Nuclear weapons didn't &quot;win&quot; the Cold War, Coca-Cola and McDonald's did. And accordingly, <i>information</i> and <i>psychological </i>warfare wins conflicts, not <i>military</i> warfare. That's not merely in the realm of international relations and conflict resolution, it manifests itself in practically every aspect of contemporary culture and <i>especially</i> the corporate cultures where true power in western society lies.<br /> <br /> Dominate and Presence are a powerful combination, don't get me wrong. But it's a combination that represents the exercise of <i>hard</i> power in a world defined and ruled by <i>soft</i> power. And it's a <i>redundant</i> combination, as typified no better by the very Ventrue who seek to exercise power and resolve conflicts through one or the other, but <i>rarely</i> both in tandem.<br /> <br /> That's taking entirely out of consideration three full levels of Presence -- Dread Gaze, Summon, and Majesty -- are manifestations of <i>hard</i> power.<br /> <br /> Auspex and one of the two is a more powerful combination by orders of magnitude in contemporary society. You'll find no better diplomat, negotiator, or arbitrator than one literally capable of figuring out opposing parties' initial positions, available leverage, final negotiation positions they'd be willing to accept, BATNA, how they perceive ongoing negotiations and their perceived strength relative to the other party, and any trump cards they have remaining up their sleeve, at a literal glance.<br /> <br /> And you'll have opposition parties walking away from the table feeling considerably better about the deal made, than had you played hardball the entire time or screwed them in a way they'll figure out later. Which means they won't be looking for payback later down the line.<br /> <br /> <i>Toreador</i>, were they so-inclined, would make for better &quot;Ventrue&quot; than the damn Ventrue in a late-20th Century or early-21st Century setting. For all intents and purposes, they already are -- they command the Camarilla's internal power structure simply by being the determiners of status and prestation. <i>Nobody</i> plays &quot;let's make a deal&quot; better than the Toreador (again, when they're so inclined). Hell, Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> would make for better &quot;Ventrue&quot; than the damn Ventrue because they give up one redundant discipline for <i>Auspex</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, when your entire framework of how one secures and preserves political influence is entirely upended by a couple dots in common blood sorcery paths...Dominate and Presence would only go so far in, say, animist or ancestor-worship cultures, compared to vampires who can <i>literally summon and control what the mortals worship</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look Sir Fucksalot, you can drop Majesty all you like. I have True Faith, don't have to sleep during the day and don't explode in sunlight, and that vampire over there literally just summoned my god. If they say you gotta go, you gotta go.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is exactly why and how we ended up with goofball shit like the Danava. &quot;Ventrue, just Ventrue whose power can be justifiably explained in a culture in which the traditional origins of their power mean precisely fuck-all&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Literally just said why. They <i>already had</i> the power, prestige, money, and influence, and leveraged that institutional momentum to successfully transition as culture and society shifted. We already know what would have happened to the Ventrue were it not for the rise and prosperity of the Holy Roman Empire: they're called the Tzimisce. This isn't about who had the power, prestige, money and influence today, it's about who had the power, prestige, money and influence a thousand years ago, and carried it to today.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hardly.</div> </div> </div> </div>i tried to explain what you got wrong point by point but really it's just all wrong you also seem to be under the impression that presence is a bad long term discipline because it's &quot;hard power&quot; but that only seems to be an issue for the ventrue and not the toreador and also auspex is the most amazing perfect discipline in existence and it is a great discipline but it's not a make or break discipline like your making it out to be. you cn use it to gether information for social interactionsbut that doesn't make it a social discipline, by that logic auspex is also a combat, financial and space travel discipline.<br /> <br /> it's ok to not like the ventrue but this reads like you started at &quot;i don't like X there for it's shit,&quot; and worked from there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T07:10:35-07:00","id":1457635,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturge: &quot;God Has Granted me Power&quot; (performs magic trick) <br /> *Crowd silent in awe*<br /> Ventrue: *smiles* <br /> *crowd cheers in rapturous adulation* <br /> <br /> The Ventrue have always been (from an in-character perspective) everyone's favourite clan. With nonchalance, they've given their chief rivals (Brujah/Lasombra) an inferiority complex. They're not known to be fickle like the Toreador, less overbearing than the Tremere, and they aren't part of a snake-worshipping cult of corruption. Even when they're screwing you, you can't help but admire them, and as friends, there aren't better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T07:30:38-07:00","id":1457636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457431#post1457431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, that seems to be a flanderized &quot;Brujah don't have any motive beyond being pissed off&quot; version of them. While the &quot;Brujah are idealists that cannot do anything but react with fury to their problems&quot; is a more interesting take.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've moved on and all but I came back to this and was intrigued. You see, to me, the Brujah are like the Toreador or the Malkavians. A toreador can have their subjective tastes influence beauty (to a degree, I really advocate for mostly-universal beauty with Toreador so I don't get a bunch of &quot;Um-Aksually&quot;) A Malkavian can have nine different flavours of madness, and a Brujah can be angry about a lot of different things.<br /> <br /> But... every member of these clans is fighting for their own goals. These clans have very loose structures, functioning like a safety net/ social support network, they're not unified towards goals like Nosferatu, Tremere or Ventrue. The Brujah, the Malkavians, the Toreador... they're individuals looking for their lot in unlife. They're vampires. Their goals are more resources, a bigger domain, a larger herd, better retainers, victory over rivals... They don't necessary need a grand narrative of Smash the State/ Cure me / This is art. Thinking they do is the real &quot;Flanderization&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Remember each of these curses is more than a surface detail to them.<br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Pre V5, the Beast didn't influence normal actions. You can feel it bubble to the surface, and a Brujah will feel that more, but they're not going to talk like Bruce banner supressing the incredible hulk all the time. If anything, I think Brujah should be naturally inclined to looking inconspicuous, acting affable, and not inviting trouble until they want trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T16:41:19-07:00","id":1457658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457629#post1457629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<i>All </i>disciplines have some social features. Celerity? Watch me dance. Potence? Worship my strength. Protean? Aren't I scary. Obviously I'm saying it's a <i>hard </i>social discipline because every fuckin' power is geared towards the direct manipulation of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what you're saying is...nothing, really. By the strawman you've built, Presence is a <i>combat</i> discipline being that three of its powers are combat powers or have combat resolutions. And guess what, all five Auspex powers can and do have applications in manipulating others -- even Spirit's Touch, something I have yet to even broach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Auspex 1, at least by V20, <i>does absolutely nothing concerning social cues</i>. You've misunderstood it. </div> </div> </div>No, it does precisely that, by RAW. It's not incumbent upon me to justify how you don't -- or won't -- see it, or lack the imagination to weaponize Heightened Senses thus. An increase in the acuity of senses that grants a difficulty bonus on rolls related to that sense, most notably Perception-based checks...of which nearly all actions to determine motive, sense deception, or simply get a read on another's emotions or mental state, are. It's not as if there's an entire Talent called Empathy in the game that exists for this exclusive purpose, or anything.<br /> <br /> Because visual and aural acuity will <i>certainly</i> aid another detect body language, facial tics, subtle changes in tone of voice, fidgeting, sidelong glances, or in some cases changes in depth and rapidity of breathing, all of which are -- you guessed it -- <i>social cues</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Auspex 2 isn't dynamic enough to be used regularly within the same conversation... </div> </div> </div>Doesn't have to be. A single read at the start of a scene will tell a character precisely how another feels moving into it. From there it's a simple matter of discerning the &quot;how&quot; and more importantly &quot;why&quot;. Next.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well someone with Auspex avoids the threat, and in doing so hides from his own people. </div> </div> </div>How convenient you read that in the one light that best suits your argument. As opposed to more subtle actions like ensuring one isn't in a likely line of fire, watching out for and avoiding likely explosives, employing pawns to ferret out the threat before it manifests, or any other number of avoidance tactics that preclude that attack about to be made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1912 Someone shot Teddy Rosevelt Just before his speech. He went through with his speech: Absolute legend. If he hid instead knowing there's a gunman after him, or otherwise had the event disrupted, he'd instead lose reputation. </div> </div> </div>In 1912 someone shot Teddy Roosevelt...with a .38 special, a round notably low in stopping power even for its day. In the chest, through which the round penetrated a steel eyeglass case and a folded copy of his 50-page speech, resulting in a shallow flesh wound that Roosevelt himself was able to diagnose on the spot with only his experience as a hunter. &quot;Absolute legend&quot;, indeed.<br /> <br /> So congratulations on reminding everyone in the thread that not only do armor dice exist, they neither have an experience cost nor are locked behind access to a discipline.<br /> <br /> And that one should probably not botch a Firearms roll, when one has a snarky ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue Clan flaw isn't anywhere near as big a deal as you think it is... </div> </div> </div>So pray tell, what happens when a Ventrue puts their fingerprints on everything, leaving a nice, neat social and electronic trail for anyone with the least experience navigating the Jyhad to follow, leading directly to their herd and feeding preference? I highly doubt <i>someone</i> here has seen a sustained, direct attack on a Ventrue's herd play out in game, and it ain't me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand your soft power/Hard power fallacy. </div> </div> </div>Likely because you don't seem to understand what soft power is in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue make friends, therefore they have soft power. They have friends, therefore they have access to information networks. </div> </div> </div>Friends, or allies who share transient shared goals? Because &quot;everyone likes the Ventrue&quot; is quite possibly the biggest straw man I have yet to see in this thread, being that it is but the first turn of logic that's becoming increasingly circular by the post. If by &quot;everyone&quot; we mean the true believers of one sect, who are at most a plurality of not even half that sect's clans, I suppose that might be a true statement, but cherry-picking and goalpost-moving aside we can see quite clearly from the mere existence of the Anarch Free State and Anarchs' -- most of whom <i>used to be</i> Camarilla -- general opinions towards the Ventrue, precisely the impact Ventrue &quot;friendship&quot; has over the long run.<br /> <br /> Because the word you're desperately trying to avoid, which I have yet to employ but have stated all but directly, is &quot;blowback&quot;. And the Ventrue are very, <i>very</i>, good at generating blowback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1-Thaumaturgy either requires you to study really fucking hard, be a true believer, or some combination of both. The former means you've got to spend a lot of time as a shut-in, the later means you're unlikely to call upon a mainstream deity for personal gain. </div> </div> </div>The genuine irony of this is you directly stated &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot;, which is the domain of one and precisely one clan, among all possible forms of blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> And what are the Tremere's <i>other</i> two disciplines?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2-You aren't summoning &quot;gods&quot; till at minimum the third dot of thaumaturgy, while Dominate and Presence are strong from the first level. Ventrue are a lot easier to raise than thaumaturges... </div> </div> </div>Again, acting as if blood sorcerers have one and only one clan discipline. When the reality is, almost all of them have Auspex and/or at least one social discipline among them. We're to now pretend Ventrue are the only clan with three clan disciplines?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you play with some heavy houserules for Dominate/Presence? You really seem to be underselling these extremely powerful disciplines. </div> </div> </div>I mean, considering everything you just posted, you tell me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457631#post1457631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i tried to explain what you got wrong point by point but really it's just all wrong you also seem to be under the impression that presence is a bad long term discipline because it's &quot;hard power&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the opposite. Presence is one of my favorite disciplines in the game. I just don't put on rose-tinted glasses about it, and see it for what it is and what it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but that only seems to be an issue for the ventrue and not the toreador... </div> </div> </div>Because the Ventrue have a redundant discipline spread whereas the Toreador do not. As I stated earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and also auspex is the most amazing perfect discipline in existence and it is a great discipline but it's not a make or break discipline like your making it out to be. </div> </div> </div>Auspex is, in my opinion, the most powerful single discipline in the game, yes. Because of its versatility and general utility. It's to mental and social disciplines what Celerity is to physical. And indeed when used properly, it really is that powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...you cn use it to gether information for social interactionsbut that doesn't make it a social discipline, by that logic auspex is also a combat, financial and space travel discipline. </div> </div> </div>...yeah?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's ok to not like the ventrue but this reads like you started at &quot;i don't like X there for it's shit,&quot; and worked from there </div> </div> </div>Ventrue is one of my favorite clans actually, behind Lasombra anyways. It's not my most-played clan by a longshot, which is a tie between Lasombra and Toreador, but it's definitely #3. I just don't put on rose-tinted glasses about them, and see them for what they are and what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-25-2021, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T22:49:48-07:00","id":1457686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457658#post1457658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what you're saying is...nothing, really. By the strawman you've built, Presence is a <i>combat</i> discipline being that three of its powers are combat powers or have combat resolutions. And guess what, all five Auspex powers can and do have applications in manipulating others -- even Spirit's Touch, something I have yet to even broach.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, it does precisely that, by RAW. It's not incumbent upon me to justify how you don't -- or won't -- see it, or lack the imagination to weaponize Heightened Senses thus. An increase in the acuity of senses that grants a difficulty bonus on rolls related to that sense, most notably Perception-based checks...of which nearly all actions to determine motive, sense deception, or simply get a read on another's emotions or mental state, are. It's not as if there's an entire Talent called Empathy in the game that exists for this exclusive purpose, or anything.<br /> <br /> Because visual and aural acuity will <i>certainly</i> aid another detect body language, facial tics, subtle changes in tone of voice, fidgeting, sidelong glances, or in some cases changes in depth and rapidity of breathing, all of which are -- you guessed it -- <i>social cues</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doesn't have to be. A single read at the start of a scene will tell a character precisely how another feels moving into it. From there it's a simple matter of discerning the &quot;how&quot; and more importantly &quot;why&quot;. Next.<br /> <br /> <br /> How convenient you read that in the one light that best suits your argument. As opposed to more subtle actions like ensuring one isn't in a likely line of fire, watching out for and avoiding likely explosives, employing pawns to ferret out the threat before it manifests, or any other number of avoidance tactics that preclude that attack about to be made.<br /> <br /> <br /> In 1912 someone shot Teddy Roosevelt...with a .38 special, a round notably low in stopping power even for its day. In the chest, through which the round penetrated a steel eyeglass case and a folded copy of his 50-page speech, resulting in a shallow flesh wound that Roosevelt himself was able to diagnose on the spot with only his experience as a hunter. &quot;Absolute legend&quot;, indeed.<br /> <br /> So congratulations on reminding everyone in the thread that not only do armor dice exist, they neither have an experience cost nor are locked behind access to a discipline.<br /> <br /> And that one should probably not botch a Firearms roll, when one has a snarky ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> So pray tell, what happens when a Ventrue puts their fingerprints on everything, leaving a nice, neat social and electronic trail for anyone with the least experience navigating the Jyhad to follow, leading directly to their herd and feeding preference? I highly doubt <i>someone</i> here has seen a sustained, direct attack on a Ventrue's herd play out in game, and it ain't me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Likely because you don't seem to understand what soft power is in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friends, or allies who share transient shared goals? Because &quot;everyone likes the Ventrue&quot; is quite possibly the biggest straw man I have yet to see in this thread, being that it is but the first turn of logic that's becoming increasingly circular by the post. If by &quot;everyone&quot; we mean the true believers of one sect, who are at most a plurality of not even half that sect's clans, I suppose that might be a true statement, but cherry-picking and goalpost-moving aside we can see quite clearly from the mere existence of the Anarch Free State and Anarchs' -- most of whom <i>used to be</i> Camarilla -- general opinions towards the Ventrue, precisely the impact Ventrue &quot;friendship&quot; has over the long run.<br /> <br /> Because the word you're desperately trying to avoid, which I have yet to employ but have stated all but directly, is &quot;blowback&quot;. And the Ventrue are very, <i>very</i>, good at generating blowback.<br /> <br /> <br /> The genuine irony of this is you directly stated &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot;, which is the domain of one and precisely one clan, among all possible forms of blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> And what are the Tremere's <i>other</i> two disciplines?<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, acting as if blood sorcerers have one and only one clan discipline. When the reality is, almost all of them have Auspex and/or at least one social discipline among them. We're to now pretend Ventrue are the only clan with three clan disciplines?<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, considering everything you just posted, you tell me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quite the opposite. Presence is one of my favorite disciplines in the game. I just don't put on rose-tinted glasses about it, and see it for what it is and what it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because the Ventrue have a redundant discipline spread whereas the Toreador do not. As I stated earlier.<br /> <br /> <br /> Auspex is, in my opinion, the most powerful single discipline in the game, yes. Because of its versatility and general utility. It's to mental and social disciplines what Celerity is to physical. And indeed when used properly, it really is that powerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...yeah?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ventrue is one of my favorite clans actually, behind Lasombra anyways. It's not my most-played clan by a longshot, which is a tie between Lasombra and Toreador, but it's definitely #3. I just don't put on rose-tinted glasses about them, and see them for what they are and what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>the thing i take away from this is that ventrue are bad because of game balance, which is probably true but the issue there is that the games have wack game balance to the point that it's perfectly valid to ignore it for lore discussions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T22:54:57-07:00","id":1457688,"title":"","content":"You're not fun to argue with. <br /> <br /> RAW Heightened senses doesn't help with social rolls. Do note that most people who are good at lying don't have ticks or tells that they're lying. A fast heart rate just means they're stressed, a change doesn't mean they've gotten dishonest on you, that's fiction. Your nonsense here is built upon Hollywood lies.<br /> <br /> It's generally easy to Gauge someone's emotions, you don't need aura perception for it, and if you aren't good at telling someone's emotions, Aura perception is not going to be useful for you. The spirits touch is.. extremely situational when it comes to social use. <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy means wonderworking, or miracle working. It's the best catch-all term for magic that isn't necromancy. This belief is prevalent in many WoD books. You're really grasping at straws here. As for the Tremere? Yes, they're remarkably successful, and yet nobody likes them. <br /> <br /> You're just being a Pedant with Roosevelt. The precise details don't matter once it becomes shared enough. The man got shot in the chest, he then gave a speech. For all you know he was a Ventrue who got shot, put a hole in a notebook, put some blood on his shirt, and carried on. Fact is, people love a hero that can take hits. Think of all the protagonists in action films that take unbelievable punishment and carry on through gritted teeth. Someone who's evasive isn't worth relying on. Someone with <i>Fortitude</i> is a man's man. <br /> <br /> I fully understand what soft power is. Cut the shit. If you need to imagine someone as stupid to feel better about your argument, your argument is stupid. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, acting as if blood sorcerers have one and only one clan discipline. When the reality is, almost all of them have Auspex and/or at least one social discipline among them. We're to now pretend Ventrue are the only clan with three clan disciplines? </div> </div> </div>Finally, a point that seems fair. I have thusfar avoided talking about the other disciplines of magical bloodlines. <br /> <br /> <br /> Assamite Sorcerers use Obfuscate because they need to hide from people. Their organizational structure is a mess, and they're dependent on the other two castes. Their other discipline is all about poisons. They're not a pleasant bunch, and they have more to lose than to gain by showboating magic. <br /> <br /> The Tremere are very successfull in that they're well organized (Dominate) and astute (auspex). However, everyone loaths them. The Malkavians avoid this trap by being low key, the Ventrue avoid this trap by being nice. The Tremere are neither nice nor low key. They're arrogant nerds by most reckonings who think it's better to be feared than loved. And they're kinda right about that. The Assamites sorcerers/Followers of Set protect their magic by keeping it hidden. The Tremere protect their magic with fortresses and reputation. <br /> <br /> The Followers of Set learn magic out of clan. They also need to keep more-hidden than others due to persecution. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If the Ventrue wanted to learn magic out of clan... they wouldn't really need to change much for it. They have the resources and a desirable clan structure. I don't think it'd do them much good, because they're simply amazing with people and don't need to pull some new tricks to convince others of their divinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T07:57:31-07:00","id":1457977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457688#post1457688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW Heightened senses doesn't help with social rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, yes it does, you are not understanding how. What heightened senses does, is provide information the player can then use to press advantages in later parts of the interaction. For example, if the character uses it to discern another is apprehensive, they can then tailor their next interaction(s) to that apprehension: to intimidate, reassure, or similar.<br /> <br /> Compare it to, for example, Daimonion 1. The information gleaned from Daimonion 1 is useful in and of itself because it provides information the activating character can exploit later, Daimonion 2 synergy notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do note that most people who are good at lying don't have ticks or tells that they're lying. A fast heart rate just means they're stressed, a change doesn't mean they've gotten dishonest on you, that's fiction. </div> </div> </div><i>That's</i> Hollywood bullshit. People who are good at lying are simply good at <i>hiding</i> their tells. And indeed there are decades of studies about the physiology of lying, that do show release of stress hormones, and involuntary or reflexive physiological reactions to telling lies.<br /> <br /> And, I'm sure at this point you'd be happy to bring up polygraph tests, inadmissibility in court, and <i>perceived</i> inaccuracy thereof as proof of your case. No, polygraphs are entirely adequate <i>when properly administered</i> (they rarely are); inadmissibility in court does not equate to inaccuracy, and indeed it is entirely possible to &quot;cheat&quot; a polygraph...<i>by intentionally throwing false positives during the baseline portion of the test</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's generally easy to Gauge someone's emotions, you don't need aura perception for it, and if you aren't good at telling someone's emotions, Aura perception is not going to be useful for you. </div> </div> </div><i>You're</i> the one arguing people who are good at lying don't have &quot;tells&quot;. <i>You</i> do the math on <i>your own</i> logic here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The spirits touch is.. extremely situational when it comes to social use. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Shit, I forgot my pen to sign this contract, can I borrow yours? Thanks...hmm...actually, I'm not so sure about this, do you think we can go back over sub-section 3 of clause 2?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, I'll be happy to e-sign the document, just hand your tablet over and I'll get right on it...&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thaumaturgy means wonderworking, or miracle working. It's the best catch-all term for magic that isn't necromancy. </div> </div> </div>Nope, no rhetorical games here. Thaumaturgy is in WoD terms a proper noun, which specifically refers to a single discipline possessed solely by the Tremere, which is in itself one form of blood sorcery. Which is why in the V20 books, in sections about Thaumaturgy the Tremere are referred to specifically, whereas generalized sections are under &quot;sorcery&quot; or &quot;blood sorcery&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're just being a Pedant with Roosevelt. </div> </div> </div>You're the one who chose poorly in historic analogies, not me.<br /> <br /> Here's another historic analogy. At the Battle of Spotsylvania Courthouse, John Sedgwick was shot in the head and instantly killed by a Confederate sharpshooter when he was inspecting and rallying his troops on the front line and refused to take cover from enemy fire. Reports differ as to whether he <i>actually</i> said &quot;they couldn't hit an elephant at this distance&quot; and being there are no primary sources verifying it it can't be definitively said, but as you said &quot;precise details don't matter once it becomes shared enough&quot;. His bullet-riddled skull is evidence enough.<br /> <br /> What you're describing, and the perspective you're describing it from, is not leadership but rather <i>hubris</i>. Which is, by my reckoning, the leading root cause of death among Ventrue. Visibility and leading from the front is great and all...that is, until you run into an Assamite with a grudge or a Brujah with a double-barreled shotgun loaded with incendiary rounds. Then you just have a dead Ventrue, and likely a bunch of confused or highly amused bystanders when all those blood bonds, supernatural emotional influence, and mental commands that form the foundation of a Ventrue's power instantly break.<br /> <br /> The perspective you're playing down is strategic logic and mediated decision-making. Here are two more nice, neat historic analogies since you like them.<br /> <br /> During the Battle of Ia Drang, Lt. Col. Hal Moore refused evac three times. Sure, he <i>spun</i> it as hoo-rah, heroic, leadership bullshit for his men, that's what made him a good commanding officer. The bottom line is he did the math: PAVN had eyes on the LZ, and they'd know when and if the command staff got evacuated. That would indicate a lack of commitment and coordination, provoking an attempt to overrun the already-landed troops when there'd be no command hierarchy to coordinate any sort of defense. And, PAVN was simply targeting the Hueys; any attempt to evac would have a high risk of him not leaving the AO alive anyways, dead birds on helis serve no purpose.<br /> <br /> On D-Day+6, Dick Winters was leading E-Company on an assault into Carentan, when they encountered and were momentarily pinned by a German machine gun nest. He managed to get them on their feet and advancing, by running along the road in plain view, screaming obscenities at them. Inspiring, sure, but hardly hoo-rah bullshit: Winters did the math. He and his men were still in enfilade regardless of having taken cover in ditches alongside the road, he was likely to get turned into leaky swiss cheese regardless where he was and so were his men if they remained in that position, and they needed to move up to get into <i>actual</i> cover.<br /> <br /> Mediated decisions based upon the best-possible information at any given time is the foundation of good leadership. And in WoD terms, there is one discipline that stands head and shoulders above any other in terms of ensuring characters have the best-possible information at any given time. It's one Ventrue <i>lack</i> in-clan, in exchange for two redundant disciplines and a third that <i>can be</i> rendered largely obsolete by...fashion choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fully understand what soft power is. </div> </div> </div>No, I submit you rather don't if you believe it's vested in &quot;being nice&quot; and manifested by being &quot;a man's man&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...If the Ventrue wanted to learn magic out of clan... they wouldn't really need to change much for it. They have the resources and a desirable clan structure. I don't think it'd do them much good, because they're simply amazing with people and don't need to pull some new tricks to convince others of their divinity. </div> </div> </div>And here we are, the final canard.<br /> <br /> Sure, Ventrue could learn magic out of clan. They're proprietary and rare disciplines, that those in possession thereof are generally loathe to share. So, good luck finding a blood sorcerer. Better luck finding a blood sorcerer with the right paths. Best of luck finding a blood sorcerer with the right paths, that'll teach them, that just won't seize the opportunity and the mandatory one-point blood bond to manipulate the Ventrue into being a fully-bound pawn completely lacking in agency and autonomy.<br /> <br /> But I mean, there <i>are</i> two clans with a propensity for blood sorcery, who are happy to teach it. I <i>do</i> think a Ventrue lector-priest could be cool as hell to play, or a Baali apostate who <i>used to be </i>Ventrue. You wanna talk having Dominate, Presence, <i>and</i> Daimonion? <i>That's</i> a discipline spread to be feared. That, or Presence, Daimonion, and Fortitude maybe; being able to soak that double Faith damage would actually be pretty nice. Atop learning freaking <i>Dur-an-Ki</i> out of clan.<br /> <br /> Just like any other vampire could learn Presence, Dominate, or Fortitude...common disciplines multiple clans share, that are far less guarded and readily-exchanged for cheaper boons.<br /> <br /> But I mean, you <i>might have</i> otherwise said Ventrue could far more easily learn Auspex out of clan, than blood sorcery. It is one of the eight non-proprietary disciplines, after all. Hell, the <i>antitribu</i> bloodline learn it in-clan in exchange for Presence, for Pete's sake. But that'd just be conceding my point about the discipline, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...don't need to pull some new tricks to convince others of their divinity. </div> </div> </div>You're right, they don't need <i>new</i> tricks per se. Rather the opposite, <i>old </i>tricks work just fine. Just stay away from 11th-generation Assamite neonates.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-29-2021, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T11:18:29-07:00","id":1457989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Shit, I forgot my pen to sign this contract, can I borrow yours? Thanks...hmm...actually, I'm not so sure about this, do you think we can go back over sub-section 3 of clause 2?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, I'll be happy to e-sign the document, just hand your tablet over and I'll get right on it...&quot; </div> </div> </div>What book are you reading to think Spirit's touch works like this?<br /> How it'd actually work<br /> &quot;Can I borrow your pen&quot;<br /> A: He doesn't have an attachment to the pen<br /> B: You work out he's 34, male, and uncomfortable, but not because of you being in a trance which is kinda rude, he was uncomfortable the time he most used this pen.<br /> <br /> Let's not even get into how absurdly specific your refute to &quot;this is situational&quot; is. Really, what edition are you reading, can you provide evidence for your claims? I get it, Auspex is a good discipline, but you've really gone wild with your imagination here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Historical examples </div> </div> </div>This is just anal. If someone gives you an anecdote, don't give them a lecture of cherry picked examples. Historians like to talk about exceptions, not the rule, and painfully... you're talking about people. We're talking about Vampires, and ones with Fortitude at that. If Hardestardt got JFK'd, he'd laugh it off, the bullet would go through his face and he'd heal it before the shooter got another shot, and most assassins aren't Assamites with .50 BMG, most assassins try to succeed with much less than a Carcano through the face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Soft power </div> </div> </div>Everyone likes the Ventrue. Many are economically tied to the Ventrue. The Ventrue can surely lead everyone against you if you upset the Ventrue. He also wears a nice suit, hosts elysiums, mediates disputes between kindred, hosts guests in his territory. His sire is distinguished, and his childer is likely a model neonate.<br /> <br /> Compared to what clan do the Ventrue lack &quot;soft power&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, Ventrue could learn magic out of clan. They're proprietary and rare disciplines, that those in possession thereof are generally loathe to share. So, good luck finding a blood sorcerer. Better luck finding a blood sorcerer with the right paths. Best of luck finding a blood sorcerer with the right paths, that'll teach them, that just won't seize the opportunity and the mandatory one-point blood bond to manipulate the Ventrue into being a fully-bound pawn completely lacking in agency and autonomy. </div> </div> </div>Hahahahahahahaha.<br /> First off, <u>t</u>haumaturgy (gotta make sure that t isn't capitalized or you'll act like you own the parking lot) <i>isn't </i>a unicorn discipline, but something anyone can develop a variety of. If you read <i>Rites of The Blood</i> you'll note that <i>New Age</i> sorcery was literally found by anarchs finding new religious practices and applying Vitae. Dur-An-Ki isn't exclusive to the Assamites, and I'm fairly sure the Nosferatu would've spirited away a few Tremere tomes.<br /> Now, as to finding a teacher that won't blood bond the Ventrue? Could you just... like... fucking consider what you've just said there for a mere moment? The Ventrue has Presence, Dominate, millions of dollary-doos, and a legion of adoring fans to hold someone down. If they wanted a thaumaturge that isn't part of some big fuck-off organization like the Tremere, very few are going to be in a possition to say anything other than &quot;of course!&quot;. That, and they have the resources to scour the earth for mortal hedge magicians to embrace into the clan. Science has always been at the mercy of politicians. Religion without politics loses to politics, and all the other magic clans have questionable political acumen.<br /> <br /> Lastly, and this is a big one, Animist and ancestor cultures don't really have much in the way of a big unified religion. The Ventrue could use their social sway to define what is god, what is worth worshipping, and so on and so forth. A wizard will get killed out of fear and jealousy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Oh, and there's nothing bad about Ventrue having common disciplines. That's actually a really good thing. Common disciplines are broadly applicable, which is why the Ventrue, Nosferatu, Toreador, Brujah and Malkavians are the most successful clans in spreading out and seizing power. Being specialized isn't necessarily a good thing. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're right, they don't need <i>new</i> tricks per se. Rather the opposite, <i>old </i>tricks work just fine. Just stay away from 11th-generation Assamite neonates. </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue have the best method of dealling with an Assamite<br /> Offer a better deal.<br /> That said, soft power again: of all the people to kill, siding against the Ventrue is often the worst choice. You've got the most guards to get past, you need to hit them more or harder than other targets, and there will be plenty of folks who will want to avenge him, or at least appear to want to avenge him because there's probably other Ventrue in the city...<br /> If your opponent has higher Obfuscate than you have Auspex, your Auspex is entirely useless. If they have an ingenious method of getting a bomb to you without sensory giveaways, your auspex is useless. Fortitude? Yeah it probably won't save you from Artillery or a truck bomb, but it's always going to be there whether you sense it or not. Auspex lets you avoid mistakes, but it's impossible to live completely avoiding mistakes, and sometimes just being aware of a danger doesn't mean you can avoid it. Fortitude mitigates the damage of mistakes. Fortitude allows you to survive failure. Better to be scarred ten times than killed once.<br /> <br /> And yeah the Ventrue are fucking better leaders than the Toreador and Tremere. Nobody wants a mage in power, those guys are cunts. There are multiple reasons why the Tremere are exceptionally rare princes, why Assamite sorcerers are the most marginalized caste, and why Settites stay hidden despite big followings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-29-2021, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T10:17:40-07:00","id":1458063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457989#post1457989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...He doesn't have an attachment to the pen...</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly don't know business types and their pens, especially when you start talking expensive fountain or ballpoint pens that approach or well exceed the point of being status symbols within the social microcosm of business culture. And, while completely ignoring the resonance left behind that can be read by Spirit's Touch is not merely a factor of <i>emotional</i> attachment to the item; it's a sympathetic link, emotional attachment merely <i>amplifies</i> that connection.<br /> <br /> Especially in the days before e-signing. Which, it's funny you seem to prefer to ignore (a running trend, here) because contemporary e-signing is performed via tablet or <i>smartphone</i> both of which are personal effects carried at all times, which individuals tend to feel quite personally linked to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone gives you an anecdote, don't give them a lecture of cherry picked examples. </div> </div> </div>Your example of Teddy Roosevelt was the very definition of a cherry-picked example. It also happened to be a exceedingly <i>bad</i> one, which I pointed out as an example <i>against</i> the point you were trying to make. Then I gave three others.<br /> <br /> Should I provide more? I just got out of a week-long binge of historical documentaries and books about the Cuban Missile Crisis, I can <i>certainly</i> provide examples of strategic logic and soft power winning the day, as arrayed against hardline politics and hard power in more ways than one, particularly now of all times as you so neatly bring up JFK later in your own post...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Historians like to talk about exceptions, not the rule... </div> </div> </div>My degrees are in political science and history, we historians like to talk about exceptions as novelties or oddities. &quot;The rule&quot; is far more important for identifying overall historic trends and causal links between events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and painfully... you're talking about people. </div> </div> </div>You're the one that brought it up, don't get buttmad and try to change the subject to retreat from a point you broached.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...If Hardestardt got JFK'd... </div> </div> </div>Yeah, <i>what would</i> happen if Hardestadt got &quot;JFK'ed&quot;? Ask Tyler and Theo Bell, I guess. <i>They're</i> the reason there were <i>two</i> vampires named Hardestadt, and why there are <i>no</i> vampires named Hardestadt (or Jan Pieterzoon for that matter) in V5.<br /> <br /> I mean, I only alluded to that...three times, now? it's almost as if Ventrue do indeed have problems with hubris and blowback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone likes the Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>A. Soft power has nothing to do with whether one &quot;likes&quot; another.<br /> B. Literally the only vampire that &quot;like&quot; the Ventrue are other Ventrue, and even that's a crap shoot given their obligation to help one another is precisely that, an <i>obligation</i> that most Ventrue are rather loathe to admit. You're arguing against multiple clan splatbooks, the Camarilla books, high clan books, LotC, the Anarch books, the Sabbat books...<br /> <br /> &quot;Liking&quot; another party, and <i>doing business with another party</i>, are two completely different topics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...He also wears a nice suit, hosts elysiums, mediates disputes between kindred, hosts guests in his territory... </div> </div> </div>Literally which clan makes up the majority of Keepers of Elysium and Harpies? Ain't the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compared to what clan do the Ventrue lack &quot;soft power&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head? That would be the one that makes up the majority of Keepers of Elysium, and Harpies. AKA, &quot;the ones who control status, access, and prestation within the Camarilla&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...The Ventrue has Presence, Dominate, millions of dollary-doos, and a legion of adoring fans to hold someone down...and they have the resources to scour the earth...Science has always been at the mercy of politicians...Religion without politics loses to politics... </div> </div> </div>In other words, there are no more perfect fully-bound thralls in the entirety of the World of Darkness than the Ventrue. And, a Ventrue would be is voluntarily one-third of the way there simply by merit of having to learn the discipline...that trivializes the act of blood bonding another in a way no other does.<br /> <br /> And if &quot;liking&quot; someone is the key to soft power as your ultimate, hidden, thesis is...what does the blood bond do at even one point, again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, and this is a big one, Animist and ancestor cultures don't really have much in the way of a big unified religion. The Ventrue could use their social sway to define what is god, what is worth worshipping, and so on and so forth. </div> </div> </div><i>I guess</i> if you're a fourth-generation methuselah, you could have pulled it off at the dawn of organized religion. I'd posit if your counter example of how to overpower two or three dots in blood sorcery in addition to what else you have, is &quot;just have Dominate 9 and Presence 8, lol&quot;...you <i>probably</i> don't have a very good point to begin with.<br /> <br /> Just so we're clear since you don't exactly seem like you're picking up on the analogies here, I'm talking about Mithras. Who did exactly what you're talking about. And it took centuries for the <i>fourth-gen Ventrue methuselah with a methuselah's discipline spread</i> to coopt a cult <i>that already existed</i>.<br /> <br /> He was also eaten by an 11th-generation neonate Assamite. So...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue have the best method of dealling with an Assamite<br /> Offer a better deal. </div> </div> </div>lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T07:16:00-07:00","id":1458140,"title":"","content":"I think we just have to look at the results in the lore to determine the suitability of the Ventrue to rule. I'm no fan of V5 or it's rushed lore changes, but due to the Ventrue &quot;leadership&quot; we see Hardestadts death, the collapse of the Camarilla's claim to universal cainite membership, the retreat to outdated methods of communication and in the past 30 years, 2 clans have left the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Sure they got the Assamites, but they could have potentially gotten the Setites as well if they were better at detecting plots since it was the Assamites that sabotaged the Settites joining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T07:47:43-07:00","id":1458143,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue ruled pretty well for ~1000 years. And they're still in a better spot than many other clans that focus on leadership. The Tremere had their entire leadership decapitated by the Second Inquisition. The Lasombra's sect completely imploded to the point that they had to beg the Ventrue to join the Camarilla. The Brujah are now Philosopher Kings of a bunch nothing. Really the Toreador are about the only real &quot;leading&quot; clan that's in a decent spot. I don't know though that things would have gone any better if they'd been in control of the Camarilla. And to be fair the Camarilla is still pretty strong - yeah they lost the Gangrel and Brujah but they have the Assamites and a bunch of Lasombra so it's mostly a wash, and further the Camarilla's traditional enemy the Sabbat is in even worse shape so there's less competition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T08:52:40-07:00","id":1458148,"title":"","content":"It's quite easy to spin that the other way: The Cam lasts 500 years, very impressive for a vampire government. Note that things go to shit only after they kill the Ventrue?<br /> <br /> The Ventrue don't actually &quot;lead&quot; the Camarilla. I'm sure they punch above their weight in terms of inner-circle membership, but they don't dictate the course of the Camarilla.<br /> Hardy's death is one of the sketchiest bits of writing. Is it because it's actually a cunning plot, or is it because the writers didn't put much thought into how they wanted their big changes to be made? Dragonsbreath rounds are like throwing knives; Amazing in video games, actual garbage in any realistic scenario, nevermind that Hardy junior should have enough Fortitude and that nobody should've been able to make it in with a shotgun, there's also the part where Theo isn't tortured to death because... well, I suppose he was Dominated into doing this stupid shit. As for the reaction to that? The Brujah leaving the Cam and the Cam shrinking?<br /> <br /> ...it's a lot of contrivances. Either some methuselah machinations forcing all the Bad decisions on people, or it's just bad writing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Literally which clan makes up the majority of Keepers of Elysium and Harpies? Ain't the Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>\u200bThese aren't positions of honour, they're jobs. The term <i>harpies</i> is an insult and KoE are some of the lowest tier public servants the Camarilla has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You clearly don't know business types and their pens </div> </div> </div>And you clearly don't know auspex and it's fucking rules. Which one's more pressing here? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022 The Spirit\u2019s Touch<br /> When someone handles an object for any length<br /> of time, he leaves a psychic impression on the item.<br /> A vampire with this level of Auspex can \u201cread\u201d these<br /> sensations, learning who handled the object, when he<br /> last held it, and what was done with it recently. (For these purposes, a corpse counts as an \u201cobject\u201d and can<br /> be read accordingly.) These visions are seldom clear<br /> and detailed, registering more like a kind of \u201cpsychic<br /> snapshot.\u201d Still, the Kindred can learn much even<br /> from such a glimpse. Although most visions concern<br /> the last person to handle the item, a long-time owner<br /> leaves a stronger impression than someone who held<br /> the object briefly.<br /> Gleaning information from the spiritual residue requires<br /> the vampire to hold the object and enter a shallow<br /> trance. She is only marginally aware of her surroundings<br /> while using The Spirit\u2019s Touch, but a loud<br /> noise or jarring physical sensation breaks the trance<br /> instantly.<br /> System: The player rolls Perception + Empathy. The<br /> difficulty is determined by the age of the impressions<br /> and the mental and spiritual strength of the person or<br /> event that left them. Sensing information from a pistol<br /> used for a murder hours ago may require a 4, while<br /> learning who owned a bloodstained puppet fashioned a<br /> century ago might be a 9.<br /> The greater the individual\u2019s emotional connection<br /> to the object, the stronger the impression he leaves<br /> on it \u2014 and the more information the Kindred can<br /> glean from it. Events involving strong emotions (a giftgiving,<br /> a torture, a long family history) likewise leave<br /> stronger impressions than short or casual contact do.<br /> Assume that each success offers one piece of information,<br /> as per the chart below.<br /> Successes Information<br /> Botch The character is overwhelmed by<br /> psychic impressions for the next 30<br /> minutes and unable to act.<br /> Failure No information of value.<br /> 1 success Very basic information: the last<br /> owner\u2019s gender or hair color,<br /> for instance.<br /> 2 successes A second piece of basic information.<br /> 3 successes More useful information about the<br /> last owner, such as age and state of<br /> mind the last time he used the item.<br /> 4 successes The person\u2019s name.<br /> 5+ successes A wealth of information: nearly<br /> anything you want to know about the<br /> person\u2019s relationship with that object<br /> is available. </div> </div> </div>Wrong, sir! Wrong! You aren't going to learn the details of a contract by holding someone's pen, you're going to learn the pen owner's name if get a really good roll, and if you max out your successes, you'll learn if they liked the pen or not....&quot;Fax mentis incendium gloria cultum,&quot; et cetera, et cetera...&quot;Memo bis punitor delicatum!&quot; It's all there, black and white, clear as crystal! You <b>don't know how Auspex works</b>. You bumped into the ceiling which now has to be washed and sterilized, so you get nothing! You lose! Good day sir!<br /> <br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess </div> </div> </div></i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you're a fourth-generation methuselah, you could have pulled it off at the dawn of organized religion. I'd posit if your counter example of how to overpower two or three dots in blood sorcery in addition to what else you have, is &quot;just have Dominate 9 and Presence 8, lol&quot;...you <i>probably</i> don't have a very good point to begin with. </div> </div> </div>Try Dominate 2 or 3, Presence 3 or 5. Or money. Just money and a good plan will do. You don't need to co-opt everyone, just key figures, corrupt a few priests, and if you want to go big; Jesus and Buddha were individuals with a few disciples.<br /> In any case, If someone uses thaumaturgy (small t, I hope you're paying attention) even if that thaumaturgy works well with the local faith, it's very easy for someone with Dominate/Pressence at mid-low levels to get a dedicated following of people who believe that the thaumaturge is an evil trickster that must be purged. From the perspective of vampires, if six vampires live in a city, and one decides he's the master because he uses religious magic... the other five will screw the mage, because a threat like that isn't welcome. If one decides he's everyone should pay more attention to him because he's the most likable dude there... well, he might make things easier for the rest of them doing that, so they may listen to him. Doesn't really matter what culture you're in. Hell at a point, Christianity was fully on board with all the Hermetic stuff people were doing, there was even a Pope practicing his wizard skills. it wasn't at all witchy. That changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> RE: Toreador<br /> They've always had a reputation for being feckless. All that celerity making them evasive and flighty. Oh they're respected, but it's a very different kind of respect than you'd give the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-31-2021, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T09:31:55-07:00","id":1458152,"title":"","content":"Sadly the Ventrue are the vanilla option.<br /> <br /> If I was redoing V:TM, I'd ditch the Ventrue and have the Tzimisce as the rulers of the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T09:36:14-07:00","id":1458153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458152#post1458152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly the Ventrue are the vanilla option.<br /> <br /> If I was redoing V:TM, I'd ditch the Ventrue and have the Tzimisce as the rulers of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzmisce without Vicissitude are just a racist Eastern-Europe Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <i>Vanilla is Strength</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-31-2021, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T10:48:19-07:00","id":1458158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458152#post1458152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly the Ventrue are the vanilla option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Lasombra, I don't think the Tzimisce would be an interesting option.<br /> <br /> Vanilla is vanilla for a reason, you need that kind of baseline. Any clan can be on top at any particular city, and this makes things interesting, but what do you do when you want just to be practical and focus on something else? You need vanilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T11:18:16-07:00","id":1458160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458148#post1458148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it's a lot of contrivances. Either some methuselah machinations forcing all the Bad decisions on people, or it's just bad writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't like it therefore it didn't happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, so long as you're discounting that it was a natural progression from...well, basically everything written previous about Bell, how big of assholes both Hardestadts were and how long their lists of enemies were, relations between Ventrue and Brujah throughout the centuries up to and including the latter's tendency to whack the former, resentment towards the Ventrue by younger vampires and particularly Anarchs, and that whole neat &quot;nice bookending paralleling Bell ganking Hardestadt the Younger, the same way Tyler ganked Hardestadt the Elder, amidst major political upheaval between vampires&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThese aren't positions of honour, they're jobs. The term <i>harpies</i> is an insult and KoE are some of the lowest tier public servants the Camarilla has. </div> </div> </div>Yet not one word about what those jobs do, the level of access they grant, the level of <i>control</i> over access they grant, the level of <i>information</i> they grant, and the power any and all of the above ultimately give them. Funny, that.<br /> <br /> Yep, they're bureaucrats...in a world where bureaucrats have the power. You really do have your perception fundamentally out of whack if you believe the pomp and circumstance mean anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you clearly don't know auspex and it's fucking rules...Wrong, sir! Wrong! </div> </div> </div>&quot;When someone handles an object <b>for any length of time</b>, he leaves a psychic impression on the item...<b>and what was done with it recently</b>. [...] ...<b>a long-time owner leaves a stronger impression than someone who held the object briefly</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Literally the first paragraph. If you're going to quote something...read it first.<br /> <br /> You seriously think business and legal types are running around treating Montblancs, Parkers, Crosses, Watermans, and Fabers that can cost thousands or tends of thousands of dollars on the <i>low end</i> like they're clickers an unpaid intern bought wholesale at Office Depot? To say nothing in the era of e-signing, in which case we're then talking about personal effects which cost a thousand on the low end, that are in an individual's possession 24/7. <i>Because they're smartphones and tablets</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You aren't going to learn the details of a contract by holding someone's pen... </div> </div> </div>Don't have to. All you need, is once again since you clearly didn't read what you copy-pasted before you did it, is &quot;...the state of mind the last time [they] used the item&quot;. That's three successes, the statistical average as rolled by a user with a six dice pool (in other words, the <i>low end</i> of dice pools for a dedicated Auspex user) at difficulty 6, which is right where you'd peg the difficulty for a Spirit's Touch roll on a long-time personal effect of which the user may be particularly proud or regard as a status symbol, which <i>they just used</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Then</i> you get whether the owner of that pen is feeling self-satisfied, sneaky, proud of themselves, or any other number of emotions that implicate them as thinking they've gotten something past the other party. Or if they're unhappy or resentful of the deal, or any sort of other negative feeling.<br /> <br /> Do you understand now, or are you going to continue (being charitable) playing dumb?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's all there, black and white, clear as crystal! </div> </div> </div>You're right, it rather is. It's on your head you fail to understand the full implications of what you literally just copy-pasted, especially as pertains to this conversation, as I've repeatedly tried to explain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Try Dominate 2 or 3, Presence 3 or 5. Or money. Just money and a good plan will do. You don't need to co-opt everyone, just key figures, corrupt a few priests, and if you want to go big; Jesus and Buddha were individuals with a few disciples. </div> </div> </div>So why did it take a literal fourth generation centuries to do it, during of all times the classical period when vampiric might was at its absolute apex?<br /> <br /> Let me guess, &quot;I don't like it therefore it didn't happen that way&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it's very easy for someone with Dominate/Pressence at mid-low levels to get a dedicated following of people who believe that the thaumaturge is an evil trickster that must be purged. </div> </div> </div>And we're right back to &quot;blood sorcerers only have one discipline&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the perspective of vampires, if six vampires live in a city, and one decides he's the master because he uses religious magic... the other five will screw the mage, because a threat like that isn't welcome. </div> </div> </div>And if six vampires live in a city, and one decides he's the master because they merely have Dominate, Presence, and the right sire...the other five will do the exact same because he's a pompous ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If one decides he's everyone should pay more attention to him because he's the most likable dude there... </div> </div> </div>And we're right back to equating influence with likability, and equating Ventrue to likability. Because apparently, somehow and somewhere along the line, we've forgotten that Dominate and Presence do indeed wear off, and when they do the target figures out they've been had.<br /> <br /> Which causes potential blowback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh they're respected, but it's a very different kind of respect than you'd give the Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>Because one party is good at soft power, and the other is good at hard power. And today's world is all about <i>soft</i> power.<br /> <br /> Bloody a Ventrue's nose, you lose some domain, feeding privileges, maybe some influence and resources in the short term when they punch back; worst case scenario, you find yourself the recipient of a trumped-up blood hunt and have to find some place to lay low for a while. Then the Anarch status, Anarch allies, and gestures of friendship from the Ventrue's rivals and enemies, you get from having punched the Ventrue in the nose, show up. Then the Ventrue's in a lose-lose proposition: back off and try to spin it to save face, or double down and face deposition.<br /> <br /> Bloody a Toreador's nose, you kiss your status and prestation goodbye, right then and there. And that's not just in <i>that</i> city, that's in <i>every</i> city in which a bored Toreador has an internet connection, a cell phone, or a messenger ghoul. <i>And</i> they're likely to have Anarch back-channels to shit-talk through, keeping local Anarchs wary of working with you. <i>And</i> they're the ones with the boons, and knowledge of who owes whom what, to start tugging strings and setting off prestation Rube Goldberg machines to surgically strip you of every other background in turn.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, even that Toreador's rivals and enemies aren't doing a damn thing to help you, <i>unless</i> they can figure out some way to work <i>your</i> foolishness into <i>their</i> plans. Last, the Toreador will neither stop nor be deterred in their efforts to make your unlife a constant hell, because they're social piranhas who do that shit for <i>fun</i>; meaning, your only reprieve is to find them a new chew-toy of equal or greater amusement.<br /> <br /> But nothing compares to what happens if you bloody a Nosferatu's nose. <i>They</i> just call their <i>antitribu</i> clanmates, since they give less of a shit about sect than clan, and let their clanmates' packs know where your haven is. Then you just...disappear.<br /> <br /> Which is my whole-ass point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T13:04:24-07:00","id":1458169,"title":"","content":"The tunnel vision is strong with this one.<br /> Prestation isn't something Harpies keep in their pockets and get to chuck out when they decide they don't like you. If a harpy were to decide that they weren't going to acknowledge a deal, and another third party comes up to acknowledge that the harpy did indeed witness a transaction, the harpy reputation and status will be trashed so hard that they might even get blood hunted. Prestation is sacred. It transcends sects. You only reneg if you're absolutely sure the guy will die before news can get out you didn't play fair.<br /> <br /> Bloody the Ventrue's nose and he'll screw you just so, and then if you're dumb enough to survive and make good friends with his enemies then... well... you're only cementing your status as a loser, right? Getting closer to the anarchs will help you? might as well save your failing political career by tattooing a swastika to your head. Between the Ventrue and his Ventrue mates and you with your neonate anarch buddies.... Most are going to side with the Ventrue, unless he really is out of favour. Going against a well established Ventrue will have you ostracised because it's simply not worth upsetting a powerful market force for... some fool who wants to bloody noses.<br /> <br /> Granted, most of this is the same for Toreador. The Toreador has an advantage in that they expect a lower bottom line: A Toreador's allowed to be petty, expected to be petty. But that's a double edged sword. A vampire who's petty is simply someone you want to avoid dealing with. Get a close relationship with a Ventrue and fall out? His response will be proportionate and appropriate. Bonus? The Ventrue will let a lot of minor issues things slide, and when you try to patch things up, you've got reasonable confidence that when he accepts your reconciliation, he won't go back on it. Get a close relationship with a Toreador and fall out? By reputation, they'll escalate the conflict, they'll never let it go, and they're probably mad about something really minor you did. They'll take great joy in that you gave them an excuse to victimise you... That's not someone you really want to get all that close to.<br /> If you have to depend on someone for business, your average Ventrue will always be better than your average Toreador.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Averages....<br /> <br /> Ventrue almost always hit night society after a clan-scrutinized selection and a period of heavy tutelage. If they lack in one, they'll usually be made up for in the other. 9 times out of 10, your Ventrue will at least be adequate in all the things that matter to being a Ventrue, if not exceptional.<br /> <br /> Toreador are infamous for lax embraces and frequently hap-hazard tutoring. There certainly are prestigious, well selected, well groomed, well taught Toreador that can rival the best Ventrue, but in modern nights, they're the minority. Even if you've got a discerning sire, there's a good chance that much of your selection and education revolved around art, rather than the practical. With elites, the mediocre, and absolute trash-tier embraces that naturally fall in with Anarchs, the Toreador have little consistency, and most often the greatest enemy of a Toreador is...another Toreador. The clan culture is toxic. the brand value of the clan suffers in comparison to the blue bloods as the clan is messy, decadent and disharmonious.<br /> <br /> (also, if you read those &quot;the view of&quot; sections where the clans talk shit about one another? The Toreador cop way more flak than the Ventrue. The Ventrue often get grudging admiration from the low clans. The Toreador just get hate.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-31-2021, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T15:22:55-07:00","id":1458181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458153#post1458153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce without Vicissitude are just a racist Eastern-Europe Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <i>Vanilla is Strength</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly you don't have any appreciation for the Tzimisce who runs an old apartment building they've filled with secret security cameras and control all the rats inside.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T16:23:08-07:00","id":1458191,"title":"","content":"Vampire society is in many ways feudal. This doesn\u2019t just mean that vampires are like lords that have control of domains and have fealty to higher lords, it means that politics is based on personal relationships. Who someone is matters and your personal ties to them matter. This is where the Ventrue draw much of their power. Maybe being willing to paint a target on their own backs does put them at certain disadvantages and perhaps they would have longer unlives if they didn\u2019t have Fortitude but instead had a Discipline that let them avoid danger rather than survive it. But then they wouldn\u2019t be who they are, the leaders of the vampiric world.<br /> <br /> The fact that they are willing to take on those dangerous positions, which also include responsibilities, and put themselves in harms way does earn them respect and in a world where personal relationships matter, respect is power. <br /> <br /> The two other Camarilla establishment Clans - the Toreador and Tremere - have Auspex as well as a social Discipline. Yet despite every Clan being selfish, the Toreador and the Tremere both throw their support behind the Ventrue. Can any of us imagine the Ventrue and Toreador supporting Tremere as the leadership Clan of the Camarilla? Can we imagine the Ventrue and Tremere supporting the Toreador as the leadership Clan? I can\u2019t in either case. Because the Ventrue actually have what it takes to be leaders - putting themselves in harms way, taking on the responsibilities, taking on the blame, painting big targets on their backs. They also take their leadership role seriously and despite being bastards like all vampires, their leadership actually is beneficial to the vampires that they lead. Which I think most Camarilla vampires understand deep down, which is why they support the Ventrue or at least work with them to facilitate their rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 08-31-2021, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T16:22:26-07:00","id":1458267,"title":"","content":"The heated nature of the discussion aside I'm genuinly bemused by the Suggestion the Ventrue and their disciplines are a relic, they're easily one the most suited to modern nights. their disciplines are excellent for control and they excersive hard and soft power in a way which is incredably effective IRL. Genuinly a bizzare statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T06:52:39-07:00","id":1458336,"title":"","content":"I agree, but that wouldn't be a problem and I would be open to the arguments weren't the discussion that rancid. Personal attacks and aggression do not an argument make, specially when it clearly became for the sole sake of winning the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T08:33:23-07:00","id":1458354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458152#post1458152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly the Ventrue are the vanilla option.<br /> <br /> If I was redoing V:TM, I'd ditch the Ventrue and have the Tzimisce as the rulers of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Ventrue, but I do think that you have a point. They are rather on the vanilla side. Tzimisce are a ruler Clan and have a lot of additional flavor. Maybe a V:tM where the Tzimisce replaced the Ventrue would be cool. The Tzimisce themselves would have to be tweaked a bit to make that happen, but it could and I think it would be cool.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce or something like them as the head of the Camarilla would create a different dynamic within the Camarilla. As MWiS said, vanilla is strength. Tzimisce for all their flavor would have a number of drawbacks in ruling the Camarilla and I would imagine if that was the scenario, that the Tzimisce would represent an old money style of leadership - hyper-conservative, rigid, traditional, harsh yet honorable. They would also be in decline in comparison to new money.<br /> <br /> In the human world: bankers, stock brokers, and media moguls have way more power than land owning aristocrats. Lawyers and contracts are more powerful than oaths or bonds of blood. That doesn't necessarily hold true among vampires, especially the Camarilla, which is an extremely conservative elder dominated society where personal power and relationships is going to matter more. Maybe the Camarilla would be more interesting for this changed dynamic, with the Tzimisce representing traditional power through territory, oaths of fealty, personal power and abilities, boons and favors - while a rival Clan could represent new money.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting idea to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:13:00-07:00","id":1458360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458354#post1458354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the Ventrue, but I do think that you have a point. They are rather on the vanilla side. Tzimisce are a ruler Clan and have a lot of additional flavor. Maybe a V:tM where the Tzimisce replaced the Ventrue would be cool. The Tzimisce themselves would have to be tweaked a bit to make that happen, but it could and I think it would be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>The already &quot;tweaked&quot; Tzimisce in that direction by removing Auspex, which supplied the clan with facets of spiritualism, occultism, insight, preternatural awareness, a sense of learning and higher understanding, and giving them Dominate, the most ham-fisted Social Discipline. Remove the scalpel, replace with club. <br /> <br /> I guess I don't understand why people don't just play a Ventrue with Protean instead of trying to reinvent Clan Tzimisce as Ventrue with Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:22:59-07:00","id":1458362,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes, I got a bit uglier than I'd have liked. But imagine someone being <i>wrong </i>on the internet? (especially when you really didn't want to get into what should've been an open and shut case, but someone tells you to humour them) <br /> <br /> <br /> The in-clan disciplines tend to say a lot about the character of the vampires in that clan<br /> Animalism- Bit of a wild card really (Could say they like animals?) <br /> Auspex- Obsessive<br /> Celerity- Evasive<br /> Dominate- Organized<br /> Fortitude- Enduring. <br /> Obfuscate-Paranoid (or safety obsessed?) <br /> Potence- Aggressive <br /> Presence- Charming<br /> <br /> Now yeah, i could easily change out some of these words for more positive or negative connotations. I'm also of the belief that Disciplines are cultivated according to the way you/your clan hunts rather than your personality, but your personality is obviously going to have a big influence on how you choose to hunt. <br /> <br /> Just using this the most reliable clan to do business with are... clearly the Ventrue. Above and beyond. <br /> <br /> Now I didn't just throw this down to &quot;win&quot; an argument. It also goes into some V5 changes; Discipline changes. <br /> The Ravnos are... debatably fine... Many think of them as charming tricksters so the charisma makes sense... only they've been unlikable vegabonds who've had to endure hardship and who aren't especially subtle about who they are and what they do... <br /> <br /> The Tzmisce... completely fall apart. They were never meant to be organized, that's the whole reason they didn't destroy the Tremere within 10 years of the omen wars. They claim territory, barely keep in contact, and obsess over whatever it is that catches their interest, be it flesh or sorcery. They're Obsessive intellectuals. They need Auspex, they absolutely don't want Dominate (as an in-clan, as a group, shut up about Dracula, he's an exception, and a revenant besides) <br /> <br /> The other clans with changes have correspondingly had a personality change... It doesn't work so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:31:02-07:00","id":1458364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458360#post1458360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The already &quot;tweaked&quot; Tzimisce in that direction by removing Auspex, which supplied the clan with facets of spiritualism, occultism, insight, preternatural awareness, a sense of learning and higher understanding, and giving them Dominate, the most ham-fisted Social Discipline. Remove the scalpel, replace with club.<br /> <br /> I guess I don't understand why people don't just play a Ventrue with Protean instead of trying to reinvent Clan Tzimisce as Ventrue with Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>They denied the Tzimisce Thaumaturgy as a Clan Discipline while giving them Auspex, which was a huge mistake, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Auspex provides an individual with insights into a person and other beings.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are some of the most utterly self-absorbed, unobservant, internal looking beings in the world. It was never a good fit versus giving the Tzimisce Dominate (which fits with the fact they make SLAVES of their servants) or their Mad Scientist needs with Blood Sorcery/Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Auspex always felt like a terrible addition to the Tzimisce, IMHO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:44:44-07:00","id":1458370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458360#post1458360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The already &quot;tweaked&quot; Tzimisce in that direction by removing Auspex, which supplied the clan with facets of spiritualism, occultism, insight, preternatural awareness, a sense of learning and higher understanding, and giving them Dominate, the most ham-fisted Social Discipline. Remove the scalpel, replace with club.<br /> <br /> I guess I don't understand why people don't just play a Ventrue with Protean instead of trying to reinvent Clan Tzimisce as Ventrue with Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there are some interesting arguments for or against replacing Auspex with Dominate. Personally, I think that Dominate undermines the reliance that Tzimisce have traditionally had on blood bonds and ghouls. They are masters of the blood bond because they don't have a social Discipline, another reason why they would create Revenant families. I think it's cool that they can be in charge without using Auspex or Dominate.<br /> <br /> I don't think that Dominate is terrible for them though.<br /> <br /> Making them the traditional leaders of the Camarilla as CTP suggests goes a little beyond that. Maybe the Ventrue should be made a little more like the Tzimisce instead of the reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:52:18-07:00","id":1458373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458364#post1458364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They denied the Tzimisce Thaumaturgy as a Clan Discipline while giving them Auspex, which was a huge mistake, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Auspex provides an individual with insights into a person and other beings.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are some of the most utterly self-absorbed, unobservant, internal looking beings in the world. It was never a good fit versus giving the Tzimisce Dominate (which fits with the fact they make SLAVES of their servants) or their Mad Scientist needs with Blood Sorcery/Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Auspex always felt like a terrible addition to the Tzimisce, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzmisce are perhaps genrally self absorbed (more honestly I'd say they just lack emphaphy) but to suggest they're unobservant is a catagorically false. They're incredably mindful of both their surroundings and topics of interest and have historically been depicted as such. Auspex also better reflects their inituative non-linear mystic tendancies over the more scientific thaumaturgy. I don't really think Dominate is a bad fit for them but I really don't get were your coming from with them being unobservant. Especially now they're incredably possesive in V5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T10:17:09-07:00","id":1458377,"title":"","content":"Tzmisce are more the lovechild of gangrel and malkavians than anything to do with the Ventrue. They're obsessive lunatics who want their own very private domain and they're willing to live further out to achieve that level of privacy. They're not good leaders, Infact they only really &quot;lead&quot; so that their followers can grant them the convenience they require to focus on their own studies. They're a very private people at heart, relying on very few close aides rather than the extensive organizations the Ventrue build under them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T10:58:11-07:00","id":1458382,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say they're bad leaders, but certainly I do envision them with Auspex more than with Dominate.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are archetypal old blood local nobility. That doesn't mean they're bad leaders, but that they're focused leaders, less preoccupied with extending their power and more with making it unchecked in their own turf. This isn't bad leadership, it is another kind of leadership.<br /> <br /> But also a kind of leadership that isn't conducive of commanding a sect. They wouldn't be good leaders for the Camarilla as a whole, but would be splendid Princes in many domains, and certainly be a power player in sect politics. Not even for the Sabbat I think the Tzimisce are good primary leaders, I'm not into V5 enough yet to know if the Lasombra left the sect, but if they did the Tzimisce are unlikely to stay alone on the top. Time for some Antitribu to rise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T11:15:13-07:00","id":1458384,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude was the Tzmisce's great social discipline. <br /> <br /> -I made you/your ghouls look the way you wanted to look, now pay up. <br /> -yeah I disfigured you/your loved one, so what? I can fix it, if you just do as I say... you have no choice but to work with me now, nobody will ever accept you looking like that. <br /> -Yes, it is I, your long lost father. <br /> <br /> Dominate would just be superfluous. <br /> Animalism works great because you can lobotomize people and then animalism applies to them... Also 1 and 2 are great for finding practice materials, 3 is good for keeping them still to shape, <br /> Auspex allows you to observe the fine details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T13:14:58-07:00","id":1458400,"title":"","content":"I have a similar outlook on their Discipline set.<br /> <br /> Animalism allows for a natural progression of social control via subduing minions and lessers: first beasts, then humans, then The Beast. <br /> <br /> Auspex is the expression of &quot;Knowledge is Power&quot; in Discipline form. Tzimisce are often presented first and foremost as a scholarly clan with \u201ca thirst for knowledge.\u201d It's also possibly the most underrated Discipline in the books. It's subtle, but has amazingly useful applications in settings from social debates to hunting and tracking to monitoring one's expansive demesne without leaving one's basement sanctum. Far Sight, Telepathy, Heightened Senses, Spirit's Touch...solid gold to a clan of territorial, anti-social shut-ins.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is a physical culmination of similar masteries and insights as above, but with an added horror aspect not available anywhere else in the game (outside of a couple static, uncontrollable clan weaknesses, maybe). This is the game's resource for Cronenberg, Charles Dexter Ward, The Thing, etc. Otherworldly, inhuman, terrifying to others yet liberating, enlightening and empowering to Fiends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T14:28:23-07:00","id":1458416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458373#post1458373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tzmisce are perhaps genrally self absorbed (more honestly I'd say they just lack emphaphy) but to suggest they're unobservant is a catagorically false. They're incredably mindful of both their surroundings and topics of interest and have historically been depicted as such. Auspex also better reflects their inituative non-linear mystic tendancies over the more scientific thaumaturgy. I don't really think Dominate is a bad fit for them but I really don't get were your coming from with them being unobservant. Especially now they're incredably possesive in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't lead cattle. You ranch them. A Tzimisce OWNS his domains. Why would you lead it?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which is why Dominate is a good Discipline for them but not, say, Presence as a Tzimisce does not persuade anyone and does need anyone to like them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458384#post1458384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude was the Tzmisce's great social discipline.<br /> <br /> -I made you/your ghouls look the way you wanted to look, now pay up.<br /> -yeah I disfigured you/your loved one, so what? I can fix it, if you just do as I say... you have no choice but to work with me now, nobody will ever accept you looking like that.<br /> -Yes, it is I, your long lost father.<br /> <br /> Dominate would just be superfluous.<br /> <br /> Animalism works great because you can lobotomize people and then animalism applies to them... Also 1 and 2 are great for finding practice materials, 3 is good for keeping them still to shape,<br /> <br /> Auspex allows you to observe the fine details.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very transactional way of viewing a Tzimisce's relationship with his followers. A Tzimsice doesn't need to threaten you with your father or disfigurement. You are property and you will obey because why wouldn't you? I tend to view the Tzimisce as mad scientists and Vicissitude as a fully explored version of their Discipline that other vampires mostly just rely on the nature of.<br /> <br /> Its not that it's different from Protean, it's that the Tzimisce took it further than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce are perhaps genrally self absorbed (more honestly I'd say they just lack emphaphy) but to suggest they're unobservant is a catagorically false. They're incredably mindful of both their surroundings and topics of interest and have historically been depicted as such. Auspex also better reflects their inituative non-linear mystic tendancies over the more scientific thaumaturgy. I don't really think Dominate is a bad fit for them but I really don't get were your coming from with them being unobservant. Especially now they're incredably possesive in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to explain via example:<br /> <br /> I think the best example of a Western non-Vampire Tzimisce in media would be Mr. House from Fallout: New Vegas. Mr. House is a figure who wants nothing more than to transform New Vegas into a perfect simaculum of Pre-War Vegas and has a mono-obsessive focus on recreating everything from the buildings to the mob. He has an army of scientifically engineered slaves (robots in his case) to enforce his will and identifies as an autocrat without irony.<br /> <br /> I think that Tzimisce by nature are somewhat monofocused on their domains and properties so Auspex feels like an odd fit to them. Tzmisce do not strike me as particularly insightful to other people or their motivation and its hard to believe a Tzimisce views anyone else (let alone his slaves) as &quot;people.&quot; Auspex is about gaining supernatural insights as mentioned but Tzimisce don't view people as &quot;people' as they're some of the most detached sociopathic Kindred alive. Why would they have a Discipline that shows them what other people think and feel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0s4sIY3bYEE\" data-code=\"0s4sIY3bYEE\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0s4sIY3bYEE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-02-2021, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T16:34:31-07:00","id":1458424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458400#post1458400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also possibly the most underrated Discipline in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about this. I mean, almost everyone I asked loves Auspex and deems it powerful and useful to a fault, even if YMMV. So it doesn't strikes me as underrated, but as adequately recognized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458416#post1458416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex is about gaining supernatural insights as mentioned but Tzimisce don't view people as &quot;people' as they're some of the most detached sociopathic Kindred alive. Why would they have a Discipline that shows them what other people think and feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>So they don't have to waste their time asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T16:59:00-07:00","id":1458428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which is why Dominate is a good Discipline for them but not, say, Presence as a Tzimisce does not persuade anyone and does need anyone to like them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's a very transactional way of viewing a Tzimisce's relationship with his followers. A Tzimsice doesn't need to threaten you with your father or disfigurement. You are property and you will obey because why wouldn't you? I tend to view the Tzimisce as mad scientists and Vicissitude as a fully explored version of their Discipline that other vampires mostly just rely on the nature of.<br /> <br /> Its not that it's different from Protean, it's that the Tzimisce took it further than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Allow me to explain via example:<br /> <br /> I think the best example of a Western non-Vampire Tzimisce in media would be Mr. House from Fallout: New Vegas. Mr. House is a figure who wants nothing more than to transform New Vegas into a perfect simaculum of Pre-War Vegas and has a mono-obsessive focus on recreating everything from the buildings to the mob. He has an army of scientifically engineered slaves (robots in his case) to enforce his will and identifies as an autocrat without irony.<br /> <br /> I think that Tzimisce by nature are somewhat monofocused on their domains and properties so Auspex feels like an odd fit to them. Tzmisce do not strike me as particularly insightful to other people or their motivation and its hard to believe a Tzimisce views anyone else (let alone his slaves) as &quot;people.&quot; Auspex is about gaining supernatural insights as mentioned but Tzimisce don't view people as &quot;people' as they're some of the most detached sociopathic Kindred alive. Why would they have a Discipline that shows them what other people think and feel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0s4sIY3bYEE\" data-code=\"0s4sIY3bYEE\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0s4sIY3bYEE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Tzim do not rule through Dominate, they had to rule through fear and blood bond, their entire culture makes no sense of they had Dominate as an option, with ot they are yet another high clan, without it they actually make sense and are interesting, all the archetypes of Tzim disintegrate into idiocy if they could just use Dominate, they would never develop war ghouls, or revenant families, because Dominate is just easier and better than either of those.<br /> <br /> Auspex however makes perfect sense, even with the dumpster fire new flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 09-02-2021, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T17:02:53-07:00","id":1458429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458428#post1458428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tzim do not rule through Dominate, they had to rule through fear and blood bond, their entire culture makes no sense of they had Dominate as an option</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how Dominate precludes the need to rule through fear and blood.<br /> <br /> That makes Dominate EASIER as a tool.<br /> <br /> Besides, this is not a new thing. The Old Clan Tzimisce had Dominate before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T17:35:37-07:00","id":1458430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458429#post1458429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how Dominate precludes the need to rule through fear and blood.<br /> <br /> That makes Dominate EASIER as a tool.<br /> <br /> Besides, this is not a new thing. The Old Clan Tzimisce had Dominate before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Justifying Tzimisce having Dominate in place of Auspex because OCT had Dominate in place of Vicissitude is like saying Ministry should have Potence instead of Protean because Warrior Setites had Potence instead of Obfuscate. Feels uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Concerning ruling through Dominate vs fear, it's really one or the other. Some people seem to think of Dominate working like Kilgrave from Jessica Jones (including Outstar, sadly enough), but Dominate is the opposite of fear. It's outright mind control, and the subjects rarely have any idea it's being used on them (Masquerade Threat: Low). There is no finesse. No intimacy. No hands-on training. Hardly any bloodshed at all. It's uncouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T17:57:06-07:00","id":1458433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458430#post1458430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Justifying Tzimisce having Dominate in place of Auspex because OCT had Dominate in place of Vicissitude is like saying Ministry should have Potence instead of Protean because Warrior Setites had Potence instead of Obfuscate. Feels uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Concerning ruling through Dominate vs fear, it's really one or the other. Some people seem to think of Dominate working like Kilgrave from Jessica Jones (including Outstar, sadly enough), but Dominate is the opposite of fear. It's outright mind control, and the subjects rarely have any idea it's being used on them (Masquerade Threat: Low). There is no finesse. No intimacy. No hands-on training. Hardly any bloodshed at all. It's uncouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a way of breaking the will of lesser beings to you. The weak and terrified are easier to control. AT least in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T19:34:08-07:00","id":1458439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458429#post1458429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how Dominate precludes the need to rule through fear and blood.<br /> <br /> That makes Dominate EASIER as a tool.<br /> <br /> Besides, this is not a new thing. The Old Clan Tzimisce had Dominate before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Old Clan Tzimisce also had zero in common with main line Tzim, whether the Dark Ages version or the Sabbat version, mostly because they had Dominate they turned into Ventrue wannabes, rather than being the quasi mystic transcendentalist body horror weirdos we get squicked out by and love. Plus Old Clan are dirty secrets of the Black Hand, viscititude is an alien parasite etc etc....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 09-02-2021, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T19:38:00-07:00","id":1458440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458439#post1458439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Old Clan Tzimisce also had zero in common with main line Tzim, whether the Dark Ages version or the Sabbat version, mostly because they had Dominate they turned into Ventrue wannabes, rather than being the quasi mystic transcendentalist body horror weirdos we get squicked out by and love. Plus Old Clan are dirty secrets of the Black Hand, viscititude is an alien parasite etc etc....</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm of the mind if you think Vicissitude is the most interesting part of the Tzimisce then you've missed the vast majority of their appeal. I'm not saying Vicissitude isn't interesting but it's kind of a surface level appeal.<br /> <br /> Its like loving Lasombra for Obternation.<br /> <br /> It's their culture and attitude that make them cool, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T19:49:29-07:00","id":1458441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458440#post1458440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I'm of the mind if you think Vicissitude is the most interesting part of the Tzimisce then you've missed the vast majority of their appeal. I'm not saying Vicissitude isn't interesting but it's kind of a surface level appeal.<br /> <br /> Its like loving Lasombra for Obternation.<br /> <br /> It's their culture and attitude that make them cool, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The culture and attitude have been made none sensical by the addition of dominate and the removal of auspex, and the OCT remain bad Ventrue wannabes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T19:58:49-07:00","id":1458442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458169#post1458169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prestation isn't something Harpies keep in their pockets and get to chuck out when they decide they don't like you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prestation is <i>exactly</i> something Harpies keep in their pockets and chuck out when it suits them. Or a party happens to be a rival or enemy. Or they just did something plain stupid. Or if the Harpy is just bored and wants the stir the pot a little. They just do it covertly, and with plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> What you're describing is what an idiot would do, perfectly in tune with your &quot;least charitable interpretation of everything&quot;, in contrast to practically everything ever published, shtick. The sort of person who'd never be a Harpy in the first place, because they don't know how to navigate prestation let alone control it, or <i>exploit</i> it.<br /> <br /> Simplest possible version, since swinging for the fences we're not, here: &quot;did you hear Elaine called in the boon she's owed by Chuck, to do a minor favor? Bum deal, if you ask me...oh, it seemed minor, but if you take a step back and look at the big picture, that 'minor favor' saved Elaine's domain. This led to that, and next thing you know, the real estate deal fell apart...but you know how these things go. That's way, way more than just a minor boon, really...but who am I to say? A deal's a deal...&quot; That gets heard by the right parties, word gets around the city Chuck's a shmuck. Chuck starts feeling cheated, gets pissed at Elaine, and that grudge gets a nice head start to explode later into something truly worth talking about, while Chuck now has to defend his status from being considered a shmuck by every lick in town.<br /> <br /> If only anyone in the city remembered that thirty or forty years ago, the Harpy was eyeing that same domain and Elaine snatched it right out from under them. And now that Elaine fixed up the place and the domain's secure, it's all the more tempting a target should something unfortunate happen to her at Chuck's hands...<br /> <br /> ...and all because of one &quot;tiny&quot;, &quot;innocuous&quot;, &quot;off the cuff&quot; comment, that happened to be said by the right person, at the right time, in the right place, and overheard by the right people.<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> soft power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a harpy were to decide that they weren't going to acknowledge a deal, and another third party comes up to acknowledge that the harpy did indeed witness a transaction, the harpy reputation and status will be trashed so hard that they might even get blood hunted. </div> </div> </div>Ya don't refuse to acknowledge a deal, or reneg. Ya <i>fuck with it</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most are going to side with the Ventrue, unless he really is out of favour. Going against a well established Ventrue will have you ostracised because it's simply not worth upsetting a powerful market force for... some fool who wants to bloody noses. </div> </div> </div>Not that Ventrue have a rep for overstepping their limitations, or massively overestimating their own esteem in the city while leaving a trail of quietly resentful vampires eager to leap at the chance of deposing the bastard, or anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampire who's petty is simply someone you want to avoid dealing with. </div> </div> </div>As opposed to a vampire who...evaluates their ongoing relationships in near-exclusive terms of the utility those relationships offer?<br /> <br /> Because that's the Ventrue. Bottom line uber alles. Never mix business, politics, and friendship and all that, can't have it both ways. You're either a rational actor who's going to cut ties when those ties cease to be beneficial, or you can be loyal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have to depend on someone for business, your average Ventrue will always be better than your average Toreador. </div> </div> </div>As long as someone else doesn't offer...how did you put it? &quot;a better deal&quot;?<br /> <br /> No having your cake and eating it too, here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ventrue almost always hit night society after a clan-scrutinized selection and a period of heavy tutelage. If they lack in one, they'll usually be made up for in the other. 9 times out of 10, your Ventrue will at least be adequate in all the things that matter to being a Ventrue, if not exceptional. </div> </div> </div>Or the Ventrue's sire did what every other Ventrue does: kiss the Gerousia's collective ass enough to ensure the Accounting is purely a ceremonial affair and the childe will be accepted unanimously regardless what they've done to that point. So long as they manage to not completely shit the bed during it, to the point voting &quot;yes&quot; or abstaining would be a stain on the Gerousia's dignitas. All else in the agoge is indoctrination and teaching the fledgling Ventrue how not to embarrass their sire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Toreador are infamous for lax embraces and frequently hap-hazard tutoring... </div> </div> </div>Yup, and as you yourself pointed out, the chaff separates itself from the wheat. No point spending decades investing heavily in a potential embrace or neonate if they're just going to turn out a fuck-up regardless, let 'em sink or swim on their own merit.<br /> <br /> Somehow I think this would be a <i>very</i> different conversation with <i>very</i> different outcomes, were we discussing which clan's neonates turn out tougher for how they're treated as fledglings: Ventrue or Gangrel. After all, the Ventrue are the Ventrue, but the Gangrel have <i>the exact same practices</i> as the Toreador when it comes to &quot;lax embraces&quot; and &quot;frequently haphazed tutoring&quot;...it just happens to be the case Gangrel do it in lupine-infested forests, Toreador do it in Toreador-infested Elysiums.<br /> <br /> Hell, at least the Lasombra do potential embraces the favor of fucking them up and seeing who perseveres <i>before</i> the embrace, to keep from embracing fuckup neonates in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The clan culture is toxic. the brand value of the clan suffers in comparison to the blue bloods as the clan is messy, decadent and disharmonious. </div> </div> </div>As compared to a blood bond- and conditioning-enforced monoculture second in all Kindred society to the Tremere? <i>You're</i> the one who decided to bring up the agoge, let's talk about <i>all</i> the implications of the agoge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also, if you read those &quot;the view of&quot; sections where the clans talk shit about one another? The Toreador cop way more flak than the Ventrue. The Ventrue often get grudging admiration from the low clans. The Toreador just get hate.) </div> </div> </div>And yet, Elysiums don't exactly seem to get firebombed, or raided with incendiary rounds and willy pete grenades, to whack a <i>Toreador</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The heated nature of the discussion aside I'm genuinly bemused by the Suggestion the Ventrue and their disciplines are a relic, they're easily one the most suited to modern nights. their disciplines are excellent for control and they excersive hard and soft power in a way which is incredably effective IRL. Genuinly a bizzare statement. </div> </div> </div>This whole thing started when someone took exception to my statement the Ventrue's power is a vestige of feudal Europe, carried over the course of centuries into modern nights; given that historical context, it's no given Ventrue would have been able to replicate that feat elsewhere in the world. And that to simply assume so, based on eurocentric social analysis, is eurocentric.<br /> <br /> Simply pointing out Ventrue holding praxis anywhere but Europe and North America is an exceeding rarity, even where Cainites are native or grew to dominance among other supernaturals, ought to be enough to make the point, but apparently not. Regardless of sect <i>or</i> subtype: there are Ventrue in the Laibon and Ashirra, not to mention Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> in the Sabbat; why are they neither hegemons, nor have elevated their status to that of hegemonic, in any of those three? Should be an easy question...that is, if Ventrue are the &quot;natural&quot; leaders, who always come out on top, they've been proposed in this thread to be.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, Ventrue have power in modern nights because they <i>had</i> power in the Industrial age, Renaissance, all the way back to the rise and hegemony of the Holy Roman Empire. Realistically, simply stating <i>that</i> is enough to irrevocably break this notion of unchallengeable Ventrue might in perpetuity. The Ventrue were forced to resettle in Germania for a reason, after all (getting deposed and evicted from Rome does that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-02-2021, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T20:54:37-07:00","id":1458446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458441#post1458441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The culture and attitude have been made none sensical by the addition of dominate and the removal of auspex, and the OCT remain bad Ventrue wannabes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue are lame.<br /> <br /> (Old Clan) Tzimisce are awesome.<br /> <br /> That's just my opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:22:14-07:00","id":1458458,"title":"","content":"has this forum gone absolutely mad? replace the ventrue with the tzimisce of all things?<br /> <br /> first of the tzimisce aren't interested in ruling a domain, they're interested in spiritualism, the crafts, occult research, finding new ways to entertain themselves. lording over a domain is just something they have to do because of their bane and traditions. the tzimisce is more interested in the rats in their basement then their subjects. by giving them dominate they've basically changed the tzimisce from being shit rulers because they have no interest in it to the point they don't develop any skills that might be usefull to rulership, to them being just shit at it because they have and develop the tools for it. the tzimisce not only make for shit rulers they have nothing in common with the ventrue other then &quot;they're in positions of power&quot;.<br /> <br /> on top of that the ventrue's issue isn't that they're vanilla, the most popular fantasy race is human ffs. if them being vanilla was truly the issue alot more ppl would be playing them. the issue is that, and pardon the d&amp;d jargon, that they're the most lawful clan which makes them very difficult to be creative with, that's their issue. the most common way ppl are creative with the ventrue is by making them caiti