nothing in common with the ventrue other then &quot;they're in positions of power&quot;.<br /> <br /> on top of that the ventrue's issue isn't that they're vanilla, the most popular fantasy race is human ffs. if them being vanilla was truly the issue alot more ppl would be playing them. the issue is that, and pardon the d&amp;d jargon, that they're the most lawful clan which makes them very difficult to be creative with, that's their issue. the most common way ppl are creative with the ventrue is by making them caitiff ventrue and at that point you might as well just play a caitiff.<br /> <br /> absolute lunacy this forum i tell you what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to underscore this but the people LITERALLY tied to the land because they are so incredibly obsessive about their rulership. I mean, there's a reason they have dirt in previous editions. I actually was really sad they changed the Weakness for V5 because it was so embellic of the Tzimisce's bond to the land as their lords and ladies/masters/rulers. Some powerful symbolism there.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, may I ask why people keep saying the Tzimisce are shit rulers? They managed to rule over Russia and Eastern Europe for most of human civilization.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T00:06:01-07:00","id":1458474,"title":"","content":"I guess good leadership is subjective. Both Ventrue and Tzimisce are extremly possessive and want to gain power and wealth. They both have their means to get a following and succeed in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T00:07:58-07:00","id":1458475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458474#post1458474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess good leadership is subjective. Both Ventrue and Tzimisce are extremly possessive and want to gain power and wealth. They both have their means to get a following and succeed in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ventrue and Tzimisce: Good leadership is being too strong to be overthrown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T01:00:57-07:00","id":1458480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458475#post1458475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ventrue and Tzimisce: Good leadership is being too strong to be overthrown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. But in case of Ventrue it is only a question of time when they will be overthrown given their obsession with Rome and the way the metaplot is written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T02:11:55-07:00","id":1458484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458442#post1458442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prestation is <i>exactly</i> something Harpies keep in their pockets and chuck out when it suits them. Or a party happens to be a rival or enemy. Or they just did something plain stupid. Or if the Harpy is just bored and wants the stir the pot a little. They just do it covertly, and with plausible deniability.<br /> What you're describing is what an idiot would do,<br /> Ya don't refuse to acknowledge a deal, or reneg. Ya <i>fuck with it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because what people really love is to have some meddlesome fop screw with their money. &quot;oh he owes you less&quot; and &quot;Oh he owes you more&quot;. This might work on naive fledglings, but it's little better than spam mail for most vampires. Doing this really is going to risk your position. I wouldn't do it unless someone's so out-of-favour that others would want me to screw them. If you're going to keep score, you need the facade of trust and honour for it, and you'll lose it like that <i>fast </i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not that Ventrue have a rep for overstepping their limitations, or massively overestimating their own esteem in the city while leaving a trail of quietly resentful vampires eager to leap at the chance of deposing the bastard, or anything. </div> </div> </div>There isn't a clan that doesn't do this. I'd argue it's only a prominent problem with the Ventrue because they can actually hold their claims. The Brujah are far more agressive in expansion, but they can't hold for shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As opposed to a vampire who...evaluates their ongoing relationships in near-exclusive terms of the utility those relationships offer?<br /> Because that's the Ventrue. Bottom line uber alles. Never mix business, politics, and friendship and all that, can't have it both ways. You're either a rational actor who's going to cut ties when those ties cease to be beneficial, or you can be loyal.As long as someone else doesn't offer...how did you put it? &quot;a better deal&quot;? </div> </div> </div>That's not the Ventrue. More Lasombra territory, or Toreador territory, it may apply to some extent towards the Tremere. The Ventrue wants nothing more than stability, they have an old-money attitude; favouring a long standing partner over a new and unproven undercutter is in their bones. The Ventrue are obliged to help friends and clan when they're down, the clan has written down rules for some of this. The clan has <i>F</i><i>ortitude </i>so it's in their nature to accept small losses for long term security and of course, reputation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the Ventrue's sire did what every other Ventrue does: kiss the Gerousia's collective ass enough to ensure the Accounting is purely a ceremonial affair and the childe will be accepted unanimously regardless what they've done to that point. So long as they manage to not completely shit the bed during it, to the point voting &quot;yes&quot; or abstaining would be a stain on the Gerousia's dignitas. All else in the agoge is indoctrination and teaching the fledgling Ventrue how not to embarrass their sire. </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;perfectly in tune with your &quot;least charitable interpretation of everything&quot;&quot;.<br /> Note that even if the Ventrue need to bribe their way into embracing, they're paying other members of the clan, so the clan grows stronger. Because the sire needs to go through such a tax to embrace, they're going to make damn sure their childe meets the bar and doesn't end up the worst investment ever. So even in corruption, the Ventrue work better than most other clans. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yup, and as you yourself pointed out, the chaff separates itself from the wheat. No point spending decades investing heavily in a potential embrace or neonate if they're just going to turn out a fuck-up regardless, let 'em sink or swim on their own merit. </div> </div> </div>This heavily comes at the cost of reputation. And fact is, Ventrue exel in resources to the point that that they can take the luxury of investing heavily into each embrace, not only can they delegate a good chunk of training to their plentiful retainers, but they also tend to build self sustaining empires that allow them to spend time away from work and on personally training new childer. The Toreador are up at the top when it comes to &quot;most childer turned anarch&quot; and &quot;most embarassing childer&quot;. The Gangrel at least don't give a fuck, their failed embraces were done with purpose, the Toreador's failed embraces are mistakes, and there's no mistake about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As compared to a blood bond- and conditioning-enforced monoculture second in all Kindred society to the Tremere? <i>You're</i> the one who decided to bring up the agoge, let's talk about <i>all</i> the implications of the agoge. </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue chose this system because it suits them. It may not suit you, but it suits them. The Ventrue may be old school, but they're adaptive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This whole thing started when someone took exception to my statement the Ventrue's power is a vestige of feudal Europe, carried over the course of centuries into modern nights; given that historical context, it's no given Ventrue would have been able to replicate that feat elsewhere in the world. And that to simply assume so, based on eurocentric social analysis, is eurocentric. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I'm just having a real hard time comprehending how a naturally charismatic, naturally well organized and naturally enduring clan wouldn't be one of the most dominant clans anywhere in the world. I'm... well travelled, if I put it modestly; if I want to be honest, my parents dragged me around everywhere when I was young to the point that I resent it somewhat (it came at the expense of other things). I also have A levels in sociology, politics, psychology and english lit. I also... read a lot of garbage asian novels... (you've flexed, I'll do it too)<br /> <br /> Point being, if you ignore cathayans for a moment, there's no way the Ventrue wouldn't do well in China, Japan, Malaysia, Thailand, India, west africa, before or after colonization. Cultures and systems may differ, but there's plenty of universalities and the Ventrue's advantages work on those universalities, while they have no inbuilt weakness that prevents them from adapting to the differences. The idea that a culture would be fundamentally different enough that the Ventrue wouldn't be an A tier clan because of, say, a history of Animist or Ancestor veneration is.... an assumption entirely born of ignorance and fetishization of the other. Especially when we talk modernity, where traditions have largely been pushed aside in the name of capital. You seem to have a very -never left America- view on things, and i find it quite infuriating that you want to export your patronizing, idealistic view on the rest of the world. That's ignorance and cultural imperialism if I ever saw it. No, animists aren't going to worship you if you conjure a fucking fireball anymore than a white anglo-saxon protestant would, and hard power is still extremely relevant in the modern world, otherwise military budgets wouldn't have shot up in real terms over the past two decades. Stop pretending you know better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply pointing out Ventrue holding praxis anywhere but Europe and North America is an exceeding rarity, even where Cainites are native or grew to dominance among other supernaturals, ought to be enough to make the point, but apparently not. Regardless of sect <i>or</i> subtype: there are Ventrue in the Laibon and Ashirra, not to mention Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> in the Sabbat; why are they neither hegemons, nor have elevated their status to that of hegemonic, in any of those three? Should be an easy question...that is, if Ventrue are the &quot;natural&quot; leaders, who always come out on top, they've been proposed in this thread to be. </div> </div> </div>First, we know fuck-all about regions outside of North America, we don't even have a good grasp of contemporary europe. Berlin by night and Fall of london are IIRC the only city books we have in english. Do you know how many cities there are in europe? Meanwhile the US has books on... Gary, Indianna.<br /> Second, The Ventrue in the Sabbat changed their Presence for Auspex, that's why they're not Sabbat leaders <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (and also because Tremere and orthadox Ventrue are immense threats to the dominant sabbat clans, and as elder Ventrue are generally smart enough to avoid the sabbat, a few neonates aren't going to last long against the machinations of elders)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or to put it another way, Ventrue have power in modern nights because they <i>had</i> power in the Industrial age, Renaissance, all the way back to the rise and hegemony of the Holy Roman Empire. Realistically, simply stating <i>that</i> is enough to irrevocably break this notion of unchallengeable Ventrue might in perpetuity. The Ventrue were forced to resettle in Germania for a reason, after all (getting deposed and evicted from Rome does that). </div> </div> </div>Serious posts only. Do you have a single fact to back such bold claims up? The Ventrue definetly have changed themselves with the times. Once merchants were pariahs to be kept out of the nobility, but once merchants really took over, the Ventrue happily embraced them. Nowadays, the Board meetings are as contemporary-corporate as they are Roman. I don't see anything which suggests Ventrue fail to adapt or that their power is a vestige. Aside from Revised tanking Fortitude, their disciplines haven't exactly gotten less competitive over the years (hell, despite Dominate going to shit, they're clearly some of the winners in V5, with both Presence and Fortitude getting sizable buffs relative to others)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-03-2021, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T03:18:57-07:00","id":1458486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458463#post1458463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, may I ask why people keep saying the Tzimisce are shit rulers? They managed to rule over Russia and Eastern Europe for most of human civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue are very much &quot;Go big or die&quot;<br /> The Tzmisce are &quot;Go big and you'll die&quot;<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the Ventrue's disciplines are the best option for acruing large amounts of wealth (OK you could probably swap Fortitude for Auspex or Obfuscate and do a little better, but that would undermine cohesion and how honourable Ventrue are) and the Ventrue weakness is a great encouragement to acquire large amounts of backgrounds and wealth.<br /> The Tzmisce's disciplines are.... really good for a small group of people, and animals, but they're very poor for dealing with lots of people. The land requirement doesn't actually push them to gain much more wealth than just enough to own the land, and actually it pushes them away from others because they're more loath to leave their territories and thus help others. They probably don't want lots of people in their territory because it might ruin the land, but also their privacy lets them get up to weird shit and thus you don't want many people in the territory because they might see the weird shit... <br /> <br /> Geography wise, the thing is, for most of european history, Russia wasn't considered europe, but a poor and backwards region of tundra. It wasn't till Peter the Great annexed a pathway into the baltics, built a western fleet, brought Russian Christianity in line with normal eastern orthadoxy, and tried to shave the beards off his people that Russia even tried to be considered &quot;european&quot;. The Tzmisce holding russia is... well... nobody wanted it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Poland on the otherhand was considered european. Poland and it's fractured commonwealth are no doubt a great source of inspiration for the Tzmisce, it can be seen in the way they name things. Anyhow, Poland got screwed over because it was a fractured commonwealth where nobles would elect weak kings so that they can gain more power and autonomy for themselves. Tzmisce are just like that. Ventrue are happy to work under and alongside other Ventrue. Tzmisce aren't, as soon as the childer is ready, they're pushed to get their own domain and to get away from their horrid sire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-03-2021, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T04:25:56-07:00","id":1458488,"title":"","content":"As I said, I think calling the Tzimisce bad leaders isn't actually true. But they do have a different style of leadership than the Ventrue. A local ruler isn't less of a ruler just because they want to keep local, and the Tzimisce still keep a strong network among themselves. Their rules on hospitality specially guarantee that, despite their propensity to isolation, they still get news on the world beyond their land and communication with other lords.<br /> <br /> They are also as good rulers over anyone on their domain as any vampire can be, <u>on a broad sense</u>, because for such old lords the people is a part of the land. They aren't equals, maybe not seem as &quot;people&quot;, but they need to be cared for, even if sometimes culled to not grow too much in numbers, because they're as much of a part of your possessions as anything else, and the Tzimisce take care of their possessions in their own way.<br /> <br /> I still think that Dominate isn't a good addition to their style of leadership. Their more spiritual side still calls for another kind of Discipline. It is important to remember that they aren't just owner of their lands, but a part of it. Their Disciplines are meant to represent their connection. Auspex let them be constantly in tune with their lands and surroundings, Animalism makes them not only command every denizen of the land, but also hear them, and through them get news of what the very land feels.<br /> <br /> Viscissitude is the only Discipline that really makes sense to be changed, although I see no need for it. But if it was, it should be by Koldunic Sorcery, or at least Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> On another note, our warring parties both called the other some variation of <u>ethnocentric</u>. Before I give my opinion on this regard, if I even will, that made me curious:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a>, what would you say about the vampiric leadership in Brazil? Discuss at your hearts content, if you would amuse me, I'm sincerely curious and may have actual use for the result, whatever it may be, for a future chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T05:02:57-07:00","id":1458491,"title":"","content":"\u200bI can't say I know much about Brazil.<br /> <br /> Assuming Camarilla and Orthodox (pre-5) VTM, You're more likely to have established Lasombra thanks to Portugese roots , with a good chance of a Lasombra primogen and a small but fair chance for a prince. Some Samedi might help the Nosferatu a little, but not much. Some historical instabilities may lead you to want to use more Brujah/Lasombra in your plots, but on the whole there's not really much to change who are most likely to dominate cities. From most likely to least likely: Ventrue, Toreador/Brujah, Lasombra/Malk, Nos/Gangrel, Tremere. Liberally add Independent/anarch subdomains as you see fit. Brazil's wealth divide means good eating for vampires, so overpopulate your cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:24:03-07:00","id":1458547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458463#post1458463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to underscore this but the people LITERALLY tied to the land because they are so incredibly obsessive about their rulership. I mean, there's a reason they have dirt in previous editions. I actually was really sad they changed the Weakness for V5 because it was so embellic of the Tzimisce's bond to the land as their lords and ladies/masters/rulers. Some powerful symbolism there.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, may I ask why people keep saying the Tzimisce are shit rulers? They managed to rule over Russia and Eastern Europe for most of human civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>i kind of expected this response: when i say the tzimisce aren't interested in ruling a domain i mean they do not care about the responsibilities of rulership. they're rulers because their bane and tradition requires them to be for the sake of survival not because they have a desire to rule (the ventrue and lasombra both do have a desire to rule). they need to rule but they don't want to. it was basically the reason the clan fell so hard in modern times. in the olden day they could just indulg in their sick desires and ppl would fall in line out of fear, a lack of other options and nobody was gonna help them. tht doesn't work in modern days because most ppl can just leave nowadays because they know there are other options so rulers need to put actual effort into preventing their domains from collapsing to which the tzimisce basically reacted with &quot;i could put effort into prevent my domain from collapsing but on the other hand, this is a really interesting book.&quot;<br /> <br /> the tzimisce by far lends itself best to a resentfull ruler character (the type of character that neglects his duties as a lord because he doesn't want to be one he just has to be) because any other clan can just try to leave, a tzimisce needs to overcome their clan bane before they can even bother to try that or has to constantly come back to refill their dirt bags which makes him extremely vunerable to anybody that wants to fuck him over in any way.<br /> <br /> the weird thing about V5 tzimisce is that they kinda seemed to understand that in the flavour text but then gave them a social discipline for ruling anyway because the ppl that desided on the disciplines didn't know or understand that dominate undermines the flavor text they gave the clan. (also old clan tzimisce was a decent idea that fails as a bloodline and only exists as one because some players didn't like vic and didn't have the backbone to create a character that didn't have dots in all their clan disciplines)<br /> <br /> ventrue on the other hand very big into the whole ruling thing, fairly certain they can only pitch a tent when they're sitting on a throne if you know what i mean. and when they wll do whatever it takes to prevent their domain from collapsing, if that means keeping ppl happy then he'll keep ppl happy and he'll take your happiness very serious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T13:39:46-07:00","id":1458564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458547#post1458547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i kind of expected this response: when i say the tzimisce aren't interested in ruling a domain i mean they do not care about the responsibilities of rulership. they're rulers because their bane and tradition requires them to be for the sake of survival not because they have a desire to rule (the ventrue and lasombra both do have a desire to rule). they need to rule but they don't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, if you believe rulership is about responsibility and not perks then you're not voivoding right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T14:04:24-07:00","id":1458565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458564#post1458564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bah, if you believe rulership is about responsibility and not perks then you're not voivoding right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>and that's why the tzimisce make for terrible lords/leaders/princes/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T14:15:27-07:00","id":1458570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458565#post1458565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that's why the tzimisce make for terrible lords/leaders/princes/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that would be every vampire ruler who ever lived.<br /> <br /> Is there a vampire who claims to be ruling for the people?<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe some Anarchs would be fooled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]