"value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T20:52:07-07:00","id":1458610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458570#post1458570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue that would be every vampire ruler who ever lived.<br /> <br /> Is there a vampire who claims to be ruling for the people?<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe some Anarchs would be fooled?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah when they wax nostalgic about what a utopia Carthage was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T02:53:28-07:00","id":1458633,"title":"","content":"No, I don't think the Ventrue are anything but Bastards, but they're lawful bastards, at least, they want to appear to be lawful, and they don't want to appear as bastards. <br /> <br /> Reputation is very important for Ventrue. It means more allies, and less people going after your special and limited herd. That means, more often than not, doing the right thing by others, investing in other vampires, giving people a clap on the shoulder and welcoming them into your house with a beaming greeting. You don't learn 4 dots of etiquette purely because it lets others know of your good breeding, you learn 4 dots of etiquette to please others and to avoid offending the wrong people even in difficult circumstances. Reputation means you need the semblance of honesty, a good dose of fairness, and you can't be so catty like the Toreador are. The Ventrue are famed for their old money values, which means they look down on those who are taking risks and recklessly expanding. Such behaviours invite hostility thus undermining the stability. The Ventrue need reputation for stability, and stability for their herds. They can't be free and fickle like the Toreador, they have something to protect more than shiny things, they've got a herd to worry about. <br /> <br /> Draconian Ventrue are rare, and can only really exist in cities with lots of ventrue that can shelter them, or with individuals that have a broad feeding type and don't have to overly worry about herd (IE total hack Caitiff that are posing as Ventrue) or when the Ventrue is so phenomneally powerful and has half the city under his thumb. <br /> <br /> It's really not fair to draw examples from city books. It's not the job of writers to provide good examples of the setting, it's up to writers to provide drama and intrigue, so dysfunctional Ventrue leading failing states are going to be grossly overrepresented. (see also: Nosferatu with hearts of gold, Malkavians who insist they're healthy, Brujah Barbarians, True-faith Lasombra, Toreador who are useful)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T14:14:01-07:00","id":1458727,"title":"","content":"I think the Assamite change was an attempt to undo the perception that Assamites=Arabic vampires.<br /> <br /> And now they're ironically more the Middle Eastern vampires rather than insane evil Blood Cult.<br /> <br /> YMMV.<br /> <br /> I think Ur-Shulgi was originally created to basically go, &quot;Yeah, all you think you know about the Assamites was actually just the followers of this dude.&quot; I was kind of disappointed that we didn't get the Web of Knives in Blood Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-04-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T00:12:42-07:00","id":1458787,"title":"","content":"Muslim Assamites should be an oxymoron. Islam doesn't work well for vampires, and it fundamentally doesn't work with the Zealous Khornate Assamites I like to imagine. My headcanon? The Ashirra was created to beat the Assamites: A sect wide agreement that nobody is to work with Assamites on the path of blood, and a sect wide agreement that giving Assamites mortal religions would utterly screw their cohession and willingness to devour other vampires. It worked well, and Ur-Shulgi, demon-spawn psycho that he is, was smart to try and purge such an influence from the clan. He got rid of the dissidents and the remaining Assamites are all on the same page, ready to devour their enemies with full willingness and efficiency. <br /> <br /> Also from a Sorcery perspective, Dur-An-ki would benefit very much from smashing monothiests and bringing old faiths back. You can't have cult members that are religiously opposed to the cult's sorcery. That just doesn't work. As a sorcerer, Ur-Shulgi's extreme prejudice makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T01:29:13-07:00","id":1458792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458787#post1458787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Muslim Assamites should be an oxymoron.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are both correct and missing the point, I think.<br /> <br /> Christian vampires should be an oxymoron too.<br /> <br /> Jewish vampires.<br /> <br /> Buddhist.<br /> <br /> Almost every single faith in the world is inherently opposed to being a blood drinking monster of pure evil. However, people aren't going to stop believing in their religion because they have become a monster. I mean, the inherent incompatibility with being a &quot;good person' and being a vampire is kind of one of the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> V:TM could never have been made anywhere but the Bible Belt of the American South, IMHO.<br /> <br /> But in the case of the Assamites specifically, I think the conflict between Ur-Shulgi and the Muslim vampires is basically just to make the cannibalistic psychopath Assamites into something completely removed from a religion that has a billion adherents. The developers had a choice between making the Assamites into a crazy cult like the Setites or a &quot;Middle Eastern Clan&quot; with far more variety.<br /> <br /> They chose the latter.<br /> <br /> So Ur-Shulgi is kind of the head of a Proto-Sabbat since the Web of Knives predates the Sword of Caine and passed down a lot of its insane beliefs. Indeed, it's very possible that the only reason Caine worship exists as we know it is because of the Assamite Antitribu. The Caine myth might even be originally Assamite legends that fell into the hands of Constantinople Christians who translated it.<br /> <br /> (I am referencing this book from V:TDA: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Book_of_the_Shining_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bo..._Shining_Blood</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-05-2021, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T04:26:23-07:00","id":1458807,"title":"","content":"No, I didn't miss the point, but I think it is more prudent for some faiths than others. Buddha offers recommendations, not commandments. A good chunk of very vocal &quot;Christians&quot; (the ones who will define themselves by faith) don't know shit about Jesus, so all that pacifism / don't judge/ prostitute's are fine stuff gets chucked out of the window because the Old Testament was more Badass, despite Jesus opposing most of it. &quot;Christians&quot;, especially Protestants, have a pick and choose attitude. Muslims are generally far more aware not only of what they should and shouldn't do, but also of what separates them from others and is thus integral to their identity (even if some of those things are more Tribal traditions than something the book told them to do)<br /> <br /> The Path of Blood is a really metal religion. Real religion just ties Assamites down (and comes across as mean and foolish). Ur-Shulgi made Assamites great again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T04:41:27-07:00","id":1458810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458807#post1458807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Blood is a really metal religion. Real religion just ties Assamites down (and comes across as mean and foolish). Ur-Shulgi made Assamites great again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is an argument that makes sense. Objections withdrawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T08:08:22-07:00","id":1458837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458484#post1458484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because what people really love is to have some meddlesome fop screw with their money.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/eOHiGhO.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> It's only the entire basis of the post-Bretton Woods global economy. So, I guess you're <i>technically</i> right, we don't &quot;like&quot; it.<br /> <br /> We <b>love</b> it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...This might work on naive fledglings, but it's little better than spam mail for most vampires... </div> </div> </div>You mean a given city's bored elders who need nightly drama and distractions, and tend to stir the pot for amusement, cash, and prizes? The ones for whom bickering about prestation would be a valuable way to pass the time and push the nagging understanding they're condemned to an eternity of stagnancy and existence, for the sake of existence?<br /> <br /> Now you're obliquely arguing the Jyhad just, doesn't exist or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're going to keep score, you need the facade of trust and honour for it, and you'll lose it like that <i>fast </i>. </div> </div> </div>An astute reader might wonder about your need to disclaim that with the word &quot;facade&quot;. The dictionary definition of that word being, &quot;an outward appearance that is maintained to conceal a less pleasant or creditable reality&quot;. In other words, thanks for admitting what I'm saying goes on, does indeed go on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue it's only a prominent problem with the Ventrue because they can actually hold their claims. </div> </div> </div>Which is why the supposed monolithic clan of politicians and merchants can't hold the finance capitol of the world, or the capitol of the country it's in which happens to be the world's foremost economic and military superpower, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not the Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>Well in the case of the latter city I mentioned...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...More Lasombra territory... </div> </div> </div>What was the clan of the last Prince to hold Washingon, DC, before it fell to the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue wants nothing more than stability, they have an old-money attitude; favouring a long standing partner over a new and unproven undercutter is in their bones. </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue want power. And you still haven't answered to the &quot;rational actor or loyal&quot; dichotomy, and how your characterization of the clan is self-contradictory; quit trying to change the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that even if the Ventrue need to bribe their way into embracing, they're paying other members of the clan, so the clan grows stronger. </div> </div> </div>No, their <i>elders</i> grow stronger. Key point, when one reads into the specific grievances of those Ventrue who <i>do</i> go Anarch, or even the case of the Ventrue<i> antitribu</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue chose this system because it suits them. It may not suit you, but it suits them. The Ventrue may be old school, but they're adaptive. </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue didn't &quot;choose&quot; this system. Their methuselahs did; they brainwashed elders into accepting it, who in turn brainwash the ancillae, and in turn the neonates. It suits those who <i>benefit</i> from it. Ventrue clan hierarchy is a bigger pyramid scheme than the Tremere's, and the Tremere <i>literally call their clan hierarchy the Pyramid</i>.<br /> <br /> Casting out those who resist indoctrination, or fail to conform to standards adopted millennia ago with practically zero substantive change over that time, is the opposite of adaptivity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sorry, I'm just having a real hard time comprehending how a naturally charismatic, naturally well organized and naturally enduring clan wouldn't be one of the most dominant clans anywhere in the world. </div> </div> </div>Well you better start real fast, because they're not. They like to <i>pretend</i> otherwise, but the reality is Camarilla influence extends little further than Europe, certain parts of North America, and a handful of enclaves in the economic south. If the Ventrue <i>were</i> capable of the feats you claim, they <i>would</i> be in charge globally; they are <i>not</i>, which means your argument is incorrect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that a culture would be fundamentally different enough that the Ventrue wouldn't be an A tier clan because of, say, a history of Animist or Ancestor veneration is.... an assumption entirely born of ignorance and fetishization of the other... </div> </div> </div>There's something really, <i>really</i> funny about this statement, but I'll drop the punchline in a minute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...You seem to have a very -never left America- view on things, and i find it quite infuriating that you want to export your patronizing, idealistic view on the rest of the world... </div> </div> </div>Ah, diet &quot;I'm not racist, you're racist!&quot;. Are we <i>really</i> that low on arguments, now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...That's ignorance and cultural imperialism if I ever saw it... </div> </div> </div>I don't recall the Abrahamic faiths being indigenous to the Americas. What were most Native American faiths again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and hard power is still extremely relevant in the modern world, otherwise military budgets wouldn't have shot up in real terms over the past two decades. </div> </div> </div>Okay, so that's called &quot;inflation&quot;. Defense spending as percentage of GDP has remained stable, but trending <i><b>downwards</b></i>, globally over the past twenty years, with two notable exceptions: during the 2008 economic crisis when global GDP sharply dropped, and during the 2020 economic crisis when global GDP likewise dropped, but with no corresponding reduction in defense budgets leading to a higher percentage of GDP spent. Notable exceptions do exist, like NATO countries which have finally figured out sucking the US defense teat is no longer sustainable and are therefore <i>normalizing</i> defense spending, and countries like Saudi Arabia which have a genocide to conduct and have been buying (from the US) accordingly.<br /> <br /> We're actually in the <i>lowest</i> period of global defense spending as percentage of GDP since 1960; i.e., the height of the Cold War.<br /> <br /> And when we're talking about the country that spends more than the next ten in defense combined when eight of those are allies, that's not about the relevance of hard power in geopolitics at all. If it were, the US wouldn't be blowing trillions on planes the Pentagon didn't even want and don't work, and a new fleet of aircraft carriers in a naval doctrine landscape increasingly dominated by submarines, while ignoring severe and ongoing strategic deficiencies in asymmetric conflict and even land warfare in <i>symmetric</i> conflict that have been known factors since Vietnam. And not to be blunt, if it were about hard power Riyadh would have been transformed into a glowing green parking lot twenty years ago, instead of the US having <i>just </i>withdrawn from Afghanistan...having its ass handed to it for the same twenty years, by the kids and grandkids of the guys our own intelligence community trained and armed to fight the Soviets.<br /> <br /> No, it's not about the relevance of hard power <i>at all</i>. It's about the <i>soft </i>power of defense lobbyists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have a single fact to back such bold claims up? </div> </div> </div>Other than the giant freaking map in the DAV core book that shows Ventrue domains as largely coterminous with the Holy Roman Empire? Other than the entire sourcebook and pre-published chronicle about this specific topic? The clanbook itself literally explains this all as part of the clan's history, up to and including the Ventrue clan's infiltration of the Carolingian and Habsburg dynasties and the embrace of Carolingian and Habsburg scions.<br /> <br /> The <i>one</i> section of Ventrue domains outside the HRE is Hungary, and there nearly every published Ventrue is either literally named Arpad, has a sire or childe named Arpad, or is politically or financially tied to the Arpad dynasty. The Arpad dynasty being the <i>founders of the Principality and Kingdom of Hungary</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>At least</i> bother to read the damn clan books (and <i>DA:Europe</i>, <i>Under the Black Cross</i>, <i>Transylvania by Night</i>, or at least <i>Lore of the Clans</i>) before asking for sources. Hell, at least bother to read the <i>core books</i>' sections on history and the clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue definetly have changed themselves with the times. Once merchants were pariahs to be kept out of the nobility, but once merchants really took over, the Ventrue happily embraced them. </div> </div> </div>Now we're just going to repeat what I said pages ago, and hope no one notices?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457577#post1457577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it another way, Ventrue aren't &quot;rulers&quot; just because they one night collectively decided writ nothing they were going to be &quot;rulers&quot;; the clan leveraged its military might through mortal pawns in the Dark Ages into feudal wealth, leveraged that feudal wealth and influence through the Renaissance to reform as an aristocratic, mercantile, clan, then leveraged its mercantile influence to rebuild itself into the political class of the Modern era through the rise of western liberal democracy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457590#post1457590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally just said why. They <i>already had</i> the power, prestige, money, and influence, and leveraged that institutional momentum to successfully transition as culture and society shifted. We already know what would have happened to the Ventrue were it not for the rise and prosperity of the Holy Roman Empire: they're called the Tzimisce. This isn't about who had the power, prestige, money and influence today, it's about who had the power, prestige, money and influence a thousand years ago, and carried it to today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny how those were &quot;fallacies&quot; then, to which you took great exception. What changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-05-2021, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T11:18:11-07:00","id":1458855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well you better start real fast, because they're not. They like to <i>pretend</i> otherwise, but the reality is Camarilla influence extends little further than Europe, certain parts of North America, and a handful of enclaves in the economic south. If the Ventrue <i>were</i> capable of the feats you claim, they <i>would</i> be in charge globally; they are <i>not</i>, which means your argument is incorrect. </div> </div> </div>That's not really accurate pre 5th edition, in which the Ashirra had functionally caved to them in V20, for instance. Pre 5e, Turkey was Camarilla influenced as presented, they otherwise held not insignificant territory in South Asia with the Kuei Jin having been retconned out of their attack wave in V20, relatedly V20 had them as managing to keep their hold on Macau despite being outright in China. They otherwise since 2e had a variety of cities in South and Central America (and even managed a degree of reach into Mexico itself with their hold of Veracruz, as far as managing to reach outside of the US/Canada in North America otherwise, which is impressive given that the country is/was otherwise largely heavily Sabbat territory). The Camarilla, while I wouldn't call them <i>in charge</i> globally per se, certainly had impressive and significant global reach and influence to leverage just fine. The idea of them being restricted to Europe and parts of North America doesn't really bear out with the material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What was the clan of the last Prince to hold Washingon, DC, before it fell to the Sabbat? </div> </div> </div>Up until his faked death, part of how he held it within the Camarilla was by pretending to be Ventrue and going along with them as a crucial part of his overall ruse. That's really worth noting, as far as how important he viewed not being on the radar and otherwise being thought of as Ventrue in terms of the (admittedly hilarious and silly, even for early VtM) master plans he had before he got exposed, faked his death and seems to have proclaimed &quot;well screw my whole previous thing then&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The <i>one</i> section of Ventrue domains outside the HRE is Hungary, and there nearly every published Ventrue is either literally named Arpad, has a sire or childe named Arpad, or is politically or financially tied to the Arpad dynasty. The Arpad dynasty being the <i>founders of the Principality and Kingdom of Hungary</i>. </div> </div> </div>To take a moment to be specific on the Ventrue during the Medieval Period and their reach of influence and territory in that time: As far as the conditions of the Dark Medieval and any statements that can be made there: Under Mithras, a bunch of England was also Ventrue held. There were several cities otherwise, significant ones even, certainly in DAV, that had Ventrue princes. Anna Comnena held authority over the Empire of Nicaea for example, which was in a growing and ascendant phase overall in terms of post fourth crusade recovery, Jerusalem being held by a Ventrue (sure Qawiya the Salubri held Outremer overall, but Jerusalem specifically had a Ventrue prince), The Danava were a significant presence in India (though not to the tune that they would be later certainly). In Italy the Ventrue held Ravenna, Verona and Siena, and Fabrizio Ulfila wielded vast influence across the entire area (obviously not including Sicily). Milan in 1230 still has the Ventrue holding on there, even if we know how that story is ultimately going to end. Camilla, despite being The Worst, held significant power over Rome. The Ventrue had managed to extend their reach into Scandinavia as well, with several Ventrue princes there. It was noted that Poland was a fractious mess with territory being held by a variety of clans, including the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Really while certainly there were territories that squeezed the Ventrue out or certainly kept them at bay (France for instance and the Courts of love making them a nonentity. Though being fair to Geoffrey du Temple, he was managing to cling to some power in Paris such that he was starting to be feared again), it's entirely fair to view them as regardless having managed to extend tendrils, and entirely significant ones, across Europe and even some places beyond during the Long Night/War of Princes era and held significant, even verging on foundational influence in any number of places not the HRE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  Briefly looked like I said Mexico wasn't part of North America, just wanted to fix for clarity. 09-05-2021, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T12:31:44-07:00","id":1458862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458837#post1458837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You mean a given city's bored elders who need nightly drama and distractions, and tend to stir the pot for amusement, cash, and prizes? The ones for whom bickering about prestation would be a valuable way to pass the time and push the nagging understanding they're condemned to an eternity of stagnancy and existence, for the sake of existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>First point goes to you: you're right, dicking around with shit like this is entertainment and somewhat of an accepted practice... among elders. You're still going to wrack up enemies and lose reputation for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An astute reader might wonder about your need to disclaim that with the word &quot;facade&quot;. The dictionary definition of that word being, &quot;an outward appearance that is maintained to conceal a less pleasant or creditable reality&quot;. In other words, thanks for admitting what I'm saying goes on, does indeed go on. </div> </div> </div>The issue is you make it sound like it's something people do openly. It ain't. You hide that shit. You do it in moderation, when you can get away with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why the supposed monolithic clan of politicians and merchants can't hold the finance capitol of the world, or the capitol of the country it's in which happens to be the world's foremost economic and military superpower, right? </div> </div> </div>If these things were important, they'd have them. Wait sorry that's a bit flippant: The Ventrue hold London. They also hold... most of the states. They also hold.. a lot of europe. Let's be honest, the Ventrue don't need to go directly to washington to influence policies. That's a terrible idea. They just need to hire people to do that for them. Lobbying. It's fairly standard practice in that crazy land, in other countries you need to be subtle about bribes and corruption... ah. Anyhow, Dominating heads of state has... never been a good idea, and since it isn't a good idea, there's no reason to personally be in these locations. It's not like the Sabbat have a vested interest in undoing America's corruption, they probably patronize the same people with the same ideas.<br /> <br /> No, their <i>elders</i> grow stronger. Key point, when one reads into the specific grievances of those Ventrue who <i>do</i> go Anarch, or even the case of the Ventrue<i> antitribu</i>.[/quote]<br /> Elders growing stronger is still good for the clan as a whole. Those elders obviously have better ideas on what to do with their gains than you did, trading them away for some foolish want of a childer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue didn't &quot;choose&quot; this system. Their methuselahs did; they brainwashed elders into accepting it, who in turn brainwash the ancillae, and in turn the neonates. It suits those who <i>benefit</i> from it. Ventrue clan hierarchy is a bigger pyramid scheme than the Tremere's, and the Tremere <i>literally call their clan hierarchy the Pyramid</i>.<br /> <br /> Casting out those who resist indoctrination, or fail to conform to standards adopted millennia ago with practically zero substantive change over that time, is the opposite of adaptivity. </div> </div> </div>Source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well you better start real fast, because they're not. They like to <i>pretend</i> otherwise, but the reality is Camarilla influence extends little further than Europe, certain parts of North America, and a handful of enclaves in the economic south. If the Ventrue <i>were</i> capable of the feats you claim, they <i>would</i> be in charge globally; they are <i>not</i>, which means your argument is incorrect. </div> </div> </div> MarkK has some pretty interesting facts for you here (IE you're very wrong) but even if they did only have the USA and Europe, that'd be, like, the two wealthiest and most influentual regions in the world. If it weren't for the Cathayans, who's to say they wouldn't have east asia too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's something really, <i>really</i> funny about this statement, but I'll drop the punchline in a minute. </div> </div> </div>Enlighten us. I don't see the joke, or the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, diet &quot;I'm not racist, you're racist!&quot;. Are we <i>really</i> that low on arguments, now? </div> </div> </div>ad hominem. If you want to elevate the argument, Address the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't recall the Abrahamic faiths being indigenous to the Americas. What were most Native American faiths again? </div> </div> </div>In the north? Animist, yes, they didn't have much of a Ventrue presence while they were animalist, but they also... weren't urbanized... and that's a far more pressing issue. Before Europeans we know the Americas had Settites, Gangrel and Nosferatu, and I think Baali. The South had impressive cities, but there's the issue of getting there: special diet Ventrue aren't well suited for travel.<br /> <br /> (also note: indigenous faiths in the Americas are now minority faiths. Abraham is the only dude that matters if we want to look at things on a macro scale.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so that's called &quot;inflation&quot;. Defense spending as percentage of GDP has remained stable, but trending <i><b>downwards</b></i>, globally over the past twenty years, with two notable exceptions: during the 2008 economic crisis when global GDP sharply dropped, and during the 2020 economic crisis when global GDP likewise dropped, but with no corresponding reduction in defense budgets leading to a higher percentage of GDP spent. Notable exceptions do exist, like NATO countries which have finally figured out sucking the US defense teat is no longer sustainable and are therefore <i>normalizing</i> defense spending, and countries like Saudi Arabia which have a genocide to conduct and have been buying (from the US) accordingly.<br /> <br /> We're actually in the <i>lowest</i> period of global defense spending as percentage of GDP since 1960; i.e., the height of the Cold War.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Did you not read that i wrote <i>real</i> terms? percentage of GDP spending isn't really that reliable either, absolute terms are more relevant. Nato normalizing defense spending isn't something to trivialize. The US inflates it's budget because it's corrupt, it doesn't really matter if they increase or decrease spending by 5%, it won't have an impact on war. US tanks literally waste ammo because they have too much of it and need to buy more. If anyone else in Nato increased their percentage of GDP budget by 1%, that could be an increase of 50%, even 100%; that's double the money. It's relative. Wave the flag a little less, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T15:57:57-07:00","id":1458886,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No personal attacks please. Disagree with a poster's point and not accuse them of anything. </span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T16:47:54-07:00","id":1458887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458862#post1458862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First point goes to you: you're right, dicking around with shit like this is entertainment and somewhat of an accepted practice... among elders. You're still going to wrack up enemies and lose reputation for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does everything else if you cock it up. Welcome to the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue is you make it sound like it's something people do openly. It ain't. You hide that shit. You do it in moderation, when you can get away with it. </div> </div> </div>What part about the words &quot;covertly&quot; and &quot;plausible deniability&quot; were particularly unclear? And indeed, a Harpy &quot;simply&quot; opining on a debt owed and repaid is the very definition of, unless there's an alternate interpretation of &quot;...and all because of one &quot;tiny&quot;, &quot;innocuous&quot;, &quot;off the cuff&quot; comment, that happened to be said <i>by the right person</i>, <i>at the right time</i>, <i>in the right place</i>, and <b><i>overheard by the right people</i></b>&quot; of which I'm unaware.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be honest, the Ventrue don't need to go directly to washington to influence policies. That's a terrible idea. They just need to hire people to do that for them. </div> </div> </div>Except as even <i>you</i> admit, the clan lives and dies on dignitas, <i>perception</i> of strength and unity, &quot;stability&quot;, and &quot;reliability&quot;. Being unable to hold the financial capitol of the world and the <i>actual</i> capitol of the country with a <i>few dozen thousand</i> nuclear warheads, really has to be a stain on that so-precious dignitas, strength, and stability, yes? We ain't talking about a state capitol, we're talking about domain with control over the plurality of global GDP and the <i>majority</i> of global military might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Source. </div> </div> </div>Literally the ones I stated in the previous post. You can add <i>Clanbook: Ventrue</i> and <i>Lore of the Clans</i> to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MarkK has some pretty interesting facts for you here (IE you're very wrong)... </div> </div> </div>Not really. The only domain worth mentioning was Britannia, care of a single methuselah I already mentioned. He quite openly mentioned other key domains were soon to fall, or ultimately within the power of <i>other</i> key players and sects. Those sections of Italy mentioned were, at the time, still part of the Holy Roman Empire (only having gained independence in the 14th Century if I remember correctly). &quot;Tendrils&quot; of influence isn't synonymous with praxis.<br /> <br /> And the bit about Camilla isn't just irrelevant (<i>Roman</i> prince), it's honestly ironic. Camilla's deposition being why Ventrue retreated to Germania in the first place...a feat soon replicated by the Toreador in the Courts of Love, something MarkK himself mentioned. So, about Ventrue actually being able to hold domains...wanna rethink that a bit?<br /> <br /> So, I suppose we have <i>two more</i> Ventrue -- methuselahs in <i>this</i> case -- who fall right into the &quot;totally an exception, not the rule&quot; category of being complete assholes who overreached, overestimated their own power in hubris, and got what was rightfully coming to them in the end.<br /> <br /> The list is...what, now? Alexander of Paris, Mithras, Camilla, Hardestadt the Elder, Hardestadt the Younger, Jurgen, Jan Pieterzoon, Sebastian LeCroix (not that I mentioned him), and since I mentioned them obliquely, we can add Bulscu, Geza Arpad, Zombar, and Nova Arpad, too. I haven't even mentioned Erik Eigermann or Gustav Breidenstein's <i>literal </i>Nazi ass, <i>yet</i>. I mean, I was being nice up until this point letting the Gary, IN, comment slide because the <i>other</i> half of <i>that</i> equation is, well...<i>Lodin</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Totally</i> exceptions to the rule. I promise.<br /> <br /> That leaves the thing about Marcus Vitel's true clan...which is honestly, the single funniest thing about it. This supposedly big, all-encompassing, monoculture with its fingers in everything, eyes everywhere, endless influence, beloved by everyone, and the tightest-knit clan culture sparing the Tremere...and a member of <i>that clan's nemeses</i>, an apparently inferior clan made of inferior stock, just...slides right in there and outdoes the Ventrue in everything they're supposedly best at.<br /> <br /> And when he was <i>finally</i> found out, it took a bunch of <i>Brujah</i> to take him down...because the Ventrue in the fight got the <i>dogshit</i> kicked out of them, and were the <i>first</i> to get KO'ed. If I remember right, it was Theo Bell and his &quot;not that great, really&quot; incendiary rounds, and Christof's fresh-out-of-torpor, Dark Ages neonate, Ainkurn-swinging, ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ad hominem. If you want to elevate the argument, Address the point. </div> </div> </div>You're the one who said,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457581#post1457581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...The dude just wants to project his opinions on a class he doesnt like and ascribe these faults to the Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Now </i>all of a sudden you want me to play by Marquess of Queensberry rules and bemoan my...what was the term again, &quot;rancidity&quot;? Whilst accusing me of bigotry, and expecting me to back down after that allegation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...they didn't have much of a Ventrue presence while they were animalist, but they also... weren't urbanized... and that's a far more pressing issue. </div> </div> </div>It's almost as if in environments that lacked the precise causal chain of social, economic, and political development that Europe underwent for the millennium and a half following the fall of Rome, the Ventrue turned out to not do so great.<br /> <br /> i.e., &quot;my entire point with which you took issue in the first place&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...special diet Ventrue aren't well suited for travel. </div> </div> </div>Well, well, well. It's almost as if this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457590#post1457590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and almost all of them lack monstrous Achilles' heels on the scale of the Ventrue as a clan flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>didn't turn out to be quite the &quot;fallacy&quot; you thought it was in the first place, eh? This is what you had to say about it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457629#post1457629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ventrue Clan flaw isn't anywhere near as big a deal as you think it is...Really, the flaw drives Ventrue to work together and excel. What does a Ventrue need most to alleviate his curse? Backgrounds. What do Ventrue and their amazing people skills excel at most? Acquiring backgrounds. Ethnic group? Foster a community for them, encourage them to have more kids. Amputees? Reintroduce corporal punishment, or set yourself up at a hostpital/Veteran gathering site. Virgins? Encourage and fund those weird &quot;Christian&quot; abstinence groups, or anime. A vampire should always be trying to rig the game in their favour, and the Ventrue are the extreme of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That opinion sure seemed to change right fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also note: indigenous faiths in the Americas are now minority faiths. Abraham is the only dude that matters if we want to look at things on a macro scale.) </div> </div> </div>This rather speaks for itself, coming from someone accusing <i>others</i> of bigotry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did you not read that i wrote <i>real</i> terms? percentage of GDP spending isn't really that reliable either, absolute terms are more relevant. Nato normalizing defense spending isn't something to trivialize. The US inflates it's budget because it's corrupt, it doesn't really matter if they increase or decrease spending by 5%, it won't have an impact on war. US tanks literally waste ammo because they have too much of it and need to buy more. If anyone else in Nato increased their percentage of GDP budget by 1%, that could be an increase of 50%, even 100%; that's double the money. It's relative. Wave the flag a little less, please. </div> </div> </div>The US defense budget of FY1945 was $59.8bn, about twelve times less than the proposed $715bn US defense budget for FY2022. In &quot;real&quot; terms. That's today, versus the peak of the US war economy during the largest conflict in human history. In other words, an estimated today's 3.7% of GDP, versus World War II's 26% of GDP (allocated) and 37% of GDP (total outlays).<br /> <br /> With regards to NATO defense spending, you <i>do</i> realize the US <i>subsidizes</i> those countries' defense, correct? What has happened, is NATO countries are <i>onloading</i> the cost of <i>their own</i> defense, to meet agreed-upon spending goals of...wait for it...<i>2% of GDP</i>. The <i>actual</i> change to date, in &quot;real&quot; and &quot;relative&quot; terms as you apparently &quot;demand&quot;, is...3.9 <i>percent</i>.<br /> <br /> Is 3.9% what you mean by defense budgets having &quot;shot up&quot;?<br /> <br /> That's why &quot;real&quot; terms are meaningless, and only useful if you're a professional wrong person getting paid big bucks to yell on the idiot box to misinform people into voting for corrupt assholes, in between Lockheed, Boeing, General Dynamics, and BAE Systems commercials. If you want actual, substantive, analysis of economic and political KPI's over time, you look at inflation-agnostic statistics like percentages of GDP/GNP, or state budgets, revenues, or outlays.<br /> <br /> This concludes today's episode of &quot;Fuck Neocons&quot;. But thanks for at least admitting the foibles of the US defense budget boil down to defense lobbyists' <i>soft</i> power, as opposed to the relevance of <i>hard</i> power in international relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-05-2021, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T20:13:23-07:00","id":1458919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. The only domain worth mentioning was Britannia, care of a single methuselah I already mentioned. He quite openly mentioned other key domains were soon to fall, or ultimately within the power of <i>other</i> key players and sects. Those sections of Italy mentioned were, at the time, still part of the Holy Roman Empire (only having gained independence in the 14th Century if I remember correctly). &quot;Tendrils&quot; of influence isn't synonymous with praxis. </div> </div> </div>You don't then remember correctly. Starting in the late 12th century with conflicts like the Lombard League vs Barbarossa, The HRE's hold over those sections of Italy was increasingly tenuous to at times outright nonexistent (or at best theoretical and involved treaties that gave various cities what amounted to independence that both parties would be polite enough to pretend still had HRE authority over it) and in that era exacerbated by the Guelph/Ghibelline conflict. Northern Italy was independent to the point that in the 1230s Frederick was having to wage active war on its city states to try and exert his authority over them, an authority often actively undermined by the ongoing Papal efforts to more or less wipe out the Hohenstaufen dynasty. Frederick's death in 1250 made Imperial authority over northern Italy increasingly nonexistent as far as his being the last guy with a really good shot of making it happen, and the Battle of Parma 2 years before his death would regardless destroy that authority for a functional generation. Many of the cities I mentioned had extended bouts of full on independence. While the HRE would sometimes manage brief revivals of authority here and there in Northern Italy, mostly facilitated by cities that would profess loyalty to the Empire despite in any practical sense existing as independent political entities, as a thing they held full dominion over, the 13th century was the era where for all functional intents and purposes Northern Italy slipped out of their hold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Tendrils&quot; of influence isn't synonymous with praxis. </div> </div> </div>If you don't believe that multiple Ventrue princes in an area is reflective of Ventrue holding significant influence in an area, I'm not really sure what to tell you? You seem to be demanding some kind of binary view that if the Ventrue did not hold total dominion over an area, you can ignore that they nevertheless could and did hold entirely significant influence in it. The idea that the Ventrue did not have influence that extended across Europe and beyond it in the Dark Medieval is not actually borne out by the actual printed content of Dark Ages stuff. If an area has multiple Ventrue princes, it's a really odd stance to say the Ventrue did not have influence in that area. It feels sort of goal post shifting to in the face of that being pointed out to say something like &quot;well, those places don't count.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He quite openly mentioned other key domains were soon to fall, or ultimately within the power of <i>other</i> key players and sects. </div> </div> </div>The domain that was going to fall soon was Milan really (noted as going to fall soon to the Lasombra, which we know happens for Giangaleazzo to take it). Nicaea under Anna for instance would ultimately re-establish the Byzantine Empire for a few centuries (I like the idea that she died on the walls in 1452 against the Turks, it feels poetic. She apparently didn't, but I like the idea as my personal headcanon). The Ventrue holdings in Italy, Poland, Scandinavia, were not within the power of other key players or sects. And again, the holdings in Italy, not part of the HRE. Dark Ages Europe itself refers to them as independent and waiting to see if Frederick is going to invade and try and assert his authority there (which, as per above, he does, the wars go back and forth for almost two decades, he ultimately fails. Which is a little sad really? I can't help but root for ol Stupor Mundi and his wacky ideas like &quot;Trial by Ordeal is insane nonsense&quot; and &quot;Hey, what if I use diplomacy to get Jerusalem back instead of waves of futile rolling zealot bloodshed that go nowhere.&quot;)<br /> <br /> To go even further afield, the Dark Medieval is when Antonius the Ventrue (not Michael's dead lover, different Antonius) held Cairo from the 10th century until his death in the early 15th, well after the end of that era. The Hijazi, a bloodline of Arabic Ventrue, hold significant holdings in Arabia around that period as well. The Ventrue and their influence get around just fine in DAV times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the bit about Camilla isn't just irrelevant (<i>Roman</i> prince), it's honestly ironic. Camilla's deposition being why Ventrue retreated to Germania in the first place...a feat soon replicated by the Toreador in the Courts of Love, something MarkK himself mentioned. So, about Ventrue actually being able to hold domains...wanna rethink that a bit? </div> </div> </div>He's a Ventrue who held domain in Italy, an extremely significant one, to the point that he could manipulate politics to mess with the Pope. Now, that was a terrible idea, but the idea that he wasn't there in the Dark Medieval and didn't wield considerable power is off. He ruled over Rome and was a unwitting proxy of another Ventrue in his doing so besides. I'm not sure what point you feel you're making here in the face of my own? My note was that you could find Ventrue princes and influences well across Europe outside of the HRE across the Dark Medieval period. He's an example of that. That he's a Roman prince is in fact specifically the point. There's... not really any irony there?<br /> <br /> Similarly, the idea that Camilla's deposition (which some books don't treat as a thing that happened, I guess I should say, compared to people erroneously thinking the Great Fire killed him, or what have you) being why the Ventrue retreated to Germania doesn't feel like it makes sense. I'm sure you're getting it from somewhere? But in other places Camallia first slipped into torpor in the mid first century CE. The Ventrue were written of as being a considerable force in the Roman empire long after that in several places, right up to the fall of the Western Empire (and in the Eastern one they were 1/3rd of its ruling clan structure until the fourth crusade). What are you otherwise referring to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I suppose we have <i>two more</i> Ventrue -- methuselahs in <i>this</i> case -- who fall right into the &quot;totally an exception, not the rule&quot; category of being complete assholes who overreached, overestimated their own power in hubris, and got what was rightfully coming to them in the end. </div> </div> </div>Ulfila maintained his considerable power just fine throughout Italy into the modern nights (and the Catholic Church beyond it) without any personal consequence to himself, for all that he had one coming. Camilla effed about with Rome as Cretheus' pawn just fine and while he eventually went into torpor and thus had his title slide away from him yet again (which seemed to be a cycle with him and Rome at that point), survived into the modern nights and across his career overall with seemingly such little issue that Noddist scholars find him remarkable as a figure who survives whatever all gets thrown at him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only domain worth mentioning was Britannia </div> </div> </div>No, that's the only domain you feel is worth mentioning, that's not the same thing. It's impressive just fine as far as the medieval period to have multiple Ventrue princes in Italy, Scandinavia, Poland (unnamed, but present enough for the country to be noted as essentially split in conflict between multiple clans, including theirs), and various other places besides.<br /> <br /> It's strange to read as a take on this. The notion that the Medieval era showed Ventrue as having influence that ran across Europe would seem to be a pretty basic and uncontroversial statement as far as just the actual game material. Most territories that were not considered some other clan's personal overbloc had several Ventrue princes (and even within said overblocs it was not unheard of to find a Ventrue prince, stubbornly or fluidly holding on).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except as even <i>you</i> admit, the clan lives and dies on dignitas, <i>perception</i> of strength and unity, &quot;stability&quot;, and &quot;reliability&quot;. Being unable to hold the financial capitol of the world and the <i>actual</i> capitol of the country with a <i>few dozen thousand</i> nuclear warheads, really has to be a stain on that so-precious dignitas, strength, and stability, yes? We ain't talking about a state capitol, we're talking about domain with control over the plurality of global GDP and the <i>majority</i> of global military might. </div> </div> </div>This is a minor thing, but as far as holding onto &quot;the financial capital of the world&quot;, Michaela was Prince of Manhattan for nearly a century to the point of holding it through repeated attack. She and her childer held considerable, demonstrable influence over Wall Street. They did this throughout the 20th century despite being in the heart of Sabbat territory. After her death (the thing I guess you will probably focus on to ignore the rest of this?) the Sabbat got to enjoy taking Manhattan from her for a year and change before the Siege of New York, whose major organizers from on high in a grand strategic sense (and also financial backers) were Lucinde, Jan Pieterszoon, Ulfila, and Queen Anne. Ultimately in V20 the princedom of New York would go to a Ventrue, Helene Panhard, who held it even into V5 (not that this wasn't the most absolutely boring way to resolve the &quot;who shall be Camarilla Prince of New York?&quot; plot from New York by Night, but it's how they resolved it all the same). I'm not really sure thereby what you're trying to say there.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you feel you're trying to argue with in what I said here really in any sense, so let me try and note this as clearly as I can.<br /> <br /> 1) You noted a thing about how you felt the Ventrue's influence was portrayed in the Dark Ages part of the setting in terms of geographical constraint, that you seem to be saying it was in fact a nonentity outside the HRE without significant presences. I am noting that what you said does not fit with the actual game material, and giving examples. It seems otherwise you feel that unless a given clan absolutely controls some area as a bloc, they can't otherwise have strong influence in it. Which just doesn't feel like it fits with things.<br /> <br /> 2) You noted a thing about the Camarilla being restricted to Europe and parts of North America, which is difficult to see as being the case. As far as the state of things pre V5, various products that note the modern nights Camarilla having things like multiple cities in South and Central America, that the sect's influence extends just fine into Asia Minor, that the Ashirra went through various motions of caving and affiliating to them, that the Camarilla had cities in India (and particularly with V20 basically taking the Cathayan resurgence off the board, still did), that they had managed even otherwise to force holdings in the very hearts of power of their enemies with regards Veracruz in Mexico and Macau in China (and Hong Kong for a bit, I suppose while we're there). They were a global sect with global reach and leverage just fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  corrected a grammatical thing 09-06-2021, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T20:19:34-07:00","id":1458921,"title":"","content":"I always found it weird they made New York the heart of the Sabbat but for some reason wanted Wallstreet to be controlled by the Ventrue anyway.<br /> <br /> It's like they didn't think the Tzimisce and Grimaldi could handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T20:34:28-07:00","id":1458922,"title":"","content":"I suppose I liked the idea that Manhattan was this weird outpost under siege for the better part of a century as an image and Michaela doing increasingly ruthless things to hold it (like the occassional mass embrace). Also hey, want a convenient canonical origin for that low gen Ventrue neonate pc of yours? One of Michaela's waves of childer.<br /> <br /> (Her death was also really dumb. Yeah, the writers needed to remove her from the board to be able to make &quot;who shall be Prince of New York after the Siege?&quot; a plotline in Revised edition, but they could have removed her in a less dumb way)<br /> <br /> Y'know, that's also what bugs me about Helene ending up Prince. They kill a more interesting npc, they make a huge plotline of &quot;New York is conquered, who shall be prince!&quot; and then one edition later they resolve it in the most predictable, boring way possible.<br /> <br /> And then V5, Mr Big Deal Let's Shake Everything Up for the Sake of Shaking Everything Up edition leaves in the fact that the most boring candidate for prince possible still rules New York.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T20:41:53-07:00","id":1458924,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it was the decision of the COTERIES OF NEW YORK people there. I feel like Paradox probably let's a reasonably free hand to its licensees as long as it's just one city.<br /> <br /> The reason Montreal fell to the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> The Montreal based team for CHAPTERS wanted to write about the Camarilla and use their home city.<br /> <br /> (It was in one of their interviews and I always found that fascinating)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T20:46:54-07:00","id":1458926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458921#post1458921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found it weird they made New York the heart of the Sabbat but for some reason wanted Wallstreet to be controlled by the Ventrue anyway.<br /> <br /> It's like they didn't think the Tzimisce and Grimaldi could handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce are more about biology and medicine in general, right? I don't think they'd be good at Wall Street, especially considering how social you have to be in that place. All the Ghouls they make and Reverents they have aren't very Charismatic either, but I suppose they can Ghoul some stock guys anyway (they'd need Ghouls or Reverents to manage Wall Street, since its mostly only opened during the day, right?); but still, Tzimisce Ghouls &amp; Reverents wouldn't be as goodly directed in the stock exchange industry than Venture Ghouls would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T21:01:04-07:00","id":1458930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458924#post1458924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it was the decision of the COTERIES OF NEW YORK people there. I feel like Paradox probably let's a reasonably free hand to its licensees as long as it's just one city.<br /> <br /> The reason Montreal fell to the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> The Montreal based team for CHAPTERS wanted to write about the Camarilla and use their home city.<br /> <br /> (It was in one of their interviews and I always found that fascinating)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean Michaela was killed in Revised, New York was conquered from the Sabbat in Revised, and New York By Night's &quot;Who prince now!&quot; was a revised thing. Helene turning out to be the &quot;me am the prince now!&quot; was a V20 thing. It's just that they kept her into V5.<br /> <br /> So probably not. Still boring though.<br /> <br /> (I was personally rooting for either Qadir or some total out of nowhere dark horse candidate)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T21:14:12-07:00","id":1458933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458926#post1458926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tzimisce are more about biology and medicine in general, right? I don't think they'd be good at Wall Street, especially considering how social you have to be in that place. All the Ghouls they make and Reverents they have aren't very Charismatic either, but I suppose they can Ghoul some stock guys anyway (they'd need Ghouls or Reverents to manage Wall Street, since its mostly only opened during the day, right?); but still, Tzimisce Ghouls &amp; Reverents wouldn't be as goodly directed in the stock exchange industry than Venture Ghouls would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always had the idea the Tzimisce do not share power but they do delegate very well.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce aren't innately good rulers but unlike the Ventrue, they're far more willing to create slaves or servants that fulfill their needs that they don't have. The Revenant Families are full of people who can do the stuff they're not great at.<br /> <br /> The Grimaldi being their own mini-Giovanni family but actually loyal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T21:14:54-07:00","id":1458934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458919#post1458919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't then remember correctly....</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the territory was <i>contested</i> for two hundred years. Having established that,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't believe that multiple Ventrue princes in an area is reflective of Ventrue holding significant influence in an area, I'm not really sure what to tell you? You seem to be demanding some kind of binary view that if the Ventrue did not hold total dominion over an area, you can ignore that they nevertheless could and did hold entirely significant influence in it... </div> </div> </div>I'm attacking a specific position having taken by an opposition, that Ventrue power:<br /> <br /> A) is universal, and<br /> B) uncontestable regardless of social, political, economic, or technological context, due to its universality.<br /> <br /> This was the counter-position to my own: the Ventrue's success is the product of a specific historic context, and that feat was not replicable elsewhere -- nor was replicated elsewhere. The conclusion of that counter-position, in turn, would be Ventrue power is:<br /> <br /> A) ubiquitous,<br /> B) hegemonic, and lastly,<br /> C) uncontested.<br /> <br /> The failure to satisfy any of those three preconditions indicates the counter-position to be, at the very least, poorly-founded if not outright incorrect. Because if the Ventrue are indeed as powerful, and their power so universal, as the opposition would claim, the situation would indeed be binary. Ergo, citing domains or regions in which Ventrue influence is not ubiquitous, hegemonic, and uncontested are not sufficient to support that counter-position. This is why I am looking exclusively at domains in which Ventrue influence is ubiquitous, hegemonic, and uncontested. Mere influence in a region is not synonymous with hegemony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...The Ventrue and their influence get around just fine in DAV times. </div> </div> </div>Just not enough to support that position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That he's a Roman prince is in fact specifically the point. There's... not really any irony there? </div> </div> </div>A Roman prince who was deposed during the height of the Roman Empire, spent a millennium in torpor only having woken up <i>after</i> the nominal point in time of the DA:V setting, and rose to -- as you pointed out -- promptly become the pawn of <i>another</i> vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, the idea that Camilla's deposition (which some books don't treat as a thing that happened, I guess I should say, compared to people erroneously thinking the Great Fire killed him, or what have you) being why the Ventrue retreated to Germania doesn't feel like it makes sense. I'm sure you're getting it from somewhere? </div> </div> </div>More notably, the collapse of the Eternal Senate in the wake of Camilla's fall to torpor, and the heritance of the empire by Toreador and Malkavians. As relayed in Encyclopaedia Vampirica and Lore of the Clans -- of course in the latter the Toreador tell a different story, albeit one that ends in a Ventrue bloodbath at the hands of the Tzimisce. As for the Ventrue, it's left at &quot;we fled and regrouped among the barbarians&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in other places Camallia first slipped into torpor in the mid first century CE. The Ventrue were written of as being a considerable force in the Roman empire long after that in several places, right up to the fall of the Western Empire (and in the Eastern one they were 1/3rd of its ruling clan structure until the fourth crusade). What are you otherwise referring to? </div> </div> </div>Yes, unreliable narrators and all. The common threads are that Camilla went into torpor, the Ventrue fled Rome or died when Rome fell, and ended up in Gaul, Germania, and parts of Illyria. Ultimately, they proved incapable of <i>holding</i> Rome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a minor thing, but as far as holding onto &quot;the financial capital of the world&quot;, Michaela was Prince of Manhattan for nearly a century to the point of holding it through repeated attack... </div> </div> </div><i>Manhattan</i>, yes; the rest of the city is very much contested. But for the purposes of this discussion, Manhattan is the only part that really matters, isn't it.<br /> <br /> And indeed, the key part of this is that the city fell in the first place; and once retaken, it's clearly not the most <i>stable</i> domain. Not fertile ground for supporting the counter-position as stated above. Especially when the primary reason the Siege of New York succeeded, was due to an untimely eleventh-hour intervention by a certain cathedral of flesh which disrupted an otherwise successful counter-attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems otherwise you feel that unless a given clan absolutely controls some area as a bloc, they can't otherwise have strong influence in it. Which just doesn't feel like it fits with things. </div> </div> </div>Because that's the nature of the position I'm attacking. If the Ventrue are as powerful, and their power as universal, as some parties claim, what <i>is</i> the case <i>would not be</i> the case. The Ventrue <i>would</i> control those areas as a bloc; they clearly do not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were a global sect with global reach and leverage just fine. </div> </div> </div>Just not to the extent this overly rose-tinted perspective of the Ventrue would necessarily entail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-06-2021, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T22:04:33-07:00","id":1458938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, the territory was <i>contested</i> for two hundred years. Having established that, </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the more the Popes got involved and city state alliances like the Lombard Leagues strengthened, the more it became increasingly generous to say the HRE had any real lasting power over Northern Italy. If it's any consolation, this would completely backfire on the papacy once there was no political force in existence for them to now appeal to to prevent things like Charles of Anjou running rougshod over the papal throne, or the Avignon Papacy in general. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Roman prince who was deposed during the height of the Roman Empire, spent a millennium in torpor only having woken up <i>after</i> the nominal point in time of the DA:V setting, and rose to -- as you pointed out -- promptly become the pawn of <i>another</i> vampire. </div> </div> </div>It should be noted Cretheus himself (the dude who made a pawn out of him) was also a Ventrue, just one who plays the game at a higher level than most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More notably, the collapse of the Eternal Senate in the wake of Camilla's fall to torpor, and the heritance of the empire by Toreador and Malkavians. As relayed in Encyclopaedia Vampirica and Lore of the Clans -- of course in the latter the Toreador tell a different story, albeit one that ends in a Ventrue bloodbath at the hands of the Tzimisce. As for the Ventrue, it's left at &quot;we fled and regrouped among the barbarians&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Lore of the Clans is an odd duck for rolling with that Camilla didn't go into torpor until the 5th century CE, as opposed to much earlier during Nero's fire (and he did that intentionally out of boredom, it should be said), but Lore of the Clans has that &quot;all or any of this could be lies&quot; thing (so does the Encyclopedia really), I suppose. All the same, Lore of the Clans, for going with the 5th century CE for Camilla's torpor, does at least stick with the notion that the Ventrue rolled around just fine in the Western Roman Empire until the fall. Most sources roll with that the Ventrue were a part of the power of the Roman Empire fine until it kicked it. The Antonian Ventrue would otherwise continue on as holding a third of the Eastern Empire's cainite power until 1204, with Anna as their survivor holding onto Nicaea and the various other things I'd noted. The decline of the Eternal Senate was otherwise not the end of the Ventrue as a major power bloc in the Empire (also the Lasombra would argue in places that the triumverate of clans that held power in the empire was them, the Ventrue, and the Malkavians, so, Vampire Rome is not really the clearest story either way). <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, unreliable narrators and all. The common threads are that Camilla went into torpor, the Ventrue fled Rome or died when Rome fell, and ended up in Gaul, Germania, and parts of Illyria. </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue held on in the Eastern Empire just fine really for centuries after the fall of Rome. Even the non Antonian Ventrue. Also not leaving Rome until Rome fell, my point there is the Ventrue remained a powerful force in the Western Roman Empire for the duration of its existence, that's what I'm getting at. Them leaving Rome isn't really about losing out to other vampires so much as it is &quot;oh crap, the whole place is on fire&quot;. They also weren't the only ones booking it out of there (see angry Lasombra recriminations at, well, everyone but themselves for being the ones that failed the Roman Empire. Which I've always been annoyed by as a Byzantophile. The East continued on just fine for centuries you guys! Look slightly to your right!). And really all the clans have a &quot;well we didn't see this human historical development coming&quot; moment that screws them up at times. Vampires of all sorts of clans running out of Rome for their lives is why the city of Rome itself ended up majority Nosferatu for a while. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Manhattan</i>, yes; the rest of the city is very much contested. But for the purposes of this discussion, Manhattan is the only part that really matters, isn't it.<br /> And indeed, the key part of this is that the city fell in the first place; and once retaken, it's clearly not the most <i>stable</i> domain. Not fertile ground for supporting the counter-position as stated above. Especially when the primary reason the Siege of New York succeeded, was due to an untimely eleventh-hour intervention by a certain cathedral of flesh. </div> </div> </div>Manhattan and more particularly Wall Street were the financial capital bits and the ones the Camarilla/Michaela controlled in the 20th century is my point, and until her stupid death, in a ruthless grip. And again, while I found it boring as crap (well, the conquest itself wasn't boring, New York by Night for instance gives a really fun breakdown of how the Siege happened), New York was conquered as a whole from the Sabbat and then stabilized just fine at the end of said century/beginning of the 21st. Helene's rule ultimately stabilized the city. Just because I don't like that doesn't mean it didn't happen (I can at least argue that Calebros' temporary princedom laid the groundwork for that stability, I suppose). <br /> <br /> Where are you otherwise taking from that the Siege of New York succeeded because of the Cathedral of Flesh though? You mean Lambach Ruthven finding Tzimisce under the city and freaking right out? I wouldn't really say that was a major factor in the Sabbat's loss. It was a major factor in Ruthven freaking right out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T22:08:58-07:00","id":1458940,"title":"","content":"I mean, I wouldn't be SURPRISED if the Camarilla took New York because the Tzimisce Antediluvian willed it, but I don't think there's any evidence he cared either way.<br /> <br /> In the end, all vampires dance to the whims of the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Your decision to rebel against them was very likely planted in your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T22:20:40-07:00","id":1458942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Ventrue's success is the product of a specific historic context, and that feat was not replicable elsewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>This matches up at least in Laibon society. In there, the Guruthi, which are the &quot;loose cousins&quot; of the Nosferatu, rule the majority of all Laibon Domains throughout the African continent. It was actually a good shake up that surprised me when I read the Ebony Kingdom book. As a matter of fact, the Venture have little-to-no influence over much of Africa at all and the Camarilla tried to ride the waves of mortal European Imperialism to uproot the Laibon, but failed in that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T23:15:27-07:00","id":1458954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458942#post1458942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This matches up at least in Laibon society. In there, the Guruthi, which are the &quot;loose cousins&quot; of the Nosferatu, rule the majority of all Laibon Domains throughout the African continent. It was actually a good shake up that surprised me when I read the Ebony Kingdom book. As a matter of fact, the Venture have little-to-no influence over much of Africa at all and the Camarilla tried to ride the waves of mortal European Imperialism to uproot the Laibon, but failed in that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehhh, The Camarilla and Ventrue within them have had varied success enough that I wouldn't really see it as being supported that their success boils down to a specific historic context. While not some kind of hegemonic clan (there's no such thing), the Ventrue have managed to spread, adapt and establish themselves and monger significant influence in a variety of places (this is for instance why you get bloodlines like the Danava and Hijazi flourishing in the way that they do in the places that they have, or why the Antonian Ventrue were one of the governing powers in the vampiric side of the Byzantine Empire for centuries on end).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla beyond the Ventrue as a multi clan entity has managed to adapt itself into functioning up and down the world map. <br /> <br /> The failure of outsider vampires to gain traction in Africa is more a testament to the strength of the Laibon than the weakness or specificity of those seeking purchase over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T02:27:22-07:00","id":1458972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458934#post1458934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the territory was <i>contested</i> for two hundred years. Having established that,<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm attacking a specific position having taken by an opposition, that Ventrue power:<br /> <br /> A) is universal, and<br /> B) uncontestable regardless of social, political, economic, or technological context, due to its universality.<br /> <br /> This was the counter-position to my own: the Ventrue's success is the product of a specific historic context, and that feat was not replicable elsewhere -- nor was replicated elsewhere. The conclusion of that counter-position, in turn, would be Ventrue power is:<br /> <br /> A) ubiquitous,<br /> B) hegemonic, and lastly,<br /> C) uncontested.<br /> <br /> The failure to satisfy any of those three preconditions indicates the counter-position to be, at the very least, poorly-founded if not outright incorrect. Because if the Ventrue are indeed as powerful, and their power so universal, as the opposition would claim, the situation would indeed be binary. Ergo, citing domains or regions in which Ventrue influence is not ubiquitous, hegemonic, and uncontested are not sufficient to support that counter-position. This is why I am looking exclusively at domains in which Ventrue influence is ubiquitous, hegemonic, and uncontested. Mere influence in a region is not synonymous with hegemony.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A: Yes. Or close enough<br /> B: No. First, Uncontestable is a gross exaggeration of what we believe . Second, Your argument was that the Ventrue would do poorly in contexts like where have animist or ancestor veneration beliefs IE religion or culture would decide who rules. Economic or technological context absolutely isn't what you opened your argument with, and nobody has tried to make the case that Ventrue would be the default leaders of hunter-gatherers. &quot;Animist&quot; or &quot;ancestor worshipping&quot; doesn't mean primitive, yet you've clearly lumped them together.<br /> <br /> A: Ubiquitous in settlements large enough to support a vampire governance which isn't of an extremist nature (IE not the Sabbat)<br /> B: Yes<br /> C: A gross exaggeration. We might as well say you think the Ventrue don't rule anywhere or that the Brujah have never not been supportive.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The failure to satisfy any of those three preconditions indicates the counter-position to be, at the very least, poorly-founded if not outright incorrect. </div> </div> </div> so to be correct we need to argue extremes beyond what we actually believe, extremes that you have ascribed for us as? That's a high chair. Howabout you give us good reasoning as to why the Ventrue wouldn't be strong. No, they don't need to be all the princes, and no they don't need to compete with 4th gen methuselah. All I'm getting is that you like the Toreador and Tremere more, and don't seem to want to acknowledge their deep flaws while assuming we think the absolute most of a perfect Ventrue so that you can pretend your claims are more reasonable (and that a certain way of thinking is the only way of thinking.) </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-06-2021, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T10:47:08-07:00","id":1459026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458972#post1458972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> B: No. First, Uncontestable is a gross exaggeration of what we believe.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457581#post1457581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...They're the <b>perfect</b> officer, the <b>perfect</b> merchant, the <b>perfect</b> leader. <b>Doesn't matter where they are, if there are people, they are going to excell</b>. The Clan weakness encourages them to go all in on those people skills. Building up friends, resources and reputation to protect the herd. Is there a culture that does not care for friends, resources, reputation? There is not, so why would the Ventrue only work in Europe? Why would it need a drastic change to work in, say, the Golden Horde, the Tang Dynasty, or the Mali empire? How the fuck can you possibly conclude that the Ventrue are a relic when their abilities so perfectly compliment the modern oligarchy? The dude just wants to project his opinions on a class he doesnt like and ascribe these faults to the Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post, not mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, Your argument was that the Ventrue would do poorly in contexts like where have animist or ancestor veneration beliefs IE religion or culture would decide who rules. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457476#post1457476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see ventrue being the leaders in China (ancestor veneration, Astrology) and Japan (Animism) so I don't know what the f... <b>Oh, you mean like... non urbanized people?</b> Then yeah you don't really have a population to support more than Gangrel, Nosferatu or Ravnos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post, not mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Economic or technological context absolutely isn't what you opened your argument with... </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1457577#post1457577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I elucidate this...<br /> <br /> <b>No individual culture sprang into existence, fully-formed, in an <u>industrialized </u>or <u>urbanized </u>context. All cultures were <u>preindustrial </u>at some point, and <u>industrial</u>/<u>postindustrial </u>societies are built upon historico-cultural contexts that inform them. In WoD, the current &quot;niches&quot; vampire clans nominally occupy are informed by those contexts, and how each individual clan has adapted to the ages over time.</b><br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, Ventrue aren't &quot;rulers&quot; just because they one night collectively decided writ nothing they were going to be &quot;rulers&quot;; <b>the clan leveraged its <u>military might</u> through mortal pawns in the Dark Ages into <u>feudal wealth</u>, leveraged that <u>feudal wealth</u> and influence through the <u>Renaissance</u> to reform as an aristocratic, <u>mercantile</u>, clan, then leveraged its <u>mercantile influence</u> to rebuild itself into the political class of <u>the Modern era</u> through the rise of <u>western liberal democracy</u>.</b><br /> <br /> The stark reality is, the Ventrue are a relic. Their flaw and discipline spread are representative of the era of hard power, empire, and serfdom. <b>They've only been able to navigate the <u>transition from Dark Ages to post-industrialism</u>, by leveraging institutional momentum to preserve their grasp on power.</b> All things being equal, they're neither positioned or endowed to negotiate the postmodern climate of soft power, negotiation and dealmaking, and fluidity in alliance particularly well, least of all in comparison to <i>other</i> clans that could readily supplant them if so-inclined.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean when I say the clans' &quot;hats&quot; are necessarily eurocentric. <b>Clans' archetypes can only be fully understood in that specific European historico-cultural context. So what of other continents, regions, and cultures in which that specific causal chain from the fall of Rome to <u>the invention of the steam engine</u> didn't happen, or didn't happen in that precise order?</b> Where <i>would</i> the clans, for their flaws and discipline spreads, <i>really</i> fall in those historico-cultural contexts, thereby granting the institutional momentum they would carry<b> from prehistoric or <u>preindustrial</u> times into modern nights?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><i>My</i> post. Bolded and underlined for emphasis.<br /> <br /> I fail to see how usage of the words &quot;industrial&quot;, &quot;preindustrial&quot;, &quot;urbanized&quot;, &quot;feudal wealth&quot;, &quot;mercantile&quot;, &quot;postindustrial&quot;, and &quot;steam engine&quot; -- in some cases, <i>repeatedly</i> -- fail to convey that I was speaking specifically about economic and technological development, as well as cultural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and nobody has tried to make the case that Ventrue would be the default leaders of hunter-gatherers. </div> </div> </div>Except this is literally what you did, as I quoted earlier, in pointing out how the clan flaw isn't dispositive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Animist&quot; or &quot;ancestor worshipping&quot; doesn't mean primitive, yet you've clearly lumped them together. </div> </div> </div>As I just quoted, that was <i>your</i> assumption and not mine.<br /> <br /> Stop projecting to continue attempting the &quot;I'm not racist, you're racist!&quot; canard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...so to be correct we need to argue extremes beyond what we actually believe, extremes that you have ascribed for us as? That's a high chair. </div> </div> </div>It's a chair you built and sat in yourself. Own it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Howabout you give us good reasoning as to why the Ventrue wouldn't be strong. </div> </div> </div>Ain't my problem if you ignored them to cherry pick quotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-06-2021, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T11:07:39-07:00","id":1459029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458926#post1458926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tzimisce are more about biology and medicine in general, right? I don't think they'd be good at Wall Street, especially considering how social you have to be in that place. All the Ghouls they make and Reverents they have aren't very Charismatic either, but I suppose they can Ghoul some stock guys anyway (they'd need Ghouls or Reverents to manage Wall Street, since its mostly only opened during the day, right?); but still, Tzimisce Ghouls &amp; Reverents wouldn't be as goodly directed in the stock exchange industry than Venture Ghouls would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be surprised, the Revenant Families are pretty good at getting things done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T12:53:56-07:00","id":1459051,"title":"","content":"<i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All things being equal, they're neither positioned or endowed to negotiate the postmodern climate of soft power, negotiation and dealmaking, and fluidity in alliance particularly well, least of all in comparison to </div> </div> </div></i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>other</i><i> clans that could readily supplant them if so-inclined.</i> </div> </div> </div><i>I'm sorry, I'm just really stuck at... this.... What are you trying to say here?<br /> <br /> Postmodern Climate; are we in one?<br /> Soft power; Ventrue are bad at this?<br /> Negotiation; Ventrue are bad at this?<br /> Dealmaking; Ventrue are bad at this?<br /> Fluidity in alliance? Ventrue are bad at this? </i><br /> <br /> I feel like you're trying to convince me that black is white and white is black, the moon landing was fake, the earth is cuboid, and that JJ Abrams is the greatest director of our time. The Ventrue are really good at all these things. Yeah, the Toreador are occasionally good at them too, but they're a fractious bunch, and the Tremere are garbage here. What clans do you have in mind that would beat the Ventrue in our so-called &quot;postmodern&quot; climate? Malks? Nosferatu? If they mustered the effort, maybe. I don't think it's in their nature.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>So what of other continents, regions, and cultures in which that specific causal chain from the fall of Rome to <u>the invention of the steam engine</u> didn't happen, or didn't happen in that precise order? </b> </div> </div> </div>So Japan resisted imperialism by becoming an empire itself. I don't think it's reasonable to assume a Japanese Ventrue would have less of a shot there because they imported the steam engine rather than invented it themselves. Oh yes, contact with any more advanced power is going to create a turbulent time, but it isn't going to stop the Ventrue from &quot;winning&quot; So there's european colonialism which impacted... everywhere. There's the middle east and india not actually having any good reason why Ventrue wouldn't be doing well. The parts of Africa that reached the medieval stage don't really have anything that'd screw the Ventrue... Aside from whiter Ventrue of course... uhm.... Ignoring the hostility of Cathayans and the Sabbat or the Brujah council and their successful mass murder, I really, truly can't think of anywhere that has some degree of Urbanization that would be bad for Ventrue. They're better with people than any other Vampire clan, and they're not surpassed dealing with other vampires... What is a context in which they wouldn't work? One without people? How does a Ventrue struggle more in a place already developed than a place developing, or a place that has had modernity thrust upon them? All the Ventrue needs to do is control the right people and he's good wherever there's people. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>the clan leveraged its <u>military might</u> through mortal pawns in the Dark Ages into <u>feudal wealth</u>, leveraged that <u>feudal wealth</u> and influence through the <u>Renaissance</u> to reform as an aristocratic, <u>mercantile</u>, clan, then leveraged its <u>mercantile influence</u> to rebuild itself into the political class of <u>the Modern era</u> through the rise of <u>western liberal democracy</u>.</b><br /> <br /> <i>The stark reality is, the Ventrue are a relic. Their flaw and discipline spread are representative of the era of hard power, empire, and serfdom. </i><b>They've only been able to navigate the <u>transition from Dark Ages to post-industrialism</u>, by leveraging institutional momentum to preserve their grasp on power. </b> </div> </div> </div>So the clan reinvented itself five times and you're thinking they can't do it a sixth because their disciplines and weaknesses are dated...<br /> <br /> If anything, they're stronger. More emphasis on the masquerade greatly increases the value of Dominate. Presence works the same, and Fortitude in an era of handguns and bombs? It's arguably the most valid physical (even if mechanics leave something to be desired) As for the weakness? It's actually far less of a problem now than it would've been ever before in the past. nightlife actually being a thing, Larger, denser cities, mobile apps massively cutting down the effort required to search for new herd members, the anonymity of too-many people letting them get away with what others would perceive as a weird fetish, and the Ventrue can easily create support groups, charities, group things, whatever to get his eggs in one basket. Surely now is the primetime of the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-06-2021, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T13:34:42-07:00","id":1459056,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a>, would the Ventrue work in Brazil? If not, who would work better in your opinion? Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T17:26:30-07:00","id":1459081,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to also think that it's maybe less the &quot;Ventrue&quot; as a culture than specific Ventrue are immortal and have been influencing and making the stereotypes of the Clan for millennia.<br /> <br /> Plus any culture a Ventrue is embraced in will be influencing it and by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T18:29:04-07:00","id":1459085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1459051#post1459051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they mustered the effort, maybe. I don't think it's in their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Winner, winner, chicken dinner. Ventrue don't rule because of some divine, thaumaturgical, darwinistic, supernatural, or sanguineous mandate. They rule because the other clans <i>allow</i> it. And when they decide they've had enough of the Ventrue's shit -- Rome (regardless of the story's details), the Courts of Love, and so on -- Ventrue tend to not last too long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Japan resisted imperialism by becoming an empire itself. </div> </div> </div>So, boy howdy, do I have some news for you about the Meiji Restoration if you think that shit began at sonno joi and fukoku kyouhei...it really wasn't a &quot;restoration&quot; at all, and in practice it was simply a transition from one bakufu to another, albeit under a different name, a constitution, and a nominal (but in no meaningful way whatsoever) abolition of the samurai caste.<br /> <br /> That wasn't even the point the Japanese &quot;became&quot; an empire in the first place, they were just...not very good at it. At least, in terms of invading and holding parts of the mainland. Islands such as Okinawa, on the other hand, made for ripe conquest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think it's reasonable to assume a Japanese Ventrue would have less of a shot there because they imported the steam engine rather than invented it themselves... </div> </div> </div>Sure. So long as they existed there to begin with, and were intertwined particularly with the Sat-Cho alliance opposed to the Tokugawa bakufu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...So there's european colonialism which impacted... everywhere. </div> </div> </div>So, the global exportation of the very wealth, power, and influence I cited in the very beginning. In other words, <i>power they already had</i>. Which necessitates the question of how they got <i>that</i> power in the first place, as opposed to elsewhere and by other means. And, that it's <i>still</i> eurocentricity.<br /> <br /> And we return to that very circularity I called out pages ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the clan reinvented itself five times and you're thinking they can't do it a sixth because their disciplines and weaknesses are dated... </div> </div> </div>Not when Ventrue overstep their bounds, and when other clans collectively realize they're a paper tiger and decide to do something about it, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1459056#post1459056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a>, would the Ventrue work in Brazil? If not, who would work better in your opinion? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question is more, what <i>ought to be done</i> if one were to publish something about the region than the same old, same old.<br /> <br /> In the past five or so years, thanks to technological advancements in mapping and jungle canopy-penetrating scanning (not to mention the ongoing and accelerating depletion of Central and South American rainforests), we've learned Native American civilization was <i>way</i> fucking larger, urbanized, and advanced than anthropologists ever would have guessed. To the point that in the last two or so years, a new theory has emerged and is rapidly gaining acceptance, that imported European diseases such as smallpox devastated Native cultures, to the point rainforest regrowth in depopulated areas may have been a major contributor to the Little Ice Age.<br /> <br /> So, there've always been Native American vampires of various clans and bloodlines in the game. Gangrel, definitely. The Tlacique were already there chilling among the Aztecs, and Baali certainly had a presence <i>somehow</i>. And we have the newer concept of the Drowned Legacies, of course.<br /> <br /> So we have huge tracts of land that were highly developed, urbanized even, in a preindustrial society. Key vampire territory. Those peoples were wiped out by European diseases long before Conquistadors (and Sabbat) rolled in. So what happened to those vampires?<br /> <br /> I think it's a much more entertaining -- and narratively compelling -- possibility for the Sabbat to have been dicking around down there for centuries, hunting some <i>really</i> old vampires who fell to torpor when their societies collapsed around them and their herds died out. They might even have been successful, in some limited capacity. And depending on one's use of V5 metaplot, the region's in current varying states of &quot;the Sabbat fucked off&quot; leaving a power vacuum for the Camarilla to potentially inhabit.<br /> <br /> But in the wake of the political fuckery and widescale environmental devastation of the past forty to sixty years, the chances of some really old, <i>really</i> pissed off, motherfuckers of God only knows what clans or bloodlines, waking up has increased exponentially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-06-2021, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T07:57:56-07:00","id":1459137,"title":"","content":"Random silly thoughts, but I complained about the Salubri disciplines in V5, and looking at them again I just noticed they line up with the Tremere<br /> Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude.<br /> Auspex, Dominate, Blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> This amuses me, because I always treated the Tremere as a Salubri bloodline (or the Salubri as a Tremere bloodline. It doesn't matter, bloodlines are annoying clutter that I prune and tone down anwyay. The point is that they cultivate slightly different disciplines and have a different culture but in my games they're still of the same clan)<br /> <br /> Their new weaknesses would be interesting if rolled together. Ignoring the weeping third eye stuff, because that's a bit much - but you get vampires with vitae that not only is extremely tasty to the point of triggering hunger frenzies in nearby vampires by scent alone, but drinking it doesn't start enslaving you to your victim's will (although it will draw the ire of a community of sorcerers). Slap that on the Tremere and it puts a new edge on their hostile relationship with the clan of vitae-addicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 09-07-2021, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T21:03:03-07:00","id":1459246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1459137#post1459137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random silly thoughts, but I complained about the Salubri disciplines in V5, and looking at them again I just noticed they line up with the Tremere<br /> Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude.<br /> Auspex, Dominate, Blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> This amuses me, because I always treated the Tremere as a Salubri bloodline (or the Salubri as a Tremere bloodline. It doesn't matter, bloodlines are annoying clutter that I prune and tone down anwyay. The point is that they cultivate slightly different disciplines and have a different culture but in my games they're still of the same clan)<br /> <br /> Their new weaknesses would be interesting if rolled together. Ignoring the weeping third eye stuff, because that's a bit much - but you get vampires with vitae that not only is extremely tasty to the point of triggering hunger frenzies in nearby vampires by scent alone, but drinking it doesn't start enslaving you to your victim's will (although it will draw the ire of a community of sorcerers). Slap that on the Tremere and it puts a new edge on their hostile relationship with the clan of vitae-addicts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always treated the Tremere as a Tzimisci bloodline and assumed that the elder vampires they first used in their ritual were members of the Old Clan Tzimisci bloodline. The Old Clan has Auspex, Dominate and Animalism so the Tremere just swapped Animalism for Thaumaturgy. That would technically makes Tremere a bloodline of the bloodline but that sort of fits with how weird and unusual they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T02:46:36-07:00","id":1459264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1459085#post1459085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Winner, winner, chicken dinner. Ventrue don't rule because of some divine, thaumaturgical, darwinistic, supernatural, or sanguineous mandate. They rule because the other clans <i>allow</i> it. And when they decide they've had enough of the Ventrue's shit -- Rome (regardless of the story's details), the Courts of Love, and so on -- Ventrue tend to not last too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give an inch and you'll take a mile.<br /> The Malkavians and Nosferatu were rhetorical: They could likely build up money, contacts and allies up very fast if they were so inclined, but they also could be some of the best in purge the city of all other vampires if they were so inclined (obfuscate+Animalism/Auspex+Dominate and explosives... hell of a drug) If the six other core clans decided they really didn't want the Ventrue in charge, and we're assuming the ventrue don't have some other overwhelming advantage in age or numbers, the ventrue wouldn't be able to do a thing about it, which is why the Sabbat's ventrue presence is limited largely to LARPers. But the issue is, most clans see the Ventrue in charge as the least-evil option. That's their strength. Toreador are fickle and petty, Brujah are bullies, Malkavians are.. complicated. The Tremere? Insufferable. Giovanni? Ditto. Settites? Slimy cult. Lasombra? Rule of terror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, the global exportation of the very wealth, power, and influence I cited in the very beginning. In other words, <i>power they already had</i>. Which necessitates the question of how they got <i>that</i> power in the first place, as opposed to elsewhere and by other means. And, that it's <i>still</i> eurocentricity.<br /> <br /> And we return to that very circularity I called out pages ago.<br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Have you ever played Ventrue? It's alarming how you can create rabid, unimaginative fantasies of their modern inadequacy without actually understanding how they work in play. Your modern Ventrue neonate is an absolute puppet master, easily able to snowball in assets even without help from his clan mates (we're assuming he's been trained to standard).<br /> <br /> Fuck soft power. Fuck the horse it rode in on. It's ok, we bought the horse, it's ours. We paid the cops off. All hail the almighty dollar.<br /> Modern power is about Capital. It's about owning stuff. No Clan can own stuff quite so well as the Ventrue. Even if they start from nothing, From the first ghoul embezzlment to the first hundred suckers investing to the first holding company (or the Ventrue can Emulate Kenneth Copeland ), Ventrue rapidly outpace any other clan in the acquisition of <i>people</i> and <i>stuff</i> and<i> image</i>. To say nothing of the clan's willingness to give them a grant or loan allowing them to skip the initial steps. If they really need the push, they can helm a few companies of mind-controlled slaves and still seem like good guys doing it. You can own the companies, you can fuck with the markets, this in turn allows you substantial influence, and you're the most agreeable chap in Elysium. Every cell of blue blood is geared towards the control of others and thus the acquisition of wealth and influence. Having rich predecessors who can help you is a massive advantage, but it's not at all necessary. The Clan doesn't emulate mortal business dynasties, where the first person acquires wealth and the rest are sheltered fools that just maintain it until they inevitably decline. The Clan embraces new people to spread out, take advantage of new trends, and build upon the wealth that the clan already has while older assets wither away with time. The modern world is at the mercy of billionaires and the many multi-millionaires beneath them: No clan is better suited for raising billionaires than the Ventrue*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Tremere excluded. They're basically big-tech metaphores, but Nobody will let the Tremere start running things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-08-2021, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T03:03:07-07:00","id":1459267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1459246#post1459246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always treated the Tremere as a Tzimisci bloodline and assumed that the elder vampires they first used in their ritual were members of the Old Clan Tzimisci bloodline. The Old Clan has Auspex, Dominate and Animalism so the Tremere just swapped Animalism for Thaumaturgy. That would technically makes Tremere a bloodline of the bloodline but that sort of fits with how weird and unusual they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere work as Tzimisce too. They can also work as the world's only successful organised body of Caitiff (being self-created, they don't really have a clan curse)<br /> <br /> I go for Salubri for a couple of reasons:<br /> 1) The Salubri are one of the 13, yet are basically extinct and thus feel out of place for me. Making the Tremere and the remnants of the original clan one is how I fix that feeling<br /> 2) I think I saw something about a flaw where Tremere manifest a third eye years ago, but I could be confusing half-remembered Gehenna events with flaws and merits<br /> 3) Saulot's diablerie<br /> 4) The Tzimisce hate them, the Assamite hate them, the Gangrel hate them, the Nosferatu hate them, nobody else is terribly fond of them... but it's the Salubri they seem most tangled with.<br /> <br /> Although it could be a mixture, due to the Tremere having an unorthodox origin. 50% of the clan qualifies as Salubri, the other as Tzimisce. Or you have Salubri-Tremere, Tzimisce-Tremere and Tremere unaffected by either Tzimisce vitae or Saulot who are technically Caitiff and could be considered &quot;pure/real Tremere&quot;.<br /> (Actually, if Tremere have been ritually created, perhaps it's not totally out of imagination for a portion of the Tremere to have been created afresh a second time, free of the influences affecting the pyramid... Might try that for a twist on Tremere antitribu sometime, with a second generation of fresh, Ante-free Tremere following Tremere/Goratrix while Saulot and the Eldest are doing the one-worm tango for control of the main clan - uh, edit; you probably need an actual mage... uhh... well, I'm sure there's <i>somebod</i>y out there amongst the awakened who could be convinced.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 09-08-2021, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T15:05:18-07:00","id":1459347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1459264#post1459264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...But the issue is, most clans see the Ventrue in charge as the least-evil option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most clans see Ventrue &quot;in charge&quot; as the best &quot;better them than us&quot; option. They're the Camarilla's frontend; nothing more, nothing less. They're the ones telling everyone what the &quot;decisions&quot; are, the ones who take the blame when things go sideways whether it's <i>actually</i> their fault or not, and the ones getting deposed while the elders and primogen point and laugh...before deciding who the next greater fool shall be.<br /> <br /> And that's what the Ventrue are: the greater fool.<br /> <br /> When there's a frontend, there's a backend, and nothing gets done without a functional backend. <i>That's </i>where the other three to six clans come in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you ever played Ventrue? </div> </div> </div>In Dark Ages and modern nights, as Camarilla, Sabbat, <i>and</i> Anarch. My favorite one I ever played was a Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> who defected to the Camarilla. And let me tell you, Auspex is a <i>hard</i> carrier discipline when you're playing a Ventrue Sheriff, and you got that job because the Prince is <i>also </i>a Ventrue and your sponsor for your proud &quot;return to the fold&quot; moment.<br /> <br /> At least until the Prince dies to a Sabbat raid that just, by <i>some</i> miracle, happened to be in the right place at the right time. Then, that Sabbat pack <i>also</i> dies, coincidentally destroying any evidence my PC may or may not have been involved, and you suddenly find yourself the one calling the shots having saved the city from a potential siege...<br /> <br /> And of course, I <i>storytell</i> also, and in the course of storytelling, I've run damn near everything under the sun related to the Ventrue. Ask me how I took my TC players from being pants-shittingly terrified of Bulscu, to actually thinking he's one of the more badass NPC's in the chronicle to date...and <i>actually feeling a bit sympathetic towards him</i> for being a dying breed of proud warlords evocative of a supposed golden age of the clan, and for the the untimely and unpreventable death of one of his childer, in the course of about three game sessions.<br /> <br /> And ask me how much I've made them utterly <i>revile</i> Nova Arpad, to the point I make them physically wince when she shows up in a game session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's alarming how you can create rabid, unimaginative fantasies of their modern inadequacy without actually understanding how they work in play. </div> </div> </div>I understand <i>quite</i> well, thank you. Do <i>you</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your modern Ventrue neonate is an absolute puppet master, easily able to snowball in assets even without help from his clan mates (we're assuming he's been trained to standard). </div> </div> </div>Insofar as they're incapable of stepping on their elder clanmates' toes, who pretty much already &quot;own&quot; everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fuck soft power. </div> </div> </div>...and then, finally having discarded the mask and gone full Krauthammer (you never go full Krauthammer), you go on to list a bunch of examples of how finances are used in the exercise of <i>soft</i> power.<br /> <br /> As if any of us in the thread still belabored under the delusion you actually know what the distinction between soft power and hard power is.<br /> <br /> Hint: yes, money can be used for both soft and hard power. Examples of use of money in <i>hard</i> power would be things like hostile takeovers and exit strategies, adverse possession, vexatious litigation, malicious use and abuse of process, SLAPP's, delay-and-dump, deliberately externalizing costs. You know, use of money to <i>coerce</i> a predetermined course of action.<br /> <br /> Otherwise known as, &quot;the kinds of shit Ventrue pull with their money&quot;. Had you bothered to read the clanbook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...You can own the companies, you can fuck with the markets... </div> </div> </div>...until a bunch of bored crayon-eaters on Reddit catch wise. Then you're just a living meme e-filing for chapter 11.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T15:20:49-07:00","id":1459350,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Guys this is getting overly aggressive and starting to attack the posters directly. Please tone it down or I'll have to close the thread.<br /> <br /> Remember this is all for fun and no one is &quot;right&quot; save at their own table.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}